<graph edgedefault="undirected"><node id="C1/RIPE3b1 Binding Factor">
  <data key="d0">C1/RIPE3b1 Binding Factor</data>
  <data key="d1">Biological Process</data>
  <data key="d2">The C1/RIPE3b1 binding factor is a transcriptional regulator that binds to the −118/−107 bp region and controls pancreatic-β-cell-specific and glucose-regulated transcription of the insulin gene.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bf89ad08d3f81ffe84c9bf7f208c604b</data>
  <data key="d4">Members of the large Maf transcription family regulate insulin gene transcription in islet beta cells.</data>
  <data key="d5">1778560728</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">0</data>
  <data key="d8">beta cell / MAFA / MAFB</data>
  <data key="d9">0.00030027</data>
  <data key="d10">0.00071622</data>
  <data key="d11">0.00805172</data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Gene">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Gene</data>
  <data key="d1">Method</data>
  <data key="d2">The insulin gene is the target gene whose transcription is regulated by the C1/RIPE3b1 binding factor and members of the large Maf transcription family in islet β cells.&lt;SEP&gt;The insulin gene is a target of MAFA transcriptional activation, with MAFA serving as a glucose-regulated and pancreatic beta-cell-specific transcriptional activator for its expression.&lt;SEP&gt;The insulin gene is the genetic sequence encoding insulin, transcriptionally activated by MafA and regulated by multiple transcription factors including MafB and other large Maf family members.&lt;SEP&gt;The gene encoding insulin, activated by MafA and subject to oxidative stress-mediated loss of expression in glucotoxic beta cells.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bf89ad08d3f81ffe84c9bf7f208c604b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fffe587d9d8a94d6179115102ef90a2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4e0ae079210c3ef99872d0747c5a9b88&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f64af938dff7c5f186bd7024d92cbc0</data>
  <data key="d4">Members of the large Maf transcription family regulate insulin gene transcription in islet beta cells.&lt;SEP&gt;MafB Is Important for Pancreatic β-Cell Maintenance under a MafA-Deficient Condition.&lt;SEP&gt;Sex-biased islet β cell dysfunction is caused by the MODY MAFA S64F variant by inducing premature aging and senescence in males.&lt;SEP&gt;MAFA missense mutation causes familial insulinomatosis and diabetes mellitus.</data>
  <data key="d5">1778562649</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">0</data>
  <data key="d8">beta cell / MAFA / MAFB</data>
  <data key="d9">0.00019486</data>
  <data key="d10">5.481e-05</data>
  <data key="d11">0.01617947</data>
</node>
<node id="Large Maf Transcription Family">
  <data key="d0">Large Maf Transcription Family</data>
  <data key="d1">Biological Process</data>
  <data key="d2">The large Maf transcription factor family includes MafA, MafB, and c-Maf, all of which play roles in regulating insulin gene transcription in islet β cells.&lt;SEP&gt;The large Maf transcription family includes members such as MafA and MafB that regulate insulin gene transcription in islet β cells.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bf89ad08d3f81ffe84c9bf7f208c604b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9ed09558012a9cb8eba4b1efe943943</data>
  <data key="d4">Members of the large Maf transcription family regulate insulin gene transcription in islet beta cells.&lt;SEP&gt;MafA and MafB regulate genes critical to beta-cells in a unique temporal manner.</data>
  <data key="d5">1778561066</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">0</data>
  <data key="d8">beta cell / MAFA / MAFB</data>
  <data key="d9">0.00033279</data>
  <data key="d10">0.00041296</data>
  <data key="d11">0.01619807</data>
</node>
<node id="βTC-3 Cells">
  <data key="d0">βTC-3 Cells</data>
  <data key="d1">Biological Process</data>
  <data key="d2">βTC-3 is a mouse β-cell line from which nuclear extracts were used to purify the C1/RIPE3b1 activator and to study MafA binding to the insulin gene enhancer region.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bf89ad08d3f81ffe84c9bf7f208c604b</data>
  <data key="d4">Members of the large Maf transcription family regulate insulin gene transcription in islet beta cells.</data>
  <data key="d5">1778560729</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">0</data>
  <data key="d8">beta cell / MAFA / MAFB</data>
  <data key="d9">0.00013544</data>
  <data key="d10">0.0</data>
  <data key="d11">0.00803323</data>
</node>
<node id="Islet β Cells">
  <data key="d0">Islet β Cells</data>
  <data key="d1">Biological Process</data>
  <data key="d2">Islet β cells are pancreatic cells that specifically express and are regulated by members of the large Maf transcription family for insulin gene transcription.&lt;SEP&gt;Islet β cells are insulin-secreting pancreatic cells regulated by MAFA, and in male MafAS64F/+ mice they exhibit functional deficiencies, DNA damage markers, cell-cycle exit, senescence, and SASP.&lt;SEP&gt;Islet β cells are pancreatic cells in which MAFA protein activity and post-translational modifications are critical for appropriate function, and which are affected by MAFAS64F expression.&lt;SEP&gt;Islet β cells are pancreatic cells responsible for insulin production; their activity is regulated by MafA/MAFB and is affected by the S64F mutation in a species-specific manner.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bf89ad08d3f81ffe84c9bf7f208c604b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68488f40a0b43cd31dd09cb8c1939a9a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-427bdb72b4ec16ac96774e76f03ada77&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b3deb83588a816faad5340f542e1f43</data>
  <data key="d4">Members of the large Maf transcription family regulate insulin gene transcription in islet beta cells.&lt;SEP&gt;Sex-biased islet β cell dysfunction is caused by the MODY MAFA S64F variant by inducing premature aging and senescence in males.</data>
  <data key="d5">1778562651</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
  <data key="d8">Insulin / Pancreatic Islets / A0B0 Mice</data>
  <data key="d9">0.00037304</data>
  <data key="d10">0.00049207</data>
  <data key="d11">0.02604473</data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin C1 Element">
  <data key="d0">Insulin C1 Element</data>
  <data key="d1">Biological Process</data>
  <data key="d2">The insulin C1 element is a regulatory DNA element (−118/−107 bp) within the insulin gene promoter that mediates transcriptional activation by large Maf family members.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bf89ad08d3f81ffe84c9bf7f208c604b</data>
  <data key="d4">Members of the large Maf transcription family regulate insulin gene transcription in islet beta cells.</data>
  <data key="d5">1778560729</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">2</data>
  <data key="d8">Insulin C1 Element</data>
  <data key="d9">3.644e-05</data>
  <data key="d10">0.0</data>
  <data key="d11">0.0</data>
</node>
<node id="DNA Affinity Chromatography">
  <data key="d0">DNA Affinity Chromatography</data>
  <data key="d1">Method</data>
  <data key="d2">DNA affinity chromatography is a purification method used to isolate the C1/RIPE3b1 activator from mouse βTC-3 cell nuclear extracts.</data>
