</node>
<node id="Two-Dimensional Gel Electrophoresis">
  <data key="d0">Two-Dimensional Gel Electrophoresis</data>
  <data key="d1">Method</data>
  <data key="d2">Two-dimensional gel electrophoresis is a protein separation technique used in conjunction with DNA affinity chromatography to purify the C1/RIPE3b1 activator.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bf89ad08d3f81ffe84c9bf7f208c604b</data>
  <data key="d4">Members of the large Maf transcription family regulate insulin gene transcription in islet beta cells.</data>
