<node id="Peptide Mass Mapping">
  <data key="d0">Peptide Mass Mapping</data>
  <data key="d1">Method</data>
  <data key="d2">Peptide mass mapping is an analytical technique used to identify N- and C-terminal peptides of mouse MafA from the purified C1/RIPE3b1 binding fractions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bf89ad08d3f81ffe84c9bf7f208c604b</data>
  <data key="d4">Members of the large Maf transcription family regulate insulin gene transcription in islet beta cells.</data>
