</node>
<node id="Tandem Spectrometry">
  <data key="d0">Tandem Spectrometry</data>
  <data key="d1">Method</data>
  <data key="d2">Tandem spectrometry is a mass spectrometry method used alongside peptide mass mapping to confirm the identity of MafA peptides in the C1/RIPE3b1 binding fraction.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bf89ad08d3f81ffe84c9bf7f208c604b</data>
  <data key="d4">Members of the large Maf transcription family regulate insulin gene transcription in islet beta cells.</data>
