<node id="Chromatin Immunoprecipitation Assay">
  <data key="d0">Chromatin Immunoprecipitation Assay</data>
  <data key="d1">Method</data>
  <data key="d2">The chromatin immunoprecipitation assay is a technique used to demonstrate that MafA binds within the enhancer region (−340/−91 bp) of the endogenous insulin gene in βTC-3 cells.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bf89ad08d3f81ffe84c9bf7f208c604b</data>
  <data key="d4">Members of the large Maf transcription family regulate insulin gene transcription in islet beta cells.</data>
