<node id="Pancreatic β-Cells">
  <data key="d0">Pancreatic β-Cells</data>
  <data key="d1">Biological Process</data>
  <data key="d2">Pancreatic β-cells are insulin-producing endocrine cells in the pancreas; MafA shows selective expression in these cells in adult mice, while MafB is expressed in a subset during embryonic development.&lt;SEP&gt;Pancreatic β-cells are insulin-producing cells that are destroyed in T1D through an autoimmune process; they actively participate in their own destruction and exhibit ER stress and dysregulated UPR.</data>
