<node id="Insulin">
  <data key="d0">Insulin</data>
  <data key="d1">Biological Process</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin is a peptide hormone primarily synthesized and secreted by pancreatic β-cells (islet β-cells) in response to elevated blood glucose levels and nutritional signals. It plays a central role in glucose metabolism, blood glucose homeostasis, and the maintenance of euglycemia, and also exerts counterregulatory effects on glucagon secretion. Loss or dysregulation of insulin is a defining feature of diabetes mellitus, making it a critical focus in both diabetes research and clinical treatment.

At the genetic and transcriptional level, insulin gene expression is regulated by a network of transcription factors, including MafA, MafB, cMaf, PDX-1, and NeuroD1. Insulin is recognized as a mutual target gene of both MafA and MafB; its transcription can be selectively activated by MafA in vitro. During embryonic development, insulin is expressed in MafB+ cells, and its expression is notably reduced in MafB−/− embryos. Insulin mRNA levels are compromised in both MafB−/− and MafAΔPanc;MafB−/− samples, underscoring the collaborative importance of both transcription factors. Insulin expression has been measured in E18.5 pancreata of wild-type and mutant mice as part of developmental studies. Insulin+ cell production and β-cell activity were delayed in MafBΔpanc islets until MafA was fully expressed, and insulin-positive cell counts and the ratio of insulin+ to glucagon+ cells are reduced in 3-week-old MafAΔpanc islets. Insulin expression is also reduced in MAFB-deficient hESCs and MafAΔβ mouse islets.

Insulin secretion and maturation are modulated by several additional factors. ZnT-8 (encoded by Slc30a8), neuronatin, and glucokinase all influence insulin secretion, while Slc30a8 specifically contributes to insulin maturation and storage through zinc accumulation in intracellular vesicles. Rbp4 has also been identified as influencing insulin secretion. Notably, insulin secretion is impaired in male MafAS64F/+ islets but increased in female MafAS64F/+ islets, highlighting sex-dependent regulatory differences. Furthermore, insulin gene expression can be lost in glucotoxic β-cells through oxidative stress-mediated mechanisms.

Insulin content and secretion levels are routinely measured across different mouse genotypes — including WT, A0B2, and A0B0 mice — using ELISA on pancreatic extracts and plasma samples. Insulin expression and content are significantly reduced in A0B2 and A0B0 mice compared to wild-type mice, with production severely impaired in A0B0 mice. Insulin content is also measured relative to total islet DNA content as a standardized functional readout.

From a research and clinical perspective, insulin protein serves as a widely used cellular marker for identifying and quantifying β-cells through immunolabeling, immunohistochemistry, and histological studies, including assessments of islet cell composition in high-fat diet (HFD)-treated mice and insulinomatosis studies. Collectively, insulin content, secretion, and production serve as key measures of β-cell function across diverse experimental contexts.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin is a hormone produced by β-cells, used as a marker in immunostaining and measured in serum; levels were markedly increased in Atf6β−/− knockout mice.&lt;SEP&gt;A hormone produced by β-cells; normal insulin staining pattern was observed in Atf6β−/− mice, supporting lack of dedifferentiation.&lt;SEP&gt;A hormone produced by pancreatic beta cells whose demand regulates beta cell number via the unfolded protein response.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin is a hormone produced and secreted by pancreatic beta cells (β cells), playing a central and essential role in glucose metabolism, glucose homeostasis, and broader metabolic regulation. It is secreted in response to elevated blood glucose levels and other physiological stimuli, including incretin signals and potassium chloride (KCl), to sustain normal glucose homeostasis and meet the body's metabolic demands. Insulin secretion also exhibits sex-specific differences, particularly in diabetic patients.

The synthesis and secretion of insulin are tightly regulated by multiple molecular mechanisms. Key transcription factors include MAFA, which is required for insulin expression in beta cells, and MAFB, which contributes to beta-cell development. Insulin synthesis is also favored by the interaction between estrogen receptor alpha and NEUROD1, and more broadly regulated by sex hormones and various transcription factors. MicroRNA-mediated mechanisms also play a role; overexpression of miR-21 precursor in beta cells negatively affects glucose-stimulated insulin secretion.

Insulin deficiency is closely associated with diabetes. In type 2 diabetes (T2D), insulin secretion is notably impaired — T2D donors exhibit decreased secretion in response to high glucose, incretin, and KCl stimuli — and insufficient secretion drives hyperglycemia. Insulin secretion is similarly impaired in prediabetes. Insulin deficiency can also result from loss of CDK4 expression, and the high secretory burden of insulin production contributes to beta-cell susceptibility to DNA damage. Restored acute insulin secretion has been linked to diabetes reversal following weight loss interventions, and insulin is used as an early glucose-lowering therapy in T2D to reduce beta-cell secretory demand and preserve function.

Caloric restriction (CR) influences insulin dynamics by reducing the metabolic demand for insulin secretion and lowering blood glucose levels; CR beta cells secrete less insulin, potentially due to enhanced bioenergetics and reduced reactive oxygen species (ROS). Reduced circulating insulin has also been shown to enhance insulin sensitivity in old mice and extend lifespan.

In experimental and clinical settings, insulin is measured using ELISA kits — including the Mercodia Insulin ELISA kit — in perifusion, islet perfusion, and bioenergetics experiments. Measurements are typically performed on secreted insulin collected during perifusion experiments and normalized per total insulin content. Insulin is also used as a marker in immunostaining, measured in plasma during meal tolerance tests, and administered intraperitoneally in insulin tolerance tests.&lt;SEP&gt;Hormone secreted by pancreatic beta cells; hypersecretion is associated with senescence and prevented by mTOR inhibition.&lt;SEP&gt;Hormone produced by beta cells in pancreatic islets that regulates blood glucose levels.&lt;SEP&gt;Hormone produced by beta cells; overnutrition increases insulin demand triggering beta-cell hypersecretion and adaptive expansion.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5d5e51c0312e54ad3757625ff1041f76&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9bec3f5c6cf93d2d763da970e02d0fc3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9693157a2d458ecc8255c49ec77d95f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5f82db25373e25b34bbbcfebc1c0f861&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f7f8610c162035d52f2edbe846e8a97&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff8c5dc48dde6c3ccfdc01c9e025403d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9ed09558012a9cb8eba4b1efe943943&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc7255d0eadb6b7f3a3a51c10b8ea742&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41e9c4875e9ee2b378c620275d81fe7e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ddb7aaa2476f3163b5c3de684504f42b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a87d40ff620e7f930f155b5dea286c8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ee443fb4c37f27d6895254d3f95c708&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ecc1e3f157d04d78962c82537c6b7d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69365499ad956be649b962c79d46f483&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e531f038e6fcc1cbb89c2336af984719&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-45b0e9a843120dd461f5ba7ec823e41f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7568462935971fd17472cf21ed7b8a2b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5afa9fdb0e4f653f1c7825c0b258326d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb31cc9ec659a6d29b2ec1e3870fb57b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d01061347ba219119efa4109d89e71f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-968f694e317648c82a07ee150e63adbd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9aad668b81389b88364235018ee9c389&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5afc163e9261bd9f96c6156bfdb27585&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4e0ae079210c3ef99872d0747c5a9b88&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f64af938dff7c5f186bd7024d92cbc0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-427bdb72b4ec16ac96774e76f03ada77&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82e08f93585dc5d50ccfbac2feb8d206&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63a4c12087ceb7cec876e14e7fc45727&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce67306159c306b2c966577061cee6bd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e6c6371cdef301723817998e0efc9ec6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b13f08985b48653da8be9b63098bbb2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40e720fe9c9efb2c2c2dedf6638ae8f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d13aa78bf917b6b3ed2e772b6f010e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c625d74e06abff522b8eb3d76df6ae32&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-222f634a871d4f5fd5cffac2fce0d698&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b67e26d82684726785f1910ba6919cf0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64f42efe8d71d6b6b69c377d2a7c44b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe5b7d8c678cb311e300af3b74f19ed6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51601485f0924871a988aae2e5ce30bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a7d380dafd31120f8a1af317cfb0ab1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5f6e43723dd8061d1a0532981e4a43b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6215695e8bd809fd02cb8b9b7b4123ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-735ea17eaeb5e3524d0871e16116e986&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88b0125512b4fa44926ba8a80a62b0a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-80318e0997c6182c0124775c5f01f6a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68a87a3a1f3eb5d8b0e53b41df492512&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-364a12c675ebfd67c468ab6fc47e6696&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-002f23b1d29df711e839459b4d6f0711&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6cadc21c6ca916dd06510987c1b7dbf4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce68225f2288adf7d07962282496e8c5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-363f3a19905f833d29a7d1242acc6641&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c85c9569fee140bfd52fcc0bbfbcc9c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64b61717ec6764bc92fa7c3c5067d345&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f4fecd9e508da1daa4a0d2d27a7e759&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d0bf8cd8c8cb69199fb8f9bf6c37e70&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d41db2658ec2709309c04b39b1894e48&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5804ddf6c13fee09d00987476aa3c478&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ddac43d21e0426c8d61d02d10c0cb772&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4e8cbb766d17c90c84d2a9452a51a41e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-43761b34ecc024bd90bfa8711c45a233&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-10bdc47e4d027606476b48a401061a27&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8f09e5d1418f8ae04b43a24b97c1d52d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-15ab370ab273e97005ced113e59cc48a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28a44d52c17c29e9741a935aa76e8afe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7af94fcbbc3d167377ece712218fa36b</data>
  <data key="d4">The MafA transcription factor becomes essential to islet β-cells soon after birth.&lt;SEP&gt;MafA and MafB regulate genes critical to beta-cells in a unique temporal manner.&lt;SEP&gt;MafA is a dedicated activator of the insulin gene in vivo.&lt;SEP&gt;Sex-biased islet β cell dysfunction is caused by the MODY MAFA S64F variant by inducing premature aging and senescence in males.&lt;SEP&gt;Species-specific roles for the MAFA and MAFB transcription factors in regulating islet β cell identity.&lt;SEP&gt;MafB Is Important for Pancreatic β-Cell Maintenance under a MafA-Deficient Condition.&lt;SEP&gt;The MAFB transcription factor impacts islet α-cell function in rodents and represents a unique signature of primate islet β-cells.&lt;SEP&gt;Stress-induced β cell early senescence confers protection against type 1 diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;A switch from MafB to MafA expression accompanies differentiation to pancreatic beta-cells.&lt;SEP&gt;MAFA missense mutation causes familial insulinomatosis and diabetes mellitus.</data>
