<node id="Glucagon">
  <data key="d0">Glucagon</data>
  <data key="d1">Protein</data>
  <data key="d2">Glucagon is a peptide hormone produced and secreted primarily by α-cells (alpha cells) within the islets of Langerhans in the pancreas. It plays a central role in glucose homeostasis and maintaining euglycemia, and its release can be inhibited by β-cell secretory products acting on ATP-dependent potassium channels.

In research and clinical contexts, glucagon serves as a key biological marker across a wide range of experimental investigations, including immunohistochemistry, immunolabeling, immunofluorescence staining, ELISA-based quantification, and antibody staining studies of pancreatic tissue. It is measured relative to total islet DNA content and used to assess islet cell composition, analyze islet structure, and characterize cell populations. Anti-glucagon antibodies are employed to measure glucagon-positive cell numbers, and glucagon immunoreactivity is frequently assessed alongside insulin staining to evaluate islet architecture and potential cell conversion between glucagon-producing and insulin-producing cells. Normal glucagon staining patterns and the absence of insulin+/glucagon+ bihormonal cells have been observed in Atf6β−/− mice, and glucagon has also been used as a marker to evaluate islet morphology in Atf6fl/fl mice.

At the transcriptional level, glucagon gene expression is regulated by several large Maf transcription factors. Ectopically expressed large Maf factors — including MafA, MafB, and cMaf — are capable of inducing glucagon reporter construct expression. MafB plays a particularly prominent role, directly activating the glucagon gene in endocrine cells during both development and adulthood. In developing islets, the glucagon gene is expressed in both α- and β-cells, with MafB as a key activator. Glucagon expression and production are measurably reduced in MafB−/− embryos and mutant animals, and glucose-induced glucagon secretion is compromised in adult MafBΔpanc islet α-cells. Glucagon expression is also subject to suppression by Nkx6.1, which counteracts MafB-driven activation.

In various mouse models, glucagon expression and secretion have been further characterized. In MafaΔpanc mice, the glucagon-positive α-cell population remains numerically unchanged but becomes mislocalized into the islet core. In A0B0 islets, glucagon-expressing cell numbers are significantly increased compared to wild-type islets. Glucagon mRNA expression has been quantitatively measured in E18.5 pancreata across different genotypes, providing developmental insight into transcriptional regulation. In MafAS64F/+ mice, glucose-stimulated glucagon secretion and content were not significantly altered, though glucose-regulated secretion may be indirectly affected by counterregulatory effects of insulin, with no obvious sex-dependent impact observed.&lt;SEP&gt;Marker used to identify alpha cells in immunostaining and cell death analysis experiments&lt;SEP&gt;Glucagon is a hormone produced and secreted primarily by alpha (α) cells of the pancreatic islets, with its production and secretion in these cells critically regulated by the transcription factor MAFB. It is also coexpressed with insulin in precursor cells of the mouse endocrine pancreas, suggesting a role during early pancreatic development.

In experimental settings, glucagon secretion is commonly measured using ELISA kits in perifusion experiments, with values normalized per total glucagon content to ensure consistency across samples. Studies examining glucagon secretion under hypoglycemic conditions have generally found no significant differences based on sex or race, though some data indicate a trend toward higher glucagon secretion in females. Additionally, changes in glucagon secretion have been observed following the induction of senescence-associated secretory phenotype (SASP) in cultured human islets, highlighting its sensitivity to cellular stress states.

Circulating glucagon levels have also been assessed in vivo, including measurements in ad libitum (AL) and caloric restriction (CR) mouse models, where no significant changes were observed after two months on the respective diets.

From a methodological standpoint, glucagon serves as an important immunostaining marker for the identification and quantification of alpha cells in pancreatic tissue sections. It is detected via immunohistochemistry using a rabbit anti-glucagon antibody, making it a standard tool in histological analyses of pancreatic endocrine cell composition.&lt;SEP&gt;Hormone produced by pancreatic islet alpha cells, regulated by MAFB expression.&lt;SEP&gt;Hormone measured using the Mercodia Glucagon ELISA kit in islet experiments.&lt;SEP&gt;Hormone secreted by alpha cells, measured alongside insulin in perifusion experiments using ELISA kits.&lt;SEP&gt;Hormone whose receptor is targeted by retatrutide as part of triple agonism to improve metabolic markers.&lt;SEP&gt;Hormone produced by alpha cells; over 50% of islets mapped in whole-organ study lacked glucagon-positive cells.&lt;SEP&gt;Hormone produced by alpha cells in pancreatic islets that contributes to glucose homeostasis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5d5e51c0312e54ad3757625ff1041f76&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9bec3f5c6cf93d2d763da970e02d0fc3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9693157a2d458ecc8255c49ec77d95f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff8c5dc48dde6c3ccfdc01c9e025403d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9ed09558012a9cb8eba4b1efe943943&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc7255d0eadb6b7f3a3a51c10b8ea742&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41e9c4875e9ee2b378c620275d81fe7e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ddb7aaa2476f3163b5c3de684504f42b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a87d40ff620e7f930f155b5dea286c8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ee443fb4c37f27d6895254d3f95c708&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69365499ad956be649b962c79d46f483&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e531f038e6fcc1cbb89c2336af984719&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-45b0e9a843120dd461f5ba7ec823e41f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7568462935971fd17472cf21ed7b8a2b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5afa9fdb0e4f653f1c7825c0b258326d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb31cc9ec659a6d29b2ec1e3870fb57b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d01061347ba219119efa4109d89e71f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9aad668b81389b88364235018ee9c389&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5afc163e9261bd9f96c6156bfdb27585&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4e0ae079210c3ef99872d0747c5a9b88&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f64af938dff7c5f186bd7024d92cbc0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-427bdb72b4ec16ac96774e76f03ada77&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82e08f93585dc5d50ccfbac2feb8d206&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63a4c12087ceb7cec876e14e7fc45727&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce67306159c306b2c966577061cee6bd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40e720fe9c9efb2c2c2dedf6638ae8f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c625d74e06abff522b8eb3d76df6ae32&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e953ac093714735fa9b5b27463bf5dff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ed6515ae53fc7e07b1c44a83258c3224&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64f42efe8d71d6b6b69c377d2a7c44b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe5b7d8c678cb311e300af3b74f19ed6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a7d380dafd31120f8a1af317cfb0ab1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76049b85888e8e904e7c01de9740d34f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6215695e8bd809fd02cb8b9b7b4123ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-735ea17eaeb5e3524d0871e16116e986&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af08dcd3bdc472cb74376c18c72cf9f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6cadc21c6ca916dd06510987c1b7dbf4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d286ee457150be65228790e800b5207b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f4fecd9e508da1daa4a0d2d27a7e759&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d0bf8cd8c8cb69199fb8f9bf6c37e70&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5804ddf6c13fee09d00987476aa3c478&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cba0d7fafdd66d2ffb133e04939d15f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-10bdc47e4d027606476b48a401061a27&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28a44d52c17c29e9741a935aa76e8afe</data>
  <data key="d4">The MafA transcription factor becomes essential to islet β-cells soon after birth.&lt;SEP&gt;MafA and MafB regulate genes critical to beta-cells in a unique temporal manner.&lt;SEP&gt;MafA is a dedicated activator of the insulin gene in vivo.&lt;SEP&gt;Sex-biased islet β cell dysfunction is caused by the MODY MAFA S64F variant by inducing premature aging and senescence in males.&lt;SEP&gt;Species-specific roles for the MAFA and MAFB transcription factors in regulating islet β cell identity.&lt;SEP&gt;MafB Is Important for Pancreatic β-Cell Maintenance under a MafA-Deficient Condition.&lt;SEP&gt;The MAFB transcription factor impacts islet α-cell function in rodents and represents a unique signature of primate islet β-cells.&lt;SEP&gt;Stress-induced β cell early senescence confers protection against type 1 diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;A switch from MafB to MafA expression accompanies differentiation to pancreatic beta-cells.&lt;SEP&gt;MAFA missense mutation causes familial insulinomatosis and diabetes mellitus.&lt;SEP&gt;Developmental control of DNA damage responses in α- and β-cells shapes the selective beta-cell susceptibility in diabetes.</data>
