<node id="Pancreatic Development">
  <data key="d0">Pancreatic Development</data>
  <data key="d1">Biological Process</data>
  <data key="d2">Pancreatic development is the biological process by which the pancreas forms; it involves the regulated expression of transcription factors such as PDX-1, NeuroD1, MafA, and MafB.&lt;SEP&gt;Pancreatic development is the embryonic process during which MafB acts as a primary activator of Slc30a8 expression in α- and β-cells.&lt;SEP&gt;Developmental process during which MAFA and MAFB cooperate with other transcription factors to regulate insulin gene expression in mouse and human.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5d5e51c0312e54ad3757625ff1041f76&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc7255d0eadb6b7f3a3a51c10b8ea742&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eae638e9cabe91a68fc062c9981b0e86</data>
  <data key="d4">MafA and MafB regulate genes critical to beta-cells in a unique temporal manner.&lt;SEP&gt;A switch from MafB to MafA expression accompanies differentiation to pancreatic beta-cells.</data>
  <data key="d5">1778561067</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">0</data>
  <data key="d8">beta cell / MAFA / MAFB</data>
  <data key="d9">0.00018589</data>
  <data key="d10">1.252e-05</data>
  <data key="d11">0.01679785</data>
</node>
<node id="Endocrine Differentiation">
  <data key="d0">Endocrine Differentiation</data>
  <data key="d1">Biological Process</data>
  <data key="d2">Endocrine differentiation is the process by which pancreatic progenitor cells differentiate into hormone-producing endocrine cells, regulated by Maf factors and other transcription factors.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5d5e51c0312e54ad3757625ff1041f76</data>
  <data key="d4">A switch from MafB to MafA expression accompanies differentiation to pancreatic beta-cells.</data>
