<node id="Chick In Ovo Electroporation Assay">
  <data key="d0">Chick In Ovo Electroporation Assay</data>
  <data key="d1">Method</data>
  <data key="d2">The chick in ovo electroporation assay is an experimental method used to analyze whether MafA and MafB are sufficient to induce insulin+ and/or glucagon+ cell formation within embryonic endoderm.&lt;SEP&gt;Experimental assay used to test the ability of MAFA and MAFB chimeric proteins to promote Insulin+ cell formation and activate insulin expression in embryonic endoderm.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9bec3f5c6cf93d2d763da970e02d0fc3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eae638e9cabe91a68fc062c9981b0e86</data>
  <data key="d4">MafA is a dedicated activator of the insulin gene in vivo.</data>
  <data key="d5">1778560839</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">0</data>
  <data key="d8">beta cell / MAFA / MAFB</data>
  <data key="d9">0.00011272</data>
  <data key="d10">0.0</data>
  <data key="d11">0.00827551</data>
</node>
<node id="MafA C-Terminal DNA-Binding Domain">
  <data key="d0">MafA C-Terminal DNA-Binding Domain</data>
  <data key="d1">Biological Process</data>
  <data key="d2">The MafA C-terminal DNA-binding domain contains sequences responsible for chick Insulin activation, as demonstrated through analysis of chimeric MafA and MafB proteins.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9bec3f5c6cf93d2d763da970e02d0fc3</data>
  <data key="d4">MafA is a dedicated activator of the insulin gene in vivo.</data>
  <data key="d5">1778560839</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">0</data>
  <data key="d8">beta cell / MAFA / MAFB</data>
  <data key="d9">0.00016088</data>
  <data key="d10">0.00035816</data>
  <data key="d11">0.00776487</data>
</node>
<node id="Embryonic Endoderm">
  <data key="d0">Embryonic Endoderm</data>
  <data key="d1">Biological Process</data>
  <data key="d2">Embryonic endoderm is the tissue within which ectopic expression of MafA promoted Insulin production in the chick in ovo electroporation assay.&lt;SEP&gt;Tissue used in chick in ovo electroporation assays where MAFA promotes Insulin+ cell formation but MAFB does not, due to lack of cooperating factors.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9bec3f5c6cf93d2d763da970e02d0fc3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eae638e9cabe91a68fc062c9981b0e86</data>
  <data key="d4">MafA is a dedicated activator of the insulin gene in vivo.</data>
  <data key="d5">1778560839</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">0</data>
  <data key="d8">beta cell / MAFA / MAFB</data>
  <data key="d9">7.181e-05</data>
  <data key="d10">0.0</data>
  <data key="d11">0.00775564</data>
</node>
<node id="Mouse Embryonic Pancreas">
  <data key="d0">Mouse Embryonic Pancreas</data>
  <data key="d1">Biological Process</data>
  <data key="d2">The mouse embryonic pancreas is a biological context in which MafA was found to be bound to Insulin and Glucagon transcriptional control sequences.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9bec3f5c6cf93d2d763da970e02d0fc3</data>
  <data key="d4">MafA is a dedicated activator of the insulin gene in vivo.</data>
