<node id="Chimeric Proteins Of MafA And MafB">
  <data key="d0">Chimeric Proteins Of MafA And MafB</data>
  <data key="d1">Method</data>
  <data key="d2">Chimeric proteins of MafA and MafB are engineered proteins used to analyze which domain sequences are responsible for chick Insulin activation, demonstrating the importance of the MafA C-terminal DNA-binding domain.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9bec3f5c6cf93d2d763da970e02d0fc3</data>
  <data key="d4">MafA is a dedicated activator of the insulin gene in vivo.</data>
