  <data key="d1">Biological Process</data>
  <data key="d2">Islet α-cells are glucagon-producing cells in the pancreatic islets, in which MafB is present during development and becomes restricted after birth.&lt;SEP&gt;Islet α-cells are pancreatic islet cells responsible for glucagon secretion; MafB is essential to their activity in rodents.&lt;SEP&gt;Islet α-cells are pancreatic cells responsible for glucagon secretion, and their phenotypic markers may be expressed in β-cells undergoing dedifferentiation.</data>
