  <data key="d11">0.00751063</data>
</node>
<node id="Quantitative RT-PCR">
  <data key="d0">Quantitative RT-PCR</data>
  <data key="d1">Method</data>
  <data key="d2">Quantitative RT-PCR is a method used to evaluate candidate genes identified by microarray profiling as regulated by MafB.&lt;SEP&gt;Quantitative RT-PCR is a molecular biology method used to evaluate candidate genes identified by microarray profiling.&lt;SEP&gt;Quantitative RT-PCR is an analysis method used to reveal that G6pc2 mRNA levels were significantly downregulated in adult MafAΔPanc islets.&lt;SEP&gt;Quantitative RT-PCR is a molecular biology method used to measure mRNA levels of genes such as G6pc2 in MafAΔPanc islets.&lt;SEP&gt;Quantitative RT-PCR is a method used to independently verify mRNA changes in candidate genes in mutant pancreata.&lt;SEP&gt;Quantitative RT-PCR is a method used to detect and quantify target gene expression in human islets and other experimental samples.&lt;SEP&gt;A quantitative reverse transcription PCR method used to detect target gene expression using primers listed in Table S4.&lt;SEP&gt;Quantitative RT-PCR was conducted on total RNA from E18.5 pancreata or 12-week-old islets to measure mRNA expression levels across genotypes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9693157a2d458ecc8255c49ec77d95f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5f82db25373e25b34bbbcfebc1c0f861&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e517ac1160d78d9b935ab9b9913bf46a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9ed09558012a9cb8eba4b1efe943943&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc7255d0eadb6b7f3a3a51c10b8ea742&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9e53f09e3b38fb66b0f093b0768d32a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40bbefacfceda2b6335fdb6310e2f7ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff8c5dc48dde6c3ccfdc01c9e025403d</data>
  <data key="d4">MafA and MafB regulate genes critical to beta-cells in a unique temporal manner.&lt;SEP&gt;Stress-induced β cell early senescence confers protection against type 1 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d5">1778564586</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">13</data>
  <data key="d8">SLC30A8 / RBP4 / acinar cell</data>
  <data key="d9">0.00060583</data>
