</node>
<node id="In Situ Hybridization">
  <data key="d0">In Situ Hybridization</data>
  <data key="d1">Method</data>
  <data key="d2">In situ hybridization is a technique used alongside quantitative RT-PCR to evaluate candidate genes regulated by MafB in pancreatic tissue.&lt;SEP&gt;In situ hybridization is a technique used to evaluate candidate genes regulated by MafB in pancreatic tissue.&lt;SEP&gt;In situ hybridization assays were performed using gene probes for Neuronatin, Slc30a8, and Rbp4 to study gene expression in pancreatic tissue.&lt;SEP&gt;In situ hybridization is a technique used to detect Slc30a8 mRNA transcripts in developing pancreatic cells.&lt;SEP&gt;In situ hybridization is an analytical method used to detect and localize mRNA expression of Nnat and Rbp4 in pancreatic cells during development.&lt;SEP&gt;In situ hybridization is a technique used to examine expression within specific islet cell types during development.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9693157a2d458ecc8255c49ec77d95f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5f82db25373e25b34bbbcfebc1c0f861&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e517ac1160d78d9b935ab9b9913bf46a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9ed09558012a9cb8eba4b1efe943943&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc7255d0eadb6b7f3a3a51c10b8ea742&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41e9c4875e9ee2b378c620275d81fe7e</data>
