<node id="Embryonic Day 13.5">
  <data key="d0">Embryonic Day 13.5</data>
  <data key="d1">Biological Process</data>
  <data key="d2">Embryonic day 13.5 is the developmental time point at which MafA expression is first detected, coinciding with the secondary and principal wave of insulin+ cell production.&lt;SEP&gt;The embryonic developmental timepoint from which the second or principal wave of insulin+ cells arises, eventually becoming the β-cells of the islet.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9693157a2d458ecc8255c49ec77d95f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-207f97a443acec0faaf8f9f2d208e61f</data>
  <data key="d4">The MafA transcription factor becomes essential to islet β-cells soon after birth.&lt;SEP&gt;MafA and MafB regulate genes critical to beta-cells in a unique temporal manner.</data>
