</node>
<node id="Cre Recombinase">
  <data key="d0">Cre Recombinase</data>
  <data key="d1">Biological Process</data>
  <data key="d2">Cre recombinase is a recombinase enzyme produced from the Pdx15.5 promoter fragment in transgenic mice, used to generate the MafAΔPanc mutant mouse model.&lt;SEP&gt;An enzyme used for conditional excision of immortalizing transgenes hTERT and SV40 in EndoC-βH2 cells to activate glucose responsiveness.&lt;SEP&gt;Cre recombinase is an enzyme whose activity is induced by tamoxifen to enable conditional gene deletion in specific mouse models used in the study.&lt;SEP&gt;Recombinase used in lineage tracing experiments with ROSA26 reporter strain for conditional gene manipulation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9693157a2d458ecc8255c49ec77d95f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4b8d7d9156faa43670557fc5e83791e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9e53f09e3b38fb66b0f093b0768d32a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce72a72ed1aaea72aac97c28374f8f86</data>
  <data key="d4">MafA and MafB regulate genes critical to beta-cells in a unique temporal manner.&lt;SEP&gt;Stress-induced β cell early senescence confers protection against type 1 diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Species-specific roles for the MAFA and MAFB transcription factors in regulating islet β cell identity.</data>
  <data key="d5">1778564586</data>
