</node>
<node id="Nkx6.2">
  <data key="d0">Nkx6.2</data>
  <data key="d1">Biological Process</data>
  <data key="d2">Nkx6.2 is a transcription factor that, together with Nkx6.1, possesses equivalent activities in promoting β-cell fate specification in Pdx1+ pancreatic progenitor cells.&lt;SEP&gt;Nkx6.2 is an NK6 homeodomain transcription factor that disappears late in pancreatic development and contributes to β-cell formation alongside Nkx6.1.&lt;SEP&gt;Nkx6.2 is a transcription factor expressed broadly and earlier in the pancreas alongside Nkx6.1, but does not significantly influence β-cell development and function.&lt;SEP&gt;Nkx6.2 is a transcription factor with activities equivalent to Nkx6.1 in promoting beta-cell fate specification in Pdx1+ pancreatic progenitor cells.&lt;SEP&gt;Nkx6.2 is an NK6 homeodomain transcription factor expressed in early pancreatic epithelial cells whose expression ceases after birth.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9693157a2d458ecc8255c49ec77d95f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f7f8610c162035d52f2edbe846e8a97&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9ed09558012a9cb8eba4b1efe943943&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a87d40ff620e7f930f155b5dea286c8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ecc1e3f157d04d78962c82537c6b7d9</data>
  <data key="d4">The MafA transcription factor becomes essential to islet β-cells soon after birth.&lt;SEP&gt;MafA and MafB regulate genes critical to beta-cells in a unique temporal manner.</data>
  <data key="d5">1778561516</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
