</node>
<node id="MafAfl/fl Mice">
  <data key="d0">MafAfl/fl Mice</data>
  <data key="d1">Organism</data>
  <data key="d2">MafAfl/fl mice are a conditional knockout mouse line used in crossing with Cre recombinase-expressing transgenic mice to generate the MafAΔPanc pancreas-wide MafA mutant model.&lt;SEP&gt;MafAfl/fl mice carry a conditional MafA allele with loxP sites flanking the MafA exon, used as the parental strain for generating MafAΔPanc mice by crossing with Pdx15.5-Cre mice.&lt;SEP&gt;MafAfl/fl mice are a mouse line with floxed MafA alleles used in combination with Ins1Cre mice to generate β cell–specific MafA deletion mutants.&lt;SEP&gt;MafAfl/fl mice carry floxed alleles of the MafA gene and are used in crossing with Ins1Cre knockin mice to generate MafA∆β mice with β cell-specific MafA deletion.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9693157a2d458ecc8255c49ec77d95f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff8c5dc48dde6c3ccfdc01c9e025403d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d1c90235486a0fe738831a720e1f94ab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e6c6371cdef301723817998e0efc9ec6</data>
  <data key="d4">MafA and MafB regulate genes critical to beta-cells in a unique temporal manner.&lt;SEP&gt;Species-specific roles for the MAFA and MAFB transcription factors in regulating islet β cell identity.</data>
  <data key="d5">1778562874</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">4</data>
  <data key="d8">Vanderbilt University Medical Center / MafA∆β Mice / Vanderbilt University</data>
  <data key="d9">0.00027263</data>
  <data key="d10">0.0004037</data>
  <data key="d11">0.00190042</data>
</node>
<node id="Pdx15.5 Promoter Fragment">
  <data key="d0">Pdx15.5 Promoter Fragment</data>
  <data key="d1">Method</data>
  <data key="d2">The Pdx15.5 promoter fragment is a regulatory DNA element used to drive Cre recombinase expression early in development in a pancreas-wide pattern, enabling generation of the MafAΔPanc mutant mouse.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9693157a2d458ecc8255c49ec77d95f8</data>
  <data key="d4">MafA and MafB regulate genes critical to beta-cells in a unique temporal manner.</data>
  <data key="d5">1778561051</data>
