  <data key="d9">9.21e-05</data>
  <data key="d10">0.0</data>
  <data key="d11">8.394e-05</data>
</node>
<node id="MafB−/− Mice">
  <data key="d0">MafB−/− Mice</data>
  <data key="d1">Organism</data>
  <data key="d2">MafB−/− mice are mutant mice generated by homologous recombination in which the MafB gene is knocked out.&lt;SEP&gt;MafB−/− is a mutant mouse model lacking MafB, used to study the regulatory roles of MafB in β-cell differentiation and insulin expression.&lt;SEP&gt;MafB−/− mice are knockout mutants used to study the role of MAFB in islet cell development; these mutants died due to problems in neural development, preventing postnatal physiological study.&lt;SEP&gt;Mafb−/− mice are homozygous knockout mice for MafB that die at birth due to central apnea, limiting the study of MafB's functional significance in neonatal β-cells.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5f82db25373e25b34bbbcfebc1c0f861&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff8c5dc48dde6c3ccfdc01c9e025403d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69365499ad956be649b962c79d46f483&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b158cd1c233246631a3b8f719a275f2f</data>
  <data key="d4">The MafA transcription factor becomes essential to islet β-cells soon after birth.&lt;SEP&gt;MafA and MafB regulate genes critical to beta-cells in a unique temporal manner.&lt;SEP&gt;The MAFB transcription factor impacts islet α-cell function in rodents and represents a unique signature of primate islet β-cells.</data>
  <data key="d5">1778561628</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
  <data key="d8">Insulin / Pancreatic Islets / A0B0 Mice</data>
  <data key="d9">0.00038345</data>
  <data key="d10">0.00051842</data>
  <data key="d11">0.01285985</data>
</node>
<node id="MafAΔPanc;MafB−/− Mice">
  <data key="d0">MafAΔPanc;MafB−/− Mice</data>
  <data key="d1">Organism</data>
  <data key="d2">MafAΔPanc;MafB−/− mice are double mutant mice lacking both MafA in the pancreas and MafB globally, used for comparative gene expression analysis.&lt;SEP&gt;MafAΔPanc;MafB−/− is a double mutant mouse model lacking both pancreatic MafA and MafB, showing more pronounced gene expression changes compared to single mutants.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5f82db25373e25b34bbbcfebc1c0f861&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff8c5dc48dde6c3ccfdc01c9e025403d</data>
  <data key="d4">MafA and MafB regulate genes critical to beta-cells in a unique temporal manner.</data>
  <data key="d5">1778561051</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
  <data key="d8">Insulin / Pancreatic Islets / A0B0 Mice</data>
