</node>
<node id="Wild-Type Mice">
  <data key="d0">Wild-Type Mice</data>
  <data key="d1">Organism</data>
  <data key="d2">Wild-type mice serve as the control group in studies comparing gene expression and pancreatic cell development against mutant models.&lt;SEP&gt;Control mice used alongside MafaΔpanc mice in mRNA microarray and other analyses to study the effect of MafA loss.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5f82db25373e25b34bbbcfebc1c0f861&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a5af2ab88dac4e2b983a277be1a9c536</data>
  <data key="d4">The MafA transcription factor becomes essential to islet β-cells soon after birth.&lt;SEP&gt;MafA and MafB regulate genes critical to beta-cells in a unique temporal manner.</data>
  <data key="d5">1778561512</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">21</data>
  <data key="d8">Microarray Analysis / Functional Genomics Core / mRNA Microarray</data>
  <data key="d9">0.00013529</data>
  <data key="d10">0.0</data>
  <data key="d11">0.00175093</data>
</node>
<node id="ZnT8">
  <data key="d0">ZnT8</data>
  <data key="d1">Protein</data>
  <data key="d2">ZnT8 is the protein product of the Slc30a8 gene, functioning as an islet-specific zinc transporter involved in insulin maturation and storage.&lt;SEP&gt;ZnT8 is an islet-specific zinc transporter encoded by Slc30a8, whose overexpression enhances glucose-stimulated insulin secretion in INS1 β-cells and whose variants are linked to type 2 diabetes in humans.&lt;SEP&gt;Putative T1D autoantigen (SLC30A8 product) found in primary mouse and human islet beta cell EVs; released at higher rates during proinflammatory cytokine exposure; also an autoantibody target in T1D.&lt;SEP&gt;Zinc transporter-8 encoded by SLC30A8; loss of function protects against diabetes by enhanced insulin secretion.&lt;SEP&gt;Zinc transporter encoded by SLC30A8; reduced activity enhances beta cell efficiency and improves proinsulin processing by alleviating zinc-mediated inhibition of granule maturation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5f82db25373e25b34bbbcfebc1c0f861&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc7255d0eadb6b7f3a3a51c10b8ea742&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08f3e602fed4b4ebfff436b75194d507&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-044fb2d3ececa99a53eb87d2ee6bf18f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e181574d19e6f17c0fd64b0feecf8f9e</data>
  <data key="d4">MafA and MafB regulate genes critical to beta-cells in a unique temporal manner.&lt;SEP&gt;Exploring senescence as a modifier of β cell extracellular vesicles in type 1 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d5">1778568445</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">22</data>
  <data key="d8">extracellular vesicles / estrogen / ZnT8</data>
  <data key="d9">0.00055384</data>
  <data key="d10">0.00127971</data>
  <data key="d11">0.03080206</data>
</node>
<node id="Islet β-Cells">
  <data key="d0">Islet β-Cells</data>
  <data key="d1">Biological Process</data>
  <data key="d2">Islet β-cells are insulin-producing cells in the pancreas whose maturation and function are regulated by transcription factors MafA and MafB.&lt;SEP&gt;Islet β-cells are pancreatic endocrine cells responsible for insulin secretion and glucose homeostasis, regulated by transcription factors such as MafA and MafB.&lt;SEP&gt;Islet β-cells are pancreatic cells responsible for insulin synthesis, storage, and secretion, and are the primary cell type affected by MafA regulation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5f82db25373e25b34bbbcfebc1c0f861&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-94526413b6fbcf0ec99212789cec9eea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ecc1e3f157d04d78962c82537c6b7d9</data>
  <data key="d4">The MafA transcription factor becomes essential to islet β-cells soon after birth.&lt;SEP&gt;MafA and MafB regulate genes critical to beta-cells in a unique temporal manner.</data>
  <data key="d5">1778561518</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">0</data>
  <data key="d8">beta cell / MAFA / MAFB</data>
  <data key="d9">0.00075275</data>
