<node id="Insulin Receptor Substrate-1">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Receptor Substrate-1</data>
  <data key="d1">Biological Process</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin receptor substrate-1 is a signaling molecule whose insulin-induced phosphorylation is attenuated by Rbp4 in human adipocytes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1f7f8610c162035d52f2edbe846e8a97</data>
  <data key="d4">MafA and MafB regulate genes critical to beta-cells in a unique temporal manner.</data>
  <data key="d5">1778561058</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">13</data>
  <data key="d8">SLC30A8 / RBP4 / acinar cell</data>
  <data key="d9">7.712e-05</data>
  <data key="d10">0.0</data>
  <data key="d11">0.0015489</data>
</node>
<node id="Glucagon+ Cells">
  <data key="d0">Glucagon+ Cells</data>
  <data key="d1">Data</data>
  <data key="d2">Glucagon-positive cells are pancreatic α-cells that produce glucagon and are examined in the context of Nnat and Rbp4 expression regulation.&lt;SEP&gt;Glucagon-producing cells in the pancreas in which MafB mutant expression of Slc30a8 was compromised during development.&lt;SEP&gt;Glucagon-positive cells counted alongside insulin+ cells to determine the β- to α-cell ratio.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1f7f8610c162035d52f2edbe846e8a97&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e517ac1160d78d9b935ab9b9913bf46a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a5af2ab88dac4e2b983a277be1a9c536</data>
  <data key="d4">The MafA transcription factor becomes essential to islet β-cells soon after birth.&lt;SEP&gt;MafA and MafB regulate genes critical to beta-cells in a unique temporal manner.</data>
  <data key="d5">1778561505</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">0</data>
  <data key="d8">beta cell / MAFA / MAFB</data>
  <data key="d9">7.271e-05</data>
  <data key="d10">0.0</data>
  <data key="d11">0.0069073</data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin+ Cells">
  <data key="d0">Insulin+ Cells</data>
  <data key="d1">Data</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin-positive cells are pancreatic β-cells that produce insulin and serve as a key cellular context for studying MafA, MafB, Nnat, and Rbp4 expression.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin-producing cells in the pancreas in which MafB mutant expression of Slc30a8 was compromised during development and in adult MafA mutant cells.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin-positive cells identified in pancreatic sections, used to calculate β- to α-cell ratio and relative β-cell mass.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1f7f8610c162035d52f2edbe846e8a97&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e517ac1160d78d9b935ab9b9913bf46a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a5af2ab88dac4e2b983a277be1a9c536</data>
  <data key="d4">The MafA transcription factor becomes essential to islet β-cells soon after birth.&lt;SEP&gt;MafA and MafB regulate genes critical to beta-cells in a unique temporal manner.</data>
  <data key="d5">1778561505</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">0</data>
  <data key="d8">beta cell / MAFA / MAFB</data>
  <data key="d9">0.00018846</data>
  <data key="d10">0.0010739</data>
  <data key="d11">0.01468041</data>
</node>
<node id="Myoblast">
  <data key="d0">Myoblast</data>
  <data key="d1">Biological Process</data>
  <data key="d2">Myoblasts are precursor muscle cells whose formation is critically regulated by Myf-5 and MyoD, analogous to MafB's role in islet cell development.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1f7f8610c162035d52f2edbe846e8a97</data>
  <data key="d4">MafA and MafB regulate genes critical to beta-cells in a unique temporal manner.</data>
  <data key="d5">1778561058</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">25</data>
  <data key="d8">MYOGENIN</data>
  <data key="d9">0.00015978</data>
  <data key="d10">2.1e-07</data>
  <data key="d11">0.00092346</data>
</node>
<node id="Myotube">
  <data key="d0">Myotube</data>
  <data key="d1">Biological Process</data>
  <data key="d2">Myotubes are differentiated muscle cells formed from myoblasts through a process in which myogenin plays an essential role, analogous to MafA's role in β-cell maturation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1f7f8610c162035d52f2edbe846e8a97</data>
  <data key="d4">MafA and MafB regulate genes critical to beta-cells in a unique temporal manner.</data>
  <data key="d5">1778561058</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">25</data>
  <data key="d8">MYOGENIN</data>
  <data key="d9">7.67e-05</data>
  <data key="d10">0.0</data>
  <data key="d11">0.00039334</data>
</node>
<node id="Human Adipocyte">
  <data key="d0">Human Adipocyte</data>
  <data key="d1">Biological Process</data>
  <data key="d2">Human adipocytes are fat cells in which Rbp4 attenuates insulin-induced phosphorylation of insulin receptor substrate-1.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1f7f8610c162035d52f2edbe846e8a97</data>
  <data key="d4">MafA and MafB regulate genes critical to beta-cells in a unique temporal manner.</data>
  <data key="d5">1778561058</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
