<node id="Somatostatin">
  <data key="d0">Somatostatin</data>
  <data key="d1">Biological Process</data>
  <data key="d2">Somatostatin is a hormone expressed in pancreatic islets, targeted by sheep α-somatostatin primary antibody in immunohistochemistry experiments.&lt;SEP&gt;Somatostatin is a hormone produced by pancreatic δ-cells, used as a marker in immunolabeling studies of islet cell composition.&lt;SEP&gt;Somatostatin is a hormone produced by δ-cells within the islet of Langerhans.&lt;SEP&gt;A hormone involved in negative feedback control of insulin secretion, mediated by Urocortin3 in pancreatic islets.&lt;SEP&gt;Hormone detected by immunohistochemistry using rat anti-somatostatin antibody.&lt;SEP&gt;Hormone used as an immunostaining marker to identify and quantify delta cells in pancreatic sections.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ff8c5dc48dde6c3ccfdc01c9e025403d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41e9c4875e9ee2b378c620275d81fe7e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a87d40ff620e7f930f155b5dea286c8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5f38c4d8fe95ae0a2b5cc05069361348&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af08dcd3bdc472cb74376c18c72cf9f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6cadc21c6ca916dd06510987c1b7dbf4</data>
