<node id="Pancreatic Polypeptide">
  <data key="d0">Pancreatic Polypeptide</data>
  <data key="d1">Biological Process</data>
  <data key="d2">Pancreatic polypeptide is a hormone expressed in pancreatic islets, targeted by guinea pig α-pancreatic polypeptide primary antibody in immunohistochemistry experiments.&lt;SEP&gt;Pancreatic polypeptide is a hormone produced by PP-cells in the pancreatic islet, used as a marker in immunolabeling studies.&lt;SEP&gt;Pancreatic polypeptide is a hormone produced by pancreatic polypeptide cells within the islet of Langerhans.&lt;SEP&gt;A pancreatic hormone used as a marker in immunohistochemistry assessment of pancreatic tissue in insulinomatosis studies.&lt;SEP&gt;Pancreatic polypeptide (PP), encoded by PPY, is a non–β cell hormone inappropriately expressed in MAFBKO β-like cells and upon MAFB knockdown in human EndoC-βH2 cells.&lt;SEP&gt;Pancreatic polypeptide is a hormone not expressed in precursor cells of mouse endocrine pancreas, unlike insulin, glucagon, and neuronal proteins.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ff8c5dc48dde6c3ccfdc01c9e025403d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41e9c4875e9ee2b378c620275d81fe7e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a87d40ff620e7f930f155b5dea286c8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e531f038e6fcc1cbb89c2336af984719&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e6c6371cdef301723817998e0efc9ec6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-735ea17eaeb5e3524d0871e16116e986</data>
  <data key="d4">The MafA transcription factor becomes essential to islet β-cells soon after birth.&lt;SEP&gt;MafA and MafB regulate genes critical to beta-cells in a unique temporal manner.&lt;SEP&gt;Species-specific roles for the MAFA and MAFB transcription factors in regulating islet β cell identity.&lt;SEP&gt;MAFA missense mutation causes familial insulinomatosis and diabetes mellitus.</data>
  <data key="d5">1778562887</data>
