<node id="Homologous Recombination">
  <data key="d0">Homologous Recombination</data>
  <data key="d1">Method</data>
  <data key="d2">Homologous recombination is the method used to generate MafB−/− mice by targeted disruption of the MafB gene.&lt;SEP&gt;High-fidelity DNA repair mechanism for double-strand breaks, contrasted with nonhomologous end joining.&lt;SEP&gt;Error-free DSB repair mechanism that remains active throughout G2 and M phases in both alpha and beta cells.&lt;SEP&gt;Accurate double-strand break repair pathway favored by alpha cells in S/G2 phase under HFD.</data>
