<node id="Nkx2.2">
  <data key="d0">Nkx2.2</data>
  <data key="d1">Biological Process</data>
  <data key="d2">Nkx2.2 is a transcription factor that acts upstream of Nkx6.1 in the major pathway of β-cell formation in the pancreas; NKX6 transcription factor activity is required for α- and β-cell development.&lt;SEP&gt;Nkx2.2 is a transcription factor associated with islet cell lineage commitment that is not affected by MafB regulation.&lt;SEP&gt;Nkx2.2 is a transcription factor whose concerted activities with Pax4 are essential to initiate pancreatic beta-cell differentiation, and is involved in regulating islet beta-cell-specific MafA expression.&lt;SEP&gt;A transcription factor that, along with FoxA2 and PDX-1, regulates islet beta-cell-specific mafA expression through conserved sequences located between base pairs -8118 and -7750 upstream from the transcription start site.&lt;SEP&gt;Nkx2.2 is an islet-enriched transcription factor whose downregulation does not produce Gast+ cells, indicating distinct regulation of β cell identity.&lt;SEP&gt;NKX2.2 is an islet-enriched transcription factor with binding sites near the GAST gene region, potentially cooperating with MAFB in regulating GAST expression.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b9ed09558012a9cb8eba4b1efe943943&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ddb7aaa2476f3163b5c3de684504f42b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ecc1e3f157d04d78962c82537c6b7d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5f38c4d8fe95ae0a2b5cc05069361348&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea3320816339f9f109dec0e1621420bd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c914d24696d0f6e2087f40c21ca5649</data>
