<node id="Skeletal Muscle">
  <data key="d0">Skeletal Muscle</data>
  <data key="d1">Biological Process</data>
  <data key="d2">Skeletal muscle is a muscle tissue type whose formation requires MyoD or Myf-5 transcription factors.&lt;SEP&gt;Tissue where MAFA is highly expressed, though its detailed role there remains unclear.&lt;SEP&gt;Skeletal muscle is one of the tissues where MAFA and MAFB are coexpressed.&lt;SEP&gt;Tissue where MAFA and MAFB are coexpressed along with pancreatic islets and testes.&lt;SEP&gt;One of the unusual tissues where both MAFA and MAFB are coexpressed, alongside islets and testes.&lt;SEP&gt;Tissue that indirectly impacts beta cell function via tissue-specific mediators.</data>
