  <data key="d2">Camk2b is a gene involved in Ca2+ signaling that is activated by MafB as part of mature endocrine function.&lt;SEP&gt;Camk2b is a gene involved in Ca2+ signaling and is among the MafA-regulated genes in β-cells.&lt;SEP&gt;A gene involved in Ca2+ signaling in β-cells, regulated by MafA in adult islets.</data>
