<node id="Insulin Resistance">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Resistance</data>
  <data key="d1">Biological Process</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin resistance is a physiological condition influenced by Rbp4, which is negatively regulated by MafA and MafB in islet cell types.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin resistance is a metabolic condition associated with activation of genes in Gast+ β cells and is linked to compromised MAF expression and β cell dysfunction.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin resistance is a pathophysiological condition associated with GAST+ β cell production in mice and contributes to β cell dysfunction and loss of identity.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin resistance is a metabolic condition modeled in mice using S961 or high-fat diet treatment, proposed as a context for studying early induction of GAST+ gene signatures.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin resistance is a metabolic condition characterized by the failure of cells and peripheral tissues to respond normally to insulin. It is widely recognized as a central and multifaceted feature in the pathophysiology of type 2 diabetes (T2D) and related metabolic disorders, including metabolic syndrome, obesity, hyperinsulinaemia, and dysglycaemia. Notably, insulin resistance is considered insufficient on its own to drive the full transition to hyperglycaemia, underscoring the complexity of T2D progression.

Clinically, insulin resistance serves as a key variable used to define T2D subtypes and has been identified as a notable metabolic phenotype in ketosis-prone type 2 diabetes, particularly in patients of sub-Saharan African origin. Biological sex is a significant modulating factor, influencing both disease susceptibility and progression within the context of T2D pathogenesis and broader metabolic homeostasis. Therapeutically, agents such as retatrutide have been explored to target insulin resistance in T2D and ketosis-prone T2D. Caloric restriction (CR) has also been shown to produce an insulin-sensitive state, thereby reducing demand on beta cells.

Insulin resistance is assessed through established clinical and experimental measures, including the insulin tolerance test (ITT) and the homeostatic model assessment of insulin resistance (HOMA-IR), calculated from fasting glucose and insulin values. These tools are applied across dietary and pharmacological intervention studies in mouse models.

In experimental research, insulin resistance has been extensively modeled using C57BL/6J mice fed a high-fat diet (HFD), which induces beta-cell senescence marked by elevated SA-β-gal activity and high cytoplasmic staining in the pancreas. A complementary pharmacological approach uses S961 treatment in adult mice to induce insulin resistance, associated with sequential expression of cell cycle inhibitors Cdkn1a and Cdkn2a in beta cells, reflecting progressive senescent signaling.

Mechanistically, insulin resistance is closely associated with beta-cell senescence, impaired beta-cell function during aging, and heterogeneous beta-cell aging markers. It is also linked to the accumulation of p21-expressing (p21Cip1-highly expressing) senescent cells in adipose tissue, with adipose tissue p53 identified as a regulatory factor. In INK-ATTAC mouse models, targeted clearance of senescent beta cells restored normal insulin sensitivity, establishing a causal relationship between beta-cell senescence and insulin resistance. Overall, insulin resistance is understood as a multifactorial condition shaped by diet, pharmacological agents, biological sex, and senescence mechanisms in both pancreatic beta cells and adipose tissue.&lt;SEP&gt;Metabolic condition central to the pathophysiology of type 2 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ddb7aaa2476f3163b5c3de684504f42b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c914d24696d0f6e2087f40c21ca5649&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d1c90235486a0fe738831a720e1f94ab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea3320816339f9f109dec0e1621420bd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5dc00b5dc127eca5ff2847cc45392453&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b861cee193cad9e0f142051047e83aae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-58ad905d1d148d4bbfe7ce4c29566fc6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bcadefd5324392c8a202934109c8c242&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8c7bb3e4a69884a1b79485b95f6f502&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fac258601b299e0c883e8e1c4a3030d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8f87338453daad7a9a4624ce798bcf6e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b67e26d82684726785f1910ba6919cf0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd3982c3cb7b00162818de82027a853e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-71a6a7a3a4894dbd7d979b7e5766d5a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b773584b36e5b4845bedffea9a1b6add&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d7ef738c0840825512b2cb7af5b7c3f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ff588c6efe73ecb07c6b95acb392e92&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51601485f0924871a988aae2e5ce30bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0238834380bfb40677324883af3e3004&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68a87a3a1f3eb5d8b0e53b41df492512&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-75f39153d9f864070e17a74724a6c8c6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f63ca40b092870f725a75e7a36045d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce68225f2288adf7d07962282496e8c5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c41ef398df926f1c888f284aff2a98e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d41db2658ec2709309c04b39b1894e48&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4e8cbb766d17c90c84d2a9452a51a41e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-43761b34ecc024bd90bfa8711c45a233&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-10bdc47e4d027606476b48a401061a27&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8f09e5d1418f8ae04b43a24b97c1d52d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e181574d19e6f17c0fd64b0feecf8f9e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-15ab370ab273e97005ced113e59cc48a</data>
