<node id="Glp1R">
  <data key="d0">Glp1R</data>
  <data key="d1">Biological Process</data>
  <data key="d2">Glp1R is a gene previously associated with MafA control in INS1 β-cells but not detected in MafB−/− or MafAΔPanc;MafB−/− profiling at E18.5.&lt;SEP&gt;Glp1r (glucagon-like peptide-1 receptor) is a downstream effector of Mnx1 and Pdx1 activation involved in cell signaling, contributing to β cell non-responder dysfunction in MafAS64F/+ islets.&lt;SEP&gt;Glucagon-like peptide-1 receptor mediating insulinotropic signaling in pancreatic beta cells, amplified by androgen receptor pathways in males.&lt;SEP&gt;GLP-1 receptor enriched on beta cells; proposed as a surface ligand target on engineered EVs for precision delivery to beta cells.&lt;SEP&gt;Glucagon-like peptide-1 receptor involved in cAMP signaling in beta cells; relevant to in vivo beta cell environment.&lt;SEP&gt;Incretin receptor gene not detected in the snMultiome-seq analysis of beta cells.&lt;SEP&gt;Glucagon-like peptide-1 receptor, the target of the agonist Liraglutide used in meal tolerance test experiments.</data>
