<node id="MafaΔpanc">
  <data key="d0">MafaΔpanc</data>
  <data key="d1">Biological Process</data>
  <data key="d2">MafaΔpanc refers to a mouse model with pancreas-specific deletion of MafA, exhibiting reduced β-cell gene expression, diminished β-cell replication, impaired glucose clearance, and altered islet architecture.&lt;SEP&gt;A mouse model with pancreas-specific loss of MafA, used in mRNA microarray and functional studies to understand MafA's role in β-cells.&lt;SEP&gt;MafaΔpanc refers to a mouse mutant with pancreatic-specific deletion of the MafA transcription factor, used to study β-cell function and insulin secretion.&lt;SEP&gt;MafaΔpanc refers to a pancreas-specific Mafa knockout mouse model used to study the role of MafA in islet β-cell function.&lt;SEP&gt;MafaΔpanc refers to a mouse mutant with pancreas-specific deletion of MafA, showing dysfunctional β-cells and altered islet architecture, with 741 differentially expressed genes identified at 3 months old.&lt;SEP&gt;MafaΔpanc refers to a mouse model with pancreas-specific deletion of MafA, used to study the role of MafA in β-cell function, islet architecture, and insulin secretion.&lt;SEP&gt;MafAΔPanc refers to pancreas-wide MafA deletion mutant mice, generated using the Cre-loxP recombination system, with MafA effectively removed from the pancreas by E18.5.&lt;SEP&gt;MafAΔPanc is a pancreas-wide MafA mutant mouse model generated by crossing MafAfl/fl mice with transgenic mice producing Cre recombinase from the Pdx15.5 promoter fragment, used to study MafA's role in adult islet function.&lt;SEP&gt;MafAΔPanc refers to a mutant mouse model with pancreas-specific deletion of MafA, used to study the role of MafA in β-cell differentiation and MafB expression.&lt;SEP&gt;MafAΔPanc refers to a pancreas-specific MafA knockout model where MafA is absent in pancreatic cells, leading to altered gene expression in islets.&lt;SEP&gt;MafAΔPanc is a mutant lacking MafA specifically in the pancreas, used to study the role of MafA in islet β-cell formation and function.&lt;SEP&gt;MafAΔPanc is a mutant mouse model with pancreas-specific deletion of MafA, used to study the regulatory roles of MafA in β-cell differentiation.&lt;SEP&gt;MafAΔpanc are pancreas-wide MafA mutant mice used as a reference for comparing deficiencies associated with the β-cell-enriched MafA mutant.&lt;SEP&gt;MafAΔpanc is a pancreas-specific MafA knockout mouse model used to study the role of MafA in pancreatic function and β cell activity.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b158cd1c233246631a3b8f719a275f2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a5af2ab88dac4e2b983a277be1a9c536&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f67b6052ac2da6848aaabbd71f9d4d53&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-94526413b6fbcf0ec99212789cec9eea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ee443fb4c37f27d6895254d3f95c708&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-75261aabfd0eeb269665c62f36dfeb2e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9693157a2d458ecc8255c49ec77d95f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5f82db25373e25b34bbbcfebc1c0f861&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff8c5dc48dde6c3ccfdc01c9e025403d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e517ac1160d78d9b935ab9b9913bf46a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41e9c4875e9ee2b378c620275d81fe7e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ddb7aaa2476f3163b5c3de684504f42b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69365499ad956be649b962c79d46f483&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-74fc4f55c8c6d83ebd1d8dba07d90692</data>
  <data key="d4">MafA and MafB regulate genes critical to beta-cells in a unique temporal manner.&lt;SEP&gt;The MafA transcription factor becomes essential to islet β-cells soon after birth.&lt;SEP&gt;Sex-biased islet β cell dysfunction is caused by the MODY MAFA S64F variant by inducing premature aging and senescence in males.&lt;SEP&gt;The MAFB transcription factor impacts islet α-cell function in rodents and represents a unique signature of primate islet β-cells.</data>
