<node id="Glucose Tolerance Test">
  <data key="d0">Glucose Tolerance Test</data>
  <data key="d1">Method</data>
  <data key="d2">The glucose tolerance test is a method used to measure glucose clearance, revealing impaired glucose tolerance in 4-week-old MafaΔpanc mice and more severe impairment in MafaΔpanc;Mafb+/− mice.&lt;SEP&gt;The glucose tolerance test is an assay used to measure glucose intolerance, with the area under the curve quantifying the severity of the metabolic defect.&lt;SEP&gt;Test conducted following dietary intervention to assess glucose metabolism in mice.</data>
