<node id="First-Phase Insulin Secretion">
  <data key="d0">First-Phase Insulin Secretion</data>
  <data key="d1">Biological Process</data>
  <data key="d2">First-phase insulin secretion is the initial rapid release of insulin in response to glucose, affected by MafA's regulation of granule docking.&lt;SEP&gt;First-phase insulin secretion is the initial rapid release of insulin in response to glucose, which is significantly reduced in MafaΔpanc and MafaΔpanc;Mafb+/− islets.&lt;SEP&gt;First-phase insulin secretion is the initial rapid release of insulin in response to glucose, which is specifically and significantly impaired in MafaΔpanc β-cells due to reduced predocked granules and diminished docking effector expression.&lt;SEP&gt;The rapid initial burst of insulin secretion in response to glucose, markedly reduced in individuals with impaired glucose tolerance.</data>
