  <data key="d0">Second-Phase Insulin Secretion</data>
  <data key="d1">Biological Process</data>
  <data key="d2">Second-phase insulin secretion is the sustained release of insulin following the first phase, which shows only a trending reduction in MafaΔpanc islets.&lt;SEP&gt;The sustained phase of insulin secretion following the initial burst, reduced in impaired glucose tolerance.</data>
