<node id="Insulin Granule">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Granule</data>
  <data key="d1">Biological Process</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin granules are vesicles in β-cells containing insulin; their density, size, and number of docked granules are reduced in MafaΔpanc β-cells.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin granules are dense-core secretory vesicles in β-cells responsible for insulin storage and release; their density, number, and predocked status are reduced in MafaΔpanc β-cells.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin secretory granules that control autophagy in pancreatic beta cells.&lt;SEP&gt;Mature secretory granules in beta cells; content is unchanged between AL and CR beta cells and not targeted by CR-induced autophagy.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin storage granules in beta cells; CR-induced autophagy does not target these, unlike stress-induced autophagy.&lt;SEP&gt;Electron-dense structures in beta cells with condensed insulin crystals surrounded by a large halo, used for cell type classification in SEM maps.</data>
