<node id="Intraperitoneal Glucose Tolerance Test">
  <data key="d0">Intraperitoneal Glucose Tolerance Test</data>
  <data key="d1">Method</data>
  <data key="d2">A metabolic test performed on four-week-old fasted mice to measure blood glucose response following intraperitoneal dextrose injection.&lt;SEP&gt;The intraperitoneal glucose tolerance test involves fasting mice for 16 hours and injecting glucose (2 g/kg body weight) intraperitoneally, with blood glucose measured at multiple time points using a glucometer.&lt;SEP&gt;Intraperitoneal glucose tolerance testing involves injecting D-glucose into fasted mice and measuring blood glucose levels over time to assess glucose tolerance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a5af2ab88dac4e2b983a277be1a9c536&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb31cc9ec659a6d29b2ec1e3870fb57b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68488f40a0b43cd31dd09cb8c1939a9a</data>
  <data key="d4">The MafA transcription factor becomes essential to islet β-cells soon after birth.&lt;SEP&gt;MafB Is Important for Pancreatic β-Cell Maintenance under a MafA-Deficient Condition.&lt;SEP&gt;Sex-biased islet β cell dysfunction is caused by the MODY MAFA S64F variant by inducing premature aging and senescence in males.</data>
