<node id="Triton X-100">
  <data key="d0">Triton X-100</data>
  <data key="d1">Molecule</data>
  <data key="d2">A detergent component (1%) in the lysis buffer used to lyse islets for Zn2+ content measurement.&lt;SEP&gt;Triton X-100 is a detergent used for permeabilization in immunostaining protocols, at 0.2% concentration for insulin staining and 0.5% for MAFA staining.&lt;SEP&gt;Detergent used at 0.3% concentration in blocking and permeabilizing solution for immunohistochemistry.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a5af2ab88dac4e2b983a277be1a9c536&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc527b8db70f9b6c3c8648c4a33df392&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6cadc21c6ca916dd06510987c1b7dbf4</data>
  <data key="d4">The MafA transcription factor becomes essential to islet β-cells soon after birth.&lt;SEP&gt;Sex-biased islet β cell dysfunction is caused by the MODY MAFA S64F variant by inducing premature aging and senescence in males.&lt;SEP&gt;Calorie restriction increases insulin sensitivity to promote beta cell homeostasis and longevity in mice.</data>
  <data key="d5">1778569408</data>
