<node id="Quantitative PCR">
  <data key="d0">Quantitative PCR</data>
  <data key="d1">Method</data>
  <data key="d2">Quantitative PCR is a method used to analyze mRNA expression levels of MafA-regulated genes in MafaΔpanc and control islets across different postnatal time points.&lt;SEP&gt;A gene expression quantification method used to analyze Ins1, Ins2, and other β-cell function genes during the postnatal time course study of MafA's regulatory role.&lt;SEP&gt;Quantitative PCR is a molecular technique used to measure gene expression levels of Ins1, Ins2, and Gcg in isolated pancreatic islets from different mouse genotypes.&lt;SEP&gt;Quantitative PCR (qPCR) is a method used to detect and quantify target gene expression using Power SYBR Green master mix and gene-specific primers.&lt;SEP&gt;A molecular biology technique (qPCR) used to detect and quantify target gene expression, performed using Power SYBR Green master mix.&lt;SEP&gt;Quantitative PCR (qPCR) was used to measure RNA expression levels of C-MAF in the kidneys of model mice.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a5af2ab88dac4e2b983a277be1a9c536&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ee443fb4c37f27d6895254d3f95c708&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-45b0e9a843120dd461f5ba7ec823e41f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e72d8d21ebb3fc252c498fcbfeed6c1d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a7dd7d21dd9a5aa2ba54defd650b8ebd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0be98cbe29b4c692e555154146fad640</data>
  <data key="d4">The MafA transcription factor becomes essential to islet β-cells soon after birth.&lt;SEP&gt;MafB Is Important for Pancreatic β-Cell Maintenance under a MafA-Deficient Condition.&lt;SEP&gt;Stress-induced β cell early senescence confers protection against type 1 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d5">1778564616</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
