<node id="Sytl4 (Granuphilin)">
  <data key="d0">Sytl4 (Granuphilin)</data>
  <data key="d1">Tissue</data>
  <data key="d2">Sytl4, also known as granuphilin, is an established effector of granule docking identified as being affected by MafA regulation in the microarray data.&lt;SEP&gt;Sytl4, also known as granuphilin, is a protein effector of insulin granule docking whose expression is regulated by MafA and is diminished in MafaΔpanc β-cells.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f67b6052ac2da6848aaabbd71f9d4d53&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-94526413b6fbcf0ec99212789cec9eea</data>
