<node id="Ccnd2">
  <data key="d0">Ccnd2</data>
  <data key="d1">Tissue</data>
  <data key="d2">Ccnd2, encoding cyclin D2, is a gene affected specifically in 3-month-old MafaΔpanc islets but not in E18.5 Mafb−/− pancreata, and is likely involved in β-cell replication.&lt;SEP&gt;CCND2 is a known target gene of MAFA and a key regulator of β-cell proliferation, predicted to be upregulated by the p.Ser64Phe mutant, potentially causing β-cell transformation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f67b6052ac2da6848aaabbd71f9d4d53&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6854465a5ab40a3dbe223209e2c5cd66</data>
  <data key="d4">The MafA transcription factor becomes essential to islet β-cells soon after birth.&lt;SEP&gt;MAFA missense mutation causes familial insulinomatosis and diabetes mellitus.</data>
  <data key="d5">1778561512</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">0</data>
  <data key="d8">beta cell / MAFA / MAFB</data>
