  <data key="d11">0.01182989</data>
</node>
<node id="Cyclin D2">
  <data key="d0">Cyclin D2</data>
  <data key="d1">Biological Process</data>
  <data key="d2">Cyclin D2 is a cell cycle regulator whose regulation by MafA contributes to β-cell replication.&lt;SEP&gt;Cyclin D2 is a cell cycle regulator likely involved in β-cell replication changes observed in MafaΔpanc islets.&lt;SEP&gt;Cyclin D2 is a protein likely involved in β-cell replication, and its reduced expression is associated with the decreased number of β-cells in MafaΔpanc islets.&lt;SEP&gt;Cyclin D2 is a cell cycle regulator whose levels are modulated by Akt to induce beta-cell proliferation.&lt;SEP&gt;Cyclin D2 is a cell cycle regulator whose expression is induced in islets early in high-fat feeding, concurrent with adaptive β-cell proliferation.&lt;SEP&gt;Cyclin D2 is a cell cycle regulator that is upregulated by MafB overexpression in human β-cell lines, promoting cell proliferation.&lt;SEP&gt;Cell cycle protein regulated by AKT to promote beta-cell proliferation.&lt;SEP&gt;Cyclin involved in beta cell proliferation; increased in a model of constitutively active Akt in mouse beta cells.&lt;SEP&gt;Cell cycle protein regulated by AKT to promote beta-cell proliferation.&lt;SEP&gt;Cyclin involved in beta cell proliferation; increased in a model of constitutively active Akt in mouse beta cells.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f67b6052ac2da6848aaabbd71f9d4d53&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a87d40ff620e7f930f155b5dea286c8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-75261aabfd0eeb269665c62f36dfeb2e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fffe587d9d8a94d6179115102ef90a2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5afa9fdb0e4f653f1c7825c0b258326d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4e0ae079210c3ef99872d0747c5a9b88&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ef7d4c1829099c6037d8b8b7a83c3cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8c7bb3e4a69884a1b79485b95f6f502</data>
  <data key="d4">The MafA transcription factor becomes essential to islet β-cells soon after birth.&lt;SEP&gt;MafB Is Important for Pancreatic β-Cell Maintenance under a MafA-Deficient Condition.&lt;SEP&gt;MAFA missense mutation causes familial insulinomatosis and diabetes mellitus.</data>
  <data key="d5">1778562074</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
