<node id="Islet Cell Architecture">
  <data key="d0">Islet Cell Architecture</data>
  <data key="d1">Biological Process</data>
  <data key="d2">Islet cell architecture refers to the spatial organization of endocrine cells within pancreatic islets; MafaΔpanc islets exhibit altered architecture similar to human islets, with fewer β-cells and α-cells in the core.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f67b6052ac2da6848aaabbd71f9d4d53</data>
  <data key="d4">The MafA transcription factor becomes essential to islet β-cells soon after birth.</data>
