<node id="Weaning">
  <data key="d0">Weaning</data>
  <data key="d1">Biological Process</data>
  <data key="d2">Weaning is the transition period in laboratory rodents from mother's milk to chow diet, during which MafA expression increases and significant metabolic changes occur in β-cells, marking when MafA begins to influence β-cell function.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f67b6052ac2da6848aaabbd71f9d4d53</data>
  <data key="d4">The MafA transcription factor becomes essential to islet β-cells soon after birth.</data>
