  <data key="d1">Biological Process</data>
  <data key="d2">Maturity-onset diabetes of the young (MODY) is a monoallelic form of diabetes in which six of nine associated genes encode transcription factors essential to islet cells.&lt;SEP&gt;Maturity-onset diabetes of the young is a form of diabetes associated with mutations in many islet-enriched transcription factors, whose effects on β cell activity are more severe than those caused by MafA or MAFB reduction.</data>
