  <data key="d1">Biological Process</data>
  <data key="d2">Cardiovascular disease is a long-term complication of diabetes mellitus associated with the use of exogenous insulin therapy.&lt;SEP&gt;Disease mentioned alongside diabetes and malignancies as conditions whose causative genes have been identified through advances in medical technology.&lt;SEP&gt;Disease of the heart and blood vessels; sex differences in mechanisms are being studied.&lt;SEP&gt;A disease with sex differences in mechanisms studied in illuminating research.&lt;SEP&gt;Disease of the heart and blood vessels; sex differences in mechanisms are being studied.&lt;SEP&gt;A disease with sex differences in mechanisms studied in illuminating research.&lt;SEP&gt;Cardiovascular disease context in which senescence markers accumulate in cardiomyocytes, cardiac fibroblasts, and other cardiovascular cell lineages.</data>
