<node id="Islet-Enriched Transcription Factors">
  <data key="d0">Islet-Enriched Transcription Factors</data>
  <data key="d1">Biological Process</data>
  <data key="d2">Islet-enriched transcription factors are proteins that play a central role in orchestrating the biosynthesis of islet hormone-producing cells, with six of nine MODY-associated genes encoding such factors.&lt;SEP&gt;Islet-enriched transcription factors are proteins associated with INS transcription and β cell identity, including NKX6.1, PDX1, MAFA, and MAFB, whose levels are sensitive to metabolic and oxidative stress.&lt;SEP&gt;Islet-enriched transcription factors are regulators of islet cell identity and function, including MafA, MAFB, Pdx1, Nkx6.1, Nkx2.2, and Pax6, whose deficiency can lead to misexpression of non–β cell hormones.&lt;SEP&gt;Islet-enriched transcription factors are proteins present in pancreatic islets that cooperate with MAFA and MAFB to stimulate Insulin enhancer-driven activity.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7a87d40ff620e7f930f155b5dea286c8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea3320816339f9f109dec0e1621420bd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e6c6371cdef301723817998e0efc9ec6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b5b330edc0a8ae22148338c6d94f154</data>
  <data key="d4">The MafA transcription factor becomes essential to islet β-cells soon after birth.&lt;SEP&gt;Defining unique structural features in the MAFA and MAFB transcription factors that control Insulin gene activity.&lt;SEP&gt;Species-specific roles for the MAFA and MAFB transcription factors in regulating islet β cell identity.</data>
  <data key="d5">1778563030</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">0</data>
