<node id="Islet Isolation">
  <data key="d0">Islet Isolation</data>
  <data key="d1">Method</data>
  <data key="d2">A procedure involving anesthesia, cervical dislocation, collagenase P digestion, and hand-picking under 10× magnification to isolate islets from mouse pancreas.&lt;SEP&gt;Islet isolation is a standard collagenase/protease digestion method involving pancreatic duct cannulation, enzymatic digestion, washing, and density gradient separation to obtain pancreatic islets.&lt;SEP&gt;Procedure to isolate pancreatic islets from mice using collagenase digestion and Histopaque gradient purification.&lt;SEP&gt;Procedure involving pancreatic perfusion through the bile duct with Liberase (Sigma-Aldrich) to isolate murine islets</data>
