  <data key="d4">The MafA transcription factor becomes essential to islet β-cells soon after birth.&lt;SEP&gt;Members of the large Maf transcription family regulate insulin gene transcription in islet beta cells.&lt;SEP&gt;MafA and MafB regulate genes critical to beta-cells in a unique temporal manner.&lt;SEP&gt;Defining unique structural features in the MAFA and MAFB transcription factors that control Insulin gene activity.&lt;SEP&gt;Sex-biased islet β cell dysfunction is caused by the MODY MAFA S64F variant by inducing premature aging and senescence in males.&lt;SEP&gt;Species-specific roles for the MAFA and MAFB transcription factors in regulating islet β cell identity.&lt;SEP&gt;MafA is a dedicated activator of the insulin gene in vivo.&lt;SEP&gt;MafB Is Important for Pancreatic β-Cell Maintenance under a MafA-Deficient Condition.&lt;SEP&gt;The MAFB transcription factor impacts islet α-cell function in rodents and represents a unique signature of primate islet β-cells.&lt;SEP&gt;Examining How the MAFB Transcription Factor Affects Islet β-Cell Function Postnatally.&lt;SEP&gt;Stress-induced β cell early senescence confers protection against type 1 diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;A switch from MafB to MafA expression accompanies differentiation to pancreatic beta-cells.&lt;SEP&gt;MAFA missense mutation causes familial insulinomatosis and diabetes mellitus.&lt;SEP&gt;Exploring Large MAF Transcription Factors: Functions, Pathology, and Mouse Models with Point Mutations.&lt;SEP&gt;Pancreatic β-cell senescence in diabetes: mechanisms, markers and therapies.&lt;SEP&gt;Single cell regulatory architecture of human pancreatic islets suggests sex differences in β cell function and the pathogenesis of type 2 diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;SenNet recommendations for detecting senescent cells in different tissues.&lt;SEP&gt;Exploring senescence as a modifier of β cell extracellular vesicles in type 1 diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Safeguarding genomic integrity in beta-cells: implications for beta-cell differentiation, growth, and dysfunction.&lt;SEP&gt;Calorie restriction increases insulin sensitivity to promote beta cell homeostasis and longevity in mice.&lt;SEP&gt;Sex-specific regulatory architecture of pancreatic islets from subjects with and without type 2 diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Genetic background influences the phenotypic penetrance by MAFA (S64F) MODY in male mice.&lt;SEP&gt;The role of the beta cell in type 2 diabetes: new findings from the last 5 years.&lt;SEP&gt;Nucleolar stress facilitates islet β cell senescence via hijacking the DNA damage response pathways.&lt;SEP&gt;Developmental control of DNA damage responses in α- and β-cells shapes the selective beta-cell susceptibility in diabetes.</data>
