<node id="MAFB">
  <data key="d0">MAFB</data>
  <data key="d1">Gene</data>
  <data key="d2">MAFB (also known as MafB or Musculoaponeurotic Fibrosarcoma Transcription Factor B) is a large MAF family transcription factor containing a basic leucine-zipper (bZIP) domain, with an N-terminal transactivation domain spanning approximately 240–340 amino acids. It is closely related to MAFA and MAF, and functions as a key regulator of multiple developmental and physiological processes across diverse tissue types. MAFB can act as a homodimer or heterodimer, including heterodimers with MAFA, and independently stimulates insulin-reporter activity.

In pancreatic biology, MAFB is an islet-enriched transcription factor with essential roles in both α-cell and β-cell lineages. Its transcription factor motif is highly enriched in alpha cells (fold enrichment &gt;1.5, -log10 FDR &gt;50). During embryogenesis, MAFB is expressed in all glucagon-positive and insulin-positive cells across both waves of hormone-positive cell formation, preceding MAFA expression during β-cell differentiation and serving as a more potent regulator of early β-cell development. It acts as a specific activator of glucagon gene expression, serves as the primary activator of Slc30a8, contributes to G6pc2 and Neuronatin (Nnat) expression, and binds and activates insulin C1 element-mediated expression. Deletion of MAFB from β-cells delays development and impairs Ins1, Ins2, Pdx1, and Glut2 expression. MAFB is also coexpressed in skeletal muscle and testes, cooperates with islet-enriched transcription factors, and binds MLL3 and MLL4 methyltransferases.

A critical species-specific distinction governs postnatal MAFB expression. In rodents, MAFB becomes barely detectable in β-cells approximately two weeks after birth and is largely restricted to α-cells by four weeks postnatally, though it is reexpressed in proliferative β-cells during pregnancy and obesity. Combined deletion of MafB and MafA in adult mouse β-cells causes severe islet structural destruction and glucose intolerance. In contrast, MAFB is continuously co-expressed alongside MAFA in human and nonhuman primate islet β-cells throughout adulthood. In humans, MAFB is essential for insulin production, glucose-stimulated insulin secretion (GSIS), β-cell derivation from pluripotent and embryonic stem cells, and maintenance of mature β-cell identity. Its loss contributes to GAST+ β-cell signatures and misexpression observed in type 2 diabetes (T2D), and its expression is also affected in type 1 diabetes.

Beyond the pancreas, MAFB regulates hindbrain segmentation, macrophage and monocyte differentiation, podocyte development, parathyroid and inner ear development, and atherosclerotic lesion development. It prevents apoptosis in macrophages, and Mafb−/− mice die at birth from central apnea. MAFB also displays oncogenic activity and has been identified in recurrent chromosomal translocations associated with multiple myeloma and insulinoma.

Clinically, MAFB harbors point mutations and mutations within its transcriptional activation domain associated with rare human diseases, including Multicentric Carpotarsal Osteolysis (MCTO), Duane syndrome, and Focal Segmental Glomerulosclerosis (FSGS).&lt;SEP&gt;MAFB is a transcription factor motif highly enriched in alpha cells of pancreatic islets.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-75261aabfd0eeb269665c62f36dfeb2e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69365499ad956be649b962c79d46f483&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06849490a7a3c085d30a2a392584bd67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6854465a5ab40a3dbe223209e2c5cd66&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78596a38854a9e8f2c4ef9c3dfcbbfbd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d01061347ba219119efa4109d89e71f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68488f40a0b43cd31dd09cb8c1939a9a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-74fc4f55c8c6d83ebd1d8dba07d90692&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5f38c4d8fe95ae0a2b5cc05069361348&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b3deb83588a816faad5340f542e1f43&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9977f67772ceb665bdd71b221a2d4234&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b39885796d53f3f69a4452a58c07c2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c914d24696d0f6e2087f40c21ca5649&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d1c90235486a0fe738831a720e1f94ab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce67306159c306b2c966577061cee6bd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea3320816339f9f109dec0e1621420bd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbe530a83d027293c37b530e3c376973&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-46772cbd15b1e36b4aedeac0a06fd4de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e6c6371cdef301723817998e0efc9ec6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b39e1736c730a00c8edfab90d7dc64da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-667c57ab63de668da1132b51f1e9f411&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b13f08985b48653da8be9b63098bbb2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b5b330edc0a8ae22148338c6d94f154&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01e46f30e47340f5c5b95376196543ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0be98cbe29b4c692e555154146fad640&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a91f8726a8e590e31edad7232b84804b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02381256ec5732a712b97ced237c2acb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-222f634a871d4f5fd5cffac2fce0d698&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ed6515ae53fc7e07b1c44a83258c3224&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b1a171c046b7e074fd282a07d58cc39&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe670890a826e2e1970f382c46b77260&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9693157a2d458ecc8255c49ec77d95f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b158cd1c233246631a3b8f719a275f2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a87d40ff620e7f930f155b5dea286c8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-207f97a443acec0faaf8f9f2d208e61f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9bec3f5c6cf93d2d763da970e02d0fc3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4e0ae079210c3ef99872d0747c5a9b88&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a7873cb15c71b20e5fc369a6f0ab52a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0269f34de8f0928a9614438917079ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f63ca40b092870f725a75e7a36045d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb32288d5dedac1b2