<node id="Monogenic Diabetes">
  <data key="d0">Monogenic Diabetes</data>
  <data key="d1">Biological Process</data>
  <data key="d2">Monogenic diabetes refers to diabetes caused by single gene disorders, which provide lessons for understanding diabetes pathogenesis.&lt;SEP&gt;A form of diabetes caused by mutations in single genes, discussed as a gateway to precision medicine in diabetes research.&lt;SEP&gt;Monogenic diabetes is a form of diabetes caused by mutations in single genes and serves as a gateway to precision medicine in diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;A form of diabetes caused by mutations in single genes, in which beta cell senescence has been implicated.&lt;SEP&gt;A form of diabetes caused by mutations in single genes, in which beta cell senescence has been implicated.&lt;SEP&gt;Form of diabetes caused by a missense mutation in the beta-cell transcription factor MAFA, associated with DNA damage hallmarks.&lt;SEP&gt;Form of diabetes produced by the MAFA S64F substitution that prevents priming serine 65 phosphorylation.&lt;SEP&gt;Form of diabetes sharing elevated beta-cell DNA damage as a hallmark and driver of beta-cell defects.</data>
