  <data key="d9">7.181e-05</data>
  <data key="d10">0.0</data>
  <data key="d11">0.00775564</data>
</node>
<node id="Postnatal MafB Production">
  <data key="d0">Postnatal MafB Production</data>
  <data key="d1">Biological Process</data>
  <data key="d2">Postnatal MafB production refers to the brief period after birth during which MafB is expressed in pancreatic cells, affecting the functional significance of MafA to β-cells.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3ecc1e3f157d04d78962c82537c6b7d9</data>
  <data key="d4">The MafA transcription factor becomes essential to islet β-cells soon after birth.</data>
  <data key="d5">1778561528</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">0</data>
  <data key="d8">beta cell / MAFA / MAFB</data>
  <data key="d9">7.271e-05</data>
  <data key="d10">0.0</data>
  <data key="d11">0.0069073</data>
</node>
<node id="MafA N Terminus">
  <data key="d0">MafA N Terminus</data>
  <data key="d1">Biological Process</data>
  <data key="d2">The MafA N terminus contains phosphorylation sites that regulate C-terminal dimerization and DNA binding activity of MafA.&lt;SEP&gt;The MafA N terminus is a domain in which phosphorylation regulates C-terminal dimerization and DNA binding of the MafA transcription factor.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3ecc1e3f157d04d78962c82537c6b7d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fffe587d9d8a94d6179115102ef90a2d</data>
  <data key="d4">The MafA transcription factor becomes essential to islet β-cells soon after birth.&lt;SEP&gt;MAFA missense mutation causes familial insulinomatosis and diabetes mellitus.</data>
  <data key="d5">1778561800</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">0</data>
  <data key="d8">beta cell / MAFA / MAFB</data>
  <data key="d9">7.181e-05</data>
  <data key="d10">0.0</data>
  <data key="d11">0.00775564</data>
</node>
<node id="Neonatal Rat Beta Cells">
  <data key="d0">Neonatal Rat Beta Cells</data>
  <data key="d1">Biological Process</data>
  <data key="d2">Neonatal rat beta cells are immature beta cells in which Mafa expression enhances glucose-responsive insulin secretion.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3ecc1e3f157d04d78962c82537c6b7d9</data>
  <data key="d4">The MafA transcription factor becomes essential to islet β-cells soon after birth.</data>
  <data key="d5">1778561529</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">0</data>
  <data key="d8">beta cell / MAFA / MAFB</data>
  <data key="d9">7.181e-05</data>
  <data key="d10">0.0</data>
  <data key="d11">0.00775564</data>
</node>
<node id="Human Pluripotent Stem Cells">
  <data key="d0">Human Pluripotent Stem Cells</data>
  <data key="d1">Biological Process</data>
  <data key="d2">Human pluripotent stem cells are self-renewing cells from which endodermal progenitor lines can be generated, used in research on pancreatic cell differentiation.&lt;SEP&gt;Stem cells from which beta cells can be derived; loss of MAFB limits this derivation.&lt;SEP&gt;Model system providing insights into how non-coding variants affect beta cell development.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3ecc1e3f157d04d78962c82537c6b7d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3384cef9855a1b408c68f7d1ea3153c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-044fb2d3ececa99a53eb87d2ee6bf18f</data>
  <data key="d4">The MafA transcription factor becomes essential to islet β-cells soon after birth.</data>
  <data key="d5">1778561529</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">3</data>
  <data key="d8">cellular senescence / CDKN2A / CDKN1A</data>
  <data key="d9">0.00018336</data>
  <data key="d10">0.00037578</data>
  <data key="d11">0.00771426</data>
</node>
<node id="Endoplasmic Reticulum">
  <data key="d0">Endoplasmic Reticulum</data>
  <data key="d1">Biological Process</data>
  <data key="d2">The endoplasmic reticulum is an organelle in mouse pancreatic β-cells where free Ca2+ concentration is controlled by SERCA2b and SERCA3, interplaying with cell metabolism.&lt;SEP&gt;Organelle involved in protein processing and transport; pathway enriched in CR beta cells.&lt;SEP&gt;Cellular organelle whose selective autophagy (reticulophagy) is not differentially modulated by caloric restriction in beta cells.&lt;SEP&gt;Organelle (ER) found to rarely fuse with beta cell MDVs; only one example of MDV-ER fusion was observed in the study.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3ecc1e3f157d04d78962c82537c6b7d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f0c13c5a18e2c5037815818d22c48a64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa01ef8f1657a9890660f864f52123c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0178968ab91760930c812723c60d342b</data>
  <data key="d4">The MafA transcription factor becomes essential to islet β-cells soon after birth.</data>
  <data key="d5">1778561529</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">66</data>
  <data key="d8">Endoplasmic Reticulum Stress (ER Stress) / SERCA2b / Cytokines</data>
  <data key="d9">0.00019324</data>
  <data key="d10">1.799e-05</data>
  <data key="d11">0.0002523</data>
</node>
<node id="MafBΔpanc">
  <data key="d0">MafBΔpanc</data>
  <data key="d1">Organism</data>
  <data key="d2">MafBΔpanc are pancreas-wide MafB mutant mice generated to study the postnatal significance of MafB deficiency; glucose-induced glucagon secretion was compromised in their adult islet α-cells.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-69365499ad956be649b962c79d46f483</data>
  <data key="d4">The MAFB transcription factor impacts islet α-cell function in rodents and represents a unique signature of primate islet β-cells.</data>
  <data key="d5">1778561628</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
  <data key="d8">Insulin / Pancreatic Islets / A0B0 Mice</data>
  <data key="d9">0.00010317</data>
  <data key="d10">0.0</data>
  <data key="d11">0.00406159</data>
</node>
<node id="MafABΔpanc">
  <data key="d0">MafABΔpanc</data>
  <data key="d1">Organism</data>
  <data key="d2">MafABΔpanc are pancreas-wide MafA/B double mutant mice that died soon after birth from hyperglycemia, supporting the compensatory role of MafA for MafB.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-69365499ad956be649b962c79d46f483</data>
  <data key="d4">The MAFB transcription factor impacts islet α-cell function in rodents and represents a unique signature of primate islet β-cells.</data>
