<node id="Multiple Myeloma">
  <data key="d0">Multiple Myeloma</data>
  <data key="d1">Biological Process</data>
  <data key="d2">Multiple myeloma is a hematological malignancy in which the MAF gene is up-regulated in 50% of cases, and recurrent translocations involving MAF, MAFB, and MAFA are identified in 5–10% of cases.&lt;SEP&gt;Multiple myeloma is a cancer in which overexpression of c-maf and dysregulation of MAFB are frequent oncogenic events involving chromosomal translocations at Ig loci.&lt;SEP&gt;Multiple myeloma is a human cancer associated with translocations that cause ectopic overexpression of large Maf proteins, suggesting cell transformation depends on overexpression of Maf transcription factors.&lt;SEP&gt;Multiple myeloma is a cancer in which MAF transcription factors, including C-MAF, MAFA, and MAFB, are importantly implicated.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fffe587d9d8a94d6179115102ef90a2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06849490a7a3c085d30a2a392584bd67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6854465a5ab40a3dbe223209e2c5cd66&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a91f8726a8e590e31edad7232b84804b</data>
