</node>
<node id="HNF4A">
  <data key="d0">HNF4A</data>
  <data key="d1">Gene</data>
  <data key="d2">HNF4A is a gene whose heterozygous mutations cause diazoxide-responsive hyperinsulinemic hypoglycemia, persistent hyperinsulinemic hypoglycemia, maturity-onset diabetes of the young, and macrosomia.&lt;SEP&gt;HNF4A is a transcription factor gene whose mutations can lead to a paradoxical phenotype of both diabetes and transient congenital hyperinsulinism, analogous to the p.Ser64Phe MAFA mutation.&lt;SEP&gt;Transcription factor governing beta1 cell subtype; mutations cause MODY; deregulated by chronic glucose/palmitate exposure in human islets.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fffe587d9d8a94d6179115102ef90a2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6854465a5ab40a3dbe223209e2c5cd66&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cba0d7fafdd66d2ffb133e04939d15f0</data>
  <data key="d4">MAFA missense mutation causes familial insulinomatosis and diabetes mellitus.&lt;SEP&gt;The role of the beta cell in type 2 diabetes: new findings from the last 5 years.</data>
