<node id="Prolactin Receptor">
  <data key="d0">Prolactin Receptor</data>
  <data key="d1">Biological Process</data>
  <data key="d2">The prolactin receptor is required for normal glucose homeostasis and modulation of beta-cell mass during pregnancy.&lt;SEP&gt;A receptor whose inactivation, together with MafB inactivation in islet β-cells, leads to gestational diabetes mellitus.&lt;SEP&gt;The prolactin receptor is a protein whose inactivation, along with MafB, leads to gestational diabetes mellitus in islet β-cells.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fffe587d9d8a94d6179115102ef90a2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f64af938dff7c5f186bd7024d92cbc0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b13f08985b48653da8be9b63098bbb2f</data>
  <data key="d4">Sex-biased islet β cell dysfunction is caused by the MODY MAFA S64F variant by inducing premature aging and senescence in males.&lt;SEP&gt;Species-specific roles for the MAFA and MAFB transcription factors in regulating islet β cell identity.&lt;SEP&gt;MAFA missense mutation causes familial insulinomatosis and diabetes mellitus.</data>
  <data key="d5">1778562896</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">3</data>
