<node id="Estrogen Receptor Alpha">
  <data key="d0">Estrogen Receptor Alpha</data>
  <data key="d1">Method</data>
  <data key="d2">Estrogen receptor alpha regulates beta-cell formation during pancreas development and following injury.&lt;SEP&gt;Receptor that protects pancreatic beta cells from apoptosis by preserving mitochondrial function and suppressing endoplasmic reticulum stress.&lt;SEP&gt;Estrogen receptor that protects pancreatic beta cells from apoptosis by preserving mitochondrial function and suppressing ER stress; also stimulates NEUROD1 binding to the insulin promoter via extranuclear actions.&lt;SEP&gt;Receptor that protects pancreatic beta cells from apoptosis by preserving mitochondrial function and suppressing endoplasmic reticulum stress.&lt;SEP&gt;Nuclear and extranuclear receptor for estrogen; regulates beta cell function, insulin synthesis, lipid metabolism, and protects against apoptosis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fffe587d9d8a94d6179115102ef90a2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b67e26d82684726785f1910ba6919cf0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd3982c3cb7b00162818de82027a853e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51601485f0924871a988aae2e5ce30bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0238834380bfb40677324883af3e3004</data>
