<node id="Placental Lactogen">
  <data key="d0">Placental Lactogen</data>
  <data key="d1">Method</data>
  <data key="d2">Placental lactogen is a hormone whose targeted expression in beta-cells of transgenic mice results in beta-cell proliferation, islet mass augmentation, and hypoglycemia.&lt;SEP&gt;A hormone that, along with prolactin, signals through PRLR to induce β-cell mass expansion during pregnancy, potentially influencing insulinomatosis development in female carriers.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fffe587d9d8a94d6179115102ef90a2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e531f038e6fcc1cbb89c2336af984719</data>
