<node id="Maturity-Onset Diabetes Of The Young (MODY)">
  <data key="d0">Maturity-Onset Diabetes Of The Young (MODY)</data>
  <data key="d1">Biological Process</data>
  <data key="d2">Maturity-onset diabetes of the young (MODY) is a diabetes phenotype resembled by the diabetes observed in MAFA p.Ser64Phe mutation carriers, characterized by absence of ketoacidosis and negative islet autoantibodies.&lt;SEP&gt;Maturity-onset diabetes of the young is a monogenic form of diabetes with best practice guidelines for molecular genetic diagnosis, and can be caused by HNF4A mutations.&lt;SEP&gt;MODY is a collection of monogenic diseases predominantly driven by mutations in essential islet-enriched transcription factors, for which MAFA is identified as a causative gene.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fffe587d9d8a94d6179115102ef90a2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-348e687c811009b30863b17f466ac662&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-427bdb72b4ec16ac96774e76f03ada77</data>
  <data key="d4">Sex-biased islet β cell dysfunction is caused by the MODY MAFA S64F variant by inducing premature aging and senescence in males.&lt;SEP&gt;MAFA missense mutation causes familial insulinomatosis and diabetes mellitus.</data>
  <data key="d5">1778562666</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
