<node id="MAF">
  <data key="d0">MAF</data>
  <data key="d1">Protein</data>
  <data key="d2">MAF is a large Maf transcription factor that is up-regulated in 50% of human multiple myelomas and 60% of angioimmunoblastic T cell lymphomas, and is involved in recurrent translocations in multiple myelomas.&lt;SEP&gt;MAF is a bZIP transcription factor whose domain disruption and mutation are associated with cataract, ocular anterior segment dysgenesis, and coloboma.&lt;SEP&gt;MAF is a member of the Maf transcription factor family displaying oncogenic activity, related to MAFA and MAFB.&lt;SEP&gt;Large musculoaponeurotic fibrosarcoma transcription factor family containing acidic, basic, and leucine zipper regions; includes c-MAF, MAFA, MAFB, and NRL subtypes.&lt;SEP&gt;A large MAF transcription factor (c-Maf) involved in lens development, IL-4 expression, erythropoiesis, and associated with cataract and other diseases when mutated.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fffe587d9d8a94d6179115102ef90a2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06849490a7a3c085d30a2a392584bd67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6854465a5ab40a3dbe223209e2c5cd66&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02381256ec5732a712b97ced237c2acb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ed6515ae53fc7e07b1c44a83258c3224</data>
  <data key="d4">MAFA missense mutation causes familial insulinomatosis and diabetes mellitus.&lt;SEP&gt;Exploring Large MAF Transcription Factors: Functions, Pathology, and Mouse Models with Point Mutations.</data>
  <data key="d5">1778566107</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">6</data>
  <data key="d8">C-MAF / MAF / MAF transcription factors</data>
  <data key="d9">0.00274041</data>
  <data key="d10">0.01166819</data>
  <data key="d11">0.02419254</data>
</node>
<node id="Hyperinsulinemic Hypoglycemia">
  <data key="d0">Hyperinsulinemic Hypoglycemia</data>
  <data key="d1">Biological Process</data>
  <data key="d2">Hyperinsulinemic hypoglycemia is the clinical manifestation of insulinomatosis caused by excessive insulin secretion from multiple pancreatic neuroendocrine tumors.&lt;SEP&gt;Hyperinsulinemic hypoglycemia is a clinical condition secondary to insulinomatosis, observed in 10 subjects from the two families with the MAFA p.Ser64Phe mutation.&lt;SEP&gt;Hyperinsulinemic hypoglycemia is a condition of excess insulin causing low blood sugar, associated with HNF4A mutations and insulinomatosis.&lt;SEP&gt;Hyperinsulinemic hypoglycemia is a condition characterized by abnormally low blood glucose due to excess insulin, observed in patients with MAFA mutation-positive insulinomatosis.&lt;SEP&gt;A phenotype characterized by excessive insulin secretion causing low blood sugar, secondary to insulinomatosis in patients carrying the p.Ser64Phe MAFA mutation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fffe587d9d8a94d6179115102ef90a2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-71db066aa18a18c64b2b33ad26f7bfab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06849490a7a3c085d30a2a392584bd67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-348e687c811009b30863b17f466ac662&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e531f038e6fcc1cbb89c2336af984719</data>
