  <data key="d0">Cyclin D1</data>
  <data key="d1">Method</data>
  <data key="d2">Cyclin D1 is a cell cycle regulator whose levels are modulated by Akt to induce beta-cell proliferation.&lt;SEP&gt;Cell cycle protein regulated by AKT to promote beta-cell proliferation.&lt;SEP&gt;Cyclin involved in beta cell proliferation; increased in a model of constitutively active Akt in mouse beta cells.&lt;SEP&gt;Protein induced upon PTEN loss, contributing to downregulation of p16Ink4a and activation of E2F transcription factors.&lt;SEP&gt;Cell cycle protein regulated by AKT to promote beta-cell proliferation.&lt;SEP&gt;Cyclin involved in beta cell proliferation; increased in a model of constitutively active Akt in mouse beta cells.&lt;SEP&gt;Protein induced upon PTEN loss, contributing to downregulation of p16Ink4a and activation of E2F transcription factors.</data>
