</node>
<node id="Ser64">
  <data key="d0">Ser64</data>
  <data key="d1">Biological Process</data>
  <data key="d2">Ser64 is a phosphorylation-related site in MAFA; its mutation to phenylalanine (p.Ser64Phe) prevents priming phosphorylation at Ser65 and subsequent GSK3-mediated phosphorylation.&lt;SEP&gt;Ser64 is an amino acid residue located within the N-terminal transactivation domain of MAFA; its substitution with phenylalanine (p.Ser64Phe) disrupts priming phosphorylation and subsequent GSK3-mediated phosphorylation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-61ea436af2c14f0df238edb6a5db2bea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-71db066aa18a18c64b2b33ad26f7bfab</data>
