<node id="GSK3">
  <data key="d0">GSK3</data>
  <data key="d1">Protein</data>
  <data key="d2">GSK3 is a kinase responsible for mediating phosphorylation within the transactivation domain of MAFA following the priming phosphorylation at Ser65.&lt;SEP&gt;GSK3 is a kinase involved in the sequential phosphorylation of the N-terminal transactivation domain of MAFA, contributing to protein degradation and regulation of transactivation capacity.&lt;SEP&gt;Kinase whose phosphorylation of MAF, when impaired by mutations, causes cataract, deafness, intellectual disability, seizures, and Down syndrome-like facies.&lt;SEP&gt;Kinase with a phosphorylation site affected by mutations in MAFA and C-MAF, relevant to transactivation domain regulation.&lt;SEP&gt;GSK3 is a kinase that phosphorylates C-MAF at specific residues including p.Thr58, relevant to disease onset mechanisms.&lt;SEP&gt;Glycogen synthase kinase 3, mediates phosphorylation of MAFA at residues S61, T57, T53, and S49 following priming phosphorylation at S65.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-61ea436af2c14f0df238edb6a5db2bea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6854465a5ab40a3dbe223209e2c5cd66&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0be98cbe29b4c692e555154146fad640&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02381256ec5732a712b97ced237c2acb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b1a171c046b7e074fd282a07d58cc39&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb32288d5dedac1b23370508bf2f7b2a</data>
