<node id="P.Ser64Phe Mutation">
  <data key="d0">P.Ser64Phe Mutation</data>
  <data key="d1">Biological Process</data>
  <data key="d2">The p.Ser64Phe (c.191C&gt;T) missense mutation in the MAFA gene impairs phosphorylation within the transactivation domain, increases MAFA protein stability under high and low glucose concentrations, and enhances transactivation potential in β-cell lines.&lt;SEP&gt;The p.Ser64Phe mutation is a missense mutation in MAFA that prevents priming phosphorylation, dramatically increases protein stability, enhances transactivation capacity, and is associated with insulinomatosis or noninsulin-dependent diabetes resembling MODY.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-61ea436af2c14f0df238edb6a5db2bea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06849490a7a3c085d30a2a392584bd67</data>
