  <data key="d1">Method</data>
  <data key="d2">Sodium orthovanadate (Na3VO4) is a phosphatase inhibitor used in experiments to prevent dephosphorylation of MAFA protein, preserving its phosphorylated state.&lt;SEP&gt;A chemical compound used in protein mobility analysis experiments involving MAFA-transfected HeLa cell nuclear extracts.&lt;SEP&gt;Sodium orthovanadate (Na3VO4) is a phosphatase inhibitor used at 10 mM concentration in protein mobility analysis experiments.</data>
