  <data key="d1">Molecule</data>
  <data key="d2">NaCl is used in experiments as a control condition that allows endogenous phosphatase activity to dephosphorylate MAFA, altering protein mobility.&lt;SEP&gt;NaCl is a salt used in experimental conditions to assess the phosphorylation state of MAFA mutant proteins by enabling endogenous phosphatase activity to alter protein mobility.&lt;SEP&gt;NaCl (10 mM) is used as a control condition alongside sodium orthovanadate in protein mobility analysis experiments.&lt;SEP&gt;Buffer component (10 mM) used in the nuclei isolation lysis buffer for single cell multiomics sample preparation.</data>
