<node id="Ubiquitination">
  <data key="d0">Ubiquitination</data>
  <data key="d1">Biological Process</data>
  <data key="d2">Ubiquitination is a posttranslational modification targeting lysine residues in the C-terminal DNA-binding/dimerization region of MAFA for protein degradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Ubiquitination is a protein degradation process occurring in the C-terminal domain of MAFA, triggered by phosphorylation events in the N-terminal transactivation domain.&lt;SEP&gt;Post-translational modification process; CR beta cells show increased expression of ubiquitin processing, ubiquitin protein degradation, and proteasome subunit genes.&lt;SEP&gt;Posttranslational modification occurring in MAFA and MAFB proteins in mammalian cells.&lt;SEP&gt;Post-translational modification occurring on MAFAWT and MAFBWT in mammalian cells.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-61ea436af2c14f0df238edb6a5db2bea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6854465a5ab40a3dbe223209e2c5cd66&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f0c13c5a18e2c5037815818d22c48a64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f4fecd9e508da1daa4a0d2d27a7e759&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eae638e9cabe91a68fc062c9981b0e86</data>
