<node id="Transactivation Domain">
  <data key="d0">Transactivation Domain</data>
  <data key="d1">Biological Process</data>
  <data key="d2">The transactivation domain of MAFA is the region within which the p.Ser64Phe mutation impairs phosphorylation, leading to increased protein stability and enhanced transactivation activity.&lt;SEP&gt;The transactivation domain is a highly conserved functional region of the MAFA protein where the p.Ser64Phe variant is located.&lt;SEP&gt;The transactivation domain is the N-terminal region of MAFA that undergoes GSK3-mediated phosphorylation and is fused to the Gal4 DNA-binding domain in chimeric protein experiments.&lt;SEP&gt;The transactivation domain of MafA contains phosphorylation sites at positions S61, T51, T57, and S49 targeted by GSK3, which are affected by the MAFAS64F mutation.&lt;SEP&gt;N-terminal domain present in large MAF proteins (~240-340 amino acids) that mediates transcriptional activation, absent in small MAFs.&lt;SEP&gt;The transactivation domain is a region in MAFA and MAFB with variable conformation that lies near the DNA binding region of the basic-leucine-zipper domain.&lt;SEP&gt;Functional domain of MAFA and MAFB outside the basic-leucine-zipper region that is important for cooperative activation with islet-enriched transcription factors.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-61ea436af2c14f0df238edb6a5db2bea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06849490a7a3c085d30a2a392584bd67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-348e687c811009b30863b17f466ac662&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63a4c12087ceb7cec876e14e7fc45727&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84ba2041af7b71a5fc2faad1de1c95dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3384cef9855a1b408c68f7d1ea3153c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d07a2e48a0133bedad1b6e79e652b89c</data>
  <data key="d4">Sex-biased islet β cell dysfunction is caused by the MODY MAFA S64F variant by inducing premature aging and senescence in males.&lt;SEP&gt;MAFA missense mutation causes familial insulinomatosis and diabetes mellitus.</data>
  <data key="d5">1778562682</data>
