<node id="Family 1">
  <data key="d0">Family 1</data>
  <data key="d1">Organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Family 1 is the index family consisting of 29 subjects (17 females) of white Caucasian background exhibiting autosomal dominant inheritance of insulinomatosis and diabetes mellitus, in whom the p.Ser64Phe MAFA mutation was identified.&lt;SEP&gt;Family 1 is a family with multiple members carrying the MAFA p.Ser64Phe variant, exhibiting phenotypes of insulinomatosis and diabetes mellitus across generations.&lt;SEP&gt;Family 1 is a consanguineous family in the study with members carrying the MAFA mutation, some of whom present with diabetes, congenital glaucoma, congenital cataract, and insulinomatosis.&lt;SEP&gt;One of two recruited families with autosomal dominant insulinomatosis and diabetes mellitus, in which exome sequencing was performed on four affected individuals.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-71db066aa18a18c64b2b33ad26f7bfab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06849490a7a3c085d30a2a392584bd67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-348e687c811009b30863b17f466ac662&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e531f038e6fcc1cbb89c2336af984719</data>
