  <data key="d9">0.0006686</data>
  <data key="d10">0.00127554</data>
  <data key="d11">0.00556163</data>
</node>
<node id="Family 2">
  <data key="d0">Family 2</data>
  <data key="d1">Organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Family 2 is a second unrelated family consisting of 7 subjects (2 females) with the same clinical phenotype of insulinomatosis and diabetes mellitus, in whom the same p.Ser64Phe MAFA mutation was identified.&lt;SEP&gt;Family 2 is a previously clinically described family with 7 subjects (2 females) carrying the MAFA p.Ser64Phe mutation, presenting with insulinomatosis and diabetes mellitus.&lt;SEP&gt;Family 2 is a family in the study with members carrying the MAFA mutation, some of whom present with diabetes, gestational diabetes, and insulinomatosis, with no history of congenital eye disorders.&lt;SEP&gt;One of two recruited families with autosomal dominant insulinomatosis and diabetes mellitus, in which the whole coding sequence of MAFA was sequenced via Sanger sequencing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-71db066aa18a18c64b2b33ad26f7bfab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06849490a7a3c085d30a2a392584bd67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-348e687c811009b30863b17f466ac662&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e531f038e6fcc1cbb89c2336af984719</data>
