<node id="Pancreatic Neuroendocrine Tumors">
  <data key="d0">Pancreatic Neuroendocrine Tumors</data>
  <data key="d1">Biological Process</data>
  <data key="d2">Pancreatic neuroendocrine tumors are multicentric tumors ranging in size between 0.4 and 1.1 cm, identified in patients with hyperinsulinemic hypoglycemia from the MAFA mutation-carrying families.&lt;SEP&gt;Pancreatic neuroendocrine tumors are multifocal, well-differentiated tumors (Ki-67 &lt;2%) with trabecular tissue architecture found in patients with the p.Ser64Phe MAFA mutation, expressing insulin but not other pancreatic hormones.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-71db066aa18a18c64b2b33ad26f7bfab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-348e687c811009b30863b17f466ac662</data>
