<node id="H&amp;E Staining">
  <data key="d0">H&amp;E Staining</data>
  <data key="d1">Method</data>
  <data key="d2">H&amp;E staining is a histological method used to visualize the trabecular tissue architecture of MAFA mutation-positive insulinomas.&lt;SEP&gt;H&amp;E (hematoxylin and eosin) staining is a routine histological method applied to 5-μm paraffin sections of pancreatic tissue for islet visualization and counting.&lt;SEP&gt;Hematoxylin and eosin (H&amp;E) staining is a routine histological method used to stain 5-μm paraffin sections of pancreatic tissue for islet counting and size measurement.&lt;SEP&gt;Hematoxylin and eosin staining performed on one section at each of three depths of paraffin-embedded pancreatic tissue for histological evaluation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-71db066aa18a18c64b2b33ad26f7bfab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5afa9fdb0e4f653f1c7825c0b258326d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb31cc9ec659a6d29b2ec1e3870fb57b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40bbefacfceda2b6335fdb6310e2f7ae</data>
  <data key="d4">Stress-induced β cell early senescence confers protection against type 1 diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;MafB Is Important for Pancreatic β-Cell Maintenance under a MafA-Deficient Condition.&lt;SEP&gt;MAFA missense mutation causes familial insulinomatosis and diabetes mellitus.</data>
