<node id="MAFA Immunostaining">
  <data key="d0">MAFA Immunostaining</data>
  <data key="d1">Method</data>
  <data key="d2">MAFA immunostaining is a technique used to assess MAFA protein expression in tumor tissue, revealing diffuse positivity in insulinomas at lower intensity compared to neighboring normal islets.&lt;SEP&gt;Immunostaining for MAFA was performed on EndoC-βH2 cell slides using Rabbit α-MAFA antibody (1:500, Novus NBP1-00121), imaged on a Zeiss Axio Imager M2 widefield microscope with ApoTome.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-71db066aa18a18c64b2b33ad26f7bfab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc527b8db70f9b6c3c8648c4a33df392</data>
  <data key="d4">Sex-biased islet β cell dysfunction is caused by the MODY MAFA S64F variant by inducing premature aging and senescence in males.&lt;SEP&gt;MAFA missense mutation causes familial insulinomatosis and diabetes mellitus.</data>
  <data key="d5">1778562657</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
  <data key="d8">Insulin / Pancreatic Islets / A0B0 Mice</data>
