<node id="Glycogen Synthase Kinase 3 (GSK3)">
  <data key="d0">Glycogen Synthase Kinase 3 (GSK3)</data>
  <data key="d1">Method</data>
  <data key="d2">Glycogen Synthase Kinase 3 (GSK3) is a kinase that sequentially phosphorylates residues Ser61, Thr57, Thr53, and Ser49 in the MAFA transactivation domain after priming phosphorylation at Ser65.&lt;SEP&gt;Glycogen Synthase Kinase 3 (GSK3) is an enzyme that mediates phosphorylation of MafA at positions S61, T51, T57, and S49 in the transactivation domain, promoting its degradation.&lt;SEP&gt;A kinase responsible for constitutive phosphorylation of MafA at multiple sites, regulating its stability in pancreatic β cells.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-71db066aa18a18c64b2b33ad26f7bfab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f64af938dff7c5f186bd7024d92cbc0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63a4c12087ceb7cec876e14e7fc45727</data>
  <data key="d4">Sex-biased islet β cell dysfunction is caused by the MODY MAFA S64F variant by inducing premature aging and senescence in males.&lt;SEP&gt;MAFA missense mutation causes familial insulinomatosis and diabetes mellitus.</data>
  <data key="d5">1778562646</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">0</data>
  <data key="d8">beta cell / MAFA / MAFB</data>
  <data key="d9">0.00022185</data>
  <data key="d10">2.855e-05</data>
  <data key="d11">0.01343797</data>
</node>
<node id="P.Ser65Ala Mutant">
  <data key="d0">P.Ser65Ala Mutant</data>
  <data key="d1">Method</data>
  <data key="d2">The p.Ser65Ala mutant is a kinase priming-defective MAFA variant whose protein mobility is indistinguishable from the p.Ser64Phe mutant, suggesting similar disruption of the phosphorylation cascade.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-71db066aa18a18c64b2b33ad26f7bfab</data>
