</node>
<node id="Oral Glucose Tolerance Test (oGTT)">
  <data key="d0">Oral Glucose Tolerance Test (oGTT)</data>
  <data key="d1">Method</data>
  <data key="d2">The oral glucose tolerance test (oGTT) is a clinical diagnostic test used to assess glucose metabolism, employed in subjects from both family 1 and family 2 to evaluate glucose tolerance and insulin secretion.&lt;SEP&gt;The oGTT is a clinical test used to assess glucose metabolism, with results in p.Ser64Phe mutation carriers consistent with impaired glucose-stimulated insulin secretion.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-71db066aa18a18c64b2b33ad26f7bfab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6854465a5ab40a3dbe223209e2c5cd66</data>
