<node id="HOMA-IR">
  <data key="d0">HOMA-IR</data>
  <data key="d1">Method</data>
  <data key="d2">HOMA-IR (Homeostatic Model Assessment of Insulin Resistance) is a well-established quantitative measure used to assess insulin resistance in both clinical and research settings. It is calculated from fasting glucose and fasting insulin values, providing a standardized index of peripheral insulin sensitivity and overall insulin resistance.

In clinical contexts, HOMA-IR serves as an important diagnostic and monitoring variable. It is used to characterize metabolic subtypes, notably being low in individuals with severe insulin-deficient diabetes, reflecting the distinct pathophysiology of that subgroup. As an example of its application in individual patient assessment, subject IV/2 from family 2 was noted to have a normal HOMA-IR value of 1.7, illustrating its utility in evaluating insulin resistance at the individual level.

In research settings, particularly in animal studies, HOMA-IR is applied to evaluate the metabolic effects of dietary interventions. For instance, it has been calculated from fasting glucose and insulin values in mice after two months on specific diets, allowing for comparisons of insulin resistance across different dietary conditions. This dual applicability — in human clinical assessment and in preclinical animal research — underscores the versatility of HOMA-IR as a metabolic index.

Overall, HOMA-IR remains a widely used, straightforward, and reliable tool for quantifying insulin resistance, derived solely from fasting glucose and insulin measurements, and applicable across diverse populations and experimental contexts.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-71db066aa18a18c64b2b33ad26f7bfab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68a87a3a1f3eb5d8b0e53b41df492512&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2e4a544176811f5b43952b185e1ed3a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-75f39153d9f864070e17a74724a6c8c6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce68225f2288adf7d07962282496e8c5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-363f3a19905f833d29a7d1242acc6641&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d286ee457150be65228790e800b5207b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4e8cbb766d17c90c84d2a9452a51a41e</data>
