<node id="Impaired Glucose Tolerance">
  <data key="d0">Impaired Glucose Tolerance</data>
  <data key="d1">Biological Process</data>
  <data key="d2">Impaired glucose tolerance is a pre-diabetic condition observed in subject III/3 from family 2 after giving birth, and prospectively diagnosed in subject IV/2 from family 2 via oGTT.&lt;SEP&gt;Impaired glucose tolerance is a pre-diabetic state in which β-cell neogenesis is the predominant mechanism of new β-cell formation rather than replication.&lt;SEP&gt;Phenotype observed in heterozygous MAFA-mutant male mice; associated with increased MAFA protein expression prior to onset.&lt;SEP&gt;Key prediabetic state associated with discordance between beta cell mass and function, and reduced first-phase insulin secretion.&lt;SEP&gt;A key prediabetic state associated with reduced first- and second-phase insulin secretion and lower total insulin content normalized to beta cell mass.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-71db066aa18a18c64b2b33ad26f7bfab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b13f08985b48653da8be9b63098bbb2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b1a171c046b7e074fd282a07d58cc39&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4e8cbb766d17c90c84d2a9452a51a41e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-044fb2d3ececa99a53eb87d2ee6bf18f</data>
  <data key="d4">Species-specific roles for the MAFA and MAFB transcription factors in regulating islet β cell identity.&lt;SEP&gt;MAFA missense mutation causes familial insulinomatosis and diabetes mellitus.</data>
  <data key="d5">1778562899</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">14</data>
