<node id="NRL">
  <data key="d0">NRL</data>
  <data key="d1">Protein</data>
  <data key="d2">NRL is a member of the large Maf transcription factor family, along with MAFA, MAFB, and MAF.&lt;SEP&gt;Large MAF transcription factor; no genetically modified mice with the same point mutations as in humans have been documented to date.&lt;SEP&gt;One of four large MAF transcription factors identified in mice and humans; no genetically modified mouse models with point mutations in NRL have been documented.&lt;SEP&gt;Large MAF transcription factor with conserved basic region sequences similar to MAFA and MAFB.&lt;SEP&gt;Member of the large MAF transcription factor family (~240-340 amino acids).</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-06849490a7a3c085d30a2a392584bd67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01e46f30e47340f5c5b95376196543ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ed6515ae53fc7e07b1c44a83258c3224&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3384cef9855a1b408c68f7d1ea3153c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f4fecd9e508da1daa4a0d2d27a7e759</data>
