<node id="Autosomal Dominant Inheritance">
  <data key="d0">Autosomal Dominant Inheritance</data>
  <data key="d1">Biological Process</data>
  <data key="d2">Autosomal dominant inheritance is the pattern of inheritance observed in the two families carrying the p.Ser64Phe MAFA mutation, where either insulinomatosis or diabetes mellitus is transmitted across generations.&lt;SEP&gt;The assumed model of inheritance used to filter heterozygous variants in the exome sequencing analysis of Family 1, and the inheritance pattern observed in the recruited families with insulinomatosis and diabetes mellitus.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-06849490a7a3c085d30a2a392584bd67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e531f038e6fcc1cbb89c2336af984719</data>
