<node id="EndoC-βH1 Cells">
  <data key="d0">EndoC-βH1 Cells</data>
  <data key="d1">Biological Process</data>
  <data key="d2">EndoC-βH1 is a human pancreatic beta-cell line used in cycloheximide chase experiments to study MAFA-Myc protein stability.&lt;SEP&gt;EndoC-βH1 is a human pancreatic β cell line used in experiments to study the effects of MAFB knockdown on GAST expression.&lt;SEP&gt;EndoC-βH1 cells are human β cell line cells in which MAFB depletion compromises glucose-stimulated insulin secretion (GSIS), demonstrating MAFB's role in β cell function.&lt;SEP&gt;EndoC-βH1 cells are human β-cell line used to study the effects of ATF6 inhibition and p21-mediated early senescence signatures relevant to T1D.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b65a0501c576270f0560dc1e4695ef2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c914d24696d0f6e2087f40c21ca5649&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea3320816339f9f109dec0e1621420bd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea9634b81ecdb467a2b26648246e5b5c</data>
