  <data key="d10">0.0</data>
  <data key="d11">0.0</data>
</node>
<node id="Tryptophan Hydroxylase 1">
  <data key="d0">Tryptophan Hydroxylase 1</data>
  <data key="d1">Biological Process</data>
  <data key="d2">Tryptophan hydroxylase 1 is an enzyme whose mRNA production is elevated by transgenic MafB in β-cells during pregnancy, driving serotonin biosynthesis critical for adaptive maternal β-cell responses.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-78596a38854a9e8f2c4ef9c3dfcbbfbd</data>
  <data key="d4">Examining How the MAFB Transcription Factor Affects Islet β-Cell Function Postnatally.</data>
