  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">0</data>
  <data key="d8">beta cell / MAFA / MAFB</data>
  <data key="d9">7.271e-05</data>
  <data key="d10">0.0</data>
  <data key="d11">0.0069073</data>
</node>
<node id="A0B0 Mice">
  <data key="d0">A0B0 Mice</data>
  <data key="d1">Organism</data>
  <data key="d2">A0B0 mice are generated by mating MafB CKO mice with MafA-null knockout mice, lacking both MafA and MafB, and display mildly impaired glucose tolerance and more significantly impaired islet structures.&lt;SEP&gt;A0B0 mice are MafA and MafB double-knockout mice in which MafB was specifically deleted in β cells, generated to investigate the role of MafB in adult β-cell function under MafA-deficient conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;A0B0 mice are a genotype group lacking both MafA and MafB, displaying more impaired glucose tolerance, structural islet destruction, increased glucagon-expressing cells, and developing diabetes after high-fat diet treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;A0B0 mice are a genotype group used in HFD studies that exhibit severely impaired glucose tolerance, decreased total islet numbers, reduced large islet proportions, increased small islet proportions, and significantly fewer insulin-positive cells. Some A0B0 mice died due to severe diabetic conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;Double-knockout mice deficient in both MafA and MafB, exhibiting severely impaired glucose tolerance, higher α-cell/β-cell ratios, reduced insulin-positive β cells, increased β-cell apoptosis, and development of diabetes mellitus under HFD conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;A0B0 mice are MafA and MafB double-knockout mice that became more susceptible to diabetes under HFD conditions, exhibiting impaired islet morphology, decreased insulin-expressing cell numbers, and increased apoptosis.&lt;SEP&gt;A0B0 mice are a genetically modified mouse strain used in comparative pancreatic and metabolic studies alongside WT and A0B2 mice.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-45b0e9a843120dd461f5ba7ec823e41f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5afa9fdb0e4f653f1c7825c0b258326d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb31cc9ec659a6d29b2ec1e3870fb57b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d01061347ba219119efa4109d89e71f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-968f694e317648c82a07ee150e63adbd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9aad668b81389b88364235018ee9c389&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5afc163e9261bd9f96c6156bfdb27585</data>
  <data key="d4">MafB Is Important for Pancreatic β-Cell Maintenance under a MafA-Deficient Condition.</data>
  <data key="d5">1778562064</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
  <data key="d8">Insulin / Pancreatic Islets / A0B0 Mice</data>
  <data key="d9">0.00206626</data>
  <data key="d10">0.00612715</data>
  <data key="d11">0.018225</data>
</node>
<node id="A0B2 Mice">
  <data key="d0">A0B2 Mice</data>
  <data key="d1">Organism</data>
  <data key="d2">A0B2 mice are MafA-null knockout mice used as a comparison group in glucose tolerance and insulin secretion studies.&lt;SEP&gt;A0B2 mice are a genotype group with partial loss of MafA/MafB function, showing reduced insulin-expressing cells compared to WT but less severe islet destruction than A0B0 mice.&lt;SEP&gt;A0B2 mice are a genotype group used in HFD studies that show decreased percentages of large islets and increased small islets compared to WT mice, with intermediate phenotypes between WT and A0B0 mice.&lt;SEP&gt;MafA single-knockout mice used as a comparison group against A0B0 mice, showing less severe metabolic phenotypes.&lt;SEP&gt;A0B2 mice are MafA single-knockout mice used as a comparison group alongside A0B0 mice and wild-type littermates in high-fat diet and histological experiments.&lt;SEP&gt;A0B2 mice are a genetically modified mouse strain used in comparative pancreatic and metabolic studies alongside WT and A0B0 mice.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-45b0e9a843120dd461f5ba7ec823e41f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5afa9fdb0e4f653f1c7825c0b258326d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb31cc9ec659a6d29b2ec1e3870fb57b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d01061347ba219119efa4109d89e71f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9aad668b81389b88364235018ee9c389&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5afc163e9261bd9f96c6156bfdb27585</data>
  <data key="d4">MafB Is Important for Pancreatic β-Cell Maintenance under a MafA-Deficient Condition.</data>
  <data key="d5">1778562064</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
  <data key="d8">Insulin / Pancreatic Islets / A0B0 Mice</data>
  <data key="d9">0.00069097</data>
  <data key="d10">0.00023371</data>
  <data key="d11">0.00774196</data>
</node>
<node id="WT Mice">
  <data key="d0">WT Mice</data>
  <data key="d1">Organism</data>
  <data key="d2">WT (wild-type) mice serve as the control group in glucose tolerance and insulin secretion experiments.&lt;SEP&gt;Wild-type (WT) mice serve as the control group in the study, used for comparison of pancreatic islet structure, insulin and glucagon cell numbers, and glucose tolerance.&lt;SEP&gt;Wild-type (WT) mice serve as the control genotype group in HFD studies, exhibiting normal glucose tolerance, higher proportions of large islets, and higher percentages of insulin-positive cells.&lt;SEP&gt;WT (wild-type) mice are used as control subjects in pancreatic tissue analysis, islet isolation, and metabolic experiments.&lt;SEP&gt;Wild-type mice used as controls in studies comparing islet function, hormone secretion, and gene expression with MafAS64F/+ mice.&lt;SEP&gt;Wild-type (WT) mice serve as the control genotype in experiments comparing pancreatic, glycogen storage, and other physiological parameters.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-45b0e9a843120dd461f5ba7ec823e41f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb31cc9ec659a6d29b2ec1e3870fb57b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9aad668b81389b88364235018ee9c389&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5afc163e9261bd9f96c6156bfdb27585&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc527b8db70f9b6c3c8648c4a33df392&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82e08f93585dc5d50ccfbac2feb8d206</data>
  <data key="d4">MafB Is Important for Pancreatic β-Cell Maintenance under a MafA-Deficient Condition.&lt;SEP&gt;Sex-biased islet β cell dysfunction is caused by the MODY MAFA S64F variant by inducing premature aging and senescence in males.</data>
  <data key="d5">1778562657</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
  <data key="d8">Insulin / Pancreatic Islets / A0B0 Mice</data>
  <data key="d9">0.00047282</data>
  <data key="d10">0.00010863</data>
  <data key="d11">0.00242674</data>
</node>
<node id="Gcg Gene">
  <data key="d0">Gcg Gene</data>
  <data key="d1">Data</data>
  <data key="d2">The Gcg gene encodes glucagon; its relative mRNA expression was comparable among WT, A0B2, and A0B0 groups despite structural differences in islets.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-45b0e9a843120dd461f5ba7ec823e41f</data>
  <data key="d4">MafB Is Important for Pancreatic β-Cell Maintenance under a MafA-Deficient Condition.</data>
  <data key="d5">1778562065</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">0</data>
  <data key="d8">beta cell / MAFA / MAFB</data>
  <data key="d9">0.00011676</data>
  <data key="d10">9.71e-06</data>
  <data key="d11">0.00080307</data>
</node>
<node id="Hprt">
  <data key="d0">Hprt</data>
  <data key="d1">Data</data>
  <data key="d2">Hprt is a housekeeping gene used as a normalization reference for quantitative PCR measurements of Ins1, Ins2, and Gcg gene expression in pancreatic islets.&lt;SEP&gt;Hprt is a housekeeping gene used as a normalization reference for quantitative real-time PCR gene expression analysis in pancreatic islet studies.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-45b0e9a843120dd461f5ba7ec823e41f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb31cc9ec659a6d29b2ec1e3870fb57b</data>
