</node>
<node id="High-Fat Diet (HFD)">
  <data key="d0">High-Fat Diet (HFD)</data>
  <data key="d1">Method</data>
  <data key="d2">High-fat diet (HFD) is a dietary treatment used to induce a pathological diabetic condition in mice, leading to significantly elevated fasting blood glucose and severely impaired glucose tolerance in A0B0 mice.&lt;SEP&gt;High-Fat Diet (HFD) is a dietary treatment administered to mice starting at 8 weeks of age for 5 months to study metabolic and pancreatic responses across different genotypes.&lt;SEP&gt;A dietary treatment used to induce obesity and metabolic stress in mice, revealing more severe phenotypes in MafA and MafB knockout models.&lt;SEP&gt;The high-fat diet (HFD) consists of 62.2% fat, 19.6% carbohydrate, and 18.2% protein on a caloric basis and was used to induce metabolic stress in experimental mice from 6 to 8 weeks of age.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-45b0e9a843120dd461f5ba7ec823e41f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5afa9fdb0e4f653f1c7825c0b258326d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d01061347ba219119efa4109d89e71f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9aad668b81389b88364235018ee9c389</data>
  <data key="d4">MafB Is Important for Pancreatic β-Cell Maintenance under a MafA-Deficient Condition.</data>
  <data key="d5">1778562066</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
  <data key="d8">Insulin / Pancreatic Islets / A0B0 Mice</data>
  <data key="d9">0.00046313</data>
  <data key="d10">0.00039096</data>
  <data key="d11">0.00197363</data>
</node>
<node id="C57BL/6J Mouse Strain">
  <data key="d0">C57BL/6J Mouse Strain</data>
  <data key="d1">Organism</data>
  <data key="d2">C57BL/6J is an inbred mouse strain used in this study, in which MafA knockout alone produces a milder phenotype compared to the ICR strain.&lt;SEP&gt;C57BL/6J is a mouse strain sourced from the Jackson Laboratory and used as the genetic background for experimental mice in this study.&lt;SEP&gt;C57BL/6J is the mouse strain used to generate S64F MafA-expressing mice via CRISPR/Cas9 targeting.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-45b0e9a843120dd461f5ba7ec823e41f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5afa9fdb0e4f653f1c7825c0b258326d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68488f40a0b43cd31dd09cb8c1939a9a</data>
  <data key="d4">MafB Is Important for Pancreatic β-Cell Maintenance under a MafA-Deficient Condition.&lt;SEP&gt;Sex-biased islet β cell dysfunction is caused by the MODY MAFA S64F variant by inducing premature aging and senescence in males.</data>
  <data key="d5">1778562650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">28</data>
  <data key="d8">Mafa∆panc Mouse / C57BL/6J Mouse Strain / NOD/ShiLtJ Mice</data>
  <data key="d9">0.00027856</data>
  <data key="d10">0.00267394</data>
  <data key="d11">0.00786445</data>
</node>
<node id="ICR Mouse Strain">
  <data key="d0">ICR Mouse Strain</data>
  <data key="d1">Organism</data>
  <data key="d2">ICR is a mouse strain in which MafA deficiency contributes to fasting hyperglycemia at an early stage of adulthood and eventual diabetes development.</data>
