<node id="β Cells">
  <data key="d0">β Cells</data>
  <data key="d1">Biological Process</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin-producing cells within pancreatic islets; their development, maturation, and survival are regulated by MafA and MafB transcription factors.&lt;SEP&gt;β cells are insulin-producing pancreatic cells whose maintenance, proliferation, and apoptosis are regulated by transcription factors including MafA and MafB.&lt;SEP&gt;Pancreatic islet cells responsible for insulin production, whose identity and activity are compromised by loss of MafA/MAFB, leading to expression of non–β cell hormones.&lt;SEP&gt;β cells are insulin-producing pancreatic islet cells in which MAFB and MAFA repress GAST transcription; their dysfunction is associated with T2D development.&lt;SEP&gt;β cells are insulin-producing cells in the pancreatic islets, whose identity and function can be compromised by loss of MafA and MAFB, leading to dysfunction and alternative cell states.&lt;SEP&gt;β cells are insulin-secreting cells in the pancreatic islets whose function and structure are studied in relation to MafA and MafB expression.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulin-producing cells in the pancreatic islets whose mass, proliferation, apoptosis, and function are regulated by MafA and MafB.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7568462935971fd17472cf21ed7b8a2b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5afa9fdb0e4f653f1c7825c0b258326d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c914d24696d0f6e2087f40c21ca5649&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea3320816339f9f109dec0e1621420bd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4b8d7d9156faa43670557fc5e83791e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d01061347ba219119efa4109d89e71f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5afc163e9261bd9f96c6156bfdb27585</data>
  <data key="d4">MafB Is Important for Pancreatic β-Cell Maintenance under a MafA-Deficient Condition.&lt;SEP&gt;Species-specific roles for the MAFA and MAFB transcription factors in regulating islet β cell identity.</data>
  <data key="d5">1778562864</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">0</data>
  <data key="d8">beta cell / MAFA / MAFB</data>
  <data key="d9">0.00045438</data>
  <data key="d10">0.00114258</data>
  <data key="d11">0.02094371</data>
</node>
<node id="α Cells">
  <data key="d0">α Cells</data>
  <data key="d1">Biological Process</data>
  <data key="d2">α cells are pancreatic islet cells in which MafB expression is maintained after birth, and their numbers are also regulated by MafB during embryonic development.&lt;SEP&gt;Glucagon-producing cells within pancreatic islets; MafB is a key regulator of their development and mature function.&lt;SEP&gt;Pancreatic islet endocrine cells that produce glucagon; MafB is present throughout the life span of islet α cells in both rodents and humans.&lt;SEP&gt;Glucagon-producing cells in the pancreatic islets; the α-cell/β-cell ratio is remarkably higher in A0B0 islets compared to A0B2 islets.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7568462935971fd17472cf21ed7b8a2b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-968f694e317648c82a07ee150e63adbd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce67306159c306b2c966577061cee6bd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d01061347ba219119efa4109d89e71f</data>
  <data key="d4">MafB Is Important for Pancreatic β-Cell Maintenance under a MafA-Deficient Condition.&lt;SEP&gt;Species-specific roles for the MAFA and MAFB transcription factors in regulating islet β cell identity.</data>
  <data key="d5">1778562877</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">0</data>
  <data key="d8">beta cell / MAFA / MAFB</data>
  <data key="d9">0.00010445</data>
  <data key="d10">0.0</data>
  <data key="d11">0.00939156</data>
</node>
<node id="Cell Apoptosis">
  <data key="d0">Cell Apoptosis</data>
  <data key="d1">Biological Process</data>
  <data key="d2">Programmed cell death process that is more highly induced in A0B0 islets, contributing to reduced islet cell numbers observed in HFD-fed A0B0 mice.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7568462935971fd17472cf21ed7b8a2b</data>
  <data key="d4">MafB Is Important for Pancreatic β-Cell Maintenance under a MafA-Deficient Condition.</data>
