<node id="Paraformaldehyde">
  <data key="d0">Paraformaldehyde</data>
  <data key="d1">Method</data>
  <data key="d2">Paraformaldehyde (4%) is the fixative used to fix pancreatic tissues obtained from WT, A0B2, and A0B0 mice overnight at room temperature before paraffin embedding.&lt;SEP&gt;A 4% (v/v) fixative solution used to fix WT and MafAS64F/+ pancreata for immunostaining procedures.&lt;SEP&gt;4% paraformaldehyde is used as a fixative in immunostaining protocols, applied for 45 minutes for insulin staining and 12 minutes for MAFA staining.&lt;SEP&gt;4% paraformaldehyde from Electron Microscopy Services was used to fix human pancreata, mouse pancreata, and EndoC-βH1/2 cells for immunofluorescence staining.&lt;SEP&gt;A 4% fixative solution from Electron Microscopy Sciences used to fix cells during the β-cell staining protocol.&lt;SEP&gt;Fixative (PFA) used at 2% concentration alongside glutaraldehyde in transcardiac perfusion for tissue preservation in MIMS-EM sample processing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5afa9fdb0e4f653f1c7825c0b258326d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc527b8db70f9b6c3c8648c4a33df392&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82e08f93585dc5d50ccfbac2feb8d206&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-667c57ab63de668da1132b51f1e9f411&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e74e3fadd5f43dbb51005345f56dec5c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d5c817dce40d1df02e7717bb9598632</data>
  <data key="d4">Stress-induced β cell early senescence confers protection against type 1 diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;MafB Is Important for Pancreatic β-Cell Maintenance under a MafA-Deficient Condition.&lt;SEP&gt;Sex-biased islet β cell dysfunction is caused by the MODY MAFA S64F variant by inducing premature aging and senescence in males.&lt;SEP&gt;Species-specific roles for the MAFA and MAFB transcription factors in regulating islet β cell identity.</data>
  <data key="d5">1778564562</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">20</data>
  <data key="d8">ATF6 / β-Cells / Chromatin Immunoprecipitation</data>
