<node id="One-Way ANOVA">
  <data key="d0">One-Way ANOVA</data>
  <data key="d1">Method</data>
  <data key="d2">One-way analysis of variance (ANOVA) with post hoc Tukey HSD tests is used for statistical comparisons among three groups, with significance defined as P &lt; 0.05.&lt;SEP&gt;Statistical method used with Tukey's or Benjamini-Krieger-Yekutieli post-hoc tests for multi-group comparisons.&lt;SEP&gt;One-way ANOVA with Benjamini, Krieger and Yekutieli's post-hoc test is a statistical method used for analyzing 53BP1 and autophagy marker data.&lt;SEP&gt;Statistical method used for comparison of groups with Benjamini, Krieger, and Yekutieli post-hoc test.&lt;SEP&gt;One-way ANOVA is a statistical method used to compare two or more groups in experimental data.&lt;SEP&gt;Statistical test used to compare two or more groups in animal experiments and IHC microscopy data.&lt;SEP&gt;Statistical method used to compare multiple variables, followed by post hoc comparisons.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-eb31cc9ec659a6d29b2ec1e3870fb57b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56d5ffe02105b1bd6d77faab9c812433&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-75f39153d9f864070e17a74724a6c8c6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-831b74d6764559e79da6fa29d15caf42&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0178968ab91760930c812723c60d342b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c85c9569fee140bfd52fcc0bbfbcc9c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc8b7f13c10f7804685d92e4b92bc78a</data>
  <data key="d4">MafB Is Important for Pancreatic β-Cell Maintenance under a MafA-Deficient Condition.</data>
  <data key="d5">1778562084</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">16</data>
  <data key="d8">Pancreatic Islet / Bulk RNA-Seq / Islet Isolation</data>
  <data key="d9">0.00059427</data>
  <data key="d10">0.00143206</data>
  <data key="d11">9.9e-07</data>
</node>
<node id="Tukey Honestly Significant Difference (HSD) Test">
  <data key="d0">Tukey Honestly Significant Difference (HSD) Test</data>
  <data key="d1">Method</data>
  <data key="d2">The Tukey honestly significant difference (HSD) test is a post hoc statistical test used following one-way ANOVA to identify which group comparisons are statistically significant, with significance defined as P &lt; 0.05.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-eb31cc9ec659a6d29b2ec1e3870fb57b</data>
  <data key="d4">MafB Is Important for Pancreatic β-Cell Maintenance under a MafA-Deficient Condition.</data>
