  <data key="d0">Large Maf Protein Family</data>
  <data key="d1">Biological Process</data>
  <data key="d2">The large Maf protein family is a group of transcription factors, including MafA and MafB, known to play important roles in islet cell development and function.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-968f694e317648c82a07ee150e63adbd</data>
  <data key="d4">MafB Is Important for Pancreatic β-Cell Maintenance under a MafA-Deficient Condition.</data>
