<node id="MafB Conditional-Knockout (CKO) Mice">
  <data key="d0">MafB Conditional-Knockout (CKO) Mice</data>
  <data key="d1">Organism</data>
  <data key="d2">MafB conditional-knockout (CKO) mice are mice in which MafB was specifically deleted from β cells using Cre-loxP recombination, used to investigate MafB regulation of β cells independently of α cells.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-968f694e317648c82a07ee150e63adbd</data>
  <data key="d4">MafB Is Important for Pancreatic β-Cell Maintenance under a MafA-Deficient Condition.</data>
