</node>
<node id="Cre-Loxp Recombination">
  <data key="d0">Cre-Loxp Recombination</data>
  <data key="d1">Method</data>
  <data key="d2">Cre-loxP recombination is a genetic technique used to specifically delete MafB from β cells in conditional-knockout mouse models.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-968f694e317648c82a07ee150e63adbd</data>
  <data key="d4">MafB Is Important for Pancreatic β-Cell Maintenance under a MafA-Deficient Condition.</data>
