<node id="Glucose-Stimulated Insulin Secretion (GSIS)">
  <data key="d0">Glucose-Stimulated Insulin Secretion (GSIS)</data>
  <data key="d1">Biological Process</data>
  <data key="d2">Glucose-stimulated insulin secretion (GSIS) testing is an in vivo method used to measure plasma insulin levels in response to glucose stimulation in different mouse genotypes.&lt;SEP&gt;Glucose-stimulated insulin secretion (GSIS) is the process by which β cells secrete insulin in response to elevated blood glucose; this process is impaired in MafA-deficient mice.&lt;SEP&gt;A functional measure of β cell activity in which insulin is secreted in response to elevated glucose levels; regulated by MafA.&lt;SEP&gt;GSIS is an ex vivo assay used to measure insulin secretion from islets in response to glucose stimulation, showing impaired secretion in 5-week-old male MafAS64F/+ islets.&lt;SEP&gt;Glucose-stimulated insulin secretion (GSIS) is the process by which β cells secrete insulin in response to glucose, measured in perifusion assays for MafAS64F/+ and control islets.&lt;SEP&gt;A key functional process in β cells activated by MafA, representing β cell maturation and proper function.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-968f694e317648c82a07ee150e63adbd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5afc163e9261bd9f96c6156bfdb27585&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-427bdb72b4ec16ac96774e76f03ada77&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5f38c4d8fe95ae0a2b5cc05069361348&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63a4c12087ceb7cec876e14e7fc45727&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce67306159c306b2c966577061cee6bd</data>
  <data key="d4">MafB Is Important for Pancreatic β-Cell Maintenance under a MafA-Deficient Condition.&lt;SEP&gt;Sex-biased islet β cell dysfunction is caused by the MODY MAFA S64F variant by inducing premature aging and senescence in males.&lt;SEP&gt;Species-specific roles for the MAFA and MAFB transcription factors in regulating islet β cell identity.</data>
  <data key="d5">1778562875</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
  <data key="d8">Insulin / Pancreatic Islets / A0B0 Mice</data>
  <data key="d9">0.00026667</data>
  <data key="d10">0.00022817</data>
  <data key="d11">0.01318378</data>
</node>
<node id="Fasting Hyperglycemia">
  <data key="d0">Fasting Hyperglycemia</data>
  <data key="d1">Biological Process</data>
  <data key="d2">Fasting hyperglycemia is a condition of elevated blood glucose levels during fasting, observed as a phenotype in MafA-deficient adult mice.&lt;SEP&gt;Fasting hyperglycemia is an overt condition seen in humans carrying the MAFAS64F variant but not manifested in heterozygous MafAS64F/+ male mice.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-968f694e317648c82a07ee150e63adbd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b39885796d53f3f69a4452a58c07c2d</data>
  <data key="d4">MafB Is Important for Pancreatic β-Cell Maintenance under a MafA-Deficient Condition.&lt;SEP&gt;Sex-biased islet β cell dysfunction is caused by the MODY MAFA S64F variant by inducing premature aging and senescence in males.</data>
  <data key="d5">1778562687</data>
