<node id="High-Fat Diet">
  <data key="d0">High-Fat Diet</data>
  <data key="d1">Biological Process</data>
  <data key="d2">High-fat diet (HFD) is a dietary treatment used experimentally; A0B0 mice became more vulnerable to diabetes under HFD treatment, showing impaired islet formation and decreased insulin+ β cells.&lt;SEP&gt;A high-fat diet is used in rodent models to study β-cell adaptive and maladaptive mechanisms, weight cycling effects, and progression toward diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;High-fat diet is a dietary intervention proposed as a model of insulin resistance in mice, suggested for future temporal studies of GAST+ gene signature induction alongside S961 treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;High-fat diet (HFD) is a well-established dietary model and intervention widely used in experimental mouse research to investigate metabolic dysfunction, pancreatic biology, and related cellular processes.

As a dietary model, the high-fat diet is primarily employed to induce insulin resistance and obesity in mice, most commonly in C57BL/6J strains. It causes increased caloric intake and serves as a metabolic challenge, leading to conditions such as glucose intolerance and metabolic stress. When combined with streptozotocin, HFD is also used to create mouse models of type 2 diabetes mellitus, making it a versatile tool for studying the pathophysiology of metabolic disease.

A significant focus of HFD research involves its effects on pancreatic beta cells. Under HFD conditions, beta cells are expected to mount an adaptive proliferative response to compensate for elevated metabolic demand. However, studies have shown that beta cells subjected to caloric restriction (CR) exhibit compromised or impaired adaptive proliferation and expansion in response to HFD feeding, highlighting the role of prior nutritional status in beta cell plasticity. Additionally, HFD is used to study beta cell senescence, with researchers examining pancreatic cellular senescence markers in HFD-fed mouse models.

HFD has also been referenced in the context of intermittent fasting studies, where it serves as a comparison or challenge condition to assess whether intermittent fasting can maintain beta cell mass and function under metabolically stressful dietary circumstances. More broadly, HFD is utilized to study metabolic effects on pancreatic and other tissues, underscoring its broad applicability as a preclinical research tool for understanding obesity, insulin resistance, beta cell biology, and related pathological mechanisms.&lt;SEP&gt;A dietary model used to induce diabetes in which beta cell senescence is associated with impaired beta cell proliferation and insulin secretion.&lt;SEP&gt;Dietary intervention used to induce diabetic mouse models for studying beta cell senescence.&lt;SEP&gt;Dietary intervention using 55% KCal from fat (Envigo TD.93075) fed to male C57BL/6J mice for 1 and 8 weeks to induce metabolic stress&lt;SEP&gt;Dietary intervention used in mouse models to study beta-cell adaptive and maladaptive mechanisms and islet cell subpopulation metabolic adaptation.&lt;SEP&gt;Dietary condition (HFD) inducing metabolic stress that increases p53-mediated apoptotic DDR in beta cells and alters DDR programs in replicating islet cells.&lt;SEP&gt;Mouse model of metabolic stress (HFD) used to study stress-induced impairment of beta-cell DNA repair.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4e0ae079210c3ef99872d0747c5a9b88&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d1c90235486a0fe738831a720e1f94ab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b13f08985b48653da8be9b63098bbb2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-58ad905d1d148d4bbfe7ce4c29566fc6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b773584b36e5b4845bedffea9a1b6add&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d7ef738c0840825512b2cb7af5b7c3f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f25c34949789593e96b7a57ead73f11&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2e4a544176811f5b43952b185e1ed3a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6cadc21c6ca916dd06510987c1b7dbf4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-75f39153d9f864070e17a74724a6c8c6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-363f3a19905f833d29a7d1242acc6641&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0178968ab91760930c812723c60d342b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d286ee457150be65228790e800b5207b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64b61717ec6764bc92fa7c3c5067d345&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ce4f6e2d90d0c06e4549d7d45037298&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-15ab370ab273e97005ced113e59cc48a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce72a72ed1aaea72aac97c28374f8f86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e953ac093714735fa9b5b27463bf5dff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-35d7a41162ea60151fe17b4e60e06d1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6204b07313b33d741c243f18ce86735</data>
  <data key="d4">MafB Is Important for Pancreatic β-Cell Maintenance under a MafA-Deficient Condition.&lt;SEP&gt;Species-specific roles for the MAFA and MAFB transcription factors in regulating islet β cell identity.</data>
  <data key="d5">1778562874</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">23</data>
