  <data key="d1">Protein</data>
  <data key="d2">MSR1 is a receptor involved in clearance of damage signals; MAFB prevents excess inflammation after ischemic stroke by accelerating clearance through MSR1.&lt;SEP&gt;Macrophage scavenger receptor 1; MAFB accelerates clearance of damage signals through MSR1 to prevent excess inflammation after ischemic stroke.&lt;SEP&gt;MSR1 is a scavenger receptor whose expression is regulated by MAFB, contributing to macrophage phagocytic function.</data>
