  <data key="d2">The insulin promoter is a regulatory DNA sequence through which MafA contributes to specific transcriptional activity for insulin gene expression.&lt;SEP&gt;Regulatory DNA region controlling insulin gene expression; bound by NEUROD1 upon stimulation by extranuclear estrogen receptor alpha.</data>
