<node id="p16Ink4a">
  <data key="d0">p16Ink4a</data>
  <data key="d1">Protein</data>
  <data key="d2">A cyclin-dependent kinase inhibitor and senescence marker; p16Ink4a-positive senescent cells affect lifespan, and their clearance delays aging-associated disorders.&lt;SEP&gt;p16Ink4a is a cyclin-dependent kinase inhibitor involved in mediating senescence-associated stable growth arrest.&lt;SEP&gt;Cyclin-dependent kinase inhibitor p16, frequently upregulated in senescent beta cells; antibody specificity in mouse is often nonspecific.&lt;SEP&gt;p16Ink4a (encoded by CDKN2A) is a cyclin-dependent kinase inhibitor serving as a marker for senescent cells in vivo, marking a distinct subpopulation of senescent beta cells.&lt;SEP&gt;Cyclin-dependent kinase inhibitor p16, frequently upregulated in senescent beta cells; antibody specificity in mouse is often nonspecific.&lt;SEP&gt;p16Ink4a (encoded by CDKN2A) is a cyclin-dependent kinase inhibitor serving as a marker for senescent cells in vivo, marking a distinct subpopulation of senescent beta cells.&lt;SEP&gt;P16INK4A is a cyclin-dependent kinase (CDK) inhibitor encoded at the CDKN2A locus (also referred to as the Cdkn2a locus in murine contexts). It is widely recognized as a major driver of cellular senescence across a broad range of cell types, with its role established through studies on fibroblast senescence, genetic knockout mouse models, and cancer research.

P16INK4A serves as a well-established senescence marker, and p16INK4A-positive senescent cells are known to accumulate progressively during aging. Notably, its expression increases with age in both humans and mice, particularly within pancreatic beta cells. This age-related upregulation is associated with limited regenerative capacity in beta cells, as P16INK4A functions as an inhibitor of beta cell proliferation. Beyond its role in proliferative control, P16INK4A also plays roles in beta cell function and the induction and maintenance of beta cell senescence.

In the context of experimental and therapeutic research, the P16INK4A gene promoter has been utilized to drive the INK-ATTAC transgene, a system in which senescent beta cells expressing P16INK4A can be selectively targeted for removal either genetically or pharmacologically. This approach underscores the importance of P16INK4A not only as a biological marker and mediator of senescence but also as a molecular tool for investigating the consequences of senescent cell clearance on aging, beta cell regeneration, and metabolic function.&lt;SEP&gt;A key cell cycle arrest regulator involved in modulation of senescence, targeted by miRNAs.&lt;SEP&gt;Cyclin-dependent kinase inhibitor that induces senescence in pancreatic beta cells and enhances insulin secretion.&lt;SEP&gt;CDK inhibitor protein encoded by CDKN2A, upregulated in senescent beta cells; marker of cell cycle arrest.&lt;SEP&gt;CDK inhibitor protein encoded by CDKN2A, upregulated in senescent beta cells; marker of cell cycle arrest.&lt;SEP&gt;Protein encoded by CDKN2A; involved in senescence pathways and targeted by beta cell EV miRNAs.&lt;SEP&gt;A key regulator of cellular senescence that cooperates with the Rb pathway to enforce irreversible cell cycle arrest.&lt;SEP&gt;A cyclin-dependent kinase inhibitor and marker of cellular senescence, expressed in peripheral blood T-cells as a biomarker of human aging, also induced in macrophages and involved in AML-driven senescence.&lt;SEP&gt;p16INK4a (encoded by CDKN2A) is a cyclin-dependent kinase inhibitor expressed in senescent cells; naturally occurring p16INK4a-positive cells shorten healthy lifespan and sentinel p16INK4a+ cells in the basement membrane form a reparative niche.&lt;SEP&gt;p16INK4a is a key senescence biomarker expressed in sentinel cells in basement membranes and associated with lung repair, emphysema, and bone loss.&lt;SEP&gt;A senescence and aging biomarker used in a luciferase model to monitor tumorigenesis and senescence in vivo; expression is a biomarker of aging.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3f64af938dff7c5f186bd7024d92cbc0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea9634b81ecdb467a2b26648246e5b5c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5dc00b5dc127eca5ff2847cc45392453&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-add59972a262992e4bde6910520c0cdb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b861cee193cad9e0f142051047e83aae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-58c0cbc7de7a8a1060e8f1608271a28c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c72c144fce7d5c94557af956a559639&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ef7d4c1829099c6037d8b8b7a83c3cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fac258601b299e0c883e8e1c4a3030d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1628eba511291c52eab3e72ef0fd0239&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-15ab370ab273e97005ced113e59cc48a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-58ad905d1d148d4bbfe7ce4c29566fc6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6215695e8bd809fd02cb8b9b7b4123ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-71a6a7a3a4894dbd7d979b7e5766d5a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea13fe99fbc01cb6036ecddcda0aae8a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c5a8121875c37f2659ae345688f6afe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b02375738a9ebacd53446fec2077ee76&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf5aeca434044079720fd4ae2d32c9b9</data>
  <data key="d4">Stress-induced β cell early senescence confers protection against type 1 diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Sex-biased islet β cell dysfunction is caused by the MODY MAFA S64F variant by inducing premature aging and senescence in males.&lt;SEP&gt;Pancreatic β-cell senescence in diabetes: mechanisms, markers and therapies.</data>
  <data key="d5">1778566594</data>
