<node id="Senescence-Associated Secretory Phenotype (SASP)">
  <data key="d0">Senescence-Associated Secretory Phenotype (SASP)</data>
  <data key="d1">Biological Process</data>
  <data key="d2">SASP is a cellular phenotype associated with senescence, observed in male MafAS64F/+ islet β cells and in the EndoC-βH2 human β cell line expressing MAFA S64F, capable of inducing senescence in a cell non-autonomous manner.&lt;SEP&gt;The secretory profile of senescent cells, considered the dark side of tumor suppression, involving pro-inflammatory factors.&lt;SEP&gt;A secretory phenotype adopted by senescent cells that induces cellular plasticity, tissue regeneration, and immune modulation.&lt;SEP&gt;SASP is a complex and dynamic secretome consisting of growth factors, cytokines, chemokines, and other factors produced by senescent cells; it elicits immune surveillance and can contribute to tissue dysfunction when immune clearance is compromised.&lt;SEP&gt;A bioactive secretome produced by senescent cells, including those overexpressing p21, that places stressed cells under immunosurveillance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3f64af938dff7c5f186bd7024d92cbc0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-427bdb72b4ec16ac96774e76f03ada77&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea9634b81ecdb467a2b26648246e5b5c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d13aa78bf917b6b3ed2e772b6f010e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18ba6ed2ada6acd593e0a5d2f036f947</data>
  <data key="d4">Stress-induced β cell early senescence confers protection against type 1 diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Sex-biased islet β cell dysfunction is caused by the MODY MAFA S64F variant by inducing premature aging and senescence in males.</data>
  <data key="d5">1778564576</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">3</data>
  <data key="d8">cellular senescence / CDKN2A / CDKN1A</data>
  <data key="d9">0.00025839</data>
  <data key="d10">0.00011249</data>
  <data key="d11">0.01131949</data>
</node>
<node id="ABT263">
  <data key="d0">ABT263</data>
  <data key="d1">Drug</data>
  <data key="d2">A senolytic compound whose clearance of senescent cells rejuvenates aged hematopoietic stem cells in mice.&lt;SEP&gt;Senolytic drug that clears senescent cells and rejuvenates aged hematopoietic stem cells in mice.&lt;SEP&gt;Senolytic drug that clears senescent cells and rejuvenates aged hematopoietic stem cells in mice.&lt;SEP&gt;Senolytic compound that clears senescent cells to rejuvenate aged hematopoietic stem cells and improve survival after myocardial infarction.&lt;SEP&gt;Senolytic drug that clears senescent cells and rejuvenates aged hematopoietic stem cells in mice.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3f64af938dff7c5f186bd7024d92cbc0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c72c144fce7d5c94557af956a559639&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c5a8121875c37f2659ae345688f6afe</data>
