<node id="Lamin B1">
  <data key="d0">Lamin B1</data>
  <data key="d1">Protein</data>
  <data key="d2">A nuclear lamina protein whose loss serves as a senescence-associated biomarker.&lt;SEP&gt;Nuclear lamina protein whose loss is a hallmark of aging beta cells.&lt;SEP&gt;Nuclear lamina protein encoded by LAMNB1, serving as a beta cell aging marker with reduced expression under CR.&lt;SEP&gt;Nuclear lamina protein whose loss is a senescence-associated biomarker.&lt;SEP&gt;Nuclear lamina protein whose loss is a senescence-associated biomarker.&lt;SEP&gt;Nuclear lamina protein whose depletion in senescent cells triggers large-scale changes in gene expression and chromatin landscape.&lt;SEP&gt;Nuclear lamina protein detected by immunohistochemistry, used as a marker in pancreatic tissue sections.&lt;SEP&gt;A biomarker used to quantify cellular senescence in photoaged skin; its loss is associated with photoaging.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3f64af938dff7c5f186bd7024d92cbc0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68a87a3a1f3eb5d8b0e53b41df492512&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-364a12c675ebfd67c468ab6fc47e6696&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c72c144fce7d5c94557af956a559639&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b02375738a9ebacd53446fec2077ee76&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6cadc21c6ca916dd06510987c1b7dbf4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf5aeca434044079720fd4ae2d32c9b9</data>
