<node id="Oxidative Stress">
  <data key="d0">Oxidative Stress</data>
  <data key="d1">Biological Process</data>
  <data key="d2">Oxidative stress is a condition to which MAFA is particularly sensitive, alongside glucotoxic conditions, potentially affecting β cell function.&lt;SEP&gt;A condition mediating post-translational loss of MafA protein as a contributing mechanism to loss of insulin gene expression in glucotoxic beta cells.&lt;SEP&gt;Oxidative stress is a mechanism contributing to the post-translational loss of MafA protein and loss of insulin gene expression in glucotoxic beta cells, and is also linked to chronic glucose toxicity in type 2 diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Oxidative stress is a cellular condition that reduces MAFA and MAFB protein levels and is associated with T2D islet pathology.&lt;SEP&gt;A condition of cellular stress involving reactive oxygen species, against which the integrated stress response confers resistance through regulation of amino acid metabolism.&lt;SEP&gt;Oxidative stress is a condition characterized by an imbalance between the production of reactive oxygen species (ROS) and the body's antioxidant defense mechanisms, resulting in excess ROS accumulation that causes widespread cellular damage across multiple biological systems.

One of the key consequences of oxidative stress is the induction of cellular senescence. It has been identified as a driver of senescence-induced endothelial dysfunction and has been observed to induce senescence in vascular endothelial cells and other cell types. In the context of chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD), oxidative stress-induced senescence can be attenuated by erythromycin through modulation of the PI3K-mTOR signaling pathway. Oxidative stress-induced senescence has also been documented in mature, post-mature, and pathological human placentas, and stress conditions including radiation have been shown to recapitulate features of age-associated senescence in the mouse brain. Furthermore, oxidative stress can act as a stress stimulus that triggers nucleolar stress and beta cell senescence via DNA damage response (DDR) activation, and ROS can activate ATM independently of double-strand breaks (DSBs), potentially serving as an upstream trigger of nucleolar stress in beta cells.

Oxidative stress plays a significant role in pancreatic beta cell biology. Beta cells are particularly vulnerable to ROS accumulation due to their inherently limited capacity to handle oxidative stress, making them susceptible to DNA damage, increased DNA damage burden, and functional impairment relevant to metabolic diseases such as diabetes. Loss of CALCOCO2, which impairs mitophagic flux in beta cells, has been identified as a condition that promotes oxidative stress. Elevated levels of FABP4 and GPX3 serve as cellular markers reflecting oxidative stress in beta cells, and this stress state is associated with declining insulin secretion.

Several therapeutic interventions have been identified as capable of mitigating oxidative stress in beta cells. SGLT2 inhibitors have been shown to reduce oxidative stress in beta cells, thereby contributing to preserved beta cell function. Dietary restriction (DR) and caloric restriction (CR) also mitigate oxidative stress; under CR conditions, ROS accumulation in beta cells is reduced through enhanced bioenergetics and improved ROS scavenging mechanisms, helping preserve beta cell mass and function in diabetic animal models. These findings underscore the therapeutic relevance of targeting oxidative stress to maintain metabolic health.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3f64af938dff7c5f186bd7024d92cbc0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-74fc4f55c8c6d83ebd1d8dba07d90692&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbe530a83d027293c37b530e3c376973&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b13f08985b48653da8be9b63098bbb2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d13aa78bf917b6b3ed2e772b6f010e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d3b1de44d6b73a10793a43351e18e6e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea13fe99fbc01cb6036ecddcda0aae8a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c5a8121875c37f2659ae345688f6afe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf5aeca434044079720fd4ae2d32c9b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-58f0193e389064a60d513f13c5cad52b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-72bf1fbaf7a329c364247108f8b30408&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-364a12c675ebfd67c468ab6fc47e6696&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-002f23b1d29df711e839459b4d6f0711&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f63ca40b092870f725a75e7a36045d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4e8cbb766d17c90c84d2a9452a51a41e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-044fb2d3ececa99a53eb87d2ee6bf18f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8f09e5d1418f8ae04b43a24b97c1d52d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93bb74bfaf0604b4b9f891e16fc9f0ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ce4f6e2d90d0c06e4549d7d45037298&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-15ab370ab273e97005ced113e59cc48a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28a44d52c17c29e9741a935aa76e8afe</data>
