<node id="MAFAWT">
  <data key="d0">MAFAWT</data>
  <data key="d1">Protein</data>
  <data key="d2">The wild-type form of the MAFA transcription factor, used as a reference in comparisons with the MAFAS64F variant in human β cells.&lt;SEP&gt;MAFAWT is the wild-type human MAFA protein used as a control in EndoC-βH2 cell transduction experiments.&lt;SEP&gt;MAFAWT is the wild-type form of the MAFA protein, normally unstable with a half-life of approximately 30 minutes, used as a control in experiments comparing MAFAS64F effects.&lt;SEP&gt;MAFAWT is the wild-type form of the MAFA gene used as a control in transfection experiments with Human EndoC-βH2 cells.&lt;SEP&gt;MAFAWT is the wild-type form of the MAFA transcription factor expressed in EndoC-βH2 cells, serving as a control in conditioned media and immunostaining experiments.&lt;SEP&gt;Wild-type MAFA protein used as reference in phosphorylation site substitution modeling studies; all phosphorylation sites replaced with phosphomimetic residues (S→D, T→E).</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-68488f40a0b43cd31dd09cb8c1939a9a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc527b8db70f9b6c3c8648c4a33df392&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5f38c4d8fe95ae0a2b5cc05069361348&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b3deb83588a816faad5340f542e1f43&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9977f67772ceb665bdd71b221a2d4234&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19fff7a7048ab7112926e25c2e46450b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eae638e9cabe91a68fc062c9981b0e86</data>
  <data key="d4">Sex-biased islet β cell dysfunction is caused by the MODY MAFA S64F variant by inducing premature aging and senescence in males.&lt;SEP&gt;Defining unique structural features in the MAFA and MAFB transcription factors that control Insulin gene activity.</data>
  <data key="d5">1778569802</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">0</data>
  <data key="d8">beta cell / MAFA / MAFB</data>
  <data key="d9">0.00021255</data>
  <data key="d10">1.039e-05</data>
  <data key="d11">0.00858595</data>
</node>
<node id="Islet β Cell">
  <data key="d0">Islet β Cell</data>
  <data key="d1">Organism</data>
  <data key="d2">Islet β cells are pancreatic cells responsible for insulin secretion and glucose homeostasis, whose function and gene expression are altered by the MafAS64F mutation in a sex-dependent manner.&lt;SEP&gt;Islet β cells are pancreatic cells responsible for insulin secretion and glucose regulation, whose gene expression and function are altered by the MafAS64F mutation.&lt;SEP&gt;Islet β cells are insulin-secreting cells in the pancreatic islets of Langerhans, regulated by transcription factors such as MafA, MafB, Pdx1, and Nkx6.1, and responsible for glucose-stimulated insulin secretion (GSIS).</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-df94a97c87154646f3ffd59dd4b312d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63a4c12087ceb7cec876e14e7fc45727&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-74fc4f55c8c6d83ebd1d8dba07d90692</data>
  <data key="d4">Sex-biased islet β cell dysfunction is caused by the MODY MAFA S64F variant by inducing premature aging and senescence in males.</data>
  <data key="d5">1778562653</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">31</data>
  <data key="d8">islet / pancreas / snATAC-seq</data>
  <data key="d9">0.00034377</data>
  <data key="d10">0.00084917</data>
  <data key="d11">0.02035403</data>
</node>
<node id="RNA Sequencing">
  <data key="d0">RNA Sequencing</data>
  <data key="d1">Method</data>
  <data key="d2">Bulk RNA sequencing (RNA-seq) is a method used to measure gene expression in isolated islets from WT and MafAS64F/+ mice to identify differentially expressed genes.&lt;SEP&gt;RNA sequencing is a method used to obtain transcriptomic data from Atf6β−/− and Ire1αβ−/− mice to identify PASP markers.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-df94a97c87154646f3ffd59dd4b312d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c3838ae3de5236c272eda0072cc83f4e</data>
  <data key="d4">Stress-induced β cell early senescence confers protection against type 1 diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Sex-biased islet β cell dysfunction is caused by the MODY MAFA S64F variant by inducing premature aging and senescence in males.</data>
  <data key="d5">1778564605</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">23</data>
  <data key="d8">Type 2 Diabetes / Insulin Resistance / High-Fat Diet</data>
  <data key="d9">0.0001709</data>
  <data key="d10">0.00035816</data>
  <data key="d11">0.00126955</data>
</node>
<node id="Differentially Expressed Genes">
  <data key="d0">Differentially Expressed Genes</data>
  <data key="d1">Data</data>
  <data key="d2">Differentially expressed genes (DEGs) are genes with significantly altered expression levels; female heterozygous islets had 736 DEGs and male islets had 2,410 DEGs compared to their respective WT controls.&lt;SEP&gt;698 differentially expressed genes were identified between Atf6β−/− and Atf6fl/fl β-cells through RNA-seq and EdgeR analysis at FDR &lt;0.05.&lt;SEP&gt;Genes showing differential expression between groups (e.g., sex, disease state) in islet cells, including autosomal and sex chromosome genes.&lt;SEP&gt;Genes showing significant expression differences between T2D and non-diabetic donors, or between sexes, in islet cell types.&lt;SEP&gt;DEGs identified in beta and alpha cells from T2D donors with sex-specific differences in autosomal and sex chromosome genes.&lt;SEP&gt;DEGs identified by comparing transcriptional profiles of male vs. female, and T2D vs. non-diabetic islet cells.&lt;SEP&gt;Genes showing differential expression in T2D vs. non-diabetic comparisons, with females exhibiting more DEGs than males in both beta and alpha cells&lt;SEP&gt;Genes showing differential expression between MafaS64F/+ and MafaWT males, identified by bulk RNAseq; fewer DEGs in C57 background males.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-df94a97c87154646f3ffd59dd4b312d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c625d74e06abff522b8eb3d76df6ae32&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe5b7d8c678cb311e300af3b74f19ed6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd3982c3cb7b00162818de82027a853e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76049b85888e8e904e7c01de9740d34f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5cd7041acf7539c8db67413bcd98f41b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2efc110efa119e343b95df1abbd0a327&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0386e6a8316aca2a67c3466442e7e1fa</data>
  <data key="d4">Stress-induced β cell early senescence confers protection against type 1 diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Sex-biased islet β cell dysfunction is caused by the MODY MAFA S64F variant by inducing premature aging and senescence in males.</data>
  <data key="d5">1778564602</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">23</data>
  <data key="d8">Type 2 Diabetes / Insulin Resistance / High-Fat Diet</data>
  <data key="d9">0.00068512</data>
  <data key="d10">0.00286422</data>
  <data key="d11">0.03678223</data>
</node>
