</node>
<node id="MafAS64F/+ Male Islets">
  <data key="d0">MafAS64F/+ Male Islets</data>
  <data key="d1">Tissue</data>
  <data key="d2">Pancreatic islets isolated from male MafAS64F heterozygous mice, characterized by 2,410 DEGs, blunted Ca2+ entry in response to glucose, reduced KCl-induced Ca2+ influx, and upregulation of senescence and aging pathway genes.&lt;SEP&gt;MafAS64F/+ male islets are pancreatic islets from male mice carrying the MafAS64F variant, characterized by accumulation of senescent cells and a rate of β cell senescence comparable to human T2D.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-df94a97c87154646f3ffd59dd4b312d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b39885796d53f3f69a4452a58c07c2d</data>
  <data key="d4">Sex-biased islet β cell dysfunction is caused by the MODY MAFA S64F variant by inducing premature aging and senescence in males.</data>
  <data key="d5">1778562654</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">34</data>
  <data key="d8">Male MafAS64F/+ Islets / MafAS64F/+ Male Islets / Senescent Cells</data>
  <data key="d9">0.00064705</data>
  <data key="d10">0.00250267</data>
  <data key="d11">0.02003156</data>
</node>
<node id="MafAS64F/+ Female Islets">
  <data key="d0">MafAS64F/+ Female Islets</data>
  <data key="d1">Tissue</data>
  <data key="d2">Pancreatic islets isolated from female MafAS64F heterozygous mice, characterized by 736 DEGs, two distinct Ca2+ responsive populations (responders and non-responders), and greater KCl-induced Ca2+ influx compared to WT female islets.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-df94a97c87154646f3ffd59dd4b312d0</data>
  <data key="d4">Sex-biased islet β cell dysfunction is caused by the MODY MAFA S64F variant by inducing premature aging and senescence in males.</data>
  <data key="d5">1778562654</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">34</data>
  <data key="d8">Male MafAS64F/+ Islets / MafAS64F/+ Male Islets / Senescent Cells</data>
  <data key="d9">0.00040039</data>
  <data key="d10">0.00068616</data>
  <data key="d11">0.00465175</data>
</node>
<node id="Wild Type (WT) Islets">
  <data key="d0">Wild Type (WT) Islets</data>
  <data key="d1">Tissue</data>
  <data key="d2">Pancreatic islets isolated from wild type mice, used as a control for comparison with MafAS64F/+ islets in gene expression and Ca2+ handling studies.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-df94a97c87154646f3ffd59dd4b312d0</data>
  <data key="d4">Sex-biased islet β cell dysfunction is caused by the MODY MAFA S64F variant by inducing premature aging and senescence in males.</data>
  <data key="d5">1778562654</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">34</data>
  <data key="d8">Male MafAS64F/+ Islets / MafAS64F/+ Male Islets / Senescent Cells</data>
  <data key="d9">0.00013063</data>
  <data key="d10">3.1e-07</data>
  <data key="d11">0.0008508</data>
</node>
<node id="Glucose-Stimulated Calcium Response">
  <data key="d0">Glucose-Stimulated Calcium Response</data>
  <data key="d1">Biological Process</data>
  <data key="d2">The elevation of cytoplasmic Ca2+ in response to glucose stimulation in islet β cells, which mediates insulin release; this response is blunted in MafAS64F/+ islets.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-df94a97c87154646f3ffd59dd4b312d0</data>
  <data key="d4">Sex-biased islet β cell dysfunction is caused by the MODY MAFA S64F variant by inducing premature aging and senescence in males.</data>
  <data key="d5">1778562654</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">34</data>
  <data key="d8">Male MafAS64F/+ Islets / MafAS64F/+ Male Islets / Senescent Cells</data>
  <data key="d9">0.00025142</data>
  <data key="d10">0.00036498</data>
  <data key="d11">0.00100195</data>
</node>
<node id="KCl-Induced Depolarization">
  <data key="d0">KCl-Induced Depolarization</data>
  <data key="d1">Method</data>
  <data key="d2">KCl-mediated depolarization is used to assess Ca2+ influx in islets; male MafAS64F/+ islets show reduced response while female MafAS64F/+ islets show greater response compared to WT controls.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-df94a97c87154646f3ffd59dd4b312d0</data>
  <data key="d4">Sex-biased islet β cell dysfunction is caused by the MODY MAFA S64F variant by inducing premature aging and senescence in males.</data>
  <data key="d5">1778562654</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">34</data>
  <data key="d8">Male MafAS64F/+ Islets / MafAS64F/+ Male Islets / Senescent Cells</data>
  <data key="d9">0.00013063</data>
  <data key="d10">3.1e-07</data>
  <data key="d11">0.0008508</data>
</node>
<node id="Insulin Release">
  <data key="d0">Insulin Release</data>
  <data key="d1">Biological Process</data>
  <data key="d2">Insulin release is mediated by glucose-induced elevations of cytoplasmic Ca2+ in β cells, and is impaired in MafAS64F/+ islets due to altered Ca2+ handling.&lt;SEP&gt;Process of insulin secretion from beta cells; associated with molecules enriched in CR islets such as cAMP and cyclic ADP-ribose.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-df94a97c87154646f3ffd59dd4b312d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68a87a3a1f3eb5d8b0e53b41df492512</data>
  <data key="d4">Sex-biased islet β cell dysfunction is caused by the MODY MAFA S64F variant by inducing premature aging and senescence in males.</data>
  <data key="d5">1778562654</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">14</data>
  <data key="d8">caloric restriction / autophagy / beta cell state 2</data>
  <data key="d9">0.00020942</data>
  <data key="d10">0.00012468</data>
  <data key="d11">0.00435084</data>
</node>
<node id="Fasting Hypoglycemia">
  <data key="d0">Fasting Hypoglycemia</data>
  <data key="d1">Biological Process</data>
  <data key="d2">Fasting hypoglycemia is observed in female MafAS64F/+ mice, consistent with greater baseline Ca2+ levels and increased fasting insulin levels in female MafAS64F/+ islets.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-df94a97c87154646f3ffd59dd4b312d0</data>
  <data key="d4">Sex-biased islet β cell dysfunction is caused by the MODY MAFA S64F variant by inducing premature aging and senescence in males.</data>
  <data key="d5">1778562654</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">34</data>
  <data key="d8">Male MafAS64F/+ Islets / MafAS64F/+ Male Islets / Senescent Cells</data>
  <data key="d9">8.491e-05</data>
  <data key="d10">0.0</data>
  <data key="d11">0.00016033</data>
</node>
<node id="Pulsatile Insulin Secretion">
  <data key="d0">Pulsatile Insulin Secretion</data>
  <data key="d1">Biological Process</data>
  <data key="d2">Pulsatile insulin secretion is driven by glucose-stimulated Ca2+ oscillatory patterns in islets, which are significantly diminished in MafAS64F/+ islets.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-df94a97c87154646f3ffd59dd4b312d0</data>
  <data key="d4">Sex-biased islet β cell dysfunction is caused by the MODY MAFA S64F variant by inducing premature aging and senescence in males.</data>
  <data key="d5">1778562654</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">34</data>
  <data key="d8">Male MafAS64F/+ Islets / MafAS64F/+ Male Islets / Senescent Cells</data>
  <data key="d9">9.005e-05</data>
  <data key="d10">0.0</data>
  <data key="d11">3.453e-05</data>
</node>
<node id="Metabolic Pathway Genes">
  <data key="d0">Metabolic Pathway Genes</data>
  <data key="d1">Data</data>
  <data key="d2">Metabolic pathway genes implicated in cellular aging and senescence are upregulated in 5-week-old male MafAS64F/+ islets as revealed by RNA-seq data.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-df94a97c87154646f3ffd59dd4b312d0</data>
  <data key="d4">Sex-biased islet β cell dysfunction is caused by the MODY MAFA S64F variant by inducing premature aging and senescence in males.</data>
