  <data key="d10">3.1e-07</data>
  <data key="d11">0.0008508</data>
</node>
<node id="Voltage-Dependent Ca2+ Channel Genes">
  <data key="d0">Voltage-Dependent Ca2+ Channel Genes</data>
  <data key="d1">Data</data>
  <data key="d2">Voltage-dependent Ca2+ channel genes are specifically upregulated in male MafAS64F/+ islets, contributing to sex-specific changes in ion influx.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-df94a97c87154646f3ffd59dd4b312d0</data>
  <data key="d4">Sex-biased islet β cell dysfunction is caused by the MODY MAFA S64F variant by inducing premature aging and senescence in males.</data>
