</node>
<node id="β Cell Mass">
  <data key="d0">β Cell Mass</data>
  <data key="d1">Biological Process</data>
  <data key="d2">β cell mass refers to the total population of insulin-producing β cells; only roughly 20% of β cell mass is thought to be required to maintain glucose tolerance, allowing female MafAS64F/+ responder islets to compensate for non-responders.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-df94a97c87154646f3ffd59dd4b312d0</data>
  <data key="d4">Sex-biased islet β cell dysfunction is caused by the MODY MAFA S64F variant by inducing premature aging and senescence in males.</data>
  <data key="d5">1778562656</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">14</data>
  <data key="d8">caloric restriction / autophagy / beta cell state 2</data>
  <data key="d9">7.287e-05</data>
