  <data key="d11">0.00044947</data>
</node>
<node id="SA-β-gal Staining">
  <data key="d0">SA-β-gal Staining</data>
  <data key="d1">Method</data>
  <data key="d2">SA-β-gal (senescence-associated beta-galactosidase) staining is a marker used to detect cellular senescence, which was not induced in 4-week-old MafAS64F/+ β cells.&lt;SEP&gt;Senescence-associated β-galactosidase staining performed at pH 6.0 to detect cellular senescence in pancreatic cryosections.&lt;SEP&gt;SA-β-gal (senescence-associated beta-galactosidase) staining is a method used to detect cellular senescence activity, performed at pH 6.0 and developed for 18 hours at 37°C in tissue sections or 2-3 hours in cultured cells.&lt;SEP&gt;SA-β-gal staining is a marker assay for senescence-associated β-galactosidase activity, used to assess senescence in MafAS64F/+ islets.&lt;SEP&gt;Histochemical method used to detect senescent cells via senescence-associated beta-galactosidase activity.&lt;SEP&gt;Senescence-Associated beta-galactosidase staining used to identify and quantify senescent cells.&lt;SEP&gt;Senescence-associated beta-galactosidase staining used to assess cellular senescence following experimental treatments.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fc527b8db70f9b6c3c8648c4a33df392&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82e08f93585dc5d50ccfbac2feb8d206&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b39885796d53f3f69a4452a58c07c2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa2caaffb8c37fe000f2af35e115fc27&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ce1a7b385e0f22ca823c850de9bf8a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af17b436ff0aa3dd562bbc7e986cc909&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f082082b0871749ee637b1571aa95c0</data>
  <data key="d4">Sex-biased islet β cell dysfunction is caused by the MODY MAFA S64F variant by inducing premature aging and senescence in males.</data>
  <data key="d5">1778562656</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
  <data key="d8">Insulin / Pancreatic Islets / A0B0 Mice</data>
  <data key="d9">0.00057368</data>
  <data key="d10">0.00421663</data>
  <data key="d11">0.008511</data>
</node>
<node id="MafAS64F/+ Mice">
  <data key="d0">MafAS64F/+ Mice</data>
  <data key="d1">Organism</data>
  <data key="d2">MafAS64F/+ mice are a mouse model developed to study the human MAFAS64F variant, exhibiting sex-biased outcomes including glucose intolerance in males and improved glucose clearance with hypoglycemia in females.&lt;SEP&gt;A genetically modified mouse model used in studies of islet function, perifusion analysis, immunostaining, RNA sequencing, and calcium imaging.&lt;SEP&gt;MafAS64F/+ mice are a genetically modified mouse model used in experiments to study pancreatic and metabolic phenotypes compared to wild-type mice.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fc527b8db70f9b6c3c8648c4a33df392&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82e08f93585dc5d50ccfbac2feb8d206&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b3deb83588a816faad5340f542e1f43</data>
  <data key="d4">Sex-biased islet β cell dysfunction is caused by the MODY MAFA S64F variant by inducing premature aging and senescence in males.</data>
  <data key="d5">1778562657</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
  <data key="d8">Insulin / Pancreatic Islets / A0B0 Mice</data>
  <data key="d9">0.00048212</data>
  <data key="d10">0.00109369</data>
  <data key="d11">0.00653851</data>
</node>
<node id="Pancreata">
  <data key="d0">Pancreata</data>
  <data key="d1">Tissue</data>
  <data key="d2">Pancreata from WT and MafAS64F/+ mice were snap frozen in O.C.T. and cryosectioned at 16 μm thickness for SA-β-gal staining and insulin immunostaining.&lt;SEP&gt;Pancreata refers to the pancreatic tissue in which reduced M1 and increased M2 macrophage populations were observed in UPR-deficient mice.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fc527b8db70f9b6c3c8648c4a33df392&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-353703794bc6a501b5c11f84a2064293</data>
  <data key="d4">Stress-induced β cell early senescence confers protection against type 1 diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Sex-biased islet β cell dysfunction is caused by the MODY MAFA S64F variant by inducing premature aging and senescence in males.</data>
  <data key="d5">1778564619</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
  <data key="d8">Insulin / Pancreatic Islets / A0B0 Mice</data>
  <data key="d9">0.00038553</data>
  <data key="d10">0.00178955</data>
  <data key="d11">0.00029442</data>
</node>
<node id="EndoC-βH2 Cells">
  <data key="d0">EndoC-βH2 Cells</data>
  <data key="d1">Organism</data>
  <data key="d2">EndoC-βH2 cells are human β cell lines used in experiments to study the effects of MAFAS64F expression on senescence, SASP factor secretion, and calcium channel gene expression.&lt;SEP&gt;EndoC-βH2 cells are human pancreatic β cell line in which MAFAS64F expression produced senescence and development of a functional SASP.&lt;SEP&gt;A human pancreatic β-cell line used for immunostaining of LaminB1, 53BP1, and p21, as well as quantitative real-time PCR analysis.&lt;SEP&gt;EndoC-βH2 is a human pancreatic beta cell line used in experiments to evaluate SA-β-gal activity, MAFA expression effects, and conditioned media assays.&lt;SEP&gt;EndoC-βH2 is a human pancreatic β cell line used to study MAFB's role in suppressing GAST induction.&lt;SEP&gt;EndoC-βH2 cells are human pancreatic beta cell line used in bulk RNA-Seq experiments and RNA isolation.&lt;SEP&gt;EndoC-βH2 cells are a biological sample used in the study, with associated RNA-Seq data deposited under accession GSE228992.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fc527b8db70f9b6c3c8648c4a33df392&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82e08f93585dc5d50ccfbac2feb8d206&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b3deb83588a816faad5340f542e1f43&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b39885796d53f3f69a4452a58c07c2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c914d24696d0f6e2087f40c21ca5649&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-46772cbd15b1e36b4aedeac0a06fd4de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4430aecbeab4b77ba9a003f3e96de5a0</data>
  <data key="d4">Sex-biased islet β cell dysfunction is caused by the MODY MAFA S64F variant by inducing premature aging and senescence in males.&lt;SEP&gt;Species-specific roles for the MAFA and MAFB transcription factors in regulating islet β cell identity.</data>
  <data key="d5">1778562861</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">0</data>
  <data key="d8">beta cell / MAFA / MAFB</data>
