<node id="Conditioned Media">
  <data key="d0">Conditioned Media</data>
  <data key="d1">Method</data>
  <data key="d2">Conditioned media (CM) collected from EndoC-βH2 cells expressing MAFAWT or MAFAS64F was applied to untransduced EndoC-βH2 cells to determine whether SASP factors are released by human cells expressing MAFAS64F.&lt;SEP&gt;Conditioned media (CM) produced after 24 hours of culture from MAFAS64F- and MAFAWT-expressing EndoC-βH2 cells, clarified by centrifugation and stored at 4°C for up to 3 weeks.&lt;SEP&gt;Conditioned media (CM) is collected from NIT1 cells after drug treatment, filtered with a 0.2μm filter, and used in transwell migration assays.&lt;SEP&gt;Culture medium conditioned by senescent cells enriched with secreted SASP proteins; used in paracrine assays to demonstrate biological activity of senescent beta cell SASP.&lt;SEP&gt;Culture medium conditioned by senescent cells enriched with secreted SASP proteins; used in paracrine assays to demonstrate biological activity of senescent beta cell SASP.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fc527b8db70f9b6c3c8648c4a33df392&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b3deb83588a816faad5340f542e1f43&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02c41952a3f79a76f3315858bb8a14bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-58c0cbc7de7a8a1060e8f1608271a28c</data>
  <data key="d4">Stress-induced β cell early senescence confers protection against type 1 diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Sex-biased islet β cell dysfunction is caused by the MODY MAFA S64F variant by inducing premature aging and senescence in males.</data>
  <data key="d5">1778564570</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">135</data>
  <data key="d8">SASP / senescence / Senescence-Associated Secretory Phenotype</data>
  <data key="d9">0.00035996</data>
  <data key="d10">0.00167587</data>
  <data key="d11">0.00369716</data>
</node>
