<node id="S64F Substitution">
  <data key="d0">S64F Substitution</data>
  <data key="d1">Biological Process</data>
  <data key="d2">The S64F substitution is a heterozygous mutation in the MAFA transactivation domain that replaces the conserved serine at position 64 with a phenylalanine, preventing a key priming phosphorylation event at position S65 and increasing protein stability by affecting ubiquitin-mediated degradation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-427bdb72b4ec16ac96774e76f03ada77</data>
  <data key="d4">Sex-biased islet β cell dysfunction is caused by the MODY MAFA S64F variant by inducing premature aging and senescence in males.</data>
  <data key="d5">1778562665</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
  <data key="d8">Insulin / Pancreatic Islets / A0B0 Mice</data>
  <data key="d9">0.00020012</data>
  <data key="d10">1.733e-05</data>
  <data key="d11">0.01069181</data>
</node>
<node id="MafAS64F/+ Mouse Model">
  <data key="d0">MafAS64F/+ Mouse Model</data>
  <data key="d1">Organism</data>
  <data key="d2">MafAS64F/+ is a mouse model established using CRISPR-Cas9-based mutagenesis harboring the same pathogenic single base pair substitution (C&gt;T) as human MAFA S64F carriers, used to study diabetes-related and insulinomatosis-related phenotypes.&lt;SEP&gt;The MafAS64F/+ mouse model is a heterozygous mouse model carrying the MafAS64F mutation, used to study β cell dysfunction, premature aging, and senescence in a sex-dependent manner.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-427bdb72b4ec16ac96774e76f03ada77&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9977f67772ceb665bdd71b221a2d4234</data>
  <data key="d4">Sex-biased islet β cell dysfunction is caused by the MODY MAFA S64F variant by inducing premature aging and senescence in males.</data>
