  <data key="d11">0.00517347</data>
</node>
<node id="CRISPR-Cas9">
  <data key="d0">CRISPR-Cas9</data>
  <data key="d1">Method</data>
  <data key="d2">CRISPR-Cas9-based mutagenesis is the gene editing method used to establish the MafAS64F/+ mouse model by introducing the pathogenic single base pair substitution (C&gt;T).&lt;SEP&gt;Genome editing tool used to generate conditional knockout mice for studying c-MAF function in adult stages.&lt;SEP&gt;Gene editing technology used to generate an experimental mouse model harboring the same pathogenic single base pair change as human patients with MAFA mutation.&lt;SEP&gt;CRISPR-Cas9 is the gene editing system used to generate the C-MAF point-mutation mouse model with the p.Thr58Ile mutation.&lt;SEP&gt;Genome editing technology used to introduce MAFB mutations (p.Pro59Leu and p.Leu239Pro) into mouse models.</data>
