<node id="Ubiquitin-Mediated Degradation">
  <data key="d0">Ubiquitin-Mediated Degradation</data>
  <data key="d1">Biological Process</data>
  <data key="d2">Ubiquitin-mediated degradation is the cellular process by which MAFA protein is normally degraded, and which is disrupted by the S64F substitution, leading to increased MAFA protein stability.&lt;SEP&gt;Ubiquitin-mediated degradation is one of two antagonistic regulatory processes coupled to post-translational modifications of MAFA, involved in regulating islet β cell health.</data>
