<node id="MafA Protein">
  <data key="d0">MafA Protein</data>
  <data key="d1">Biological Process</data>
  <data key="d2">MafA protein is the normally unstable transcription factor encoded by the MAFA gene, whose levels are transiently increased in islet β cells of 4-week-old male MafAS64F/+ mice prior to the onset of glucose intolerance.&lt;SEP&gt;MafA protein is a key regulator of glucose-stimulated insulin secretion whose loss through oxidative stress contributes to insulin gene expression failure in glucotoxic beta cells.</data>
