<node id="LaminB1">
  <data key="d0">LaminB1</data>
  <data key="d1">Data</data>
  <data key="d2">LaminB1 is a senescence marker whose mRNA and protein levels decrease in male MafAS64F/+ islets and in human EndoC-βH2 cells expressing MAFAS64F, consistent with the senescence phenotype.&lt;SEP&gt;A protein marker used in immunostaining of EndoC-βH2 cells to assess nuclear lamina integrity.&lt;SEP&gt;Nuclear lamina protein whose expression is reduced during senescence, impacting nuclear integrity and transcriptional activity.&lt;SEP&gt;Nuclear protein whose loss is a common feature of cellular senescence; dynamically interacts with active versus repressive chromatin to establish distinct topological domains and influences SASP production.&lt;SEP&gt;Nuclear lamina protein whose expression is reduced during senescence, impacting nuclear integrity and transcriptional activity.&lt;SEP&gt;Nuclear protein whose loss is a common feature of cellular senescence; dynamically interacts with active versus repressive chromatin to establish distinct topological domains and influences SASP production.</data>
