<node id="P21">
  <data key="d0">P21</data>
  <data key="d1">Protein</data>
  <data key="d2">P21, also known as p21Cip1/WAF1 and encoded by the gene *Cdkn1a*, is a multifunctional cyclin-dependent kinase (CDK) inhibitor with well-established roles in cell-cycle regulation, cellular senescence, apoptosis, DNA damage response, and beta-cell biology. It is also referred to as WAF1/CIP1 in the literature.

As a CDK inhibitor, P21 regulates cell-cycle progression by inducing cell-cycle arrest and functions as both an early marker and an active driver of cellular senescence. Its protein levels are subject to regulation by Akt signaling, which influences beta-cell proliferation. P21-deficient mice exhibit increased tumor susceptibility, underscoring its role in suppressing uncontrolled cell growth.

In beta-cell biology, P21 plays a significant protective and regulatory role. Elevated P21 levels are associated with diabetes prevention or recovery in type 1 diabetes (T1D) animal models, and its expression is important for beta-cell survival under stress conditions. A P21-mediated early senescence signature, driven by deletion of unfolded protein response (UPR) genes, has been identified and is conserved in residual beta-cells of T1D patients. P21 also drives a downstream program known as the P21-associated secretory phenotype (PASP), which is involved in macrophage recruitment and regulation of LIF (Leukemia Inhibitory Factor) expression, ultimately influencing beta-cell survival.

P21 serves as a hallmark senescence marker in senescent beta cells across multiple genetic models, including inducible Cre mouse models, and is used as an immunostaining marker in EndoC-βH2 cells. Its expression is upregulated during nucleolar stress-induced beta-cell senescence, including following CX-5461 exposure and TIF-IA depletion in beta cells, as well as in beta-TC-6 cells. In MAFAS64F-expressing beta cells and male *MafAS64F/+* mice, P21 expression is notably elevated; 37% of male *MafAS64F/+* islets exhibit greater than 10% P21-positive β cells, compared to only 3% in male wild-type islets, implicating P21 in MAFAS64F-induced senescence progression in pancreatic islets.

From a methodological standpoint, P21 protein is detected using a rabbit monoclonal anti-p21 antibody (Abcam, ab188224), and its activity can be pharmacologically inhibited by the compound UC2288. At the gene expression level, *Cdkn1a* is quantified by qPCR using specific forward (5'-GGCTCATCGTGACGTGTTT-3') and reverse (5'-CAAGGAGTGGTGAGTCAGTTTC-3') primers targeting the coding region, as well as separate primers targeting the 3' UTR region.

It should be noted that "P21" also appears in a distinct, unrelated context referring to postnatal day 21, the age at which 15N-labeled pups were weaned from their mothers in the MIMS-EM labeling protocol. This usage is entirely separate from the CDK inhibitor protein described above.&lt;SEP&gt;p21 is a cyclin-dependent kinase inhibitor (CDKi) widely recognized as a key marker and mediator of cellular senescence across multiple biological contexts.

In its primary and most extensively characterized role, p21 is encoded by the **CDKN1A** gene (also known as WAF1/Cip1). It functions as a critical regulator of cell cycle arrest and senescence, operating within established pathways such as the p53-p21-Rb axis. In this capacity, p21 has been implicated in a senescence-like phenotype in postmitotic neurons driven by the DNA damage response, as well as in hyperglycemia-induced cellular senescence in proximal tubules during the early stages of diabetic nephropathy. It also plays a role in limiting senescence and acinar-to-ductal metaplasia during pancreatitis.

In pancreatic biology, p21 (CDKN1A) serves as a prominent senescence marker in beta cells. Its expression is markedly increased in pancreatic islets of mice fed a high-fat, high-carbohydrate (HFHC) diet. It is induced by nucleolar stress and suppressed by ATM inhibition, as demonstrated in beta cell models (e.g., β-TC-6 cells) through Western blot analysis following treatments with CX-5461 and KU60019. p21 expression is also detectable via RNAscope and is quantified per beta cell area as a senescence marker. Its expression in senescent cells has been leveraged to drive genetic tools, including p21-Cre and p21-ATTAC mouse models, enabling targeted ablation of senescent beta cells.

It is important to note a potential distinction: one description references a protein encoded by **CDKN1C** — a separate gene from CDKN1A — described as a beta cell aging marker whose expression is downregulated under caloric restriction. While CDKN1C encodes the related CDKi protein p57, this description may reflect a nomenclature ambiguity or a distinct entity. The majority of descriptions consistently refer to p21 as the CDKN1A gene product, and the CDKN1C-encoded protein should be considered a separate, though related, cyclin-dependent kinase inhibitor in the context of beta cell aging.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-82e08f93585dc5d50ccfbac2feb8d206&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8dfde3b4ec67624c5a1e8f788a0f0311&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18ba6ed2ada6acd593e0a5d2f036f947&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9bdc00ebaa404f286432a974cec96702&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c72c144fce7d5c94557af956a559639&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8c7bb3e4a69884a1b79485b95f6f502&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bdd484417981e099a8f308ba0994bcaa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8f87338453daad7a9a4624ce798bcf6e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40bbefacfceda2b6335fdb6310e2f7ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9977f67772ceb665bdd71b221a2d4234&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa2caaffb8c37fe000f2af35e115fc27&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d5c817dce40d1df02e7717bb9598632&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f008854d459401e11c35e6bd2541318&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93bb74bfaf0604b4b9f891e16fc9f0ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ce4f6e2d90d0c06e4549d7d45037298&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-15ab370ab273e97005ced113e59cc48a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f082082b0871749ee637b1571aa95c0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49e5c8949dfa6aa24ddf3e3b92d956e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fffe587d9d8a94d6179115102ef90a2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b3deb83588a816faad5340f542e1f43&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9977f67772ceb665bdd71b221a2d4234&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa2caaffb8c37fe000f2af35e115fc27&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02c41952a3f79a76f3315858bb8a14bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-23c7b10bcd96e1a6a6ea025a643b2b01&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c3838ae3de5236c272eda0072cc83f4e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40bbefacfceda2b6335fdb6310e2f7ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-71a6a7a3a4894dbd7d979b7e5766d5a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea13fe99fbc01cb6036ecddcda0aae8a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c5a8121875c37f2659ae345688f6afe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-184abd4f45a78238743890eb9d4f8c56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56d5ffe02105b1bd6d77faab9c812433&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-364a12c675ebfd67c468ab6fc47e6696&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a0590fd9be1db550e8a84c0781e8955&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-787de2a35f76e08d5b7cddadbcc01954&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e33cd1d99c96a7f6ffdd0fbea902670</data>
