<node id="SASP">
  <data key="d0">SASP</data>
  <data key="d1">Biological Process</data>
  <data key="d2">Senescence-Associated Secretory Phenotype (SASP) is a hallmark feature of cellular senescence, defined by the enhanced secretory activity of senescent cells that produces a heterogeneous mix of effector proteins. This complex secretory program encompasses pro-inflammatory cytokines (including IL-1β and IL-6), chemokines, interleukins, matrix metalloproteinases (MMPs), matrix remodeling proteins, growth factors, proteases, soluble immunogenic proteins, extracellular vesicles, and altered cargo. SASP is also regulated by microRNAs (miRNAs) and is associated with conserved signaling pathways across cell types.

SASP operates through both autocrine and paracrine mechanisms, enabling senescent cells to influence neighboring cells in a non-cell-autonomous manner. Among its most notable paracrine effects is the induction of paracrine senescence, whereby SASP factors trigger senescence in adjacent, previously non-senescent cells. Beyond this, SASP can promote tissue regeneration, drive phenotypic transformation, trigger immune-mediated clearance of senescent cells, influence macrophage polarization, contribute to phenotype diversification, and involve autocrine amplification loops — all in a context- and cell-type-dependent fashion. SASP can also exert detrimental paracrine effects on neighboring cells through extracellular vesicles and altered secretory cargo.

At the molecular level, SASP production is influenced by loss of nuclear integrity, particularly through the loss of LaminB1 and nuclear displacement of HMGB1, as well as chronic DNA damage responses. SASP can be decoupled from the growth arrest enforced by p16Ink4a and p21Cip1, and differences in the composition of secreted factors are further driven by whether p21Cip1 or p16Ink4a expression predominates, highlighting the inherent heterogeneity of the SASP profile. Additionally, SASP is associated with nucleolar stress in senescent cells.

In pancreatic beta cell biology specifically, SASP has been observed in senescent beta cells in models such as RbΔ7 knock-in and MAFA_S64F/+ mice, where it is implicated in MAFAS64F-induced β cell dysfunction. The proinflammatory secretory profile of these senescent beta cells affects neighboring cells, including triggering phenotypic changes in alpha cells and altering glucagon secretion. SASP in beta cells is also linked to type 1 diabetes (T1D), and its inflammatory activity can be suppressed by treatments such as KU60019. In this context, SASP represents an active therapeutic target for both senolytic therapies, which aim to eliminate senescent cells, and senomorphic therapies, which seek to modulate the senescent phenotype, with the goal of mitigating beta cell dysfunction and its downstream metabolic consequences.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9b3deb83588a816faad5340f542e1f43&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9977f67772ceb665bdd71b221a2d4234&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa2caaffb8c37fe000f2af35e115fc27&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b39885796d53f3f69a4452a58c07c2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-353703794bc6a501b5c11f84a2064293&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5dc00b5dc127eca5ff2847cc45392453&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-add59972a262992e4bde6910520c0cdb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b861cee193cad9e0f142051047e83aae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-58c0cbc7de7a8a1060e8f1608271a28c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bcadefd5324392c8a202934109c8c242&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fac258601b299e0c883e8e1c4a3030d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9bf309775cbb3bf74509531fe53568a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bdd484417981e099a8f308ba0994bcaa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d3b1de44d6b73a10793a43351e18e6e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-25d34b513b15180c8a2d7b57ae829067&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ca3e5da7a4fe15854dde6289fd15667&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca844018665036149579ef01b8f9ec3c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ce1a7b385e0f22ca823c850de9bf8a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a5bb73f6c7980a9f906f42f6e0e9ce27&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a471400d67fa8643230222fb3576486&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d7ef738c0840825512b2cb7af5b7c3f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b02375738a9ebacd53446fec2077ee76&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f25c34949789593e96b7a57ead73f11&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5f6e43723dd8061d1a0532981e4a43b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6215695e8bd809fd02cb8b9b7b4123ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1628eba511291c52eab3e72ef0fd0239&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a778c4bc437c223ff92d776f7ab7b6a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e32fd907a01d621388ff41b9b47bfa34&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db03a7d3c861658f2beac422f86b21ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a0590fd9be1db550e8a84c0781e8955&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ce4f6e2d90d0c06e4549d7d45037298&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f082082b0871749ee637b1571aa95c0</data>
