<node id="Hypoglycemia">
  <data key="d0">Hypoglycemia</data>
  <data key="d1">Biological Process</data>
  <data key="d2">Hypoglycemia is a pathophysiological outcome observed in female MafAS64F/+ mice, characterized by improved glucose clearance, mimicking expected outcomes in human female carriers of the MAFAS64F variant.&lt;SEP&gt;Slight hypoglycemia observed in heterozygous MAFA-mutant female mice.&lt;SEP&gt;Phenotype (fasting and fed) observed in mice with reduced p21Cip1 in the setting of constitutively active Akt signaling.&lt;SEP&gt;Phenotype (fasting and fed) observed in mice with reduced p21Cip1 in the setting of constitutively active Akt signaling.&lt;SEP&gt;Low blood glucose condition used to assess alpha cell function; T2D islets showed no difference in alpha cell function under hypoglycemic conditions compared to non-diabetic donors.&lt;SEP&gt;Condition observed in female mice on both mixed and C57 backgrounds carrying the MafaS64F/+ variant.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9b3deb83588a816faad5340f542e1f43&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b1a171c046b7e074fd282a07d58cc39&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ef7d4c1829099c6037d8b8b7a83c3cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5cd7041acf7539c8db67413bcd98f41b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0386e6a8316aca2a67c3466442e7e1fa</data>
