  <data key="d11">0.0005305</data>
</node>
<node id="BCL2 Family">
  <data key="d0">BCL2 Family</data>
  <data key="d1">Method</data>
  <data key="d2">BCL2 family members are anti-apoptosis genes whose induction in MafAS64F/+ islets is consistent with resistance to apoptosis and the senescence phenotype.&lt;SEP&gt;The BCL2 family comprises anti-apoptotic proteins that are upregulated in senescent cells, rendering them resistant to apoptosis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9977f67772ceb665bdd71b221a2d4234&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b39885796d53f3f69a4452a58c07c2d</data>
  <data key="d4">Sex-biased islet β cell dysfunction is caused by the MODY MAFA S64F variant by inducing premature aging and senescence in males.</data>
  <data key="d5">1778562683</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">34</data>
  <data key="d8">Male MafAS64F/+ Islets / MafAS64F/+ Male Islets / Senescent Cells</data>
  <data key="d9">0.00015207</data>
  <data key="d10">1.109e-05</data>
  <data key="d11">0.00523779</data>
</node>
<node id="TUNEL">
  <data key="d0">TUNEL</data>
  <data key="d1">Method</data>
  <data key="d2">TUNEL is a method used to detect apoptotic cells; TUNEL+ cells were undetectable in MafAS64F/+ islets between 4 and 7 weeks of age.&lt;SEP&gt;Terminal deoxynucleotidyl transferase dUTP nick end labeling, used to detect cell death; confirmed higher alpha-cell death at P7.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9977f67772ceb665bdd71b221a2d4234&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7af94fcbbc3d167377ece712218fa36b</data>
  <data key="d4">Sex-biased islet β cell dysfunction is caused by the MODY MAFA S64F variant by inducing premature aging and senescence in males.&lt;SEP&gt;Developmental control of DNA damage responses in α- and β-cells shapes the selective beta-cell susceptibility in diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d5">1778571464</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">153</data>
  <data key="d8">TUNEL</data>
  <data key="d9">3.644e-05</data>
