  <data key="d11">0.00580371</data>
</node>
<node id="Bulk RNA-Seq">
  <data key="d0">Bulk RNA-Seq</data>
  <data key="d1">Method</data>
  <data key="d2">Bulk RNA-seq is a transcriptomic analysis method used to analyze gene expression in 5-week-old male and female MafAS64F/+ mouse islets, revealing dysregulation of genes involved in β cell identity and ion channel function.&lt;SEP&gt;Bulk RNA-Seq is a sequencing method used to generate transcriptomic data sets deposited in the GEO database as part of this study.&lt;SEP&gt;A transcriptomic method applied to sorted fixed β-cells involving RNA extraction, library preparation, and sequencing on the Illumina HiSeq2500 platform.&lt;SEP&gt;Bulk RNA-Seq is a sequencing method used to analyze gene expression across populations of cells, applied to MafA∆β mouse β cells, ob/ob mouse islet β cells, and human EndoC-βH2 cells.&lt;SEP&gt;Bulk RNA sequencing method shown to have high concordance with pseudo-bulk single-cell profiles in validating biological ground truth.&lt;SEP&gt;Method showing high concordance with pseudo-bulk single-cell profiles.&lt;SEP&gt;Bulk RNA sequencing used for pathway enrichment analysis comparing CR-HF versus AL-HF mice.&lt;SEP&gt;Transcriptomic method used to analyze isolated islets from AL-HF and CR-HF mice to identify differentially regulated genes.&lt;SEP&gt;Bulk RNA sequencing performed on neonatal and adult C57BL/6J islets to define molecular basis of differential DNA damage vulnerability.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fa2caaffb8c37fe000f2af35e115fc27&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-667c57ab63de668da1132b51f1e9f411&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e74e3fadd5f43dbb51005345f56dec5c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-46772cbd15b1e36b4aedeac0a06fd4de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-794cb97944fe847e61831fceed4d92ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f3f8e2c47cb96d65689fa504202cd0f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2e4a544176811f5b43952b185e1ed3a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0178968ab91760930c812723c60d342b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7af94fcbbc3d167377ece712218fa36b</data>
  <data key="d4">Stress-induced β cell early senescence confers protection against type 1 diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Sex-biased islet β cell dysfunction is caused by the MODY MAFA S64F variant by inducing premature aging and senescence in males.&lt;SEP&gt;Species-specific roles for the MAFA and MAFB transcription factors in regulating islet β cell identity.</data>
  <data key="d5">1778564564</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">16</data>
  <data key="d8">Pancreatic Islet / Bulk RNA-Seq / Islet Isolation</data>
  <data key="d9">0.00116672</data>
  <data key="d10">0.01518105</data>
  <data key="d11">0.02232498</data>
</node>
