  <data key="d0">Human Islets</data>
  <data key="d1">Tissue</data>
  <data key="d2">Human islets differ substantially from rodent islets in architecture, cell composition, proliferative capacity, islet amyloid formation, antioxidant enzyme levels, and transcription factor expression including MAFA and MAFB.&lt;SEP&gt;Human islets are pancreatic structures containing β cells and other endocrine cell types, studied here in normal and T2D donors to examine the relationship between MAFB levels and GAST+ cell presence.&lt;SEP&gt;Human pancreatic islets referenced as a model in which senescent β-cells show upregulation of p21, supporting the relevance of findings from mouse models.&lt;SEP&gt;Human islets are pancreatic tissue samples procured through the IIDP under study BS480P, used for experimental treatments including tunicamycin, Ceapin-A7, and 4μ8C.</data>
