  <data key="d2">MafB is expressed in a subpopulation of maternal β cells during pregnancy and is required for regulating adult murine islet β cell function specifically during pregnancy.&lt;SEP&gt;A physiological condition during which MafB is transiently expressed in murine β cells to facilitate β cell expansion.&lt;SEP&gt;Biological state associated with placental senescence, fetal membrane signaling, and differential senescence in feto-maternal tissues.</data>
