<node id="GAST">
  <data key="d0">GAST</data>
  <data key="d1">Biological Process</data>
  <data key="d2">GAST (gastrin) is a hormone principally expressed in adult gastric G cells and transiently in the embryonic pancreas; it is inappropriately expressed in MafA∆β mouse islets, MAFBKO β-like cells, and human T2D islets.&lt;SEP&gt;A hormone gene whose expression is elevated in human β cells upon MAFB knockdown, and whose protein levels are increased in MAFBKD EndoC-βH2 cells.&lt;SEP&gt;GAST is a gene encoding gastrin, whose expression is repressed by MAFB in adult human islet β cells; GAST+ cells are found in MAFB-deficient T2D islets and fetal pancreas.&lt;SEP&gt;GAST is a hormone gene encoding gastrin, whose expression is regulated by MAFB in human β cells and is used as a marker for identifying specific cell populations in islets and stomach G cells.&lt;SEP&gt;GAST (gastrin) is a gene/protein whose misexpression is associated with type 2 diabetes (T2D), and GAST+ cells have been detected in human T2D islets, with relevance to diabetes pathogenesis.&lt;SEP&gt;GAST is a human protein measured by high-sensitivity ELISA from cell lysate, and its promoter-driven luciferase constructs were used in reporter assays.&lt;SEP&gt;Gast is a gene/protein proposed as an endocrine cell reprogramming marker, abundant during development but waning at birth and undetectable in adult pancreata, with its production representing a potentially reversible cell state.&lt;SEP&gt;Gast is a gene whose expression is upregulated in male mouse islets under hyperglycemic conditions and in MafA∆β mice, indicating metabolic stress-related alternative cell states.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2c914d24696d0f6e2087f40c21ca5649&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d1c90235486a0fe738831a720e1f94ab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbe530a83d027293c37b530e3c376973&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e6c6371cdef301723817998e0efc9ec6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4b8d7d9156faa43670557fc5e83791e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-667c57ab63de668da1132b51f1e9f411&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d1c90235486a0fe738831a720e1f94ab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea3320816339f9f109dec0e1621420bd</data>
