  <data key="d2">Human embryonic stem cell-derived β-like cells lacking MAFB (MAFBKO), used as a predictive model for MAFB function in controlling non–β cell hormone expression.&lt;SEP&gt;Human embryonic stem cell-derived β-like cells are used as a model to study the regulatory properties of MAFB in β cell formation and identity.&lt;SEP&gt;hESC-derived β-like cells are human embryonic stem cell-derived insulin-producing cells used in transplantation studies, showing faster maturation in female than male recipient mice.</data>
