<node id="PDX1">
  <data key="d0">PDX1</data>
  <data key="d1">Gene</data>
  <data key="d2">PDX1 (Pancreatic and Duodenal Homeobox 1, also referred to as PDX-1) is an islet-enriched homeodomain transcription factor that plays a central and multifaceted role in pancreatic biology, serving as a key regulator of pancreatic development, islet cell function, and whole-body glucose homeostasis. It is expressed in both the exocrine and endocrine pancreas during development and is principally found in islet β cells postnatally.

During pancreatic development, PDX1 is required for proper organogenesis, including pancreatic outgrowth, differentiation, and the regulation of endocrine progenitor cell transcriptional networks. Its enhancers are dynamically regulated by the transcription factors Foxa1 and Foxa2. MafB has been identified as a primary activator of PDX1 in developing pancreatic cells, with PDX1 mRNA levels reduced approximately 50% at embryonic day E18.5 following MafB loss. PDX1 also coordinately stimulates MafA gene transcription, and PDX1 deficiency is associated with α-cell intermingling within the β-cell-enriched islet core and compromised MafA expression. PDX1 is identified as a target gene of MAFA through gene expression analysis in pancreatic islets of Mafa-knockout ICR mice. Notably, PDX1-positive pancreatic progenitors are reduced when the ONECUT1 locus enhancer is deleted, further underscoring its role in progenitor cell maintenance.

PDX1 is a critical beta cell identity transcription factor, identified among 242 TFs enriched in beta cells via SCENIC analysis and confirmed as active across diet groups. It exhibits enriched motifs in beta and delta cells, is upregulated in beta cells irrespective of sex, and shows higher centrality in male beta cell gene regulatory networks compared to females. PDX1 is validated at higher levels in caloric restriction (CR) beta cells by immunohistochemistry and confocal microscopy. PDX1 maintains β-cell identity and function by repressing an α-cell program, and its activity is decreased in aging beta cells. It is a beta cell identity marker whose expression is progressively lost during beta cell dedifferentiation in type 2 diabetes, where it is effectively inactivated. Its downregulation does not produce Gast+ cells, indicating a distinct mechanism of β-cell identity regulation. Inactivation of PDX1 in adult pancreatic acinar cells causes senescence in mice.

As a transcription factor, PDX1 cooperates with MAFA and MAFB to activate insulin gene expression, with its activity with MAFB requiring C-terminal sequences. It provides enhanced activation of insulin-reporter constructs with MAFB but not MAFA and influences MAFAWT transactivation activity through functional interactions with MAFA/MAFB chimeric proteins. PDX1 binding sites are also found near the GAST gene, where it may act in concert with MAFB to influence GAST expression. Increased PDX1 expression has been observed in C57 MafaS64F/+ males. PDX1 is detected in pancreatic tissue sections using goat anti-PDX1 antibody immunohistochemistry.

PDX1 is classified as a MODY (maturity-onset diabetes of the young) transcription factor — specifically MODY type 4 — and is the only one among the seven known human MODY transcription factors whose heterozygous mouse phenotype is comparable to that in human carriers. The Pdx1 5.5 kb promoter fragment has been used to drive Cre recombinase expression in MafAΔPanc mice. PDX1 is also implicated in the reprogramming of adult acinar cells to β-like cells, highlighting its therapeutic potential in regenerative medicine.&lt;SEP&gt;Pancreatic and duodenal homeobox 1 gene; Cre driver used to delete Dnmt3a in pancreatic progenitor lineage&lt;SEP&gt;Transcription factor essential for pancreatic beta-cell identity and function.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2c914d24696d0f6e2087f40c21ca5649&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e6c6371cdef301723817998e0efc9ec6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b13f08985b48653da8be9b63098bbb2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b1a171c046b7e074fd282a07d58cc39&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9693157a2d458ecc8255c49ec77d95f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a87d40ff620e7f930f155b5dea286c8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ee443fb4c37f27d6895254d3f95c708&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ecc1e3f157d04d78962c82537c6b7d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7568462935971fd17472cf21ed7b8a2b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8f87338453daad7a9a4624ce798bcf6e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b67e26d82684726785f1910ba6919cf0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe5b7d8c678cb311e300af3b74f19ed6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a7873cb15c71b20e5fc369a6f0ab52a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea13fe99fbc01cb6036ecddcda0aae8a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51601485f0924871a988aae2e5ce30bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0238834380bfb40677324883af3e3004&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0269f34de8f0928a9614438917079ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f02465fe113dd488219949222d1430e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08e345f1e7ff9529c2ab94760dcb50f5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-002f23b1d29df711e839459b4d6f0711&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6cadc21c6ca916dd06510987c1b7dbf4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f63ca40b092870f725a75e7a36045d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0178968ab91760930c812723c60d342b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3384cef9855a1b408c68f7d1ea3153c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ecb3c400fe73c10974d8a6b3b2160b23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19fff7a7048ab7112926e25c2e46450b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d07a2e48a0133bedad1b6e79e652b89c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eae638e9cabe91a68fc062c9981b0e86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa2caaffb8c37fe000f2af35e115fc27&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c41ef398df926f1c888f284aff2a98e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd4f6cfb9180aade52c8cb84446ced85&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e42c3b77d3170e854edbbc691159609d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0386e6a8316aca2a67c3466442e7e1fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4e8cbb766d17c90c84d2a9452a51a41e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-044fb2d3ececa99a53eb87d2ee6bf18f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e181574d19e6f17c0fd64b0feecf8f9e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce72a72ed1aaea72aac97c28374f8f86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e953ac093714735fa9b5b27463bf5dff</data>
  <data key="d4">The MafA transcription factor becomes essential to islet β-cells soon after birth.&lt;SEP&gt;MafA and MafB regulate genes critical to beta-cells in a unique temporal manner.&lt;SEP&gt;Sex-biased islet β cell dysfunction is caused by the MODY MAFA S64F variant by inducing premature aging and senescence in males.&lt;SEP&gt;Species-specific roles for the MAFA and MAFB transcription factors in regulating islet β cell identity.&lt;SEP&gt;MafB Is Important for Pancreatic β-Cell Maintenance under a MafA-Deficient Condition.&lt;SEP&gt;Exploring Large MAF Transcription Factors: Functions, Pathology, and Mouse Models with Point Mutations.&lt;SEP&gt;Pancreatic β-cell senescence in diabetes: mechanisms, markers and therapies.&lt;SEP&gt;Single cell regulatory architecture of human pancreatic islets suggests sex differences in β cell function and the pathogenesis of type 2 diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;SenNet recommendations for detecting senescent cells in different tissues.&lt;SEP&gt;Calorie restriction increases insulin sensitivity to promote beta cell homeostasis and longevity in mice.&lt;SEP&gt;Defining unique structural features in the MAFA and MAFB transcription factors that control Insulin gene activity.&lt;SEP&gt;Sex-specific regulatory architecture of pancreatic islets from subjects with and without type 2 diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Genetic background influences the phenotypic penetrance by MAFA (S64F) MODY in male mice.&lt;SEP&gt;The role of the beta cell in type 2 diabetes: new findings from the last 5 years.&lt;SEP&gt;Developmental control of DNA damage responses in α- and β-cells shapes the selective beta-cell susceptibility in diabetes.</data>
