<node id="NKX6.1">
  <data key="d0">NKX6.1</data>
  <data key="d1">Biological Process</data>
  <data key="d2">An islet-enriched transcription factor associated with INS transcription, still produced in MAFB-deficient hESC-derived cells despite absence of insulin expression.&lt;SEP&gt;NKX6.1 is a transcription factor essential for maintaining the functional state of pancreatic beta cells.&lt;SEP&gt;NKX6.1 is an islet-enriched transcription factor associated with INS transcription that is still produced in MAFBKO β-like cells despite loss of insulin production.&lt;SEP&gt;NKX6.1 is an islet-enriched transcription factor with binding sites in the GAST gene region, potentially cooperating with MAFB to affect GAST expression.&lt;SEP&gt;Nkx6.1 is an NK6 homeodomain transcription factor that plays a critical role in pancreatic development, β-cell formation, and overall glucose homeostasis. Initially expressed broadly and at early stages across the pancreatic epithelium, Nkx6.1 expression becomes progressively confined to β-cells within the islets of Langerhans as development proceeds, ultimately being restricted to endocrine progenitors and then to mature β-cells.

As a transcription factor, Nkx6.1 functions downstream of Nkx2.2 and is integral to the major pathway of β-cell fate specification. It has been shown to suppress glucagon expression, thereby reinforcing β-cell identity, and it regulates glucose-stimulated insulin secretion in islet β-cells. Additionally, Nkx6.1 coordinately stimulates MafA gene transcription, further linking it to the transcriptional network governing β-cell maturation and function. Its activities in promoting beta-cell fate specification in Pdx1+ pancreatic progenitor cells are considered equivalent to those of the related factor Nkx6.2.

Nkx6.1 plays an important role in islet β-cell function and whole-body glucose homeostasis, with its expression found to be unaltered in MafAΔPanc islets during development, suggesting it operates within a complex but partially independent regulatory network. In research settings, Nkx6.1 protein is commonly detected using a rabbit α-Nkx6.1 antibody sourced from the Beta Cell Biology Consortium, which has been employed in immunolabeling studies of pancreatic tissue to characterize its expression patterns and functional significance.&lt;SEP&gt;An islet-enriched transcription factor essential for maintaining the functional state of pancreatic beta cells.&lt;SEP&gt;Nkx6.1 is an islet-enriched transcription factor whose downregulation does not produce Gast+ cells, indicating distinct regulation of β cell identity.</data>
