<node id="MafA∆β Mice">
  <data key="d0">MafA∆β Mice</data>
  <data key="d1">Biological Process</data>
  <data key="d2">MafA∆β mice are β cell–specific MafA deletion mutants generated by crossing MafAfl/fl mice with Ins1Cre mice, exhibiting impaired glucose tolerance and aberrant non–β cell hormone expression in islets.&lt;SEP&gt;MafA∆β mice are a mouse model with direct genetic manipulation of MafA in islet β cells, used to study gene regulatory properties of MafA.&lt;SEP&gt;MafA∆β mice are a mouse model with β cell-specific deletion of MafA, used to study the role of MafA in β cell identity and alternative cell states; generated by crossing MafAfl/fl with Ins1Cre knockin mice.</data>
