  <data key="d2">A genetic mouse model of obesity-induced glucose intolerance that manifests hyperglycemia, elevated plasma insulin, and loss of β cell MafA, analogous to S961 treatment effects.&lt;SEP&gt;ob/ob mice are a mouse model of obesity and insulin resistance used to study gene expression in Gast+ β cells and islet β cell populations.&lt;SEP&gt;Ob/ob mice are an obese mouse model obtained from The Jackson Laboratory, crossed with mIns1-H2b-mCherry reporter mice for β cell isolation studies.</data>
