<node id="Type 2 Diabetes (T2D)">
  <data key="d0">Type 2 Diabetes (T2D)</data>
  <data key="d1">Biological Process</data>
  <data key="d2">Type 2 diabetes is a metabolic disease associated with compromised identity of insulin-producing pancreatic islet β cells, characterized by inappropriate production of other islet cell–enriched hormones.&lt;SEP&gt;Type 2 Diabetes is a metabolic disease associated with β cell dysfunction, reduced cell identity, and enrichment of GAST+ cells in pancreatic islets with compromised MAFB expression.&lt;SEP&gt;Type 2 diabetes (T2D) is a metabolic disease associated with glucotoxicity and oxidative stress that reduces MAFA and MAFB protein levels in islets, correlating with enrichment of GAST+ cells in MAFB-deficient islets.&lt;SEP&gt;Type 2 diabetes is a metabolic disease associated with β cell dysfunction, loss of MafA/MAFB expression, and the appearance of GAST+ cells in islets.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2c914d24696d0f6e2087f40c21ca5649&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d1c90235486a0fe738831a720e1f94ab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce67306159c306b2c966577061cee6bd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbe530a83d027293c37b530e3c376973</data>
