<node id="GAST+ Cells">
  <data key="d0">GAST+ Cells</data>
  <data key="d1">Biological Process</data>
  <data key="d2">GAST+ cells are gastrin-expressing cells found enriched in MAFB-deficient T2D islets and produced in MAFBKD EndoC-βH1/2 cells, representing a pool of cells with loosened identity that may be reprogrammable.&lt;SEP&gt;GAST+ cells are a pool of "reprogrammable" cells of loosened identity that may be coaxed back to β cells or produce new β cells from non–β cell sources in autocrine and/or paracrine manners.&lt;SEP&gt;A rare cell population expressing the Gast gene, produced in male insulin-resistant mice and characterized by a unique gene signature including endocrine markers such as Gcg, Sst, Cck, Chga, Chgb, Pyy, and Iapp.&lt;SEP&gt;Gast+ cells are a cell population identified in mouse islets whose enriched gene expression is listed in Supplemental Table 1.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2c914d24696d0f6e2087f40c21ca5649&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea3320816339f9f109dec0e1621420bd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-46772cbd15b1e36b4aedeac0a06fd4de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4b8d7d9156faa43670557fc5e83791e</data>
  <data key="d4">Species-specific roles for the MAFA and MAFB transcription factors in regulating islet β cell identity.</data>
  <data key="d5">1778562864</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">0</data>
  <data key="d8">beta cell / MAFA / MAFB</data>
  <data key="d9">0.00095627</data>
  <data key="d10">0.00431054</data>
  <data key="d11">0.02549093</data>
</node>
<node id="Endocrine Progenitors">
  <data key="d0">Endocrine Progenitors</data>
  <data key="d1">Biological Process</data>
  <data key="d2">Ngn3+ endocrine progenitor cells are the developmental origin of pancreatic Gast+ cells, abundant during fetal development but waning at birth and undetectable in adult pancreata.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2c914d24696d0f6e2087f40c21ca5649</data>
  <data key="d4">Species-specific roles for the MAFA and MAFB transcription factors in regulating islet β cell identity.</data>
  <data key="d5">1778562865</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">158</data>
  <data key="d8">Endocrine Progenitors</data>
  <data key="d9">0.00024291</data>
  <data key="d10">0.0</data>
  <data key="d11">0.0</data>
</node>
<node id="Fetal Pancreas">
  <data key="d0">Fetal Pancreas</data>
  <data key="d1">Tissue</data>
  <data key="d2">The fetal pancreas is the developmental context in which Gast expression is normally found, with Gast uniquely restricted to this stage among mouse pancreatic islet peptide hormones.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2c914d24696d0f6e2087f40c21ca5649</data>
  <data key="d4">Species-specific roles for the MAFA and MAFB transcription factors in regulating islet β cell identity.</data>
  <data key="d5">1778562865</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">158</data>
  <data key="d8">Endocrine Progenitors</data>
  <data key="d9">0.00024291</data>
  <data key="d10">0.0</data>
  <data key="d11">0.0</data>
</node>
<node id="Mouse Pancreatic Islet">
  <data key="d0">Mouse Pancreatic Islet</data>
  <data key="d1">Tissue</data>
  <data key="d2">The mouse pancreatic islet contains multiple peptide hormone-expressing cell types, with Gast uniquely restricted to the fetal stage under normal conditions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2c914d24696d0f6e2087f40c21ca5649</data>
  <data key="d4">Species-specific roles for the MAFA and MAFB transcription factors in regulating islet β cell identity.</data>
