</node>
<node id="SST">
  <data key="d0">SST</data>
  <data key="d1">Gene</data>
  <data key="d2">SST (somatostatin) is a hormone-encoding gene that serves multiple roles in pancreatic islet biology, functioning both as a canonical cell-type marker and as an indicator of transcription factor-dependent cell identity.

Under normal physiological conditions, SST is a well-established marker gene for delta (δ) cells within pancreatic islets. It is routinely used to identify and validate delta cell clusters in single-cell and single-nucleus analyses, including scRNA-seq and snATAC-seq studies of human pancreatic islets, where it helps annotate delta cell populations based on chromatin accessibility and transcriptional profiles.

SST is also recognized as a non–β cell hormone, meaning its expression in β cells is considered inappropriate. However, several studies highlight contexts in which SST becomes ectopically expressed in β cells, reflecting intraislet cell plasticity. Specifically, SST expression is elevated in MAFB-deficient conditions: it is inappropriately expressed in MAFBKO β-like cells in mouse models, and its mRNA levels are significantly upregulated upon MAFB knockdown in human EndoC-βH2 β cells, with SST protein detected in approximately 2% of MAFBKD EndoC-βH2 cells. This induction of SST in a MAFB-deficient pure β cell line suggests potential δ cell reprogramming under conditions of MAFB loss. In contrast, MAFA depletion in EndoC-βH1 cells does not significantly alter SST mRNA levels, indicating that MAFB, rather than MAFA, is the primary transcription factor repressing SST expression in human β cells.

Additionally, SST expression has been observed in β cells within human type 2 diabetes (T2D) islets, further supporting the notion that loss of key islet transcription factors or disease-related stress can trigger inappropriate SST expression in β cells, underscoring the broader concept of islet cell plasticity in pathological contexts.&lt;SEP&gt;SST is a marker gene for pancreatic delta cells identified in scRNA-seq cluster analysis.&lt;SEP&gt;Somatostatin gene used as marker to validate delta cell cluster identity in snATAC-seq analysis.&lt;SEP&gt;SST is a hormone marker gene used as a chromatin accessibility marker for delta cells in ATAC-seq analysis.&lt;SEP&gt;Somatostatin gene used as a marker for delta cell cluster identification in snATAC-seq.&lt;SEP&gt;SST is a marker gene specifically upregulated in delta cells, expressed independently of sex and race/ethnicity.&lt;SEP&gt;SST is a marker gene for delta cells in pancreatic islets, used to identify cell types by gene accessibility.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d1c90235486a0fe738831a720e1f94ab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbe530a83d027293c37b530e3c376973&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e6c6371cdef301723817998e0efc9ec6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4b8d7d9156faa43670557fc5e83791e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e607d2cca86a6257f1db73bacae2c96&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c0d05211cf3080af14ec050e5cc97ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a7873cb15c71b20e5fc369a6f0ab52a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d7bd4bfe81f828dceb60b520d85bcf2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73a24341c9b63bd3b6313252fe6ed4b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f02465fe113dd488219949222d1430e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-87d48756321bdf8ef533359c0655a3d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da10e6374cdbd3d6e4a07d773cd172d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e42c3b77d3170e854edbbc691159609d</data>
