<node id="Single-Cell RNA-Seq">
  <data key="d0">Single-Cell RNA-Seq</data>
  <data key="d1">Method</data>
  <data key="d2">A sequencing technique used to identify genes significantly enriched in Gast+ cells compared with Gast– β cells in S961-treated male mice.&lt;SEP&gt;Single-cell RNA-Seq is a method used to analyze gene expression at the single-cell level, employed here to identify 61 genes enriched in GAST+ MAFBKO β-like cells.&lt;SEP&gt;Single-cell RNA sequencing (scRNA-seq) is a method used to analyze gene expression in individual cells of control and S961-treated diabetic mouse islets.&lt;SEP&gt;Single-cell RNA-Seq is a sequencing method used to generate transcriptomic data sets deposited in the GEO database as part of this study.&lt;SEP&gt;Single-cell RNA-Seq is a sequencing method used to analyze gene expression at the single-cell level, applied to mouse islets and other cell types in the study.</data>
