<node id="Propidium Iodide">
  <data key="d0">Propidium Iodide</data>
  <data key="d1">Molecule</data>
  <data key="d2">Propidium iodide (PI) is a viability dye from Thermo Fisher Scientific used to exclude dead cells during FACS sorting of mouse islet preparations.&lt;SEP&gt;Propidium Iodide (PI) is a fluorescent dye from Thermo Fisher Scientific used to stain cells, allowing identification of dead cells for exclusion during sorting.&lt;SEP&gt;Propidium iodide (PI) is a viability dye used to exclude non-viable cells in flow cytometry analyses including C12FDG staining, apoptosis assay, and related protocols.&lt;SEP&gt;PI fluorescent dye used to stain slides in the comet assay for DNA damage visualization.</data>
