<node id="Seurat">
  <data key="d0">Seurat</data>
  <data key="d1">Method</data>
  <data key="d2">Seurat is a widely used bioinformatics software package implemented in R, designed primarily for the analysis of single-cell genomics data, including single-cell RNA sequencing (scRNA-seq) and single-nucleus ATAC sequencing (snATAC-seq) data.

As a comprehensive computational tool, Seurat supports a broad range of analytical workflows. Its core functionalities include data merging, quality control thresholding, normalization (including variance-stabilizing normalization via SCtransform), dimensionality reduction techniques such as Principal Component Analysis (PCA), unsupervised clustering, and downstream visualization methods including UMAP. Additionally, Seurat provides functions for differential gene expression analysis, such as the FindMarkers function, enabling users to identify marker genes across distinct cell populations and support cell type assignment.

Beyond transcriptomic data, Seurat is also applicable to chromatin accessibility data (snATAC-seq), where it can be used to merge datasets, perform normalization, clustering, and differential analysis of ATAC peak levels. The software further supports multi-modal analyses by enabling the creation of objects that simultaneously contain gene expression and chromatin accessibility assays, as well as the integration of additional data modalities such as regulon activity matrices.

Seurat is commonly applied with both default and customized parameters depending on the analytical context. The version most frequently referenced in recent literature and analyses is v4.3.0 (also referred to as V4), though the tool has been utilized across multiple versions. Overall, Seurat serves as a versatile and widely adopted framework for the full spectrum of single-cell data processing, analysis, and visualization tasks in computational biology and genomics research.&lt;SEP&gt;Computational framework for comprehensive integration of single-cell data referenced in the analysis pipeline.&lt;SEP&gt;Comprehensive integration tool for single-cell data referenced in studies of multimodal single-cell data.&lt;SEP&gt;Bioinformatics software (v4.3.0) from Satija Lab used for single-cell RNA-seq data analysis.&lt;SEP&gt;Seurat v4.3.0 is a software tool used for merging, thresholding, normalization, clustering analysis, visualization, and differential gene expression analysis of single-cell RNA sequencing data.&lt;SEP&gt;R package (v4.3.0) used for merging, thresholding, normalization, dimensionality reduction, clustering, and differential gene expression analysis of snATAC data.&lt;SEP&gt;Seurat V4.0 is used for filtering, normalization, UMAP projection, clustering, and cell type identification in single-cell RNA sequencing data.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-46772cbd15b1e36b4aedeac0a06fd4de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e74e3fadd5f43dbb51005345f56dec5c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78c6090d91c84168c42d7ba3a2808633&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5bcdcae8f65f7440848eed5a2448750b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6615f49a664b0e6bfe3dc5ebc25a278f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a7d380dafd31120f8a1af317cfb0ab1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7913917fca6b789f10e2948623ce222&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56d5ffe02105b1bd6d77faab9c812433&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-831b74d6764559e79da6fa29d15caf42&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d5c817dce40d1df02e7717bb9598632&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c60bd30a96540afcdba183f8a7aa851&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c41ef398df926f1c888f284aff2a98e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d41db2658ec2709309c04b39b1894e48&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a5e348a0adb909ac9a245bd8fb1b7b7b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5804ddf6c13fee09d00987476aa3c478&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-835fc8c5c19bf30c115aefbeec789479&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c461d96db4bed849ef22472fc2b0cd0</data>
