<node id="UMAP">
  <data key="d0">UMAP</data>
  <data key="d1">Method</data>
  <data key="d2">Uniform Manifold Approximation and Projection (UMAP) is a non-linear dimensionality reduction method widely employed in the analysis and visualization of complex, high-dimensional biological datasets. At its core, UMAP reduces high-dimensional data into a low-dimensional space, enabling researchers to visually interpret structure, clustering patterns, and marker expression that would otherwise be difficult to discern.

UMAP is particularly prominent in single-cell genomics research, where it is used for clustering visualization of single-cell data, including both single-nucleus RNA sequencing (snRNA-seq) and single-nucleus ATAC sequencing (snATAC-seq) datasets. Its non-linear nature makes it well suited for capturing complex relationships between cells that linear methods may fail to represent accurately.

In the context of chromatin accessibility studies, UMAP has been applied to visualize snATAC-seq clusters, including after batch correction steps, ensuring that technical variation does not obscure meaningful biological signals. Similarly, UMAP supports the visualization of integrated transcriptome and chromatin datasets, allowing for a unified representation of multi-modal single-cell data.

UMAP has been specifically used to display integrated clustering of large-scale pancreatic islet cell datasets, including a dataset comprising 141,739 single pancreatic islet cells spanning 17 distinct cell types, as well as a separate dataset of 52,613 single pancreatic islet cells across 11 cell types. These applications highlight UMAP's scalability and utility in characterizing cellular heterogeneity within complex tissues.

Overall, UMAP serves as a versatile and powerful visualization tool in single-cell biology, enabling researchers to explore cell type diversity, validate clustering results, and interpret integrated multi-omic datasets in an accessible low-dimensional representation.&lt;SEP&gt;UMAP projection is used for dimensionality reduction and visualization of integrated single-cell RNA sequencing data.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-46772cbd15b1e36b4aedeac0a06fd4de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78c6090d91c84168c42d7ba3a2808633&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5bcdcae8f65f7440848eed5a2448750b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6615f49a664b0e6bfe3dc5ebc25a278f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7913917fca6b789f10e2948623ce222&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f02465fe113dd488219949222d1430e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c60bd30a96540afcdba183f8a7aa851&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-87d48756321bdf8ef533359c0655a3d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2496631e25b79859522b657da346b58&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da10e6374cdbd3d6e4a07d773cd172d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a5e348a0adb909ac9a245bd8fb1b7b7b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e42c3b77d3170e854edbbc691159609d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-835fc8c5c19bf30c115aefbeec789479&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c461d96db4bed849ef22472fc2b0cd0</data>
