<node id="Islets">
  <data key="d0">Islets</data>
  <data key="d1">Tissue</data>
  <data key="d2">Pancreatic islets are biological structures that were isolated, dissociated, and stained as part of the single-cell RNA-Seq experimental workflow.&lt;SEP&gt;Islets (islets of Langerhans) are pancreatic microstructures containing β-cells; they are sites of inflammation in T1D and are subject to M2 macrophage recruitment and immune modulation in the study's experimental model.&lt;SEP&gt;Pancreatic islets are isolated from control and knockout mice and used in ex vivo studies to investigate the role of p21 in cell survival during stress.&lt;SEP&gt;Pancreatic islets isolated from 6-week-old mice, dispersed into single cells for β-cell sorting and RNA-seq analysis.&lt;SEP&gt;Islets are biological samples donated by healthy donors and T1D patients, used in ex vivo culture experiments and scRNA-seq analysis.</data>
