<node id="Unfolded Protein Response">
  <data key="d0">Unfolded Protein Response</data>
  <data key="d1">Biological Process</data>
  <data key="d2">The unfolded protein response is an adaptive cellular mechanism whose failure in islets of obese mice is linked with abnormalities in β-cell gene expression and progression to diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Adaptive cellular pathway (UPR) that can be activated by enhanced secretory activity in senescent cells; whether this occurs in beta cell senescence requires further investigation.&lt;SEP&gt;Adaptive cellular pathway (UPR) that can be activated by enhanced secretory activity in senescent cells; whether this occurs in beta cell senescence requires further investigation.&lt;SEP&gt;Stressed state in beta cells contributing to T1D pathogenesis, with therapeutic modulation progressed into phase II clinical trials.&lt;SEP&gt;Cellular response to ER stress relevant to beta cell function and diabetes pathogenesis.&lt;SEP&gt;Cellular stress pathway regulating beta cell number in response to insulin demand.&lt;SEP&gt;Cellular stress pathway upregulated in non-diabetic donor islets exposed to glucolipotoxic stress and associated with beta cell failure.&lt;SEP&gt;Cellular stress response pathway upregulated under glucolipotoxic conditions associated with beta cell failure.&lt;SEP&gt;A stress stimulus that can initiate beta cell senescence, representing one of the diverse stress pathways converging on senescence programs.&lt;SEP&gt;Cellular stress response identified in pseudotime ordering of human beta cells alongside insulin production states.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b13f08985b48653da8be9b63098bbb2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-58c0cbc7de7a8a1060e8f1608271a28c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08f3e602fed4b4ebfff436b75194d507&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-72bf1fbaf7a329c364247108f8b30408&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f63ca40b092870f725a75e7a36045d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4e8cbb766d17c90c84d2a9452a51a41e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5596e00050d9f0135f87252a0093e9cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ce4f6e2d90d0c06e4549d7d45037298&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce72a72ed1aaea72aac97c28374f8f86</data>
  <data key="d4">Species-specific roles for the MAFA and MAFB transcription factors in regulating islet β cell identity.&lt;SEP&gt;Pancreatic β-cell senescence in diabetes: mechanisms, markers and therapies.&lt;SEP&gt;Exploring senescence as a modifier of β cell extracellular vesicles in type 1 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d5">1778568443</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">135</data>
  <data key="d8">SASP / senescence / Senescence-Associated Secretory Phenotype</data>
  <data key="d9">0.00025882</data>
  <data key="d10">2.188e-05</data>
  <data key="d11">0.02595038</data>
</node>
<node id="Dedifferentiation">
  <data key="d0">Dedifferentiation</data>
  <data key="d1">Biological Process</data>
  <data key="d2">Dedifferentiation is a process by which β-cells lose their identity and may transdifferentiate into other cell types, contributing to β-cell failure in diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Adult pancreatic acinar cells dedifferentiate to an embryonic progenitor phenotype with concomitant senescence activation in chronic pancreatitis.&lt;SEP&gt;Process by which acinar cells lose their identity and can acquire an embryonic progenitor phenotype during acinar-to-ductal metaplasia.&lt;SEP&gt;Process by which beta cells lose their differentiated identity, studied in type 2 diabetes and shown to play a minor role in beta cell deficit in obese T2D.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b13f08985b48653da8be9b63098bbb2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea13fe99fbc01cb6036ecddcda0aae8a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d7ef738c0840825512b2cb7af5b7c3f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-10bdc47e4d027606476b48a401061a27</data>
  <data key="d4">Species-specific roles for the MAFA and MAFB transcription factors in regulating islet β cell identity.</data>
