<node id="GLP-1">
  <data key="d0">GLP-1</data>
  <data key="d1">Molecule</data>
  <data key="d2">GLP-1 (glucagon-like peptide-1) is a hormone used in therapeutic contexts; ZP3022 is a dual GLP-1-gastrin agonist developed for diabetes treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;A glucagon-like peptide whose signaling mediates insulinotropic and anti-apoptotic effects in adult mouse beta cells via CREB.&lt;SEP&gt;Glucagon-like peptide-1, an incretin hormone whose insulinotropic action is amplified by androgen receptor pathways in male pancreatic beta cells.&lt;SEP&gt;Glucagon-like peptide-1, incretin hormone targeted by semaglutide, tirzepatide, and retatrutide.&lt;SEP&gt;Glucagon-like peptide-1, an incretin hormone whose receptor is targeted by semaglutide and tirzepatide to improve beta cell function.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b13f08985b48653da8be9b63098bbb2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d13aa78bf917b6b3ed2e772b6f010e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b67e26d82684726785f1910ba6919cf0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ddac43d21e0426c8d61d02d10c0cb772&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-10bdc47e4d027606476b48a401061a27</data>
  <data key="d4">Stress-induced β cell early senescence confers protection against type 1 diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Species-specific roles for the MAFA and MAFB transcription factors in regulating islet β cell identity.&lt;SEP&gt;Single cell regulatory architecture of human pancreatic islets suggests sex differences in β cell function and the pathogenesis of type 2 diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;The role of the beta cell in type 2 diabetes: new findings from the last 5 years.</data>
  <data key="d5">1778570781</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">23</data>
  <data key="d8">Type 2 Diabetes / Insulin Resistance / High-Fat Diet</data>
