<node id="AlphaFold 2">
  <data key="d0">AlphaFold 2</data>
  <data key="d1">Method</data>
  <data key="d2">AlphaFold 2 is an artificial intelligence-based protein structure prediction program designed to determine the three-dimensional organization of protein sequences. It employs deep iterative learning methodologies, utilizing multiple sequence alignments to perform de novo modeling of protein three-dimensional architecture.

As a computational tool, AlphaFold 2 has been applied extensively to structural studies of the MAFA and MAFB proteins, including their homodimer configurations, full-length structures, and various mutant forms such as phosphomimetic substitutions. The program has been used to generate structural models that reveal novel features, including C-terminal tail structures and disordered regions within these proteins. Specifically, AlphaFold 2 has provided structural insight into both the N-terminal transactivation domain and the C-terminal region of MAFA and MAFB, as well as predicting the three-dimensional architecture of intrinsically disordered regions present within these proteins.

Beyond its application to MAFA and MAFB, AlphaFold 2 functions as a broadly applicable deep learning-based structural prediction tool capable of modeling diverse protein targets. Its ability to predict full-length protein structures, including those of mutant variants, makes it a versatile resource for obtaining structural insights that inform understanding of protein function, organization, and regulatory mechanisms.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8b5b330edc0a8ae22148338c6d94f154&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb32288d5dedac1b23370508bf2f7b2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84ba2041af7b71a5fc2faad1de1c95dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3384cef9855a1b408c68f7d1ea3153c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f4fecd9e508da1daa4a0d2d27a7e759&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19fff7a7048ab7112926e25c2e46450b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d07a2e48a0133bedad1b6e79e652b89c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eae638e9cabe91a68fc062c9981b0e86</data>
  <data key="d4">Defining unique structural features in the MAFA and MAFB transcription factors that control Insulin gene activity.</data>
  <data key="d5">1778569788</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
