</node>
<node id="Basic-Leucine-Zipper Domain">
  <data key="d0">Basic-Leucine-Zipper Domain</data>
  <data key="d1">Biological Process</data>
  <data key="d2">The basic-leucine-zipper domain is a structural feature present in both MAFA and MAFB transcription factors, involved in DNA binding and dimerization.&lt;SEP&gt;Structural domain shared by MAFA and MAFB responsible for DNA binding and dimerization; 100% identical in basic region and 63% in leucine-zipper between MAFA and MAFB.&lt;SEP&gt;Structural domain of MAFA and MAFB responsible for DNA binding and dimerization.&lt;SEP&gt;The basic-leucine-zipper domain is a structural domain in MAFA and MAFB responsible for DNA binding and dimerization.</data>
