<node id="C-Terminal Region">
  <data key="d0">C-Terminal Region</data>
  <data key="d1">Biological Process</data>
  <data key="d2">The C-terminal region is a structural domain of MAFA and MAFB predicted by AlphaFold 2 to have unique differences that influence functional properties between the two proteins.&lt;SEP&gt;Structural region of MAFA and MAFB that differs between the two proteins and influences cooperative transcriptional activity, as revealed by chimera analysis.&lt;SEP&gt;C-terminal disordered region of MAFA and MAFB predicted by AlphaFold 2 to have unique structural features; required for ISL1 cooperation with MAFB and PDX1 activation.</data>
