  <data key="d1">Method</data>
  <data key="d2">A transwell migration assay is an in vitro method used to evaluate the migratory behavior of macrophages in response to conditioned medium from Ceapin-A7-treated NIT1 cells.&lt;SEP&gt;Transwell migration assay is an experimental method used to assess the migration of peritoneal immune cells using a transwell insert (3μm pore size, Costar, #3415) and conditioned media.&lt;SEP&gt;A laboratory technique used to assess the migration of peritoneal immune cells through a transwell insert with 3μm pore size over 42 hours.</data>
