<node id="Ire1αβ−/− Mice">
  <data key="d0">Ire1αβ−/− Mice</data>
  <data key="d1">Organism</data>
  <data key="d2">Genetically modified mice with β-cell-specific deletion of IRE1α, used to compare senescence and UPR pathway findings with Atf6β−/− mice.&lt;SEP&gt;Ire1αβ−/− mice are a knockout mouse model with specific loss of IRE1α in β-cells, used to study diabetes incidence and p21's role in β-cell survival.&lt;SEP&gt;Ire1αβ−/− mice are UPR-deficient mice lacking IRE1αβ, protected from diabetes and showing increased M2 macrophage infiltration in the pancreata.&lt;SEP&gt;Ire1αβ−/− mice are knockout mice deficient in IRE1α and IRE1β components of the UPR, used to study senescence and macrophage infiltration in islets.&lt;SEP&gt;Mice with β-cell-specific deletion of IRE1α, showing substantially decreased SA-β-gal activity and reduced cell size at 20 weeks of age.&lt;SEP&gt;Female Ire1αβ knockout mice used as an in vivo model in the study, receiving virus or antibody injections starting at 3 weeks of age.&lt;SEP&gt;Genetically modified mice lacking Ire1α and Ire1β, whose single-cell RNA sequencing data was used in differential gene expression analysis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e74e3fadd5f43dbb51005345f56dec5c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-23c7b10bcd96e1a6a6ea025a643b2b01&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40e720fe9c9efb2c2c2dedf6638ae8f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8dfde3b4ec67624c5a1e8f788a0f0311&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c3838ae3de5236c272eda0072cc83f4e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f797167cb0737019ee587d4f66f13530&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40bbefacfceda2b6335fdb6310e2f7ae</data>
  <data key="d4">Stress-induced β cell early senescence confers protection against type 1 diabetes.</data>
