<node id="Chromatin Immunoprecipitation">
  <data key="d0">Chromatin Immunoprecipitation</data>
  <data key="d1">Method</data>
  <data key="d2">ChIP (Chromatin Immunoprecipitation) followed by qPCR was used to verify CREB binding to the Cdkn1a promoter and the effect of constitutively active ATF6 on this binding.&lt;SEP&gt;A ChIP assay method used to study protein-DNA interactions in vivo, adapted from Bayam et al., 2015, performed with INS1 832/3 cells and followed by quantitative PCR.&lt;SEP&gt;Chromatin immunoprecipitation (ChIP) is an experimental method used to study protein-DNA interactions, involving immunoprecipitation of protein-antibody complexes and subsequent DNA purification and quantification.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-02c41952a3f79a76f3315858bb8a14bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8dfde3b4ec67624c5a1e8f788a0f0311&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a7dd7d21dd9a5aa2ba54defd650b8ebd</data>
  <data key="d4">Stress-induced β cell early senescence confers protection against type 1 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d5">1778564568</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">20</data>
  <data key="d8">ATF6 / β-Cells / Chromatin Immunoprecipitation</data>
  <data key="d9">0.00123335</data>
  <data key="d10">0.00368095</data>
  <data key="d11">0.0006198</data>
</node>
<node id="Hspa5">
  <data key="d0">Hspa5</data>
  <data key="d1">Tissue</data>
  <data key="d2">Hspa5 is a canonical target gene of sXBP1, used as a control in ChIP-qPCR experiments to validate sXBP1 binding.&lt;SEP&gt;Hspa5 is a gene target region amplified by qPCR using specific forward (5'-GGTGGCATGAACCAACCAG-3') and reverse (5'-GCTTATATATCCTCCCCGC-3') primers.&lt;SEP&gt;mRNA levels increase in kidney cortex with ageing.&lt;SEP&gt;HSPA5 is a protein folding and ER stress response gene with higher expression in CR state 2 beta cells.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-02c41952a3f79a76f3315858bb8a14bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c3838ae3de5236c272eda0072cc83f4e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ce1a7b385e0f22ca823c850de9bf8a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f02465fe113dd488219949222d1430e5</data>
  <data key="d4">Stress-induced β cell early senescence confers protection against type 1 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d5">1778564569</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">20</data>
  <data key="d8">ATF6 / β-Cells / Chromatin Immunoprecipitation</data>
  <data key="d9">0.00011911</data>
  <data key="d10">3.9e-07</data>
  <data key="d11">0.00058326</data>
</node>
<node id="INS1 832/3 Cells">
  <data key="d0">INS1 832/3 Cells</data>
  <data key="d1">Organism</data>
  <data key="d2">INS1 832/3 cells are a cell line used to confirm specific immunoprecipitation of endogenous sXBP1 in the study.&lt;SEP&gt;INS1 832/3 cells are a rat pancreatic beta-cell line maintained in RPMI 1640 medium and used in experiments at passages 25–40.&lt;SEP&gt;INS1 832/3 cells are a cell line used in transfection experiments involving Lipofectamine 2000 and various vectors.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-02c41952a3f79a76f3315858bb8a14bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9e53f09e3b38fb66b0f093b0768d32a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c3838ae3de5236c272eda0072cc83f4e</data>
