<node id="GFP">
  <data key="d0">GFP</data>
  <data key="d1">Protein</data>
  <data key="d2">GFP (Green Fluorescent Protein) was overexpressed as a control in EMSA experiments to confirm that transfection alone did not cause changes in Cdkn1a oligo shift.&lt;SEP&gt;GFP is a vector used in transfection experiments with INS1 832/3 cells.&lt;SEP&gt;GFP gene was used to replace the Mafb gene in Mafb-Gfp knock-in/knockout mice for lineage tracing and functional studies.&lt;SEP&gt;Green fluorescent protein used as a reporter in the TIGER transgenic mouse model to illuminate extracellular vesicle sources.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-02c41952a3f79a76f3315858bb8a14bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8dfde3b4ec67624c5a1e8f788a0f0311&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-222f634a871d4f5fd5cffac2fce0d698&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5f6e43723dd8061d1a0532981e4a43b2</data>
  <data key="d4">Stress-induced β cell early senescence confers protection against type 1 diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Exploring Large MAF Transcription Factors: Functions, Pathology, and Mouse Models with Point Mutations.&lt;SEP&gt;Exploring senescence as a modifier of β cell extracellular vesicles in type 1 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d5">1778568423</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">20</data>
  <data key="d8">ATF6 / β-Cells / Chromatin Immunoprecipitation</data>
