  <data key="d1">Organism</data>
  <data key="d2">NIT1 cells are NOD mouse-derived cells used as an in vitro model to study early senescence, PASP markers, and β-cell survival upon UPR deficiency.&lt;SEP&gt;NIT1 cells are a cell line used in experiments to investigate macrophage migration, p21 inhibition, and LIF expression.&lt;SEP&gt;NIT1 cells are a cell line purchased from ATCC (#CRL-2055), maintained in high-glucose DMEM medium and used at passages 20–35.&lt;SEP&gt;NIT1 cells are a cell line used in conditioned media collection experiments, treated with various drugs including Ceapin-A7 and p21 inhibitor.</data>
