<node id="Ceapin-A7">
  <data key="d0">Ceapin-A7</data>
  <data key="d1">Method</data>
  <data key="d2">Ceapin-A7 is a specific inhibitor of ATF6 used in INS1 832/3 cell experiments to study ATF6's role in regulating Cdkn1a expression.&lt;SEP&gt;Ceapin-A7 is a pharmacological treatment used in NIT1 cells to upregulate p21 and mimic aspects of cellular senescence, promoting macrophage migration.&lt;SEP&gt;Ceapin-A7 is a chemical compound used to inhibit ATF6, inducing macrophage migration and LIF expression in NIT1 cells.&lt;SEP&gt;A pharmacological inhibitor of ATF6 used in human β-cell and islet experiments, resulting in increased CDKN1A expression and PASP markers.&lt;SEP&gt;Ceapin-A7 is a chemical compound used at 15μM to treat human islets in experimental procedures, targeting ATF6 signaling.&lt;SEP&gt;A reagent (Sigma, #SML2330) used in the study.&lt;SEP&gt;Ceapin-A7 is a drug used at 6μM concentration to treat NIT1 cells in conditioned media collection experiments.</data>
