<node id="UC2288">
  <data key="d0">UC2288</data>
  <data key="d1">Method</data>
  <data key="d2">UC2288 is a chemical inhibitor of p21 used in ex vivo studies on isolated islets to investigate the biological significance of p21.&lt;SEP&gt;UC2288 is a pharmacological inhibitor of p21 used in NIT1 cells to demonstrate that p21 plays a role in macrophage recruitment induced by Ceapin-A7.&lt;SEP&gt;UC2288 is a pharmacological inhibitor used to inhibit p21 in NIT1 cells.&lt;SEP&gt;A p21 inhibitor (Sigma, #532813) used in the study.&lt;SEP&gt;UC2288 is a p21 inhibitor used at 2.5μM concentration to treat NIT1 cells in conditioned media collection experiments.</data>
