<node id="Atf6β−/− Mice">
  <data key="d0">Atf6β−/− Mice</data>
  <data key="d1">Organism</data>
  <data key="d2">Atf6β−/− mice are a genetically modified knockout mouse model characterized by β-cell-specific deletion of the Atf6 gene, designed primarily to investigate the role of ATF6 — a key component of the unfolded protein response (UPR) — in β-cell biology and type 1 diabetes (T1D) development.

These mice are generated on the NOD (Non-Obese Diabetic) background by mating NOD Atf6fl/fl mice with NOD Ins2CreERT mice, resulting in β-cell-specific loss of ATF6 function. As a consequence of this targeted deletion, Atf6β−/− mice exhibit a notably reduced incidence of diabetes, decreased insulitis, and preserved β-cell function compared to control counterparts.

At the cellular and molecular level, Atf6β−/− mice display several distinctive phenotypic features, including reduced SA-β-galactosidase (SA-β-gal) activity, reduced cell size, and altered expression of senescence-associated markers such as p21. These characteristics make the model particularly useful for studying early β-cell senescence and the intersection of UPR deficiency with senescent phenotypes.

In terms of immune microenvironment, Atf6β−/− mice are protected from diabetes and show increased infiltration of M2 macrophages in the islets. This model has also been used to study macrophage recruitment dynamics in the pancreatic islet environment. In experimental settings, female Atf6β−/− mice have been employed as an in vivo model to assess the effects of LIF neutralizing antibody or IgG control injections.

Additionally, RNA sequencing datasets derived from Atf6β−/− mice have been utilized to identify common paracrine senescence-associated secretory phenotype (PASP) genes, further extending the utility of this model in transcriptomic and senescence-related research contexts.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e74e3fadd5f43dbb51005345f56dec5c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea9634b81ecdb467a2b26648246e5b5c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-23c7b10bcd96e1a6a6ea025a643b2b01&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40e720fe9c9efb2c2c2dedf6638ae8f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8dfde3b4ec67624c5a1e8f788a0f0311&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c625d74e06abff522b8eb3d76df6ae32&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c3838ae3de5236c272eda0072cc83f4e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f797167cb0737019ee587d4f66f13530&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40bbefacfceda2b6335fdb6310e2f7ae</data>
