<node id="PERK">
  <data key="d0">PERK</data>
  <data key="d1">Biological Process</data>
  <data key="d2">PERK (protein kinase RNA-like ER kinase) is an ER-membrane localized protein that attenuates translation of most mRNAs while specifically inducing translation of the transcription factor Atf4.&lt;SEP&gt;A third sensor arm of the UPR explicitly noted as not being included in the UPR-deficient context studied in the text; distinct from ATF6 and IRE1α branches.&lt;SEP&gt;PERK is an arm of the UPR that is not included in the UPR-deficient models described in the study.</data>
