<node id="Type 1 Diabetes (T1D)">
  <data key="d0">Type 1 Diabetes (T1D)</data>
  <data key="d1">Biological Process</data>
  <data key="d2">An autoimmune disease in which β-cells are exposed to significant stress and require adaptive responses to survive; associated with insulitis and β-cell apoptosis.&lt;SEP&gt;Type 1 diabetes (T1D) is a disease resulting from insulin insufficiency due to near-complete autoimmune destruction of insulin-producing pancreatic β-cells.&lt;SEP&gt;Type 1 diabetes is an autoimmune disease characterized by immune cell infiltration of pancreatic islets and β-cell destruction, studied in the context of Atf6 deletion.&lt;SEP&gt;Type 1 Diabetes (T1D) is an autoimmune disease in which β-cells are destroyed; M2 macrophage transfer can prevent it in NOD mice, and UPR signaling is diminished in β-cells of T1D individuals.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ea9634b81ecdb467a2b26648246e5b5c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c625d74e06abff522b8eb3d76df6ae32&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18ba6ed2ada6acd593e0a5d2f036f947&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-353703794bc6a501b5c11f84a2064293</data>
