<node id="p21Cip1">
  <data key="d0">p21Cip1</data>
  <data key="d1">Protein</data>
  <data key="d2">p21Cip1 is a cyclin-dependent kinase inhibitor that mediates senescence-associated stable growth arrest and drives the early senescence program in β-cells upon deletion of Atf6α or Ire1α.&lt;SEP&gt;Cyclin-dependent kinase inhibitor p21, frequently upregulated in senescent beta cells in mouse and human; validated antibodies are available.&lt;SEP&gt;p21Cip1 (encoded by CDKN1A) is a cyclin-dependent kinase inhibitor involved in cell cycle arrest and senescence, marking a distinct subpopulation of senescent beta cells.&lt;SEP&gt;Cyclin-dependent kinase inhibitor p21, frequently upregulated in senescent beta cells in mouse and human; validated antibodies are available.&lt;SEP&gt;p21Cip1 (encoded by CDKN1A) is a cyclin-dependent kinase inhibitor involved in cell cycle arrest and senescence, marking a distinct subpopulation of senescent beta cells.&lt;SEP&gt;P21CIP1 is a cyclin-dependent kinase (CDK) inhibitor encoded by the gene CDKN1A (also referred to as Cdkn1a). It is widely recognized as a major driver of cellular senescence across a broad range of cell types, with particular relevance in pancreatic beta cells.

In the context of beta cell biology, P21CIP1 plays multifaceted roles encompassing the DNA damage response, cell cycle inhibition, and the regulation of beta cell survival and proliferation. It is notably upregulated during the early stages of senescence and in response to DNA damage, positioning it as an early molecular marker and mediator of these stress-associated pathways.

P21CIP1 is also expressed in a distinct population of senescent beta cells that exhibit the senescence-associated secretory phenotype (SASP). Importantly, its expression is not affected by the genetic deletion of p16INK4a-expressing senescent cells, suggesting that P21CIP1-driven senescence operates through a pathway that is at least partially independent of p16INK4a-mediated senescence.

A notable sex-dependent difference has been observed in the induction of P21CIP1 in response to DNA damage in human islets. Specifically, DNA damage induces P21CIP1 expression approximately 1.5-fold in male donors, whereas the induction is substantially greater in female donors, reaching approximately 12-fold. This sex-dependent magnitude of response highlights potential biological differences in how male and female islets engage P21CIP1-mediated stress pathways, though the precise mechanistic basis for this disparity remains an area of ongoing investigation.&lt;SEP&gt;Cyclin-dependent kinase inhibitor that controls muscle differentiation at the myogenin step together with P57KIP2.&lt;SEP&gt;CDK inhibitor protein encoded by CDKN1A, upregulated in senescent beta cells; marker of cell cycle arrest.&lt;SEP&gt;CDK inhibitor protein encoded by CDKN1A, upregulated in senescent beta cells; marker of cell cycle arrest.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ea9634b81ecdb467a2b26648246e5b5c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5dc00b5dc127eca5ff2847cc45392453&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-add59972a262992e4bde6910520c0cdb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8304b17dc893b8c9bfb7bfdb03703396&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b861cee193cad9e0f142051047e83aae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-58c0cbc7de7a8a1060e8f1608271a28c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ef7d4c1829099c6037d8b8b7a83c3cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fac258601b299e0c883e8e1c4a3030d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf5aeca434044079720fd4ae2d32c9b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-58ad905d1d148d4bbfe7ce4c29566fc6</data>
  <data key="d4">Stress-induced β cell early senescence confers protection against type 1 diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Pancreatic β-cell senescence in diabetes: mechanisms, markers and therapies.</data>
