  <data key="d1">Method</data>
  <data key="d2">Tamoxifen is a drug administered to mouse pups during postnatal days 1–3 to achieve β-cell-specific deletion of Atf6 prior to insulitis in the Atf6β−/− NOD mouse model.&lt;SEP&gt;Tamoxifen is a drug administered to mouse pups during postnatal days 1–3 to achieve β-cell-specific deletion of Atf6 prior to insulitis.&lt;SEP&gt;Tamoxifen (T5648; Sigma-Aldrich) is a compound dissolved in corn oil and used to induce Cre recombinase activity in mouse models via intraperitoneal or intragastric injection.</data>
