<node id="IRE1α">
  <data key="d0">IRE1α</data>
  <data key="d1">Biological Process</data>
  <data key="d2">IRE1α is the alpha isoform of IRE1 whose activation leads to specific splicing of XBP1 mRNA; pharmacological inhibition of IRE1α activity prevented T1D in preclinical models.&lt;SEP&gt;Another UPR sensor branch studied alongside ATF6; its β-cell-specific loss (Ire1αβ−/−) also leads to upregulation of senescence markers.&lt;SEP&gt;IRE1α is a UPR sensor whose loss in β-cells leads to increased p21 expression and features of cellular senescence.&lt;SEP&gt;A UPR sensor whose hyperactivity during early disease stages may exacerbate β-cell stress; its deletion confers a greater degree of diabetes protection than ATF6 deletion.&lt;SEP&gt;IRE1α is a key component of the unfolded protein response pathway, targeted for conditional deletion in mouse models using floxed alleles and Cre recombinase.&lt;SEP&gt;A UPR gene encoding inositol-requiring protein-1 alpha; deletion in β-cells of NOD mice prior to insulitis contributes to early senescence and altered β-cell secretome.</data>
