<node id="Islet Inflammation">
  <data key="d0">Islet Inflammation</data>
  <data key="d1">Biological Process</data>
  <data key="d2">Inflammatory process within pancreatic islets that is resolved through M2 macrophage-mediated anti-inflammatory responses following β-cell early senescence.&lt;SEP&gt;Islet inflammation refers to the inflammatory condition within pancreatic islets during T1D progression, which is resolved following M2 macrophage recruitment in β-cells lacking Atf6α or Ire1α.&lt;SEP&gt;Inflammatory process in pancreatic islets promoted by beta cell DNA damage response in type 1 diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Inflammatory process in islets thought to contribute to impaired beta cell function during aging.&lt;SEP&gt;Inflammatory process in pancreatic islets promoted by beta-cell DNA damage response in Type 1 diabetes.</data>
