</node>
<node id="UPR (Unfolded Protein Response)">
  <data key="d0">UPR (Unfolded Protein Response)</data>
  <data key="d1">Biological Process</data>
  <data key="d2">The UPR is a cellular stress response pathway involving sensors such as IRE1α and ATF6β that regulates p21 expression through direct and indirect mechanisms.&lt;SEP&gt;The UPR is a cellular stress response pathway whose deficiency in β-cells triggers early senescence mechanisms and influences macrophage recruitment in the islet microenvironment.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-23c7b10bcd96e1a6a6ea025a643b2b01&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c3838ae3de5236c272eda0072cc83f4e</data>
  <data key="d4">Stress-induced β cell early senescence confers protection against type 1 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d5">1778564582</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">20</data>
  <data key="d8">ATF6 / β-Cells / Chromatin Immunoprecipitation</data>
  <data key="d9">0.00014565</data>
  <data key="d10">0.00013095</data>
  <data key="d11">0.0177815</data>
</node>
<node id="Early Senescence">
  <data key="d0">Early Senescence</data>
  <data key="d1">Biological Process</data>
  <data key="d2">Early senescence is a transient senescence mechanism triggered when β-cell UPR is compromised, associated with a unique secretome that augments M2 macrophage recruitment and diminishes inflammation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-23c7b10bcd96e1a6a6ea025a643b2b01</data>
  <data key="d4">Stress-induced β cell early senescence confers protection against type 1 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d5">1778564583</data>
