<node id="Terminal Senescence">
  <data key="d0">Terminal Senescence</data>
  <data key="d1">Biological Process</data>
  <data key="d2">Terminal senescence is a late, permanent cell cycle arrest state in β-cells that contributes to T1D pathogenesis, distinct from early senescence.&lt;SEP&gt;An irreversible state of cell cycle arrest characterized by increased cell size and SA-β-gal activity, found to be markedly diminished in β-cells of UPR-deficient NOD mice.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-23c7b10bcd96e1a6a6ea025a643b2b01&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f797167cb0737019ee587d4f66f13530</data>
  <data key="d4">Stress-induced β cell early senescence confers protection against type 1 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d5">1778564583</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">3</data>
  <data key="d8">cellular senescence / CDKN2A / CDKN1A</data>
  <data key="d9">0.00028781</data>
  <data key="d10">0.00094102</data>
  <data key="d11">0.0171673</data>
</node>
<node id="Islet Microenvironment">
  <data key="d0">Islet Microenvironment</data>
  <data key="d1">Tissue</data>
  <data key="d2">The islet microenvironment refers to the pancreatic islets where macrophage recruitment, senescence, and immune responses are studied.&lt;SEP&gt;The local environment surrounding pancreatic islet cells, influenced by senescence.&lt;SEP&gt;The local cellular and molecular environment within pancreatic islets, influenced by senescent beta cell accumulation and SASP.&lt;SEP&gt;The local environment surrounding pancreatic islet cells, influenced by senescence.&lt;SEP&gt;The local cellular and molecular environment within pancreatic islets, influenced by senescent beta cell accumulation and SASP.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-23c7b10bcd96e1a6a6ea025a643b2b01&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9bf309775cbb3bf74509531fe53568a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8f87338453daad7a9a4624ce798bcf6e</data>
