</node>
<node id="C12FDG">
  <data key="d0">C12FDG</data>
  <data key="d1">Molecule</data>
  <data key="d2">C12FDG is a substrate cleaved by SA-β-gal to produce a fluorescent product, serving as a surrogate marker for SA-β-gal activity in senescence studies.&lt;SEP&gt;A substrate cleaved by SA-β-gal to produce a fluorescent product, used as a surrogate marker for SA-β-gal activity.&lt;SEP&gt;C12FDG is a fluorescent substrate sourced from Cayman Chemical used to measure SA-β-galactosidase (SA-β-gal) activity as a marker of cellular senescence in dispersed islet cells.&lt;SEP&gt;Fluorescent substrate used for detecting SA-βgal activity in senescent cells via fluorescence staining.&lt;SEP&gt;Fluorescent substrate used for detecting SA-βgal activity in senescent cells via fluorescence staining.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-23c7b10bcd96e1a6a6ea025a643b2b01&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f797167cb0737019ee587d4f66f13530&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e72d8d21ebb3fc252c498fcbfeed6c1d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5dc00b5dc127eca5ff2847cc45392453</data>
  <data key="d4">Stress-induced β cell early senescence confers protection against type 1 diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Pancreatic β-cell senescence in diabetes: mechanisms, markers and therapies.</data>
