</node>
<node id="G2/M Phase">
  <data key="d0">G2/M Phase</data>
  <data key="d1">Biological Process</data>
  <data key="d2">G2/M phase is a stage of the cell cycle whose proportion is altered in UPR-deficient mice, suggesting changes in cell cycle progression and senescence.&lt;SEP&gt;Cell cycle phases evaluated using pHH3 staining; G2 indicated by punctate staining and M phase by solid nuclear staining in beta cells</data>
