<node id="Flow Cytometry">
  <data key="d0">Flow Cytometry</data>
  <data key="d1">Method</data>
  <data key="d2">Flow cytometry is an immunophenotyping method used to assess immune cell populations in pancreata, spleen, and PLNs of control and knockout mice.&lt;SEP&gt;A technique used to examine cell cycle progression in islets of Atf6β−/− and Ire1αβ−/− mice.&lt;SEP&gt;Flow cytometry is used to investigate the distribution of M1 and M2 macrophages in PLN and pancreata of UPR-deficient mice.&lt;SEP&gt;Flow cytometry method used to detect senescence markers such as p21CIP1 in beta cells.&lt;SEP&gt;Flow cytometry method used to detect senescence markers such as p21CIP1 in beta cells.&lt;SEP&gt;A method applied to address EV heterogeneity and identify senescent cell-derived EVs using surface protein markers.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-40e720fe9c9efb2c2c2dedf6638ae8f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c625d74e06abff522b8eb3d76df6ae32&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c3838ae3de5236c272eda0072cc83f4e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-58ad905d1d148d4bbfe7ce4c29566fc6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-184abd4f45a78238743890eb9d4f8c56</data>
