<node id="CREB">
  <data key="d0">CREB</data>
  <data key="d1">Protein</data>
  <data key="d2">CREB (CRE Binding Protein) is a transcription factor that binds to the CRE element on the Cdkn1a promoter and activates its transcription; its activity is suppressed by ATF6.&lt;SEP&gt;A transcription factor mediating insulinotropic and anti-apoptotic effects of GLP-1 signaling in beta cells, and involved in gene transcription through cAMP-responsive elements.&lt;SEP&gt;CREB is a transcription factor inhibited by the reagent 666-15 in the study.&lt;SEP&gt;CREB mediates up-regulation of APE1 in neurons to repair glutamate-induced oxidative DNA damage.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8dfde3b4ec67624c5a1e8f788a0f0311&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d13aa78bf917b6b3ed2e772b6f010e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40bbefacfceda2b6335fdb6310e2f7ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-735ea17eaeb5e3524d0871e16116e986</data>
  <data key="d4">Stress-induced β cell early senescence confers protection against type 1 diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Safeguarding genomic integrity in beta-cells: implications for beta-cell differentiation, growth, and dysfunction.</data>
