<node id="Hormesis">
  <data key="d0">Hormesis</data>
  <data key="d1">Biological Process</data>
  <data key="d2">A biological phenomenon characterized by a beneficial response to low doses of stress; discussed in relation to resistance to type 2 diabetes mellitus and ER stress in hematopoietic stem cells.&lt;SEP&gt;A biological phenomenon where low-level stress confers protection or benefit, studied in the context of ER stress in hematopoietic stem cells and resistance to type 2 diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;A phenomenon in which low-level stress stimulates adaptive responses that enhance cellular health and resilience to subsequent severe stress, proposed as a mechanism in UPR-deficient NOD mice.&lt;SEP&gt;Hormesis is a phenomenon in which a low level of stress stimulates stress adaptation that enhances cellular and organismal health, rendering them resilient to subsequent and more severe stress.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2d13aa78bf917b6b3ed2e772b6f010e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18ba6ed2ada6acd593e0a5d2f036f947&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f797167cb0737019ee587d4f66f13530&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-353703794bc6a501b5c11f84a2064293</data>
