<node id="Gdf15">
  <data key="d0">Gdf15</data>
  <data key="d1">Biological Process</data>
  <data key="d2">Gdf15 is one of the core PASP markers identified in UPR-deficient mice.&lt;SEP&gt;GDF15, or Growth Differentiation Factor 15, is a multifunctional secreted protein with well-established roles in aging, senescence, inflammation, and tissue homeostasis.

GDF15 is consistently identified as upregulated in human senescence, as detected by both Luminex and RNA-seq methodologies. It is recognized as a key component of the Senescence-Associated Secretory Phenotype (SASP), functioning as an inflammatory molecule secreted by senescent cells. In the context of aging, GDF15 is associated with age-related disease outcomes, particularly in skin aging SASP, and its upregulation in plasma has been linked to increased susceptibility to interstitial lung abnormalities.

Despite its pro-inflammatory SASP associations, GDF15 also exhibits protective functions. Notably, it has been shown to protect against aging-mediated systemic inflammatory responses in both humans and mice, suggesting a regulatory or compensatory anti-inflammatory role in the context of systemic aging. Adding further complexity, GDF15 has also been reported as a negative regulator of cellular senescence specifically in adipose tissue, indicating that its function may be tissue-context dependent.

Beyond its role in senescence, GDF15 acts as a secretory factor through which the senescence-associated tissue microenvironment promotes colon cancer formation, implicating it in tumor-promoting paracrine signaling. Additionally, GDF15 functions as a SASP factor expressed in trophoblasts, where it mediates immune surveillance and tissue remodeling, highlighting its relevance in reproductive and developmental biology.

Collectively, GDF15 represents a pleiotropic factor at the intersection of cellular senescence, aging, inflammation, cancer biology, and tissue remodeling, with context-dependent roles that can be either protective or pathological depending on the tissue and physiological setting.&lt;SEP&gt;GDF15 is a growth factor component of the SASP secreted by senescent beta cells.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c3838ae3de5236c272eda0072cc83f4e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5dc00b5dc127eca5ff2847cc45392453&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-71a6a7a3a4894dbd7d979b7e5766d5a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b773584b36e5b4845bedffea9a1b6add&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca844018665036149579ef01b8f9ec3c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ce1a7b385e0f22ca823c850de9bf8a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a5bb73f6c7980a9f906f42f6e0e9ce27&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ff588c6efe73ecb07c6b95acb392e92&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f25c34949789593e96b7a57ead73f11&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e32fd907a01d621388ff41b9b47bfa34</data>
