<node id="Single-Cell RNA Sequencing">
  <data key="d0">Single-Cell RNA Sequencing</data>
  <data key="d1">Method</data>
  <data key="d2">A technique for transcriptomic analysis of individual cells; applied to mouse pancreatic islets in referenced research.&lt;SEP&gt;Single-cell RNA sequencing (scRNA-seq) is a high-throughput molecular technique used to profile the transcriptomes of individual cells, enabling detailed analysis of gene expression patterns at single-cell resolution. The method has been applied extensively across a wide range of biological contexts, with particular prominence in the study of human pancreatic islets and aging-related biology.

In the context of pancreatic research, single-cell RNA sequencing has been employed to profile gene expression in individual pancreatic islet cells across diverse conditions, including health, type 2 diabetes, and varying sex, race, and disease status. Notably, one large-scale application of the method involved profiling 141,739 pancreatic islet cells across 52 datasets, underscoring its capacity for high-throughput, integrative studies. A specific implementation of the technology includes the 10x Single Cell 3' RNAseq platform, which has been used to capture gene expression profiles in individual islet cells with high sensitivity and scalability.

Beyond pancreatic research, single-cell RNA sequencing has been utilized to investigate aging-associated transcriptional changes. These applications include single-cell analysis of the human pancreas to reveal transcriptional signatures of aging and somatic mutation patterns, as well as studies characterizing aging-associated alterations in mammary epithelia and stroma, postmenopausal fallopian tube, and ovary. The technique has also been applied to identify senescent cerebromicrovascular endothelial cells in the aged mouse brain, demonstrating its utility across tissue types and species.

From a technical standpoint, single-cell RNA sequencing workflows often incorporate quality control steps to ensure data integrity. These include the removal of ambient RNA contamination using tools such as SoupX and the detection of doublets — instances where two cells are captured together — using algorithms such as DoubletFinder. These preprocessing steps are critical for generating reliable, high-resolution transcriptomic data from complex tissue samples.&lt;SEP&gt;Method used to profile gene expression in individual pancreatic islet cells, identifying novel gene sets and beta-cell subpopulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Method used to reveal regulation of endocrine cell alternative splicing in T2D pathogenesis and define molecular basis of beta cell dedifferentiation.&lt;SEP&gt;Single-cell RNA-seq method used to analyze human islets from non-diabetic, prediabetic, and type 2 diabetes donors, revealing progressive beta cell dedifferentiation.&lt;SEP&gt;Single-cell transcriptomic method used to profile mouse and human islet cells, including beta-cell states and responses to diet.&lt;SEP&gt;Single-cell RNA sequencing is used to profile neonatal and adult murine islet cells and human islet cells at single-cell resolution.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-18ba6ed2ada6acd593e0a5d2f036f947&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8f87338453daad7a9a4624ce798bcf6e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b67e26d82684726785f1910ba6919cf0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c5a8121875c37f2659ae345688f6afe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf5aeca434044079720fd4ae2d32c9b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51601485f0924871a988aae2e5ce30bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64b61717ec6764bc92fa7c3c5067d345&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c41ef398df926f1c888f284aff2a98e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d0bf8cd8c8cb69199fb8f9bf6c37e70&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2496631e25b79859522b657da346b58&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da10e6374cdbd3d6e4a07d773cd172d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4e8cbb766d17c90c84d2a9452a51a41e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-10bdc47e4d027606476b48a401061a27&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e181574d19e6f17c0fd64b0feecf8f9e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce72a72ed1aaea72aac97c28374f8f86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c461d96db4bed849ef22472fc2b0cd0</data>
