<node id="Liver Fibrosis">
  <data key="d0">Liver Fibrosis</data>
  <data key="d1">Biological Process</data>
  <data key="d2">A pathological condition characterized by excessive connective tissue deposition in the liver; limited by senescence of activated stellate cells.&lt;SEP&gt;Liver fibrosis susceptibility is worsened by C-MAF deletion in endothelial cells, increasing sensitivity to pro-fibrotic chemical insults.&lt;SEP&gt;Liver fibrosis is limited by senescence of activated hepatic stellate cells.&lt;SEP&gt;A chronic liver disease in which cellular senescence has been widely implicated, with senescence markers found in multiple liver cell types.</data>
