<node id="CDKN1A">
  <data key="d0">CDKN1A</data>
  <data key="d1">Gene</data>
  <data key="d2">CDKN1A (Cyclin-Dependent Kinase Inhibitor 1A) is a gene encoding the protein p21, also referred to as p21Cip1, p21WAF1/Cip1, or P21CIP1. It functions as a cyclin-dependent kinase (CDK) inhibitor — most notably as a CDK2 inhibitor — and plays a central role in cell cycle regulation, cellular senescence, and tumor suppression.

At the molecular level, the CDKN1A promoter contains both a cAMP response element (CRE) and an unfolded protein response element (UPRE, sequence TGACGTG). Its expression is regulated by multiple transcription factors, including CREB, ATF6, and spliced XBP1 (sXBP1), positioning CDKN1A as a key downstream effector of the unfolded protein response (UPR) pathway. Critically, CDKN1A is activated by p53 to halt cell cycle progression, making it a well-established marker of the p53/p21 signaling axis.

CDKN1A/p21 accumulates in senescent cells across a broad range of tissues and biological contexts. It is upregulated in senescent adipocytes, T cells, kidney cells, liver, lung, pancreas, bone marrow, central nervous system, aged ovaries, trophoblasts, beta cells, acinar cells, osteoblasts, and osteocytes. It is also expressed early in fracture response, radiation-induced bone loss, skin aging, and following chemotherapy treatment. Furthermore, its protein levels are elevated in placentas from fetal growth restriction compared to those from normal growth fetuses. CDKN1A has been used in inducible expression systems to identify senescent cells via cell surface markers.

In the context of metabolic disease, highly expressing CDKN1A cells in adipose tissue have been identified as therapeutic targets to alleviate insulin resistance in obesity. In type 1 diabetes (T1D) research, CDKN1A is found significantly upregulated in beta cells of T1D donors and in human beta cell models where UPR signaling is inhibited, underscoring its relevance to beta cell biology. In mouse models, Cdkn1a has been investigated using shRNA knockdown approaches; notably, knockout mice lacking Cdkn1a display normal islet mass, normal beta cell replication rates, and normal function, though p21-deficient mice exhibit increased tumor susceptibility.

Overall, CDKN1A serves as a major and broadly expressed senescence marker and driver of cell cycle arrest, with context-dependent roles in senescence, tumor suppression, metabolic disease, aging, and tissue injury response.&lt;SEP&gt;p21 cyclin-dependent kinase inhibitor; part of the canonical p53/p21 senescence pathway and used as a marker for senescent cells in mouse models.&lt;SEP&gt;Cell cycle inhibitor p21, induced by p53 signaling to enforce cell cycle arrest following DNA damage.&lt;SEP&gt;CDKN1A (p21) is a senescence-associated gene whose mRNA expression is measured in beta cells using FISH; CR reduces its total expression.&lt;SEP&gt;Gene encoding p21, detected by RNAscope multiplex fluorescent assay in FFPE pancreas slices using specific probes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f797167cb0737019ee587d4f66f13530&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5dc00b5dc127eca5ff2847cc45392453&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-add59972a262992e4bde6910520c0cdb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-58ad905d1d148d4bbfe7ce4c29566fc6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-58c0cbc7de7a8a1060e8f1608271a28c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c72c144fce7d5c94557af956a559639&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ef7d4c1829099c6037d8b8b7a83c3cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fac258601b299e0c883e8e1c4a3030d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40bbefacfceda2b6335fdb6310e2f7ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d3b1de44d6b73a10793a43351e18e6e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-71a6a7a3a4894dbd7d979b7e5766d5a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-25d34b513b15180c8a2d7b57ae829067&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ca3e5da7a4fe15854dde6289fd15667&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b773584b36e5b4845bedffea9a1b6add&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca844018665036149579ef01b8f9ec3c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ce1a7b385e0f22ca823c850de9bf8a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a5bb73f6c7980a9f906f42f6e0e9ce27&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a471400d67fa8643230222fb3576486&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d7ef738c0840825512b2cb7af5b7c3f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-682da4208f0eb800bc5523bd70a84eb7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f25c34949789593e96b7a57ead73f11&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-732255e9544dde6a7dbc319c61cd8e1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-58f0193e389064a60d513f13c5cad52b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56d5ffe02105b1bd6d77faab9c812433&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-75f39153d9f864070e17a74724a6c8c6</data>
  <data key="d4">Stress-induced β cell early senescence confers protection against type 1 diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Pancreatic β-cell senescence in diabetes: mechanisms, markers and therapies.&lt;SEP&gt;SenNet recommendations for detecting senescent cells in different tissues.&lt;SEP&gt;Exploring senescence as a modifier of β cell extracellular vesicles in type 1 diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Safeguarding genomic integrity in beta-cells: implications for beta-cell differentiation, growth, and dysfunction.&lt;SEP&gt;Calorie restriction increases insulin sensitivity to promote beta cell homeostasis and longevity in mice.</data>
