<node id="DDR">
  <data key="d0">DDR</data>
  <data key="d1">Biological Process</data>
  <data key="d2">DNA damage response, one of the adaptive response pathways found significantly upregulated in residual β-cells of T1D donors.&lt;SEP&gt;DDR (DNA Damage Response) is a cellular stress response that, along with antioxidant response and early senescence, can be part of a hormetic response to achieve resolution of stress and re-establishment of homeostasis.&lt;SEP&gt;DNA damage response pathway contributing to beta-cell senescence and dysfunction in T1D and T2D contexts.</data>
