<node id="NGN3">
  <data key="d0">Ngn3</data>
  <data key="d1">Biological Process</data>
  <data key="d2">Ngn3 is a transcription factor that, when co-electroporated with MafA, results in the development of more organized cell clusters containing both insulin- and glucagon-producing cells.&lt;SEP&gt;Ngn3 is a transcription factor expressed in a small number of islet hormone-negative progenitor cells and is part of a subset of transcription factors, including MafA and Pdx1, used in reprogramming adult acinar cells to β-like cells.&lt;SEP&gt;Ngn3 (NGN3) marks islet progenitor cells that are distinct from duct progenitors, serving as direct evidence for the pancreatic lineage.&lt;SEP&gt;Ngn3 is a transcription factor involved in early islet cell specification, representing processes not affected by MafB regulation.&lt;SEP&gt;Ngn3 is a transcription factor involved in islet cell progenitor specification and used in combination with MafA and Pdx1 to reprogram pancreatic acinar cells to β-like cells.&lt;SEP&gt;Ngn3 is a gene marker associated with β cell dedifferentiation that is not detectable in MafA∆β mice of either sex.&lt;SEP&gt;Ngn3 is a transcription factor expressed in endocrine progenitor cells from which pancreatic Gast+ cells are derived during development.</data>
