<node id="SLC2A2">
  <data key="d0">Slc2a2</data>
  <data key="d1">Biological Process</data>
  <data key="d2">Slc2a2 is a gene involved in glucose sensing that is activated by MafB in mature endocrine function.&lt;SEP&gt;Slc2a2 is a candidate gene whose mRNA changes were independently verified in E18.5 MafB−/− and MafAΔPanc;MafB−/− pancreata by quantitative RT-PCR.&lt;SEP&gt;Slc2a2 is a mutual target gene of MafA and MafB that is significant to β-cell function.&lt;SEP&gt;Slc2a2 is a glucose transporter gene involved in glucose sensing, with reduced mRNA and protein expression in 3-week-old MafaΔpanc islets, required for normal β-cell function.&lt;SEP&gt;A gene involved in glucose sensing in β-cells, regulated by MafB at E18.5 and by MafA in 3-month-old islets.&lt;SEP&gt;Slc2a2 encodes the major β-cell glucose transporter GLUT and shows decreased expression in MafaΔpanc islet β-cells, contributing to impaired glucose signaling.</data>
