<node id="RBP4">
  <data key="d0">RBP4</data>
  <data key="d1">Gene</data>
  <data key="d2">Rbp4 is a gene whose mRNA expression is significantly increased in MafB−/− and MafAΔPanc;MafB−/− mutant pancreata.&lt;SEP&gt;Rbp4 is a gene for which a cDNA plasmid was obtained to generate a probe for in situ hybridization assays in pancreatic studies.&lt;SEP&gt;Rbp4 is a gene/protein that contributes to the pathogenesis of type 2 diabetes by causing systemic insulin resistance; it is released from adipocytes and is also produced in the liver. Its mRNA expression is upregulated in MafB−/− and MafAΔPanc mutants.&lt;SEP&gt;Rbp4 is a gene/protein whose mRNA expression is elevated in MafAΔPanc islets and whose protein is found specifically in somatostatin-producing δ-cells; it acts as an effector of insulin secretion and insulin resistance.&lt;SEP&gt;Rbp4 is a candidate gene whose mRNA changes were independently verified in E18.5 MafB−/− and MafAΔPanc;MafB−/− pancreata by quantitative RT-PCR.&lt;SEP&gt;Rbp4 is a gene/protein produced from rat islet cells that inhibits glucose-stimulated insulin secretion, is principally expressed in human islet δ-cells, and attenuates insulin-induced phosphorylation of insulin receptor substrate-1 in human adipocytes.&lt;SEP&gt;Gene whose expression negatively correlates with exocytosis in beta cells of non-diabetic donors, identified via Patch-seq.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5f82db25373e25b34bbbcfebc1c0f861&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f7f8610c162035d52f2edbe846e8a97&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff8c5dc48dde6c3ccfdc01c9e025403d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e517ac1160d78d9b935ab9b9913bf46a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41e9c4875e9ee2b378c620275d81fe7e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ddb7aaa2476f3163b5c3de684504f42b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cba0d7fafdd66d2ffb133e04939d15f0</data>
