<node id="GCK">
  <data key="d0">GCK</data>
  <data key="d1">Gene</data>
  <data key="d2">GCK (Glucokinase) is a gene encoding the rate-limiting enzyme glucokinase, which plays a central role in glycolytic flux and glucose metabolism, particularly within pancreatic cells.

In the context of beta-cell biology, GCK activation has been shown to induce beta-cell replication, DNA double-strand breaks (DSBs), p53 activation, and ultimately cell death, with increased glycolysis leading to chronic membrane depolarization. GCK also demonstrates lower expression in CR state 2 beta cells, suggesting reduced glycolytic flux in that cellular state. Additionally, Gck has been previously associated with MafA transcriptional control in INS1 β-cells, though it was not detected in MafB−/− or MafAΔPanc;MafB−/− profiling at embryonic day E18.5.

GCK is also a well-established type 2 diabetes (T2D) risk locus. Its T2D-associated genetic variants, including the index variant rs116913033, overlap with differentially accessible chromatin regions in a sex-specific manner. Specifically, these differentially accessible chromatin peaks are observed in male delta cells but not in female delta cells, highlighting a notable sex-dependent regulatory pattern at this locus. This male-specific chromatin accessibility at the GCK locus in delta cells has been noted across multiple analyses, consistently distinguishing GCK as a classical T2D variant gene with sexually dimorphic epigenomic characteristics.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ddb7aaa2476f3163b5c3de684504f42b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dfd4ac2599dc6d5dc028ad0e83ccf82f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f3f8e2c47cb96d65689fa504202cd0f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76049b85888e8e904e7c01de9740d34f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db03a7d3c861658f2beac422f86b21ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f02465fe113dd488219949222d1430e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ea44d17d2377f3dd0f15239a73e15e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-822d03d11fbf61e2a25591e2663ef1ca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2efc110efa119e343b95df1abbd0a327</data>
