<node id="GLUT2">
  <data key="d0">GLUT2</data>
  <data key="d1">Gene</data>
  <data key="d2">A glucose transporter protein detected by rabbit α-Glut2 antibody (supplied by Chemicon) in immunostaining of pancreatic sections.&lt;SEP&gt;Glut2 (glucose transporter type 2) is expressed in epithelial cells of the developing rat pancreas from which beta cells arise.&lt;SEP&gt;A key β-cell gene whose expression is reduced upon deletion of MafB, affecting normal β-cell development.&lt;SEP&gt;Glucose transporter 2 gene directly regulated by c-MAF in the context of diabetic nephropathy.&lt;SEP&gt;Target gene of MAFA identified through gene expression analysis in pancreatic islets of Mafa-knockout ICR mice.&lt;SEP&gt;GLUT2 is a glucose transporter expressed in the proximal tubules of kidneys, regulated by C-MAF.</data>
