<node id="P16">
  <data key="d0">P16</data>
  <data key="d1">Protein</data>
  <data key="d2">P16, also known as p16INK4a or p16Ink4a, is a cyclin-dependent kinase inhibitor and cell-cycle inhibitory protein encoded by the CDKN2A gene. It plays a central role in regulating the cell cycle by inhibiting cyclin-dependent kinases, thereby promoting cell cycle arrest.

P16 is prominently associated with cellular senescence, functioning as an early initiator of cellular arrest during the onset of this process. It is activated during senescence and has been specifically implicated in the progression of senescence induced by MAFAS64F. As a hallmark marker of senescent cells, P16 expression is notably upregulated in senescent beta cells, making it a widely recognized indicator of the senescent state in pancreatic islet biology.

In the context of islet biology, P16INK4a contributes to an age-dependent decline in islet regenerative potential. Its induction of senescence in beta cells is thought to underlie the diminishing capacity of pancreatic islets to regenerate with advancing age. Additionally, P16 has been observed as a senescence marker protein in ERCC1 hypomorphic mutant beta cells, a model associated with accelerated aging and DNA repair deficiency, further reinforcing its role as a reliable biomarker of cellular senescence across different biological contexts.

Overall, P16 serves both as a functional mediator of cell cycle arrest and as a molecular marker of senescence, with particular relevance to beta cell aging, islet regeneration, and age-related decline in pancreatic function.&lt;SEP&gt;Also known as INK4a; protects against dysfunctional telomere-induced ATR-dependent DNA damage responses.&lt;SEP&gt;A senescence marker upregulated during nucleolar stress-induced beta cell senescence.&lt;SEP&gt;Established senescence marker protein whose levels are significantly increased in beta-TC-6 cells following CX-5461 exposure.&lt;SEP&gt;A senescence-associated protein (cyclin-dependent kinase inhibitor) whose expression is elevated following TIF-IA depletion in beta cells, serving as a marker of cellular senescence.&lt;SEP&gt;P16 is a senescence marker whose elevated expression was observed following nucleolar stress-induced beta cell senescence.&lt;SEP&gt;Gene (p16-positive) used to identify senescent cells for clearance to rejuvenate aged brain immune cell landscape in mice.&lt;SEP&gt;Protein encoded by CDKN2A, serving as a beta cell senescence and aging marker whose expression is reduced under caloric restriction.&lt;SEP&gt;Protein product of CDKN2A gene, detected by RNAscope and quantified per beta cell area as a senescence marker.&lt;SEP&gt;Cyclin-dependent kinase inhibitor and senescence marker; markedly increased in pancreatic islets of HFHC diet mice.&lt;SEP&gt;p16 is a senescence marker protein whose expression is induced by CX-5461 and substantially impaired by co-incubation with KU60019 in beta cells.&lt;SEP&gt;Senescence marker protein whose expression is elevated in beta cells and primary islets following nucleolar stress induced by CX-5461.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9977f67772ceb665bdd71b221a2d4234&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa2caaffb8c37fe000f2af35e115fc27&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9bdc00ebaa404f286432a974cec96702&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8c7bb3e4a69884a1b79485b95f6f502&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bdd484417981e099a8f308ba0994bcaa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-72bf1fbaf7a329c364247108f8b30408&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f008854d459401e11c35e6bd2541318&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93bb74bfaf0604b4b9f891e16fc9f0ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ce4f6e2d90d0c06e4549d7d45037298&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f082082b0871749ee637b1571aa95c0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9977f67772ceb665bdd71b221a2d4234&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa2caaffb8c37fe000f2af35e115fc27&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c5a8121875c37f2659ae345688f6afe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56d5ffe02105b1bd6d77faab9c812433&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-364a12c675ebfd67c468ab6fc47e6696&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a0590fd9be1db550e8a84c0781e8955&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-787de2a35f76e08d5b7cddadbcc01954&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e33cd1d99c96a7f6ffdd0fbea902670</data>
  <data key="d4">Sex-biased islet β cell dysfunction is caused by the MODY MAFA S64F variant by inducing premature aging and senescence in males.&lt;SEP&gt;Pancreatic β-cell senescence in diabetes: mechanisms, markers and therapies.&lt;SEP&gt;Safeguarding genomic integrity in beta-cells: implications for beta-cell differentiation, growth, and dysfunction.&lt;SEP&gt;Nucleolar stress facilitates islet β cell senescence via hijacking the DNA damage response pathways.</data>
  <data key="d5">1778571122</data>
