<node id="V-MAF">
  <data key="d0">V-MAF</data>
  <data key="d1">Protein</data>
  <data key="d2">Oncogene discovered in the avian transforming retrovirus AS42 that causes musculoaponeurotic fibrosarcoma in chickens; cellular homologs include large MAF transcription factors.&lt;SEP&gt;A viral oncogene encoding a leucine zipper motif, representing the viral form of the MAF transcription factor.&lt;SEP&gt;v-maf is a viral oncogene that encodes a leucine zipper motif and is carried by the avian transforming retrovirus AS42.&lt;SEP&gt;V-maf is a viral oncogene from which the Maf transcription factor family derives its name, capable of inducing musculoaponeurotic fibrosarcoma in chickens.&lt;SEP&gt;v-MAF is a viral oncogene used as a homology screening target through which MAFB was isolated.</data>
