  <data key="d2">Point mutation in MAFB (p.Pro59Leu) found in mouse models that simulates features of human diseases.&lt;SEP&gt;MAFB p.Pro59Leu is a mutation identified in the transcriptional activation domain of MAFB associated with human disease.&lt;SEP&gt;MAFB point mutation c.176C&gt;T (p.Pro59Leu) found in MCTO patients, occurring at the phosphorylation site of the transcriptional activation region, causing abnormal phosphorylation and inhibiting MAFB degradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Mutation c.176C&gt;T (p.Pro59Leu) at the phosphorylation site of MAFB transcriptional activation region, inhibiting MAFB degradation and causing MCTO.</data>
