<node id="endothelial cell">
  <data key="d0">endothelial cell</data>
  <data key="d1">Cell Type</data>
  <data key="d2">Endothelial cells are a broadly distributed vascular cell type that line blood vessels and play critical roles in vascular biology, organ development, and disease. They are found across multiple tissues, including the liver, lung, aorta, central nervous system, bone marrow, pancreas, and ovaries, each context reflecting distinct functional and molecular characteristics.

In the pancreas, endothelial cells represent a non-endocrine cell population identified through single-cell multiome sequencing and snATAC-seq clustering of pancreatic islets. They are characterized by the marker genes PECAM1, VWF, and ESM1, the last of which was specifically identified through snATAC-seq cluster analysis based on gene activity. These cells are functionally enriched in pathways related to endothelial cell migration and angiogenesis within the islet microenvironment. Importantly, islet endothelial cells harbor differentially accessible chromatin regions that overlap with type 2 diabetes (T2D) risk variants regulating the transcription factors HNF1A and NEUROG3. This overlap is observed specifically in males but not females, suggesting a sex-specific role for endothelial cells in the genetic regulation of pancreatic function.

In the liver, endothelial cells of the sinusoid require the transcription factor C-MAF for normal development. Specific deletion of C-MAF in these cells inhibits liver sinusoid development and induces aberrant postnatal liver hematopoiesis, underscoring the essential role of endothelial cell identity in maintaining proper hepatic architecture and hematopoietic regulation.

A prominent theme in endothelial cell biology is their susceptibility to senescence and aging-related damage. Endothelial cells are more vulnerable to aging-induced DNA damage and telomere dysfunction compared to vascular smooth muscle cells, and they exhibit senescence-associated markers in the aorta during mouse aging. Under short-term sustained hyperglycemia, endothelial cells develop an archetypal senescence-associated secretory phenotype (SASP), linking metabolic stress to vascular dysfunction. Elevated SASP factors have also been detected in endothelial cells from Alzheimer's disease tissues, and senescence markers are observed in endothelial cells of the central nervous system, bone marrow, liver, and lung. In post-menopausal human ovaries, endothelial cells express IGFBP7 as a SASP-associated gene.

Endothelial cell senescence is further propagated through intercellular communication. Human umbilical vein endothelial cells (HUVECs), when replicatively senescent, release small extracellular vesicles enriched with pro-senescence microRNAs miR-21-5p and miR-217, which are taken up by neighboring endothelial cells to spread the senescent phenotype in a paracrine manner. Given their central role in senescence, endothelial cell senescence transcriptomic profiles have been leveraged to construct a pan-cancer signature applicable for survival prognostication and prediction of immunotherapy response, highlighting their translational relevance in oncology.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-01e46f30e47340f5c5b95376196543ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0be98cbe29b4c692e555154146fad640&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e607d2cca86a6257f1db73bacae2c96&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c0d05211cf3080af14ec050e5cc97ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a7873cb15c71b20e5fc369a6f0ab52a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d3b1de44d6b73a10793a43351e18e6e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-71a6a7a3a4894dbd7d979b7e5766d5a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b773584b36e5b4845bedffea9a1b6add&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a5bb73f6c7980a9f906f42f6e0e9ce27&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a471400d67fa8643230222fb3576486&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c5a8121875c37f2659ae345688f6afe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b02375738a9ebacd53446fec2077ee76&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ff588c6efe73ecb07c6b95acb392e92&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d7bd4bfe81f828dceb60b520d85bcf2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73a24341c9b63bd3b6313252fe6ed4b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dfd4ac2599dc6d5dc028ad0e83ccf82f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f3f8e2c47cb96d65689fa504202cd0f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76049b85888e8e904e7c01de9740d34f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6215695e8bd809fd02cb8b9b7b4123ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-732255e9544dde6a7dbc319c61cd8e1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f02465fe113dd488219949222d1430e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-87d48756321bdf8ef533359c0655a3d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da10e6374cdbd3d6e4a07d773cd172d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ea44d17d2377f3dd0f15239a73e15e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e42c3b77d3170e854edbbc691159609d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-822d03d11fbf61e2a25591e2663ef1ca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2efc110efa119e343b95df1abbd0a327</data>
