  <data key="d1">Disease</data>
  <data key="d2">Rare disease caused by point mutations in MAFA.&lt;SEP&gt;Rare syndrome associated with C-MAF mutations, characterized by intellectual and developmental disabilities; modeled in mutant mice.&lt;SEP&gt;Aymé–Gripp syndrome is caused by mutations in the transcriptional activation domain of C-MAF, resulting in congenital cataracts, deafness, mental retardation, epilepsy, and skeletal dysplasia.&lt;SEP&gt;Rare disease associated with MAF transcription factor point mutations in humans.</data>
