  <data key="d9">0.00019449</data>
  <data key="d10">8.326e-05</data>
  <data key="d11">0.00096806</data>
</node>
<node id="insulinoma">
  <data key="d0">insulinoma</data>
  <data key="d1">Disease</data>
  <data key="d2">Tumor of pancreatic beta cells; associated with MAFA and C-MAF mutations in human patients and mouse models.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulinoma is a tumor type in which MAF transcription factors, including C-MAF, MAFA, and MAFB, are importantly implicated.&lt;SEP&gt;Disease listed as caused by MAF transcription factor point mutations in humans.&lt;SEP&gt;Pancreatic tumor linked to mutations in YY1.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulinoma is a functioning insulin-producing tumor studied for incidence, recurrence, and long-term survival over a 60-year period; estrogen and progesterone receptors are expressed in human insulinomas.&lt;SEP&gt;Insulinoma refers to sporadic insulin-producing tumors that occur more frequently in females, mentioned in the context of gender differences observed in the two families with the p.Ser64Phe MAFA mutation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a91f8726a8e590e31edad7232b84804b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b1a171c046b7e074fd282a07d58cc39&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe670890a826e2e1970f382c46b77260&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db03a7d3c861658f2beac422f86b21ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fffe587d9d8a94d6179115102ef90a2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6854465a5ab40a3dbe223209e2c5cd66</data>
  <data key="d4">Exploring Large MAF Transcription Factors: Functions, Pathology, and Mouse Models with Point Mutations.&lt;SEP&gt;Safeguarding genomic integrity in beta-cells: implications for beta-cell differentiation, growth, and dysfunction.</data>
