<node id="leucine zipper">
  <data key="d0">leucine zipper</data>
  <data key="d1">Protein</data>
  <data key="d2">Structural motif encoded by the viral oncogene v-maf and present in MAF family transcription factors.&lt;SEP&gt;Structural domain present in large MAF transcription factors alongside acidic and basic regions.&lt;SEP&gt;The leucine zipper is a structural element within the basic-leucine-zipper domain of MAFA and MAFB involved in dimerization and relative positioning of the transactivation domain.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-02381256ec5732a712b97ced237c2acb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ed6515ae53fc7e07b1c44a83258c3224&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84ba2041af7b71a5fc2faad1de1c95dd</data>
