<node id="podocyte">
  <data key="d0">podocyte</data>
  <data key="d1">Cell Type</data>
  <data key="d2">Kidney cell type in which MAFB expression protects against focal segmental glomerulosclerosis development.&lt;SEP&gt;Podocytes are glomerular epithelial cells whose differentiation during development and maintenance in adults require MAFB.&lt;SEP&gt;Kidney cell type whose differentiation is impaired by MAFB p.Leu239Pro mutation; requires MAFB for proper development.&lt;SEP&gt;Podocytes are kidney cells that undergo senescence driven by age-related GSK3β overexpression and aggravated by C/EBPα deficiency.&lt;SEP&gt;Kidney cell type in which senescent markers and SASP factors are overexpressed in old mouse kidneys; SERPINE1 overexpression causes podocyte detachment and apoptosis.&lt;SEP&gt;Kidney cell type in which nuclear CDKN2A levels increase in individuals with diabetic nephropathy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-222f634a871d4f5fd5cffac2fce0d698&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ed6515ae53fc7e07b1c44a83258c3224&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe670890a826e2e1970f382c46b77260&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-71a6a7a3a4894dbd7d979b7e5766d5a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b773584b36e5b4845bedffea9a1b6add&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ce1a7b385e0f22ca823c850de9bf8a0</data>
  <data key="d4">Exploring Large MAF Transcription Factors: Functions, Pathology, and Mouse Models with Point Mutations.&lt;SEP&gt;SenNet recommendations for detecting senescent cells in different tissues.</data>
