<node id="multicentric carpotarsal osteolysis">
  <data key="d0">multicentric carpotarsal osteolysis</data>
  <data key="d1">Disease</data>
  <data key="d2">Rare disease caused by mutations clustering in the amino-terminal transcriptional activation domain of MAFB; also abbreviated as MCTO.&lt;SEP&gt;MCTO is a syndrome involving dissolution of bones of the palm and foot, caused by mutations in MAFB including the p.Pro59Leu variant; cases also show hereditary FSGS.&lt;SEP&gt;Pediatric multisystem disorder (MCTO) caused by MAFB S70A mutation, characterized by osteolysis of carpal and tarsal bones, craniofacial deformities, and nephropathy.&lt;SEP&gt;Skeletal disease with unique phenotype associated with MAFB mutations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-222f634a871d4f5fd5cffac2fce0d698&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ed6515ae53fc7e07b1c44a83258c3224&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3384cef9855a1b408c68f7d1ea3153c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f4fecd9e508da1daa4a0d2d27a7e759</data>
  <data key="d4">Exploring Large MAF Transcription Factors: Functions, Pathology, and Mouse Models with Point Mutations.&lt;SEP&gt;Defining unique structural features in the MAFA and MAFB transcription factors that control Insulin gene activity.</data>
  <data key="d5">1778569791</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">0</data>
  <data key="d8">beta cell / MAFA / MAFB</data>
  <data key="d9">0.00049549</data>
  <data key="d10">0.00118432</data>
  <data key="d11">0.00833521</data>
</node>
<node id="focal segmental glomerulosclerosis">
  <data key="d0">focal segmental glomerulosclerosis</data>
  <data key="d1">Disease</data>
  <data key="d2">Kidney disease associated with MAFB mutations; MAFB in podocytes protects against its development; also caused by a mutation in MAFB combined with Duane retraction syndrome.&lt;SEP&gt;Hereditary FSGS (focal segmental glomerulosclerosis) is observed in MCTO patients with MAFB mutations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-222f634a871d4f5fd5cffac2fce0d698&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ed6515ae53fc7e07b1c44a83258c3224</data>
  <data key="d4">Exploring Large MAF Transcription Factors: Functions, Pathology, and Mouse Models with Point Mutations.</data>
  <data key="d5">1778566120</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
