<node id="beta cell differentiation">
  <data key="d0">beta cell differentiation</data>
  <data key="d1">Biological Process</data>
  <data key="d2">Process by which pancreatic beta cells are generated and differentiated, regulated by MAFA, MAFB, and other transcription factors.&lt;SEP&gt;De-, re-, and trans-differentiation of beta cells regulated in various contexts including senescence and diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;De-, re-, and trans-differentiation of beta cells regulated in various contexts including senescence and diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Process by which progenitor cells become mature insulin-producing beta cells, regulated by the DNA damage response.&lt;SEP&gt;Beta cell differentiation involves replication, epigenetic and metabolic reprogramming that can introduce DNA breaks, with the extent of DNA damage shaping cell-fate choices.&lt;SEP&gt;Early developmental process of beta cell formation; implicated by ONECUT1 locus enhancer deletion reducing pancreatic progenitor numbers.</data>
