<node id="MMP2">
  <data key="d0">MMP2</data>
  <data key="d1">Gene</data>
  <data key="d2">MMP2 (Matrix metalloproteinase 2) is a gene encoding the Matrix metalloproteinase 2 protein, which functions as a component of the Senescence-Associated Secretory Phenotype (SASP). It is notably upregulated in senescent mouse beta cells, with its expression and activity detected through multiple complementary methodologies, including quantitative PCR (qPCR), Luminex assay, and immunofluorescence, across mouse samples and senescence models.

More specifically, MMP2 has been identified as a SASP factor expressed in late-stage senescent beta cells in euglycemic Non-Obese Diabetic (NOD) mice, highlighting its relevance in the context of beta cell senescence and the progression of cellular aging within the pancreatic islet environment. Its upregulation in mouse senescence models further underscores its role as a key molecular marker and mediator of the senescent phenotype in beta cells.&lt;SEP&gt;Matrix metalloproteinase 2, a senescence marker observed in NOD mouse islets.&lt;SEP&gt;Matrix metalloproteinase 2, upregulated in mouse models of UV radiation as part of SASP.&lt;SEP&gt;Matrix metalloproteinase 2; a gene involved in senescence/SASP that is a target of beta cell EV miRNAs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5dc00b5dc127eca5ff2847cc45392453&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-add59972a262992e4bde6910520c0cdb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-58ad905d1d148d4bbfe7ce4c29566fc6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d7ef738c0840825512b2cb7af5b7c3f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f25c34949789593e96b7a57ead73f11&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6215695e8bd809fd02cb8b9b7b4123ad</data>
