<node id="SERPINE1">
  <data key="d0">SERPINE1</data>
  <data key="d1">Protein</data>
  <data key="d2">SERPINE1, also known as Plasminogen Activator Inhibitor-1 (PAI-1), is a serine protease inhibitor gene that has been extensively characterized as a senescence-associated marker and a component of the Senescence-Associated Secretory Phenotype (SASP).

As a SASP factor, SERPINE1 has been reported in more than ten tissues as a senescence marker, reflecting its broad relevance across multiple biological systems. It is upregulated in senescent mouse beta cells, as detected through Luminex-based assays, and has been observed as a senescence marker in NOD mouse islets. Additionally, SERPINE1 expression is elevated in senescence-associated contexts in aged mouse ovaries and in stromal cells of post-menopausal human ovaries, suggesting a role in reproductive aging.

SERPINE1 also plays an active mechanistic role in driving cellular senescence. In fibrotic lung disease, SERPINE1 (Serpine1) has been shown to induce alveolar type II (AT2) cell senescence by activating the p53–CDKN1A (p21)–RB1 pathway, highlighting its function not merely as a passive marker but as an upstream inducer of senescence signaling.

In the context of metabolic and renal disease, SERPINE1 is secreted as a SASP protein by senescent adipocytes and is overexpressed by senescent glomerular endothelial cells, where it contributes to glomerulosclerosis during early kidney injury in diabetes. In the central nervous system and adipose tissue, SERPINE1 is expressed in senescent cells and has been found to be elevated in post-mortem tissues from individuals with Alzheimer's disease, implicating it in neurodegenerative pathology associated with cellular senescence.

Collectively, SERPINE1 represents a multifunctional SASP component with roles spanning tissue senescence induction, senescence biomarking, and pathological contributions to fibrosis, renal injury, metabolic disease, and neurodegeneration.&lt;SEP&gt;SERPINE1 is a matrix metalloproteinase inhibitor component of the SASP secreted by senescent beta cells.</data>
