<node id="MIN6">
  <data key="d0">MIN6</data>
  <data key="d1">Cell Type</data>
  <data key="d2">MIN6 is an immortalized mouse insulinoma (beta-cell) cell line derived from a C57BL/6 background. It is widely used as an in vitro model system for studying various aspects of pancreatic beta-cell biology, particularly in the context of cellular senescence and DNA damage responses.

As an immortalized cell line, MIN6 exhibits dysregulation of cell cycle regulators at baseline, a characteristic that is taken into account when it is employed in senescence-related research. Despite this baseline dysregulation, MIN6 remains a valuable tool for investigating DNA damage-induced senescence, including the expression of the cyclin-dependent kinase inhibitor p21Cip1 and the induction of senescent-like growth arrest following genotoxic stress.

MIN6 has also been utilized to study the nuclear exclusion of High Mobility Group Box 1 (HMGB1) protein in the context of beta-cell senescence, a process relevant to understanding how senescent beta cells alter their chromatin-associated protein dynamics. Additionally, the cell line serves as a model for examining glucose-stimulated insulin secretion (GSIS), allowing researchers to assess how DNA damage-induced senescence may impact the functional capacity of beta cells. Collectively, MIN6 represents a key experimental platform for dissecting the molecular mechanisms underlying beta-cell senescence, DNA damage responses, and insulin secretory function.&lt;SEP&gt;Mouse beta cell line that shows robust EV secretion and was among the first to demonstrate EV release from pancreatic beta cells.&lt;SEP&gt;A beta cell line in which miR-21 abundance increases during proinflammatory cytokine exposure.&lt;SEP&gt;Mouse insulinoma cell line used as a positive control nuclear extract in gel shift assays.&lt;SEP&gt;Mouse pancreatic beta cell line used for transfection and reporter assays evaluating MAFA and MAFB transactivation activity.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5dc00b5dc127eca5ff2847cc45392453&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-58ad905d1d148d4bbfe7ce4c29566fc6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ef7d4c1829099c6037d8b8b7a83c3cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bcadefd5324392c8a202934109c8c242&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6215695e8bd809fd02cb8b9b7b4123ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08f3e602fed4b4ebfff436b75194d507&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb32288d5dedac1b23370508bf2f7b2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19fff7a7048ab7112926e25c2e46450b</data>
