  <data key="d1">Phenotype</data>
  <data key="d2">A complex secretory phenotype (SASP) of senescent cells consisting of growth factors, cytokines, chemokines, proteases, shed receptors, ligands, and extracellular vesicles.&lt;SEP&gt;A complex secretory phenotype (SASP) of senescent cells consisting of growth factors, cytokines, chemokines, proteases, shed receptors, ligands, and extracellular vesicles.&lt;SEP&gt;SASP; secretory phenotype associated with senescent cells, part of the cellular senescence mechanism.&lt;SEP&gt;Pro-inflammatory secretory phenotype (SASP) associated with persistent DDR activation in beta cells, linked to chronic DDR in T1D.</data>
