<node id="hepatocyte">
  <data key="d0">hepatocyte</data>
  <data key="d1">Cell Type</data>
  <data key="d2">Liver cells whose senescence contributes to the pathology of diabetes mellitus and metabolic syndrome.&lt;SEP&gt;Liver cells whose senescence contributes to the pathology of diabetes mellitus and metabolic syndrome.&lt;SEP&gt;Hepatocytes are liver cells whose senescence and telomere shortening mark liver cirrhosis and predict progression in non-alcohol-related fatty liver disease.&lt;SEP&gt;Liver cell type exhibiting senescence-associated markers including SA-β-gal activity, TAF, karyomegaly, SADS, LINE-1 expression and SASP factors during ageing.&lt;SEP&gt;Liver cells subject to senescence, relevant to liver disease and nucleolar stress contexts.&lt;SEP&gt;Liver cells that can undergo senescence surveillance to limit pre-malignant progression and liver cancer development.</data>
