  <data key="d2">Senescence-associated beta-galactosidase, an alternative name for GLB1, used as a marker of cellular senescence with increased activity in senescent beta cells.&lt;SEP&gt;Senescence-associated beta-galactosidase; marker used to identify senescent cells in mouse islet studies.&lt;SEP&gt;Senescence-associated beta-galactosidase, an alternative name for GLB1, used as a marker of cellular senescence with increased activity in senescent beta cells.&lt;SEP&gt;Senescence-associated beta-galactosidase; marker used to identify senescent cells in mouse islet studies.&lt;SEP&gt;Senescence-associated beta-galactosidase (SA-βgal) is a lysosomal marker and hallmark of senescence in beta cells.&lt;SEP&gt;Senescence-associated beta-galactosidase; a marker of cellular senescence that accumulates in correlation with miR-29 upregulation.</data>
