<node id="antagonistic pleiotropy">
  <data key="d0">antagonistic pleiotropy</data>
  <data key="d1">Biological Process</data>
  <data key="d2">Evolutionary concept where traits beneficial early in life become detrimental later; discussed in relation to senescence and human disease.&lt;SEP&gt;An evolutionary theory suggesting senescent cells are beneficial early in life by suppressing cancer and facilitating organogenesis, but are associated with aging-related disease later in life.&lt;SEP&gt;Evolutionary concept where traits beneficial early in life become detrimental later; discussed in relation to senescence and human disease.&lt;SEP&gt;An evolutionary theory suggesting senescent cells are beneficial early in life by suppressing cancer and facilitating organogenesis, but are associated with aging-related disease later in life.</data>
