<node id="extracellular vesicle">
  <data key="d0">extracellular vesicle</data>
  <data key="d1">Molecule</data>
  <data key="d2">Extracellular vesicles (EVs) are membrane-bound, nano-sized particles released by a wide variety of cell types, carrying diverse molecular cargo including proteins, miRNAs, and other bioactive molecules. They encompass subtypes such as exosomes and microvesicles, and serve as key mediators of intercellular communication, both locally and systemically.

In the context of cellular senescence, extracellular vesicles are recognized as integral components of the senescence-associated secretory phenotype (SASP) secretome, shed by senescent cells as part of their complex secretory program. Senescent cells demonstrate increased secretion of EVs with distinctly altered protein and miRNA cargo compared to their non-senescent counterparts. These vesicles act as key regulators of non-cell-autonomous intercellular communication during senescence, with IFITM3 identified as a notable mediator in this signaling axis.

Extracellular vesicles have also been studied extensively in the context of beta cell biology and metabolic disease. Vesicles derived from visceral adipocytes have been shown to carry miR-27a-5p, which is taken up by pancreatic beta cells and impairs insulin secretion, highlighting a pathological communication axis between adipose tissue and the endocrine pancreas. Furthermore, EVs are being investigated as promising therapeutic delivery vehicles for senolytic or senomorphic miRNAs, with a particular focus on targeting senescent beta cells in the setting of type 1 diabetes (T1D).

Overall, extracellular vesicles occupy a central role at the intersection of senescence biology, intercellular signaling, and therapeutic development, with their cargo composition serving as both a reflection of the cellular state of origin and a functional determinant of their effects on recipient cells.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9bdc00ebaa404f286432a974cec96702&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ff588c6efe73ecb07c6b95acb392e92&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-184abd4f45a78238743890eb9d4f8c56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6215695e8bd809fd02cb8b9b7b4123ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1628eba511291c52eab3e72ef0fd0239&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5596e00050d9f0135f87252a0093e9cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e181574d19e6f17c0fd64b0feecf8f9e</data>
