  <data key="d2">Autoantibodies (AAbs) are immune markers used to stratify human T1D donors, with 1 or 2 AAb-positive donors showing elevated p21Cip1+ beta cells compared to healthy controls.&lt;SEP&gt;Autoantibodies (AAbs) are immune markers used to stratify human T1D donors, with 1 or 2 AAb-positive donors showing elevated p21Cip1+ beta cells compared to healthy controls.&lt;SEP&gt;Immune markers detected in T1D prior to clinical manifestation; two or more must be detected to define pre-symptomatic stages.&lt;SEP&gt;Immune marker found in children with T1D; autoantibody-positivity was associated with elevated miR-155-5p in plasma-derived EVs.&lt;SEP&gt;Diabetes-associated autoantibodies tracked in genetically at-risk children in the TEDDY study as markers of Type 1 diabetes risk.</data>
