  <data key="d0">heterochromatin</data>
  <data key="d1">Biological Process</data>
  <data key="d2">Condensed chromatin whose spatial repositioning is altered by loss of LAMINB1 and HMGB1, facilitating formation of SAHF in senescent cells.&lt;SEP&gt;Condensed chromatin whose spatial repositioning is altered by loss of LAMINB1 and HMGB1, facilitating formation of SAHF in senescent cells.&lt;SEP&gt;Compacted chromatin regions including senescence-associated heterochromatic foci; repressive histone marks and chromatin compaction are independent during senescent heterochromatic layer formation.&lt;SEP&gt;Chromatin form that undergoes global loss and focal gains during senescence due to post-translational histone modifications and DNA methylation changes.&lt;SEP&gt;Chromatin-rich nuclear domains with higher density of 15N-DNA and higher signal intensities in MIMS-EM measurements, contributing to variability in nuclear 15N measurements.</data>
