<node id="GWAS">
  <data key="d0">GWAS</data>
  <data key="d1">Method</data>
  <data key="d2">Genome-Wide Association Study; method used to identify noncoding genetic signals at the CDKN2A/B locus associated with T2D risk and beta cell function loss.&lt;SEP&gt;Genome-Wide Association Study; method used to identify noncoding genetic signals at the CDKN2A/B locus associated with T2D risk and beta cell function loss.&lt;SEP&gt;GWAS (genome-wide association study) is used to identify T2D-associated variants; a trans-ancestry GWAS reported 31 variants across 28 T2D risk loci with sex-specific effects.&lt;SEP&gt;Genome-wide association study; performed in a cell type-specific, sex-stratified manner restricted to differentially accessible chromatin peaks across T2D traits.&lt;SEP&gt;Genome-wide association studies performed for T2D, fasting glucose, and fasting insulin to identify disease-associated loci&lt;SEP&gt;Genome-wide association study used to identify T2D risk variants and sex-specific effects on T2D.</data>
