  <data key="d2">A sex hormone that promotes misfolded proinsulin degradation, inhibits ATR signaling to cell cycle checkpoints and DNA repair, and influences beta cell resilience.&lt;SEP&gt;A sex hormone that promotes misfolded proinsulin degradation, inhibits ATR signaling to cell cycle checkpoints and DNA repair, and influences beta cell resilience.&lt;SEP&gt;Female sex hormone that promotes immune modulation, islet protection, and misfolded proinsulin degradation; reduces lipid synthesis in pancreatic islets.&lt;SEP&gt;Female sex hormone that modulates immune function, islet protection, beta cell mass, and insulin synthesis.&lt;SEP&gt;Estrogen is a female sex hormone whose deficiency, induced by ovariectomy, causes glucose intolerance in WT female mice but not in MafAS64F/+ female mice.&lt;SEP&gt;Estrogen is a sex hormone examined in ovariectomized female MafAS64F/+ mice, found not to have a direct regulatory role in the sexually dimorphic phenotypes of MafAS64F mutant mice.&lt;SEP&gt;Estrogen is a sex hormone proposed to not have an impact on divergent disease processes related to MAFAS64F in humans, based on pubertal development data.</data>
