<node id="KDM5D">
  <data key="d0">KDM5D</data>
  <data key="d1">Gene</data>
  <data key="d2">KDM5D (Lysine Demethylase 5D) is a histone demethylase gene encoded exclusively on the male Y chromosome, making it a strictly male-specific gene. It functions as an H3K4 demethylase and plays a significant role in chromatin remodeling and gene regulation across multiple biological contexts.

In pancreatic islet cells, KDM5D is overexpressed in male beta (β) and alpha (α) cells compared to females, as revealed by islet transcriptome analyses. This overexpression is associated with sex-associated differences in chromatin accessibility, with the gene's regulatory regions being more accessible in male islet cells. These findings highlight KDM5D as a key contributor to sex differences in gene accessibility and expression within the pancreatic endocrine system.

Beyond islet biology, KDM5D has been implicated in several other developmental and pathological processes. It drives accelerated male craniofacial osteogenic differentiation, contributing to sex differences in male osteogenesis. In cardiac biology, downregulation of KDM5D has been shown to impair cardiomyocyte differentiation, underscoring its role in proper cardiac cell development. Additionally, KDM5D expression is inversely correlated with the malignant degree of gastric cancer, where its downregulation correlates with increased cancer malignancy, suggesting a potential tumor-suppressive role.

Note: Two descriptions reference "Lysine Demethylase 5C" (KDM5C) in association with upregulation in male alpha and beta islet cells; however, based on the broader context of all descriptions and the entity name, these are most likely attributable to KDM5D, as KDM5C is an X-linked gene and the male-specific islet overexpression pattern is consistent with a Y-linked gene.

Overall, KDM5D serves as a critical Y-chromosome-encoded epigenetic regulator with wide-ranging roles in sex-biased gene expression, osteogenesis, cardiomyocyte differentiation, and cancer progression.&lt;SEP&gt;Y-linked lysine demethylase 5D, a male-specific H3K4 demethylase involved in cardiomyocyte differentiation and craniofacial osteogenic differentiation.&lt;SEP&gt;Lysine demethylase 5C gene upregulated in male beta and alpha cells.&lt;SEP&gt;KDM5D is a sex chromosome gene showing sex differences in chromatin accessibility in beta cells.&lt;SEP&gt;Y-linked histone demethylase gene more accessible in male islet cells.&lt;SEP&gt;Histone demethylase expressed only from the male Y chromosome; overexpressed in male beta and alpha cells and drives sex differences in osteogenesis, cardiomyocyte, and cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;A chromatin remodeler expressed exclusively from the male Y chromosome, overexpressed in male beta and alpha cells, and drives sex differences in osteogenesis, cardiomyocyte, and cancer.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b67e26d82684726785f1910ba6919cf0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe5b7d8c678cb311e300af3b74f19ed6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e607d2cca86a6257f1db73bacae2c96&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd3982c3cb7b00162818de82027a853e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a7873cb15c71b20e5fc369a6f0ab52a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-794cb97944fe847e61831fceed4d92ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51601485f0924871a988aae2e5ce30bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d7bd4bfe81f828dceb60b520d85bcf2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dfd4ac2599dc6d5dc028ad0e83ccf82f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0269f34de8f0928a9614438917079ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c41ef398df926f1c888f284aff2a98e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd4f6cfb9180aade52c8cb84446ced85&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-87d48756321bdf8ef533359c0655a3d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ea44d17d2377f3dd0f15239a73e15e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e42c3b77d3170e854edbbc691159609d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-822d03d11fbf61e2a25591e2663ef1ca</data>
