<node id="mitochondrial respiration">
  <data key="d0">mitochondrial respiration</data>
  <data key="d1">Biological Process</data>
  <data key="d2">Mitochondrial respiration is a fundamental cellular energy production process that occurs within mitochondria, primarily through oxidative phosphorylation and oxygen consumption. It is characterized by distinct respiratory states, including state 3 (condensed) and state 4 (orthodox) respiration, which are quantified using the respiratory control ratio. In experimental settings, mitochondrial respiration is commonly assessed through oxygen consumption rate (OCR) measurements in islet bioenergetics experiments, often using the Seahorse bioenergetics assay with specific metabolic inhibitors.

A consistent and notable finding across multiple descriptions is that intrinsic mitochondrial respiration is superior in women compared to men, making it a central target for understanding sex differences in various pathologies. This sex-based advantage is particularly evident in pancreatic islet cells, where non-diabetic female islets demonstrate greater ATP-mediated respiration and coupling efficiency compared to male islets, as measured through oxidative phosphorylation processes in islet mitochondria.

However, this female advantage in mitochondrial respiration appears to be disrupted in the context of type 2 diabetes (T2D). Mitochondrial respiration is notably suppressed in female beta cells during the transition to T2D, and this suppression extends to both beta and alpha cells in female donors with T2D. This selective suppression in females suggests that mitochondrial respiration plays a particularly important mechanistic role in T2D pathogenesis in women, and may help explain sex-specific differences in disease progression and susceptibility. The convergence of these findings highlights mitochondrial respiration as a key biological target for investigating sex-differentiated metabolic disease mechanisms.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b67e26d82684726785f1910ba6919cf0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64f42efe8d71d6b6b69c377d2a7c44b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-794cb97944fe847e61831fceed4d92ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51601485f0924871a988aae2e5ce30bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a7d380dafd31120f8a1af317cfb0ab1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0238834380bfb40677324883af3e3004&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56d5ffe02105b1bd6d77faab9c812433&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c41ef398df926f1c888f284aff2a98e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d0bf8cd8c8cb69199fb8f9bf6c37e70&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d41db2658ec2709309c04b39b1894e48&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5cd7041acf7539c8db67413bcd98f41b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2efc110efa119e343b95df1abbd0a327</data>
