<node id="STAR">
  <data key="d0">STAR</data>
  <data key="d1">Method</data>
  <data key="d2">STAR (Spliced Transcripts Alignment to a Reference) is an ultrafast universal RNA-seq aligner widely used in transcriptomic analyses and sequencing data processing workflows. It is designed to efficiently align sequencing reads to reference genomes and transcriptomes, making it a cornerstone tool in both bulk and single-cell RNA sequencing (scRNA-seq) pipelines.

STAR is commonly employed to map sequencing reads to the human reference genome assembly GRCh38, as well as to the more specific reference build GRCh38-2020-A, which is frequently used in single-cell RNA sequencing workflows. Its application spans a variety of transcriptomic data processing contexts, demonstrating its versatility across different experimental and computational frameworks.

In terms of performance, STAR has demonstrated high mapping efficiency in empirical datasets. Notably, when applied to the Tulane dataset, it achieved a confident mapping rate of 95.33±0.75%, underscoring its reliability and accuracy in aligning reads to the human genome reference. Overall, STAR is regarded as a robust and high-performance alignment tool suitable for a broad range of RNA sequencing and transcriptomic analysis applications.&lt;SEP&gt;Ultrafast universal RNA-seq aligner used for transcriptomic data analysis.&lt;SEP&gt;STAR V2.6a is a splice-aware aligner used to align paired-end RNA-Seq reads to the mouse genome mm10.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-78c6090d91c84168c42d7ba3a2808633&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd3982c3cb7b00162818de82027a853e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5bcdcae8f65f7440848eed5a2448750b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6615f49a664b0e6bfe3dc5ebc25a278f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a7d380dafd31120f8a1af317cfb0ab1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0238834380bfb40677324883af3e3004&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c41ef398df926f1c888f284aff2a98e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d0bf8cd8c8cb69199fb8f9bf6c37e70&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-835fc8c5c19bf30c115aefbeec789479&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce72a72ed1aaea72aac97c28374f8f86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c461d96db4bed849ef22472fc2b0cd0</data>
