<node id="DoubletFinder">
  <data key="d0">DoubletFinder</data>
  <data key="d1">Method</data>
  <data key="d2">DoubletFinder is a computational software tool designed for doublet detection in single-cell RNA sequencing (scRNA-seq) data. It operates by leveraging artificial nearest neighbors to identify doublets — instances where two cells are incorrectly captured together and sequenced as a single unit — within single-cell datasets.

The tool is most commonly referenced as version 2 (v2, also noted as v2.0), developed by the Gartner Lab. In its application, DoubletFinder is used to detect, annotate, and eliminate doublets from single-cell RNA sequencing datasets, with a typical expectation of approximately 5% doublets present in a given dataset. The software specifically targets heterotypic droplet doublets, identifying them based on gene expression profiles.

DoubletFinder serves as a critical quality control step in scRNA-seq workflows, ensuring that downstream analyses are performed on accurately characterized single-cell data by removing artifactual cell combinations that could otherwise confound biological interpretations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-78c6090d91c84168c42d7ba3a2808633&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd3982c3cb7b00162818de82027a853e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7913917fca6b789f10e2948623ce222&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0238834380bfb40677324883af3e3004&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c60bd30a96540afcdba183f8a7aa851&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64b61717ec6764bc92fa7c3c5067d345&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c41ef398df926f1c888f284aff2a98e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a5e348a0adb909ac9a245bd8fb1b7b7b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5804ddf6c13fee09d00987476aa3c478</data>
