<node id="XIST">
  <data key="d0">XIST</data>
  <data key="d1">Gene</data>
  <data key="d2">XIST (X-inactive specific transcript) is an X-linked long non-coding RNA gene that plays a central role in X-chromosome dosage compensation. It is well-established as a key regulator of X-chromosome inactivation, a process that equalizes gene expression between sexes by silencing one copy of the X chromosome in female cells.

In the context of human pancreatic islet biology, XIST exhibits consistent and notable sex-associated expression patterns. The gene is upregulated across all female islet cell types, including specifically in alpha and beta cells, when compared to their male counterparts. This differential expression pattern is observed broadly throughout the islet transcriptome, underscoring XIST's role in X-chromosome dosage compensation within human islet function.

Beyond transcriptional differences, XIST also demonstrates sex-associated differences in chromatin accessibility. The genomic locus of XIST is more accessible in female islet cells compared to males, a pattern that is further supported by its proximity to sex-associated candidate cis-regulatory elements (cCREs). These chromatin accessibility differences highlight that the sex-biased regulation of XIST in islet cells operates at both the epigenomic and transcriptional levels.

Collectively, the evidence positions XIST as a prominent sex-differentially regulated gene in human pancreatic islets, with its upregulation in females and associated chromatin accessibility signatures suggesting an active and sustained role in X-chromosome dosage compensation in islet cell function.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fe5b7d8c678cb311e300af3b74f19ed6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e607d2cca86a6257f1db73bacae2c96&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a7873cb15c71b20e5fc369a6f0ab52a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d7bd4bfe81f828dceb60b520d85bcf2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dfd4ac2599dc6d5dc028ad0e83ccf82f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0269f34de8f0928a9614438917079ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd4f6cfb9180aade52c8cb84446ced85&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-87d48756321bdf8ef533359c0655a3d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ea44d17d2377f3dd0f15239a73e15e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e42c3b77d3170e854edbbc691159609d</data>
