<node id="RPS4Y1">
  <data key="d0">RPS4Y1</data>
  <data key="d1">Gene</data>
  <data key="d2">RPS4Y1 (Ribosomal Protein S4 Y-Linked 1) is a Y-chromosome-linked gene encoding the S4 ribosomal protein, with documented expression and functional relevance in male pancreatic islet cells.

In the context of islet transcriptomics, RPS4Y1 is expressed exclusively in male islet cells across all cell types, distinguishing it as a sex-specific gene within this tissue. Notably, RPS4Y1 is upregulated in male alpha and beta cells compared to their female counterparts, indicating sex-biased transcriptional activity in two of the primary hormone-secreting cell populations of the pancreatic islet. This differential expression pattern suggests that RPS4Y1 may play a functional role in male islet biology, potentially contributing to sex-specific differences in islet physiology or function.

In addition to its transcriptional profile, RPS4Y1 has been identified in proximity to sex-associated candidate cis-regulatory elements (cCREs) in male islet cells. This genomic positioning near sex-associated regulatory regions further supports the notion that RPS4Y1 is subject to sex-specific regulatory mechanisms and may participate in broader sex-linked chromatin regulatory networks within the islet microenvironment.

Collectively, the evidence positions RPS4Y1 as a Y-linked ribosomal protein gene with both transcriptional and regulatory significance in male pancreatic islet cells, with its exclusive male expression and upregulation in key islet cell types suggesting a potential contributing role in male-specific islet function.</data>
