<node id="gamma cell">
  <data key="d0">gamma cell</data>
  <data key="d1">Cell Type</data>
  <data key="d2">Gamma cells are a distinct type of pancreatic islet endocrine cell, consistently identified across multiple studies and analytical methods by their expression of the marker gene PPY (pancreatic polypeptide). These cells have been characterized through various single-cell sequencing approaches, including snATAC-seq clustering and single-cell multiome sequencing, where PPY expression and PPY gene activity serve as the primary identifiers for annotating and isolating this cell population within islet cell clusters.

At the molecular level, gamma cells are distinguished by specific transcription factor (TF) motif enrichments, notably including KLF15 and NRF1, which suggest particular regulatory programs governing their identity and function. Interestingly, despite being a distinct cell type, their regulatory programs show closer relatedness to alpha cells than to other pancreatic endocrine cell types, indicating a degree of shared transcriptional circuitry between gamma and alpha cells.

Gamma cells also exhibit sex-specific differences in chromatin accessibility, suggesting that epigenetic regulation of these cells may vary between biological sexes, with potential implications for understanding sex-based differences in pancreatic endocrine function. Overall, gamma cells represent a well-defined pancreatic islet endocrine population whose identity is robustly anchored by PPY marker expression, with regulatory and epigenetic features that continue to be elucidated through advanced single-cell genomic methodologies.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9e607d2cca86a6257f1db73bacae2c96&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c0d05211cf3080af14ec050e5cc97ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a7873cb15c71b20e5fc369a6f0ab52a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d7bd4bfe81f828dceb60b520d85bcf2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73a24341c9b63bd3b6313252fe6ed4b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0269f34de8f0928a9614438917079ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f02465fe113dd488219949222d1430e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-87d48756321bdf8ef533359c0655a3d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da10e6374cdbd3d6e4a07d773cd172d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ea44d17d2377f3dd0f15239a73e15e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e42c3b77d3170e854edbbc691159609d</data>
