<node id="ambient RNA correction">
  <data key="d0">ambient RNA correction</data>
  <data key="d1">Method</data>
  <data key="d2">Quality control step used in scRNA-seq processing to remove ambient RNA contamination from single cell transcriptomes.&lt;SEP&gt;Stringent methodology applied to remove contaminant RNA from single-cell sequencing data, particularly relevant for pancreatic cells with high INS and PRSS1 expression.&lt;SEP&gt;Ambient RNA correction was applied as a quality control step during scRNA-seq data processing to obtain high-quality single cell signatures.&lt;SEP&gt;Methodology used to reduce contaminant RNA in single-cell sequencing data, especially relevant for high-expressing pancreatic cells.&lt;SEP&gt;Computational quality control step used in scRNA-seq data processing to obtain high-quality single cell transcriptomes.</data>
