<node id="Signac">
  <data key="d0">Signac</data>
  <data key="d1">Method</data>
  <data key="d2">Signac is a bioinformatics software tool and R package designed for single-cell chromatin state analysis, developed by the Satija and Stuart Labs. It is primarily applied to the processing and analysis of single-nucleus ATAC sequencing (snATAC-seq) data, offering a comprehensive suite of computational functionalities within a unified framework.

Signac supports a wide range of analytical tasks, including peak calling, gene activity estimation, normalization, dimensionality reduction, clustering, and differential chromatin accessibility analysis. Additionally, the tool provides capabilities for filtering nuclei and identifying transcription factor (TF) motifs, making it a versatile solution for in-depth chromatin accessibility studies at the single-cell level.

Two versions of Signac are referenced in the literature: v1.9.0 and v1.10.0. Version 1.9.0 has been noted specifically for its functions related to nuclei filtering, ATAC count normalization, dimensionality reduction, and TF motif identification, while version 1.10.0 is widely cited for the full spectrum of snATAC-seq data processing tasks, including peak calling, gene activity estimation, normalization, clustering, and differential accessibility analysis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd3982c3cb7b00162818de82027a853e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5bcdcae8f65f7440848eed5a2448750b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6615f49a664b0e6bfe3dc5ebc25a278f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0238834380bfb40677324883af3e3004&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c60bd30a96540afcdba183f8a7aa851&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64b61717ec6764bc92fa7c3c5067d345&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c41ef398df926f1c888f284aff2a98e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d41db2658ec2709309c04b39b1894e48&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5804ddf6c13fee09d00987476aa3c478&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-835fc8c5c19bf30c115aefbeec789479</data>
  <data key="d4">Single cell regulatory architecture of human pancreatic islets suggests sex differences in β cell function and the pathogenesis of type 2 diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Calorie restriction increases insulin sensitivity to promote beta cell homeostasis and longevity in mice.&lt;SEP&gt;Sex-specific regulatory architecture of pancreatic islets from subjects with and without type 2 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d5">1778570229</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">31</data>
  <data key="d8">islet / pancreas / snATAC-seq</data>
  <data key="d9">0.00062832</data>
  <data key="d10">0.00082726</data>
  <data key="d11">0.00234885</data>
</node>
<node id="AMULET">
  <data key="d0">AMULET</data>
  <data key="d1">Method</data>
  <data key="d2">AMULET is a novel read count-based computational method designed for effective multiplet (doublet) detection from single nucleus ATAC-seq (snATAC-seq) data. It is specifically developed to address the challenge of identifying multiplet droplets in droplet-based single nucleus ATAC sequencing workflows, a critical quality control step in single-cell sequencing analysis.

AMULET operates by leveraging read count information to distinguish multiplet droplets from singlets. In one of its known implementations, version 1.1 of the tool utilizes mm10 repetitive elements sourced from the UCSC Genome Browser as part of its detection strategy for multiplet droplets.

The tool is integrated within the scDblFinder R package, where it serves as a specialized method for doublet and multiplet detection tailored to droplet-based snATAC-seq data. This integration allows users of the scDblFinder ecosystem to apply AMULET's read count-based approach directly within a widely used Bioconductor framework for single-cell quality control. Overall, AMULET represents a purpose-built solution for improving data quality in single nucleus ATAC-seq experiments by accurately identifying and flagging multiplet-containing droplets.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd3982c3cb7b00162818de82027a853e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5bcdcae8f65f7440848eed5a2448750b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6615f49a664b0e6bfe3dc5ebc25a278f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0238834380bfb40677324883af3e3004&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c60bd30a96540afcdba183f8a7aa851&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c41ef398df926f1c888f284aff2a98e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d41db2658ec2709309c04b39b1894e48&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-835fc8c5c19bf30c115aefbeec789479</data>
