<node id="mitochondrial dysfunction">
  <data key="d0">mitochondrial dysfunction</data>
  <data key="d1">Biological Process</data>
  <data key="d2">Reduced mitochondrial function observed in female beta cells from T2D donors compared to non-diabetic female donors.&lt;SEP&gt;Impaired mitochondrial function associated with cell senescence and aging.&lt;SEP&gt;Mitochondrial dysfunction is caused by GBP1 downregulation in macrophages and is associated with cellular senescence.&lt;SEP&gt;Mitochondrial dysfunction in senescent cells leads to NADH accumulation, ATP depletion, ROS production, and mtDNA release.&lt;SEP&gt;Mitochondrial dysfunction is caused by YY1 deficiency in beta cells and leads to diabetes in mice.&lt;SEP&gt;Reduced mitochondrial function observed preferentially in female beta cells from T2D donors compared to non-diabetic females, not observed in male beta cells.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-794cb97944fe847e61831fceed4d92ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-71a6a7a3a4894dbd7d979b7e5766d5a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ca3e5da7a4fe15854dde6289fd15667&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b02375738a9ebacd53446fec2077ee76&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-735ea17eaeb5e3524d0871e16116e986&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-822d03d11fbf61e2a25591e2663ef1ca</data>
