  <data key="d1">Method</data>
  <data key="d2">Senescence-associated beta-galactosidase; its activity is linked to increased lysosomal mass in senescent cells.&lt;SEP&gt;Senescence-associated beta-galactosidase, a marker of cellular senescence used to identify senescent cells.&lt;SEP&gt;Senescence-associated beta-galactosidase, a widely used marker of cellular senescence with increased activity in bone marrow, CNS, and adipose tissue.&lt;SEP&gt;Senescence-associated beta-galactosidase activity staining used to identify senescent cells histologically.&lt;SEP&gt;Senescence-associated beta-galactosidase; a commonly used biomarker and staining method for detecting senescent cells.&lt;SEP&gt;Senescence-associated β-galactosidase staining, a marker used to detect cellular senescence in beta cells.&lt;SEP&gt;Senescence-associated beta-galactosidase staining, used as an indicator of cellular senescence; activity is robustly increased in TIF-IA-depleted beta cells.&lt;SEP&gt;Senescence-associated β-galactosidase, a widely used biomarker of terminal senescence measured in islet cells.&lt;SEP&gt;SA-β-gal (senescence-associated β-galactosidase) is an endogenous marker of senescence detected at increased levels in male MafAS64F/+ islets, comparable to mice aged 10–12 months, but undetectable at 4 weeks or in female MafAS64F/+ islets.</data>
