  <data key="d2">Mesenchymal stem cells are multipotent stromal cells whose expansion and differentiation are negatively impacted by donor age and impaired by aging via reduced Sirtuin 1.&lt;SEP&gt;Stem cell in the bone marrow whose proliferation and differentiation supports the haematopoietic stem cell niche.&lt;SEP&gt;Adipose tissue-derived stem cells from older donors exhibiting senescence properties and impaired regenerative potential.&lt;SEP&gt;Adipose tissue-derived stem cells that develop senescent-like populations with ageing.&lt;SEP&gt;Stem/progenitor cell that undergoes normal programmed senescence in late puberty, indicated by loss of nestin expression.</data>
