<node id="ageing">
  <data key="d0">ageing</data>
  <data key="d1">Biological Process</data>
  <data key="d2">Process associated with accumulation of senescent cells in tissues and decreased immune clearance of senescent cells.&lt;SEP&gt;Normal ageing is associated with accumulation of senescence markers in multiple tissues including cardiovascular cells.&lt;SEP&gt;Biological process of growing older associated with accumulation of senescent cells, SASP induction, and tissue dysfunction across multiple organ systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Biological process associated with accumulation of senescent cells across multiple tissues including bone marrow, central nervous system, and adipose tissue.&lt;SEP&gt;Natural biological process associated with accumulation of senescent cells in adipose tissue, kidneys, and other organs.&lt;SEP&gt;Process associated with cellular senescence, studied in various tissues including the colon and placenta.</data>
