<node id="neurodegeneration">
  <data key="d0">neurodegeneration</data>
  <data key="d1">Disease</data>
  <data key="d2">Neurodegeneration is a disease process for which causative factors are identified using translatome-regulatory network analysis.&lt;SEP&gt;Progressive loss of neuronal function caused by senescent myeloid cell infiltration in histiocytic disorders and other age-related conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;Brain condition driven by circulating senescent myeloid cells along with brain inflammation.&lt;SEP&gt;Pathological condition associated with senescence profiles in brain tissue, including Alzheimer disease and Parkinson disease.&lt;SEP&gt;Disease state in which DNA damage plays a role in neural plasticity impairment.&lt;SEP&gt;DNA damage plays a role in neural plasticity in neurodegeneration.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3d3b1de44d6b73a10793a43351e18e6e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-71a6a7a3a4894dbd7d979b7e5766d5a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a471400d67fa8643230222fb3576486&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c5a8121875c37f2659ae345688f6afe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-735ea17eaeb5e3524d0871e16116e986&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-80318e0997c6182c0124775c5f01f6a0</data>
