<node id="SIRT1">
  <data key="d0">SIRT1</data>
  <data key="d1">Protein</data>
  <data key="d2">SIRT1 (Sirtuin 1) is a multifunctional protein that plays critical roles in aging, cellular senescence, metabolic regulation, and inflammatory signaling across a wide range of tissues and biological contexts.

In the context of aging and tissue differentiation, SIRT1 expression is notably reduced with advancing age, which impairs the differentiation of mesenchymal stem cells into beige adipocytes. Correspondingly, SIRT1 functions as a negative regulator of cellular senescence in adipose tissue, suggesting its downregulation may contribute to age-related adipose dysfunction. In vascular biology, the age-associated reduction of SIRT1 in vascular smooth muscle cells has been linked to vascular senescence and inflammation, connecting its decline to the pathogenesis of conditions such as abdominal aortic aneurysm.

SIRT1 also plays a regulatory role in placental biology, where it governs trophoblast senescence. Its altered activity has been implicated in premature placental aging associated with preeclampsia, highlighting its importance in reproductive health and gestational complications.

In the realm of inflammatory and metabolic disease, SIRT1 is regulated by MIR204 (miR-204) in the context of diabetic retinopathy, where it influences both inflammation and apoptosis. Notably, upregulation of SIRT1 by miR-204 has been associated with the suppression of inflammatory cytokines, indicating a protective anti-inflammatory role in this disease context.

At the metabolic and molecular level, SIRT1 acts as a key regulator within metabolic signaling pathways that control ribosomal RNA (rRNA) synthesis. It is also involved in the regulation of nucleolar stress, underscoring its broader role in maintaining cellular homeostasis and coordinating responses to metabolic perturbations.

Collectively, SIRT1 serves as a central integrator of aging, senescence, inflammation, and metabolic signaling, with its dysregulation contributing to a spectrum of age-related and metabolic diseases.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-71a6a7a3a4894dbd7d979b7e5766d5a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ce1a7b385e0f22ca823c850de9bf8a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c5a8121875c37f2659ae345688f6afe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf5aeca434044079720fd4ae2d32c9b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1628eba511291c52eab3e72ef0fd0239&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-732255e9544dde6a7dbc319c61cd8e1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ce4f6e2d90d0c06e4549d7d45037298&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e33cd1d99c96a7f6ffdd0fbea902670</data>
