  <data key="d11">0.01326785</data>
</node>
<node id="CXCR2">
  <data key="d0">CXCR2</data>
  <data key="d1">Protein</data>
  <data key="d2">CXCR2 is a receptor whose ligands, secreted by senescent hepatic stellate cells, promote liver regeneration.&lt;SEP&gt;A chemokine receptor whose signaling reinforces cellular senescence.&lt;SEP&gt;CXCR2 is a chemokine receptor whose ligands are involved in senescence-related signaling.&lt;SEP&gt;A gene involved in senescence/SASP that is a target of beta cell EV miRNAs.&lt;SEP&gt;A chemokine receptor downregulated by miR-107, contributing to decreased SASP secretion.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-71a6a7a3a4894dbd7d979b7e5766d5a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea13fe99fbc01cb6036ecddcda0aae8a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ff588c6efe73ecb07c6b95acb392e92&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6215695e8bd809fd02cb8b9b7b4123ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1628eba511291c52eab3e72ef0fd0239</data>
  <data key="d4">SenNet recommendations for detecting senescent cells in different tissues.&lt;SEP&gt;Exploring senescence as a modifier of β cell extracellular vesicles in type 1 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d5">1778568428</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">135</data>
  <data key="d8">SASP / senescence / Senescence-Associated Secretory Phenotype</data>
  <data key="d9">0.00028595</data>
  <data key="d10">0.00024746</data>
  <data key="d11">0.01050035</data>
</node>
<node id="cholangiocyte">
  <data key="d0">cholangiocyte</data>
  <data key="d1">Cell Type</data>
  <data key="d2">Cholangiocytes are bile duct cells that can become senescent, and targeting senescent cholangiocytes with BCL-XL inhibitors ameliorates fibrosis in Mdr2-knockout mice.&lt;SEP&gt;Senescent cholangiocytes are targeted by BCL-extra large inhibitors to ameliorate fibrosis in Mdr2−/− mice.&lt;SEP&gt;Liver cell type in which senescence-associated markers have been found in the context of primary biliary cirrhosis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-71a6a7a3a4894dbd7d979b7e5766d5a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b773584b36e5b4845bedffea9a1b6add&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea13fe99fbc01cb6036ecddcda0aae8a</data>
