<node id="immune cell">
  <data key="d0">immune cell</data>
  <data key="d1">Cell Type</data>
  <data key="d2">Immune cells express CD38 ecto-enzyme, which is induced during aging and regulates NAD+ and NMN levels.&lt;SEP&gt;Cells of the immune system that can become senescent, release grancalcin to promote skeletal aging, and drive senescence of solid organs when aged.&lt;SEP&gt;Immune cells in post-menopausal human ovaries expressing several CCL and CXCL genes, potentially reversing some detrimental effects of senescence.&lt;SEP&gt;Cell type that interacts with beta cells during T1D pathogenesis, with EVs proposed as conveyors of signaling between beta and immune cells.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-71a6a7a3a4894dbd7d979b7e5766d5a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a5bb73f6c7980a9f906f42f6e0e9ce27&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c5a8121875c37f2659ae345688f6afe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08f3e602fed4b4ebfff436b75194d507</data>
