  <data key="d1">Gene</data>
  <data key="d2">Mouse gene encoding p53, a tumor suppressor whose activation occurs in senescence and other forms of cell cycle arrest.&lt;SEP&gt;Trp53 is a cell cycle inhibitor upregulated in the aorta as a senescence marker during vascular ageing.&lt;SEP&gt;Tumor protein p53 (Trp53), a cell cycle inhibitor and DNA damage response protein associated with senescence.&lt;SEP&gt;Overexpressed in animal models of kidney disease alongside other senescence markers.&lt;SEP&gt;Mouse tumor suppressor gene (Trp53) whose expression is increased in airway smooth muscle cells from older individuals with asthma and in senescent pulmonary fibroblasts.&lt;SEP&gt;Mouse homolog of TP53, increased in osteocytes of aged mice as a senescence marker.</data>
