<node id="fibrosis">
  <data key="d0">fibrosis</data>
  <data key="d1">Biological Process</data>
  <data key="d2">Fibrosis is a pathological condition characterized by the excessive accumulation of connective tissue, and it has been studied across multiple organ systems, including the kidney, lung, liver, ovary, and dermis. It is broadly associated with iron accumulation, cellular senescence, and the senescence-associated secretory phenotype (SASP), with iron accumulation arising from vascular and haemolytic injuries serving as a key driver of fibrotic processes in the kidney and other organs.

Fibrosis has been identified as an age-associated process, occurring notably in the stroma of the mammalian ovary and in the dermis, where it develops alongside inflammation. In the ovarian context, while an association with senescence has been observed, a conclusive causal relationship between fibrosis and senescence has not yet been firmly established. This ambiguity is further compounded by the fact that fibrosis and senescence share overlapping molecular markers, complicating efforts to distinguish cause from consequence in research models.

In experimental settings, fibrosis has been studied using biomaterial fibrosis models designed to identify in vivo senescence heterogeneity, underscoring its utility as a model condition for understanding the diversity of senescent cell populations. Therapeutically, fibrosis has been shown to be ameliorated in Mdr2−/− mice through the targeting of senescent cholangiocytes and activated fibroblasts using BCL-extra large (BCL-XL) inhibitors, pointing toward senolytic strategies as a potential avenue for treatment.

Overall, fibrosis represents a multifaceted pathological process at the intersection of aging, iron metabolism, and cellular senescence, with its full mechanistic relationship to senescence remaining an active and complex area of investigation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-71a6a7a3a4894dbd7d979b7e5766d5a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b773584b36e5b4845bedffea9a1b6add&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ce1a7b385e0f22ca823c850de9bf8a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea13fe99fbc01cb6036ecddcda0aae8a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a5bb73f6c7980a9f906f42f6e0e9ce27&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ff588c6efe73ecb07c6b95acb392e92&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-682da4208f0eb800bc5523bd70a84eb7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf5aeca434044079720fd4ae2d32c9b9</data>
