<node id="genomic instability">
  <data key="d0">genomic instability</data>
  <data key="d1">Phenotype</data>
  <data key="d2">Hallmark of cellular senescence involving increased genomic mutations and chromosomal abnormalities.&lt;SEP&gt;Condition induced by failure to repair DNA damage, leading to altered genomic functions such as transcription.&lt;SEP&gt;Increased rate of mutations and chromosomal alterations, promoted by elevated glucose and inhibition of nucleotide excision repair.&lt;SEP&gt;Condition of compromised genome integrity that persistent DDR activation can lead to, associated with senescence and cell death.&lt;SEP&gt;Loss of beta-cell genomic stability observed in conditions such as T2D, CHI, and upon loss of DNA repair components.&lt;SEP&gt;Condition resulting from defects in DNA repair or failure to maintain DNA methylation patterns, compromising genome integrity.&lt;SEP&gt;Compromised genomic integrity resulting from failure to repair DNA breaks, particularly in beta cells.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-25d34b513b15180c8a2d7b57ae829067&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e7d877b531b99ded5aba6df6f1635f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-80318e0997c6182c0124775c5f01f6a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-58f0193e389064a60d513f13c5cad52b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-72bf1fbaf7a329c364247108f8b30408&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db03a7d3c861658f2beac422f86b21ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28a44d52c17c29e9741a935aa76e8afe</data>
  <data key="d4">SenNet recommendations for detecting senescent cells in different tissues.&lt;SEP&gt;Safeguarding genomic integrity in beta-cells: implications for beta-cell differentiation, growth, and dysfunction.&lt;SEP&gt;Developmental control of DNA damage responses in α- and β-cells shapes the selective beta-cell susceptibility in diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d5">1778571444</data>
