<node id="AMPK">
  <data key="d0">AMPK</data>
  <data key="d1">Protein</data>
  <data key="d2">AMP-activated protein kinase activated during mitochondrial dysfunction-associated senescence following ATP depletion.&lt;SEP&gt;AMPK is activated by ATP depletion during mitochondrial dysfunction-associated senescence, contributing to cell cycle arrest.&lt;SEP&gt;AMPK is a metabolic kinase involved in beta-cell metabolic plasticity during maturation, acting downstream of mTORC1 switching.&lt;SEP&gt;AMP-activated protein kinase; mediates glucose-dependent upregulation of miR-125b-5p in beta cells.&lt;SEP&gt;AMP-activated protein kinase (AMPK) mediates glucose-induced upregulation of miR-125b-5p expression.&lt;SEP&gt;AMP-activated protein kinase, a metabolic signaling pathway regulator of rRNA synthesis.&lt;SEP&gt;A metabolic signaling molecule that tightly regulates rRNA synthesis, with potential involvement in nucleolar stress in metabolic disease.</data>
