<node id="ROS">
  <data key="d0">ROS</data>
  <data key="d1">Molecule</data>
  <data key="d2">Reactive oxygen species produced by dysfunctional mitochondria contribute to induction of senescence and stabilization of cell cycle arrest.&lt;SEP&gt;Reactive oxygen species whose production is increased in syncytiotrophoblast mitochondria as an adaptation to changing oxygen tension in the placenta.&lt;SEP&gt;Reactive oxygen species; generation and accumulation are reduced in CR beta cells due to upregulation of superoxide scavengers and enhanced bioenergetics.&lt;SEP&gt;Reactive oxygen species whose reduced accumulation under CR may contribute to improved mitochondrial longevity and reduced basal hyperinsulinemia.&lt;SEP&gt;Reactive oxygen species involved in senescence induction in neuronal cells and other contexts.&lt;SEP&gt;Reactive oxygen species (ROS) are unfavorable stimuli that may serve as upstream triggers of nucleolar stress in pancreatic beta cells.</data>
