<node id="telomere">
  <data key="d0">telomere</data>
  <data key="d1">Molecule</data>
  <data key="d2">Chromosomal end structures that are favoured targets of persistent DNA damage response in ageing and stress-induced senescence.&lt;SEP&gt;Telomeric DNA damage and attrition during senescence result in formation of DDR foci co-localizing with telomeres, referred to as telomere-associated foci.&lt;SEP&gt;Structural genomic element found to be shorter in the kidney cortex but not in the medulla during ageing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6ca3e5da7a4fe15854dde6289fd15667&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ce1a7b385e0f22ca823c850de9bf8a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b02375738a9ebacd53446fec2077ee76</data>
