<node id="telomere dysfunction">
  <data key="d0">telomere dysfunction</data>
  <data key="d1">Biological Process</data>
  <data key="d2">Shortening or structural failure of telomeres contributing to cellular senescence in vascular and other cell types.&lt;SEP&gt;Paracrine telomere dysfunction is the mechanism by which senescent melanocytes drive skin ageing.&lt;SEP&gt;Dysfunction of telomeres in senescent melanocytes that drives skin aging via paracrine mechanisms.&lt;SEP&gt;Dysfunction at telomeres associated with cellular senescence, evidenced by TAF and CDKN2A-mediated senescence in CD8A+ T cell subsets.&lt;SEP&gt;Dysfunctional telomeres that induce ATR-dependent DNA damage responses, protected against by P16.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ea13fe99fbc01cb6036ecddcda0aae8a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a471400d67fa8643230222fb3576486&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c5a8121875c37f2659ae345688f6afe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf5aeca434044079720fd4ae2d32c9b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-72bf1fbaf7a329c364247108f8b30408</data>
