  <data key="d2">Novel surface and molecular markers characterizing senescent cells with prognostic potential in cancer and utility as senotherapeutic targets.&lt;SEP&gt;Senescence biomarkers include p16INK4a, H2A.J, beta-galactosidase, and other markers used to identify senescent cells in tissues and culture.&lt;SEP&gt;Validated biological markers representing a crucial advancement in identifying senescent cells across developmental stages, ageing, and various diseases.</data>
