<node id="placenta">
  <data key="d0">placenta</data>
  <data key="d1">Tissue</data>
  <data key="d2">Tissue where placenta-specific genes are reactivated through large-scale chromatin reorganization, driving cellular aging, and where senescence markers are expressed in fetal growth restriction.&lt;SEP&gt;Tissue in which cellular senescence, genome amplification, oxidative stress, and trophoblast-specific senescence markers are hallmarks of development and pathology.&lt;SEP&gt;Tissue where developmental senescence occurs in trophoblasts and where senescence plays a role in parturition.&lt;SEP&gt;Tissue that undergoes developmental senescence and can experience accelerated or premature senescence in adverse pregnancy outcomes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a5bb73f6c7980a9f906f42f6e0e9ce27&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ff588c6efe73ecb07c6b95acb392e92&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-682da4208f0eb800bc5523bd70a84eb7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf5aeca434044079720fd4ae2d32c9b9</data>
