<node id="vascular smooth muscle cell">
  <data key="d0">vascular smooth muscle cell</data>
  <data key="d1">Cell Type</data>
  <data key="d2">Vascular cell type showing less aging-induced DNA damage and telomere dysfunction compared to endothelial cells.&lt;SEP&gt;Cells of the vascular wall that undergo telomere-based senescence in human atherosclerosis and are linked to abdominal aortic aneurysm via SIRT1 reduction.&lt;SEP&gt;Primary cell type of the aorta that exhibits senescence-associated markers during mouse ageing and is isolated from atherosclerotic plaques.&lt;SEP&gt;Vascular cells that develop senescence-like phenotypes upon nucleolar stress.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6a471400d67fa8643230222fb3576486&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c5a8121875c37f2659ae345688f6afe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b02375738a9ebacd53446fec2077ee76&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-15ab370ab273e97005ced113e59cc48a</data>
  <data key="d4">SenNet recommendations for detecting senescent cells in different tissues.&lt;SEP&gt;Nucleolar stress facilitates islet β cell senescence via hijacking the DNA damage response pathways.</data>
