  <data key="d2">Tetraspanin CD63, found at increased levels in platelets of older people, suggesting age-associated platelet activation.&lt;SEP&gt;Tetraspanin marker in beta cell EVs; CD63 levels discriminate between two beta cell subsets with different metabolic and functional capacities.&lt;SEP&gt;CD63 is a tetraspanin marker expressed on beta cell EVs and used in conditional reporter mouse models (CD63-GFP) to track EVs in vivo.&lt;SEP&gt;Cell surface marker used to identify a beta cell cluster enriched for mitochondrial metabolism genes; CD63high cells show enhanced function.</data>
