  <data key="d2">Transcription factor at whose step P21CIP1 and P57KIP2 control muscle differentiation.&lt;SEP&gt;Myogenin is a muscle-specific transcription factor whose targeted mutation in mice causes muscle deficiency and neonatal death; it can substitute for Myf5 in promoting myogenesis but less efficiently.&lt;SEP&gt;Myogenin is a basic helix-loop-helix myogenic factor that plays an essential role in the late differentiation of myoblasts to myotubes, analogous to MafA in the maturing β-cell.</data>
