<node id="mitochondria">
  <data key="d0">mitochondria</data>
  <data key="d1">Tissue</data>
  <data key="d2">Mitochondria are cellular organelles with critical roles in energy metabolism, particularly in the production of ATP. They are characterized by distinct structural states — condensed and orthodox — which are defined by respiratory control ratios and directly influence their ATP production capacity.

In the context of beta cells, mitochondria are subject to significant structural and functional alterations under caloric restriction (CR). Compared to ad libitum (AL) fed beta cells, mitochondria in CR beta cells exhibit higher density, increased cristae density, and modified cristae morphology. These structural changes are accompanied by an enhanced ATP generation potential and increased mitochondrial mass. Notably, this increase in mass and function under CR conditions is attributed to reduced mitophagy, meaning CR-induced autophagy does not target mitochondria, allowing them to accumulate and function more efficiently. The ATP production rate in beta cell mitochondria has been estimated using biophysical modeling approaches that account for both condensed and orthodox mitochondrial states as defined by the respiratory control ratio.

Beyond beta cells, mitochondria are also observed to undergo transformations in the aging human placenta, suggesting their structural and functional dynamics are relevant across multiple tissue types and physiological contexts.

From a methodological standpoint, mitochondrial markers within cells have been imaged using high-resolution 63x confocal microscopy with Nyquist acquisition parameters, enabling detailed visualization of their structure and distribution within cellular environments.&lt;SEP&gt;Central target for sex differences in pathologies; mitochondrial failure implicated in T2D pathogenesis in female beta cells.&lt;SEP&gt;Organelle with increased mass in beta-high (CD24+) subtype compared to beta-low subtype.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bf5aeca434044079720fd4ae2d32c9b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56d5ffe02105b1bd6d77faab9c812433&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f0c13c5a18e2c5037815818d22c48a64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af08dcd3bdc472cb74376c18c72cf9f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-002f23b1d29df711e839459b4d6f0711&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91ed3d214b295f4a8cccdca98b3822e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa01ef8f1657a9890660f864f52123c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64b61717ec6764bc92fa7c3c5067d345&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d41db2658ec2709309c04b39b1894e48&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5596e00050d9f0135f87252a0093e9cb</data>
  <data key="d4">SenNet recommendations for detecting senescent cells in different tissues.&lt;SEP&gt;Calorie restriction increases insulin sensitivity to promote beta cell homeostasis and longevity in mice.&lt;SEP&gt;Sex-specific regulatory architecture of pancreatic islets from subjects with and without type 2 diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;The role of the beta cell in type 2 diabetes: new findings from the last 5 years.</data>
  <data key="d5">1778570826</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">14</data>
  <data key="d8">caloric restriction / autophagy / beta cell state 2</data>
  <data key="d9">0.00096138</data>
