  <data key="d1">Molecule</data>
  <data key="d2">Ambient RNA refers to extracellular RNA from cells with compromised membrane integrity that contaminates single-cell libraries in droplet-based scRNAseq technologies.&lt;SEP&gt;Background RNA signal detected in empty droplets, removed from nuclei-containing droplets using SoupX.&lt;SEP&gt;Residual contaminant RNA observed across cells in single-cell sequencing, particularly problematic in pancreatic cells with high INS and PRSS1 expression.&lt;SEP&gt;Ambient RNA refers to extracellular RNA from cells with compromised membrane integrity that contaminates single-cell libraries in droplet-based scRNAseq technologies.</data>
