<node id="HNF1A">
  <data key="d0">HNF1A</data>
  <data key="d1">Gene</data>
  <data key="d2">HNF1A is a gene encoding a transcription factor with significant roles in both diabetes-associated cellular regulation and genetic risk for type 2 diabetes (T2D).

As a transcription factor, HNF1A governs the beta1 cell subtype within pancreatic beta cells and is a primary driver of diabetes-associated beta cell heterogeneity, as identified through single-cell multiomic analysis. HNF1A expression is reduced in type 2 diabetes, and mutations in this gene are known to cause Maturity-Onset Diabetes of the Young (MODY). Mechanistically, HNF1A facilitates membrane depolarization and insulin secretion through the upregulation of FXYD2, highlighting its functional importance in beta cell physiology.

In the context of T2D genetic risk, HNF1A resides at a T2D risk locus with the index variant rs28638142. Regulatory variants associated with this locus overlap with differentially accessible chromatin regions identified in endothelial cells, with a notable sex-specific pattern: these differentially accessible regions are observed in male endothelial cells but not in female endothelial cells. This sex-dimorphic chromatin accessibility suggests that the regulatory influence of T2D-associated variants at the HNF1A locus may operate through distinct, male-specific mechanisms in the endothelium.

Collectively, HNF1A sits at the intersection of transcriptional control of pancreatic beta cell identity and sex-specific epigenomic regulation in endothelial cells, underscoring its multifaceted contribution to T2D biology and risk.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dfd4ac2599dc6d5dc028ad0e83ccf82f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f3f8e2c47cb96d65689fa504202cd0f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76049b85888e8e904e7c01de9740d34f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ea44d17d2377f3dd0f15239a73e15e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-822d03d11fbf61e2a25591e2663ef1ca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2efc110efa119e343b95df1abbd0a327&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cba0d7fafdd66d2ffb133e04939d15f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-10bdc47e4d027606476b48a401061a27&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e181574d19e6f17c0fd64b0feecf8f9e</data>
