  <data key="d2">T2D risk locus with index variant rs188247550, overlapping a differentially accessible chromatin region detected only in female lymphocytes.&lt;SEP&gt;TM6SF2 is a T2D risk locus gene; a variant near it (rs8107974) has sex-specific effects on T2D, and an accessible chromatin region in female lymphocytes overlaps with 4 T2D-associated variants at this locus.&lt;SEP&gt;Gene locus associated with differentially accessible chromatin regions near T2D variants.&lt;SEP&gt;T2D risk locus gene; a differentially accessible female lymphocyte region overlaps with 4 T2D variants at this locus (index variant rs188247550), and one variant near TM6SF2 (rs8107974) was reported to have sex-specific effects on T2D.&lt;SEP&gt;A T2D risk locus where an accessible chromatin region in female lymphocytes overlaps with 4 T2D-associated variants, with sex-specific effects reported in trans-ancestry GWAS.</data>
