  <data key="d2">Heterogeneous nanoparticle-sized membrane-bound cargo carriers secreted from most cell types, containing DNA, RNA, proteins, and metabolites; implicated in signaling between beta cells and immune cells in T1D.&lt;SEP&gt;Membrane-bound particles secreted by cells, including beta cells, that mediate intercellular communication and carry autoantigens and miRNAs.&lt;SEP&gt;Vesicles secreted by beta cells carrying proteins and miRNAs that influence cellular signaling and may contribute to T1D development; cargo is impacted by senescence.&lt;SEP&gt;Extracellular vesicles (EVs) are membrane-bound particles released by beta cells that can carry autoantigens, miRNAs, and surface proteins involved in immune signaling.</data>
