<node id="miRNA">
  <data key="d0">miRNA</data>
  <data key="d1">Molecule</data>
  <data key="d2">miRNA, or microRNA, refers to a class of small non-coding RNA molecules that are typically 21–23 nucleotides in length. These molecules play a fundamental role in post-transcriptional gene regulation by inhibiting mRNA translation or reducing mRNA stability, thereby influencing a wide range of biological processes.

miRNAs are critically important in the context of pancreatic beta cell biology and diabetes. They have been identified as key regulators of human beta cell function and are implicated in the pathophysiology of both type 1 diabetes (T1D) and type 2 diabetes (T2D). In the context of T2D, miRNAs function as epigenetic modulators of beta cell activity, and their expression profiles in pancreatic islets have been studied extensively through large-scale genetic and mechanistic investigations to better understand their contribution to T2D risk and progression.

miRNAs also play a significant role in regulating senescence-associated signaling pathways, including the senescence-associated secretory phenotype (SASP). By modulating SASP, miRNAs hold potential for limiting the detrimental inflammatory effects of senescent beta cells, which are relevant to both T1D and T2D. In the setting of T1D specifically, miRNAs have been proposed as therapeutic cargo packaged within extracellular vesicles (EVs), with the aim of targeting senescent beta cells to mitigate their inflammatory impact.

Overall, miRNAs represent a versatile and therapeutically promising class of molecules, with established roles in gene regulation, beta cell function, diabetes pathophysiology, and the modulation of cellular senescence pathways.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6215695e8bd809fd02cb8b9b7b4123ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1628eba511291c52eab3e72ef0fd0239&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a778c4bc437c223ff92d776f7ab7b6a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08f3e602fed4b4ebfff436b75194d507&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cba0d7fafdd66d2ffb133e04939d15f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-43761b34ecc024bd90bfa8711c45a233&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-044fb2d3ececa99a53eb87d2ee6bf18f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8f09e5d1418f8ae04b43a24b97c1d52d</data>
