</node>
<node id="DNA demethylation">
  <data key="d0">DNA demethylation</data>
  <data key="d1">Biological Process</data>
  <data key="d2">Progressive oxidation of 5mC resulting in formation of 5hmC, 5fC, and 5caC; can introduce genomic vulnerability during differentiation.&lt;SEP&gt;DNA demethylation is a form of epigenetic modulation contributed to by programmed BER and plays a critical role in embryogenesis and cell fate specification.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-de697a7536ea955d878a95580bf8aa11&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e7d877b531b99ded5aba6df6f1635f3</data>
  <data key="d4">Safeguarding genomic integrity in beta-cells: implications for beta-cell differentiation, growth, and dysfunction.</data>
