<node id="beta cell autoimmunity">
  <data key="d0">beta cell autoimmunity</data>
  <data key="d1">Disease</data>
  <data key="d2">Beta cell autoimmunity has peak incidence in early life and during puberty, periods of significant beta cell stress and turnover, potentially linked to unresolved DNA damage.&lt;SEP&gt;Immune-mediated attack on beta cells with peak incidence during infancy and puberty, potentially linked to replication-associated DNA damage vulnerability.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-de697a7536ea955d878a95580bf8aa11&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-35d7a41162ea60151fe17b4e60e06d1b</data>
  <data key="d4">Safeguarding genomic integrity in beta-cells: implications for beta-cell differentiation, growth, and dysfunction.&lt;SEP&gt;Developmental control of DNA damage responses in α- and β-cells shapes the selective beta-cell susceptibility in diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d5">1778571470</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">3</data>
  <data key="d8">cellular senescence / CDKN2A / CDKN1A</data>
