  <data key="d1">Molecule</data>
  <data key="d2">5-Hydroxymethylcytosine (5hmC) marks sites of DNA damage, promotes genome stability, mediates active demethylation required for neuronal differentiation, and regulates beta-cell maturation and expansion.&lt;SEP&gt;5hmC, an oxidation product of 5mC during DNA demethylation; its genomic content progressively increases during progenitor differentiation and beta-cell maturation.</data>
