<node id="DNA double-strand break">
  <data key="d0">DNA double-strand break</data>
  <data key="d1">Biological Process</data>
  <data key="d2">DNA double-strand breaks are a form of DNA damage induced by topoisomerase II and associated with gammaH2AX; cohesin protects against their effects.&lt;SEP&gt;Severe form of DNA damage primarily sensed by ATM, observed in beta cells in T1D, T2D, and rodent models.&lt;SEP&gt;Severe form of DNA damage repaired by NHEJ; induced by GCK activation and associated with p53 activation and cell death in beta cells.</data>
