  <data key="d0">beta-cell maturation</data>
  <data key="d1">Biological Process</data>
  <data key="d2">Beta-cell maturation is regulated by DNA methylation, 5-hydroxymethylcytosine, circadian entrainment, mTORC1-AMPK switching, and postnatal ontogenesis of the islet circadian clock.&lt;SEP&gt;Process by which neonatal beta cells transition from replicative to functionally mature state with glucose responsiveness, involving metabolic reprogramming.&lt;SEP&gt;The process by which beta-cells achieve functional maturity, involving metabolic changes, epigenetic reprogramming, and transcriptional programming.</data>
