<node id="pancreatic progenitor">
  <data key="d0">pancreatic progenitor</data>
  <data key="d1">Cell Type</data>
  <data key="d2">Embryonic progenitor cells from which beta-cells initially differentiate during embryonic life.&lt;SEP&gt;Progenitor cells involved in pancreas development that coordinate cell cycle exit with self-renewal.&lt;SEP&gt;Progenitor cells (PPs) with very low genomic 5hmC content that progressively increases with cell-cycle exit during differentiation.&lt;SEP&gt;Early developmental cell type positive for ONECUT1 and PDX1; numbers reduced by deletion of a type 2 diabetes-associated enhancer in the ONECUT1 locus.&lt;SEP&gt;Developmental precursor cells of the pancreas in which DNMT3A loss selectively increases beta-cell DNA damage vulnerability.&lt;SEP&gt;Progenitor cells of pancreatic lineage in which DNMT3A establishes methylation patterns directing islet cell identity and DNA damage vulnerability.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9e7d877b531b99ded5aba6df6f1635f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-80318e0997c6182c0124775c5f01f6a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-72bf1fbaf7a329c364247108f8b30408&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-044fb2d3ececa99a53eb87d2ee6bf18f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28a44d52c17c29e9741a935aa76e8afe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6204b07313b33d741c243f18ce86735</data>
  <data key="d4">Safeguarding genomic integrity in beta-cells: implications for beta-cell differentiation, growth, and dysfunction.&lt;SEP&gt;The role of the beta cell in type 2 diabetes: new findings from the last 5 years.&lt;SEP&gt;Developmental control of DNA damage responses in α- and β-cells shapes the selective beta-cell susceptibility in diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d5">1778571428</data>
