<node id="LAMP1">
  <data key="d0">LAMP1</data>
  <data key="d1">Protein</data>
  <data key="d2">LAMP1 is an autophagy-associated gene with higher expression in CR state 2 beta cells.&lt;SEP&gt;An autophagy marker with increased expression in CR beta cells.&lt;SEP&gt;LAMP1 is a lysosome marker used to assess autophagy in beta cells; CR significantly increases LAMP1 vesicle density in beta cells.&lt;SEP&gt;Lysosome marker used to assess lysosomal activity and autophagy in beta cells under caloric restriction.&lt;SEP&gt;Lysosomal marker with increased density in CR beta cells, associated with autophagy vesicles.&lt;SEP&gt;Lysosomal marker protein detected by immunohistochemistry using rat anti-LAMP1 antibody.&lt;SEP&gt;Lysosomal marker protein detected as granules in beta cell cytosol and used in colocalization studies with LC3.</data>
