<node id="ad libitum">
  <data key="d0">ad libitum</data>
  <data key="d1">Biological Process</data>
  <data key="d2">Unrestricted dietary feeding condition used as control in caloric restriction experiments, where mice consume food freely.&lt;SEP&gt;Ad libitum (AL) feeding is the control dietary condition used for comparison in single-cell multiome sequencing of islets.&lt;SEP&gt;Standard unrestricted feeding condition (AL) used as a control diet group in the study.&lt;SEP&gt;Ad libitum (AL) feeding is the control dietary condition compared against caloric restriction in mouse studies of beta cell aging.&lt;SEP&gt;Ad libitum (AL) feeding condition used as a control dietary group in the study.&lt;SEP&gt;Normal unrestricted feeding condition (AL) used as control group compared to caloric restriction in beta cell mitochondria studies.&lt;SEP&gt;AL feeding condition used as control in mice for comparison with CR and HFD groups.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f02465fe113dd488219949222d1430e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08e345f1e7ff9529c2ab94760dcb50f5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6cadc21c6ca916dd06510987c1b7dbf4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-75f39153d9f864070e17a74724a6c8c6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-363f3a19905f833d29a7d1242acc6641&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa01ef8f1657a9890660f864f52123c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c85c9569fee140bfd52fcc0bbfbcc9c2</data>
