<node id="meal tolerance test">
  <data key="d0">meal tolerance test</data>
  <data key="d1">Method</data>
  <data key="d2">In vivo metabolic test measuring blood glucose and insulin levels to assess glucose homeostasis in mice.&lt;SEP&gt;Oral mixed-meal tolerance test (MTT) using a high-carbohydrate nutrient shake to quantify beta cell insulin release and glucose homeostasis in vivo.&lt;SEP&gt;In vivo test measuring blood glucose and insulin levels in response to a meal to assess glucose homeostasis.&lt;SEP&gt;Test used to measure blood glucose and insulin levels in AL and CR mice after 12 months on diet.&lt;SEP&gt;The meal tolerance test (MTT) is used to measure blood glucose and insulin levels and their ratio over time in dietary intervention studies.&lt;SEP&gt;Test performed in 6-hour fasted mice using a gavage of Ensure Original Shake to assess glucose homeostasis and insulin secretion.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-68a87a3a1f3eb5d8b0e53b41df492512&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2e4a544176811f5b43952b185e1ed3a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-75f39153d9f864070e17a74724a6c8c6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce68225f2288adf7d07962282496e8c5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-363f3a19905f833d29a7d1242acc6641&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d286ee457150be65228790e800b5207b</data>
