<node id="beta cell dedifferentiation">
  <data key="d0">beta cell dedifferentiation</data>
  <data key="d1">Biological Process</data>
  <data key="d2">Loss of beta cell identity proposed as a mechanism of diabetic beta cell failure.&lt;SEP&gt;Progressive loss of beta cell identity markers and gain of stress response gene expression observed in type 2 diabetes islets.&lt;SEP&gt;Beta cell dedifferentiation is a process in type 2 diabetes characterized by de-repression of immature genes and loss of beta cell maturity.&lt;SEP&gt;Process by which beta cells lose their differentiated identity; suppressed by sustained weight loss.&lt;SEP&gt;Loss of beta-cell identity and differentiation status proposed as a mechanism of diabetic beta-cell failure.&lt;SEP&gt;Loss of beta-cell identity driven by unrepaired DNA damage under metabolic stress, predisposing to type 2 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3f63ca40b092870f725a75e7a36045d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ddac43d21e0426c8d61d02d10c0cb772&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4e8cbb766d17c90c84d2a9452a51a41e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8f09e5d1418f8ae04b43a24b97c1d52d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce72a72ed1aaea72aac97c28374f8f86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-35d7a41162ea60151fe17b4e60e06d1b</data>
