  <data key="d1">Molecule</data>
  <data key="d2">Nitrogen-15 stable isotope used to label mice in utero; retained in nuclei of long-lived post-mitotic cells as a measure of cell age.&lt;SEP&gt;Nitrogen-15 stable isotope used to label mice for MIMS-EM studies, enabling tracking of cell division cycles through dilution of the isotope in cell nuclei.&lt;SEP&gt;Stable isotope measured by MIMS to determine cell age through 15N/14N ratios in cell nuclei; proliferating cells lose 50% of nuclear 15N per division.</data>
