  <data key="d0">RMSD</data>
  <data key="d1">Method</data>
  <data key="d2">Root mean square deviation (RMSD) is a metric used to measure structural similarity between paired protein models, applied here to compare MAFA and MAFB structural models across phosphorylation states.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-84ba2041af7b71a5fc2faad1de1c95dd</data>
  <data key="d4">Defining unique structural features in the MAFA and MAFB transcription factors that control Insulin gene activity.</data>
