<node id="TIF-IA">
  <data key="d0">TIF-IA</data>
  <data key="d1">Protein</data>
  <data key="d2">Transcription initiation factor for RNA Pol I; its depletion genetically induces nucleolar stress and beta cell senescence by inhibiting rRNA synthesis.&lt;SEP&gt;Transcription initiation factor IA (TIF-IA/Rrn3), an essential transcriptional co-factor required for rRNA transcription by the RNA Pol I machinery; its depletion impairs rRNA synthesis and induces nucleolar stress and beta cell senescence.&lt;SEP&gt;Essential transcription factor for rRNA synthesis; its genetic ablation triggers nucleolar stress leading to smooth muscle cell senescence and vascular degeneration via ATM/ATR-p53 axis.&lt;SEP&gt;TIF-IA is a transcription initiation factor targeted by shRNA knockdown constructs in the study, associated with ribosomal RNA transcription.&lt;SEP&gt;Mouse protein targeted for knockdown using shRNA in beta-TC-6 cells to examine senescence-associated phenotypes.&lt;SEP&gt;Gene targeted by shRNA constructs (pLKO.1-mTIF-IA-shRNA) in experimental knockdown studies.</data>
