  <data key="d1">Tissue</data>
  <data key="d2">A subnuclear organelle that serves as a sensor of DNA damage and site of rRNA transcription, subject to morphological disruption in nucleolar stress.&lt;SEP&gt;Subnuclear organelle where rRNA synthesis occurs; undergoes fragmentation and NPM diffusion under nucleolar stress conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;Subnuclear organelle coordinating stress response, genome stability, and DNA damage recognition.&lt;SEP&gt;The nucleolus is a cellular organelle that acts as a sensor of various stress signals and is involved in rRNA transcription and genomic stability surveillance.</data>
