  <data key="d0">double-strand breaks</data>
  <data key="d1">Biological Process</data>
  <data key="d2">Double-strand breaks (DSBs) are a form of DNA damage classically linked to ATM activation, although ATM can also be activated independently of DSBs by nucleolar stress.</data>
