<node id="DNMT3A">
  <data key="d0">DNMT3A</data>
  <data key="d1">Protein</data>
  <data key="d2">De novo DNA methyltransferase whose loss in pancreatic progenitors selectively increases DNA damage vulnerability of beta cells.&lt;SEP&gt;DNA methyltransferase 3a gene conditionally deleted in pancreatic progenitor lineage using Pdx1-Cre mice&lt;SEP&gt;De novo DNA methyltransferase with essential role in paternal and maternal imprinting.&lt;SEP&gt;Gene encoding DNA methyltransferase 3a that establishes DNA methylation patterns defining beta- versus alpha-cell identity and shapes DNA damage susceptibility during pancreatic progenitor differentiation.&lt;SEP&gt;DNA methyltransferase 3a, crucial for beta cell genomic integrity during rapid postnatal expansion and DNA methylation maintenance.&lt;SEP&gt;DNA methyltransferase 3a, required for maintaining genomic stability in beta cells during postnatal growth and maturation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-28a44d52c17c29e9741a935aa76e8afe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c63b5ad461844f8e5d9a90f5dfc52f1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce72a72ed1aaea72aac97c28374f8f86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e953ac093714735fa9b5b27463bf5dff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-35d7a41162ea60151fe17b4e60e06d1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6204b07313b33d741c243f18ce86735</data>
