<node id="G2/M checkpoint">
  <data key="d0">G2/M checkpoint</data>
  <data key="d1">Biological Process</data>
  <data key="d2">Cell cycle phase during which beta cells resolve DNA breaks more efficiently and prioritize error-free DNA repair compared to alpha cells.&lt;SEP&gt;Cell-cycle checkpoint mechanism with cell-type-specific roles; alpha cells appear to allow DNA damage through mitosis while beta cells resolve damage before mitosis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-28a44d52c17c29e9741a935aa76e8afe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-35d7a41162ea60151fe17b4e60e06d1b</data>
