<node id="cell replication">
  <data key="d0">cell replication</data>
  <data key="d1">Biological Process</data>
  <data key="d2">Beta and alpha cell proliferation measured using KI67 marker in multiple diabetic and metabolic mouse models&lt;SEP&gt;Cell replication in neonatal alpha and beta cells declines from postnatal day 7 to day 21, with alpha cells showing higher replication rates.&lt;SEP&gt;Cell division process; alpha cells replicate at higher rates than beta cells during the neonatal growth phase.&lt;SEP&gt;Cellular proliferation process; beta cells in 3aPKO mice show reduced replication at P7 yet increased DNA damage.&lt;SEP&gt;Cell division process; reduced in 3aPKO beta cells at P7, while alpha cells retain replicative capacity postnatally.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c63b5ad461844f8e5d9a90f5dfc52f1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e953ac093714735fa9b5b27463bf5dff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7af94fcbbc3d167377ece712218fa36b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c461d96db4bed849ef22472fc2b0cd0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-35d7a41162ea60151fe17b4e60e06d1b</data>
