<edge source="Insulin Gene" target="MAFA">
  <data key="d12">1.0</data>
  <data key="d13">MAFA is a glucose-regulated and pancreatic beta-cell-specific transcriptional activator for the insulin gene.&lt;SEP&gt;MafA binds to the C1 element and the enhancer region of the insulin gene, activating its transcription in islet β cells.&lt;SEP&gt;MafA activates insulin gene expression in pancreatic islet β cells as a member of the large Maf transcription family.&lt;SEP&gt;MafA is a dedicated activator of the insulin gene in vivo.</data>
  <data key="d14">beta-cell-specific,transcriptional activation&lt;SEP&gt;binding,islet β-cell expression,transcriptional activation,transcriptional regulation</data>
  <data key="d15">chunk-fffe587d9d8a94d6179115102ef90a2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf89ad08d3f81ffe84c9bf7f208c604b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4e0ae079210c3ef99872d0747c5a9b88&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f64af938dff7c5f186bd7024d92cbc0</data>
  <data key="d16">Members of the large Maf transcription family regulate insulin gene transcription in islet beta cells.&lt;SEP&gt;MafB Is Important for Pancreatic β-Cell Maintenance under a MafA-Deficient Condition.&lt;SEP&gt;Sex-biased islet β cell dysfunction is caused by the MODY MAFA S64F variant by inducing premature aging and senescence in males.&lt;SEP&gt;MAFA missense mutation causes familial insulinomatosis and diabetes mellitus.</data>
  <data key="d17">1778561818</data>
  <data key="d18"></data>
</edge>
