<edge source="G6pc2" target="MAFA">
  <data key="d12">5.0</data>
  <data key="d13">MafA stimulates G6pc2 transcription by binding to the −177/−164 bp element in its promoter region, with G6pc2 significantly downregulated in adult MafAΔPanc islets.&lt;SEP&gt;MafA regulates G6pc2 expression in adult islets; loss of MafA leads to significant downregulation of G6pc2 mRNA and protein levels.&lt;SEP&gt;MafA regulates the mRNA expression of G6pc2 in β-cells, with reduced levels observed in 3-week-old MafaΔpanc islets.&lt;SEP&gt;MafA regulates G6pc2, a gene involved in glucose metabolism in β-cells.&lt;SEP&gt;MafA regulates G6pc2 expression in β-cells, and its decreased level in MafaΔpanc islets contributes to impaired glucose-stimulated insulin secretion.&lt;SEP&gt;MafA regulates islet-specific G6PC2 (glucose-6-phosphatase catalytic subunit-related protein) gene expression together with Foxa2.</data>
