<edge source="Type 2 Diabetes" target="cellular senescence">
  <data key="d12">5.0</data>
  <data key="d13">Beta cell senescence has been demonstrated to contribute to the pathogenesis of type 2 diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Beta cell senescence occurs during the development and onset of T2D in mouse models and human pancreas tissue.&lt;SEP&gt;Type 2 diabetes mellitus is associated with cellular senescence in the skeleton, with increased CDKN2A and CDKN1A expression in osteocyte-enriched samples.&lt;SEP&gt;Acceleration of beta cell aging and senescence determines diabetes, and senolysis of senescent beta cells improves disease outcomes.&lt;SEP&gt;Pancreatic beta cell senescence contributes to the pathogenesis of type 2 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d14">associated_with,contributes_to,pathogenesis</data>
  <data key="d15">chunk-9bdc00ebaa404f286432a974cec96702&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8f87338453daad7a9a4624ce798bcf6e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f25c34949789593e96b7a57ead73f11&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f63ca40b092870f725a75e7a36045d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-15ab370ab273e97005ced113e59cc48a</data>
