  <data key="d12">5.0</data>
  <data key="d13">Beta cell failure is a key feature of type 2 diabetes, observed more often in males.&lt;SEP&gt;Beta cell failure contributes to type 2 diabetes pathogenesis, with sex-specific heterogeneity in males and females.&lt;SEP&gt;Beta cell failure is a central feature of T2D, with sex differences in severity and prevalence.&lt;SEP&gt;Type 2 diabetes is characterized by beta cell failure, with males being more prone to this failure than females.&lt;SEP&gt;Beta cell failure driven by developmental, genetic, and environmental factors influences diabetes risk.</data>
