  <data key="d13">MafaΔpanc is a mouse model with pancreas-specific loss of MafA, used to study MafA's role in β-cell function.&lt;SEP&gt;MafAΔPanc mice have MafA deleted pancreas-wide using the Cre-loxP system, with MafA effectively removed by E18.5.</data>
  <data key="d14">functional study,gene knockout&lt;SEP&gt;gene deletion,mutant model</data>
  <data key="d15">chunk-a5af2ab88dac4e2b983a277be1a9c536&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff8c5dc48dde6c3ccfdc01c9e025403d</data>
  <data key="d16">MafA and MafB regulate genes critical to beta-cells in a unique temporal manner.&lt;SEP&gt;The MafA transcription factor becomes essential to islet β-cells soon after birth.</data>
  <data key="d17">1778561533</data>
  <data key="d18"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="MafaΔpanc" target="MAFB">
  <data key="d12">5.0</data>
  <data key="d13">MafB is retained in a fraction of the mutant insulin+ cell population in MafAΔPanc islets, suggesting an unusual interrelationship between MafA and MafB.&lt;SEP&gt;In MafAΔPanc islets, MafB-dependent target gene expression was compromised in adult islets, even though MafB was retained in a fraction of the mutant insulin+ cell population.&lt;SEP&gt;In MafAΔPanc mutant islets, MafB expression is sustained in a fraction of insulin-positive cells, unlike in wild-type where MafB is absent from adult insulin-positive cells.&lt;SEP&gt;MafB levels were amplified at E18.5 in embryonic MafAΔPanc mutants, suggesting MafB may serve a compensatory role.&lt;SEP&gt;MafB protein expression is retained in a fraction of insulin+ cells in adult MafAΔPanc mice, but does not compensate for the loss of MafA.&lt;SEP&gt;Misexpressing MafB in MafAΔpanc β cells cannot rescue MafA function, illustrating functional differences between MafA and MafB.</data>
  <data key="d14">compensation failure,compensatory retention,compensatory upregulation,gene expression impact,mutant model,protein retention,sustained expression,transcription factor interaction&lt;SEP&gt;functional rescue,misexpression</data>
  <data key="d15">chunk-9693157a2d458ecc8255c49ec77d95f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5f82db25373e25b34bbbcfebc1c0f861&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff8c5dc48dde6c3ccfdc01c9e025403d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41e9c4875e9ee2b378c620275d81fe7e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ddb7aaa2476f3163b5c3de684504f42b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-74fc4f55c8c6d83ebd1d8dba07d90692</data>
  <data key="d16">MafA and MafB regulate genes critical to beta-cells in a unique temporal manner.&lt;SEP&gt;Sex-biased islet β cell dysfunction is caused by the MODY MAFA S64F variant by inducing premature aging and senescence in males.</data>
  <data key="d17">1778561081</data>
  <data key="d18"></data>
</edge>
