<edge source="MAFA" target="GAST">
  <data key="d12">3.0</data>
  <data key="d13">MafA represses postnatal gastrin production in mouse β cells; its loss leads to inappropriate Gast expression in MafA∆β islets.&lt;SEP&gt;MAFA directly represses GAST transcription in mouse β cells, with the conserved MAFB binding site in mice also effectively binding MAFA.&lt;SEP&gt;MAFA depletion in EndoC-βH1 cells did not significantly change GAST mRNA levels, in contrast to MAFB depletion, indicating MAFA does not principally regulate GAST in human β cells.&lt;SEP&gt;MafA actively represses GAST+ cell-associated transcriptional programs; loss of MafA leads to induction of GAST expression in β cells.</data>
