  <data key="d13">MAFA directly represses GAST transcription in mouse islet β cells, playing a role in maintaining β cell identity.&lt;SEP&gt;MafA is expressed in human β cells and, as homodimers, regulates adult β-cell function alongside MafB.&lt;SEP&gt;MafA is predominantly produced in adult mouse β cells and in postnatal human islet β cells after the juvenile period, playing a role in β cell identity and insulin expression.&lt;SEP&gt;MafA deficiency leads to MafB reexpression in adult β cells, affecting glucose tolerance and islet structure.</data>
