<edge source="MAFA" target="SLC30A8">
  <data key="d12">9.0</data>
  <data key="d13">The relation (MafA, Slc30a8) describes a regulatory relationship in which the transcription factor MafA directly controls the expression of Slc30a8 in pancreatic islet β-cells.

MafA regulates both the mRNA and protein expression of Slc30a8, a gene encoding a zinc transporter that plays a critical role in vesicle maturation and insulin granule production in β-cells. This regulatory relationship is essential for normal β-cell function, as Slc30a8 is involved in the proper maturation of secretory vesicles and the maintenance of insulin granule integrity.

The functional significance of this regulation is evidenced by studies using MafAΔPanc (also referred to as MafaΔpanc) mouse models, in which functional MafA is selectively ablated in pancreatic cells. In these models, Slc30a8 expression is profoundly and significantly reduced in adult insulin-positive β-cells. Notably, Slc30a8 has been identified as the first gene to show significant reduction — detectable as early as 2 weeks — in MafaΔpanc islets, underscoring its position as an early and sensitive downstream target of MafA. The loss of Slc30a8 expression in MafA mutant β-cells contributes to diminished insulin granule production, linking MafA-mediated transcriptional control to a critical aspect of β-cell secretory function.

This regulatory relationship is specific to adult islet β-cells, as MafA regulates Slc30a8 specifically within mature, adult insulin-expressing β-cells. Slc30a8 has also been detected in pancreatic immunostaining studies examining MafA-regulated pathways, further supporting its status as a key target within the MafA transcriptional network in the endocrine pancreas.</data>
  <data key="d14">adult expression,adult islet,adult regulation,gene expression,gene regulation,granule production,target protein,transcription factor target,transcriptional activation,transcriptional regulation,β-cell function</data>
  <data key="d15">chunk-5f82db25373e25b34bbbcfebc1c0f861&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f7f8610c162035d52f2edbe846e8a97&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc7255d0eadb6b7f3a3a51c10b8ea742&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ddb7aaa2476f3163b5c3de684504f42b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a5af2ab88dac4e2b983a277be1a9c536&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f67b6052ac2da6848aaabbd71f9d4d53&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-94526413b6fbcf0ec99212789cec9eea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-207f97a443acec0faaf8f9f2d208e61f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ee443fb4c37f27d6895254d3f95c708</data>
  <data key="d16">The MafA transcription factor becomes essential to islet β-cells soon after birth.&lt;SEP&gt;MafA and MafB regulate genes critical to beta-cells in a unique temporal manner.</data>
