<edge source="MAFB" target="GAST">
  <data key="d12">4.0</data>
  <data key="d13">MAFB negatively regulates GAST expression; knockdown of MAFB in EndoC-βH2 cells leads to inappropriate GAST expression.&lt;SEP&gt;MAFB directly represses GAST transcription in adult human islet β cells by binding to specific sites approximately 1.5 kb upstream of the GAST gene transcriptional start site.&lt;SEP&gt;MAFB represses GAST expression in human β cells, and its depletion leads to upregulation of GAST mRNA and protein in EndoC-βH2 cells.&lt;SEP&gt;MAFB represses GAST-associated transcriptional programs; reduced MAFB levels are associated with enrichment of GAST+ gene signatures in β cells.</data>
