<edge source="MAFB" target="PDX1">
  <data key="d12">3.0</data>
  <data key="d13">MAFB and PDX1 have binding sites near the GAST gene and may act in concert to regulate GAST expression.&lt;SEP&gt;MafB loss is associated with an approximately 50% reduction in Pdx1 mRNA levels at E18.5, reflecting loss of the MafB−/− insulin-negative cell population.&lt;SEP&gt;MafB serves as the primary activator of Pdx1 in developing pancreatic cells.&lt;SEP&gt;MafB was identified as a primary activator of Pdx1.&lt;SEP&gt;MafB maintains normal expression levels of Pdx1; its deletion reduces Pdx1 expression affecting β-cell development.&lt;SEP&gt;MAFB provides enhanced activation of Insulin-reporter in the presence of PDX1, while MAFA does not.&lt;SEP&gt;MAFBWT cooperates with PDX1 for Insulin reporter activation; PDX1 activity requires MAFB C-terminal sequences.</data>
  <data key="d14">activates,cooperates,cooperates_with,cooperative regulation,gene activation,gene expression,primary activator,primary regulator,requires,transcription factor interaction,transcriptional regulation</data>
