<edge source="MAFB" target="β Cells">
  <data key="d12">1.0</data>
  <data key="d13">MAFB is essential in adult human β cells for maintaining cell identity by repressing non-β cell hormone expression such as GAST.&lt;SEP&gt;MafB deletion from β cells delays β-cell development and reduces expression of key β-cell genes including Ins1, Ins2, Pdx1, and Glut2.&lt;SEP&gt;MafB is expressed in human β cells throughout adulthood and is important for maintaining mature β-cell function, proliferation, and survival.&lt;SEP&gt;MAFB, but not MAFA, prevents GAST, SST, and PPY gene expression in human β cells, maintaining β cell identity.&lt;SEP&gt;MafB is reexpressed in adult β cells under MafA-deficient conditions and plays a postnatal role in β cell function.&lt;SEP&gt;Removing MafB from β cells is speculated to further inhibit β-cell mass expansion by reducing islet numbers and islet size under HFD conditions.</data>
  <data key="d14">cell identity,transcription factor&lt;SEP&gt;developmental role,functional regulation,gene expression,gene regulation,maintenance,transcription factor regulation,β cell identity&lt;SEP&gt;adaptation,cellular function,gene expression,inhibition,β-cell mass</data>
