<edge source="MAFB" target="AlphaFold 2">
  <data key="d12">8.0</data>
  <data key="d13">AlphaFold 2 was employed extensively in structural studies of MAFB, serving as the primary computational tool for predicting and modeling the three-dimensional organization of this protein across multiple functional and pathological states.

Specifically, AlphaFold 2 was used for de novo structural modeling of full-length MAFB homodimers, encompassing unphosphorylated, fully phosphorylated, and phosphomimetic variant forms, as well as pathogenic mutant forms. These modeling efforts allowed researchers to examine the conformational effects associated with phosphorylation and disease-associated mutations. The tool was also applied to determine the three-dimensional architecture of disordered and otherwise underdefined regions of MAFB, providing structural insight into domains that had previously lacked clear characterization.

Through these predictions, AlphaFold 2 revealed novel structural features of MAFB, including the C-terminal tail and various disordered regions, as well as structurally unique regions within the homodimeric assembly. Collectively, AlphaFold 2 enabled comprehensive structural coverage of MAFB in its wildtype, mutant, and post-translationally modified states, significantly advancing the understanding of MAFB's three-dimensional organization and its alterations under pathogenic conditions.</data>
  <data key="d14">analysis,analyzes,models,predicts,predicts_structure,protein analysis,structural prediction</data>
  <data key="d15">chunk-8b5b330edc0a8ae22148338c6d94f154&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb32288d5dedac1b23370508bf2f7b2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84ba2041af7b71a5fc2faad1de1c95dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3384cef9855a1b408c68f7d1ea3153c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f4fecd9e508da1daa4a0d2d27a7e759&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19fff7a7048ab7112926e25c2e46450b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d07a2e48a0133bedad1b6e79e652b89c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eae638e9cabe91a68fc062c9981b0e86</data>
  <data key="d16">Defining unique structural features in the MAFA and MAFB transcription factors that control Insulin gene activity.</data>
  <data key="d17">1778569850</data>
  <data key="d18"></data>
</edge>
