  <data key="d13">MAFB contains a basic-leucine-zipper domain involved in DNA binding and dimerization functions.&lt;SEP&gt;MAFB contains a basic-leucine-zipper domain (residues 211–302) responsible for DNA binding and dimerization.&lt;SEP&gt;MAFB contains a basic-leucine-zipper domain responsible for DNA binding and dimerization.</data>
