<edge source="MAFB" target="ISL1">
  <data key="d12">4.0</data>
  <data key="d13">Pan-endocrine Isl1 expression is unaffected in MafB−/− mutants, supporting that MafB is linked to cell maturation but not islet cell formation or viability.&lt;SEP&gt;MAFB provides enhanced activation of Insulin-reporter in the presence of ISL1, while MAFA does not.&lt;SEP&gt;MAFBWT cooperates with ISL1 to activate the Insulin -238 WT reporter; ISL1 stimulation is lost when either N- or C-terminal regions of MAFB are exchanged with MAFA sequences.&lt;SEP&gt;MAFB specifically recruits ISL1 to activate the INS-driven reporter, a property not shared by MAFA.</data>
  <data key="d14">activates,cell formation,cooperates,cooperates_with,independence,recruits</data>
  <data key="d15">chunk-5f82db25373e25b34bbbcfebc1c0f861&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ecb3c400fe73c10974d8a6b3b2160b23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d07a2e48a0133bedad1b6e79e652b89c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eae638e9cabe91a68fc062c9981b0e86</data>
