<edge source="MAFB" target="MAFB_S70A">
  <data key="d12">8.0</data>
  <data key="d13">MAFB_S70A is a pathogenic mutant form of the MAFB protein, generated by substituting serine at position 70 (Ser70) with alanine (Ser70Ala). This mutation is located within the transactivation domain of MAFB, and the resulting variant is characterized primarily by the loss of the S70 phosphosite, rendering it an underphosphorylated or hypophosphorylated form relative to the wild-type protein.

Despite its pathogenic classification, MAFB_S70A does not exhibit significant structural differences compared to wild-type MAFB, and it retains a similar DNA binding capacity. However, the absence of phosphorylation at serine 70 leads to altered functional interactions, distinguishing it from the wild-type in terms of its biological activity and regulatory behavior. Due to its reduced phosphorylation state, MAFB_S70A has been utilized in partial phosphorylation mimicry modeling studies to investigate the functional consequences of this post-translational modification.

The mutant has also been specifically analyzed in the context of cooperative transcriptional activation, particularly with respect to its interactions with PDX1 and ISL1, highlighting its relevance in understanding how phosphorylation at Ser70 modulates MAFB's cooperative activity with other transcription factors. Overall, MAFB_S70A serves as an important research tool for elucidating the role of Ser70 phosphorylation in MAFB-mediated transcriptional regulation and its contribution to disease-associated mechanisms.</data>
  <data key="d14">mutant_of,pathogenic mutation,reduced_phosphorylation,structural similarity</data>
  <data key="d15">chunk-8b5b330edc0a8ae22148338c6d94f154&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb32288d5dedac1b23370508bf2f7b2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84ba2041af7b71a5fc2faad1de1c95dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3384cef9855a1b408c68f7d1ea3153c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ecb3c400fe73c10974d8a6b3b2160b23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f4fecd9e508da1daa4a0d2d27a7e759&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19fff7a7048ab7112926e25c2e46450b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d07a2e48a0133bedad1b6e79e652b89c</data>
  <data key="d16">Defining unique structural features in the MAFA and MAFB transcription factors that control Insulin gene activity.</data>
  <data key="d17">1778569832</data>
