  <data key="d12">3.0</data>
  <data key="d13">Mutations clustering in the amino-terminal transcriptional activation domain of MAFB cause multicentric carpotarsal osteolysis.&lt;SEP&gt;MAFB was identified as the causative gene for multicentric carpotarsal osteolysis (MCTO) by whole exome sequencing.&lt;SEP&gt;MAFB is associated with multicentric carpotarsal osteolysis, a skeletal disease with unique phenotype.</data>
