<edge source="MAFB" target="INS">
  <data key="d12">8.0</data>
  <data key="d13">The relation (INS, MAFB) describes the regulatory role of MAFB, a transcription factor, in controlling the expression and transcription of the insulin gene (INS).

MAFB directly stimulates insulin enhancer-driven reporter activity, as demonstrated through transfection assays, and independently activates insulin-reporter expression. It physically binds to the insulin control element DNA, including the human INS MAFA/B binding site, as confirmed by electrophoretic mobility shift assays (EMSA), underscoring its direct molecular interaction with regulatory regions of the INS gene.

Beyond its independent activity, MAFB also regulates INS gene transcription in cooperation with several islet-enriched transcription factors, including PDX1, ISL1, and GLIS3. MAFB interacts with ISL1 and other transcription factors to collectively activate INS enhancer-driven transcription, highlighting its role within a broader transcriptional regulatory network in pancreatic islet beta cells.

The importance of MAFB in insulin gene transcription has been established across multiple species, indicating a conserved and fundamental role in pancreatic islet biology. Collectively, MAFB regulates INS gene expression through both direct DNA binding and cooperative interactions with key islet transcription factors, making it a critical component of the transcriptional machinery governing insulin production in beta cells.</data>
  <data key="d14">activates,binds,regulates,targets</data>
  <data key="d15">chunk-eb32288d5dedac1b23370508bf2f7b2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84ba2041af7b71a5fc2faad1de1c95dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3384cef9855a1b408c68f7d1ea3153c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ecb3c400fe73c10974d8a6b3b2160b23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f4fecd9e508da1daa4a0d2d27a7e759&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19fff7a7048ab7112926e25c2e46450b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d07a2e48a0133bedad1b6e79e652b89c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eae638e9cabe91a68fc062c9981b0e86</data>
  <data key="d16">Defining unique structural features in the MAFA and MAFB transcription factors that control Insulin gene activity.</data>
  <data key="d17">1778569823</data>
  <data key="d18"></data>
</edge>
