<edge source="Insulinomatosis" target="MAFA_S64F">
  <data key="d12">1.0</data>
  <data key="d13">The MAFAS64F variant is associated with insulinomatosis in affected heterozygous human carriers, studied using the MafAS64F/+ mouse model.&lt;SEP&gt;The p.Ser64Phe MAFA mutation is associated with insulinomatosis, a multicentric insulin-producing neuroendocrine tumor condition.&lt;SEP&gt;The p.Ser64Phe MAFA mutation is identified as the genetic cause of familial insulinomatosis, leading to hyperinsulinemic hypoglycemia.&lt;SEP&gt;The p.Ser64Phe MAFA mutation is causally associated with insulinomatosis, manifesting as multiple pancreatic neuroendocrine tumors and hyperinsulinemic hypoglycemia in affected patients.&lt;SEP&gt;The p.Ser64Phe MAFA mutation is associated with the development of insulinomatosis by increasing protein stability and transactivation, potentially inducing β-cell transformation.&lt;SEP&gt;The MAFA p.Ser64Phe variant is associated with the development of insulinomatosis in affected family members.&lt;SEP&gt;Individuals carrying the heterozygous MAFA S64F mutation may develop insulinomatosis, a condition of hyperinsulinemic hypoglycemia.&lt;SEP&gt;The MAFA S64F mutation is associated with adult-onset β cell dysfunction including insulinomatosis in human carriers.&lt;SEP&gt;The MAFA_S64F missense mutation induces the phenotype of insulinomatosis in human patients.&lt;SEP&gt;MAFA_S64F variant predisposes female carriers to insulinomatosis at a 4:1 female-to-male ratio.&lt;SEP&gt;MAFA_S64F mutation is associated with insulinomatosis, more prevalent in females (4:1).&lt;SEP&gt;MAFA_S64F variant predisposes female carriers to insulinomatosis at a 4:1 female-to-male ratio.&lt;SEP&gt;MAFA_S64F mutation is associated with insulinomatosis, more prevalent in females (4:1).&lt;SEP&gt;The S64F substitution in MAFA prevents priming serine 65 phosphorylation and produces insulinomatosis.&lt;SEP&gt;MAFA missense mutation Ser64Phe causes familial insulinomatosis and diabetes mellitus.</data>
  <data key="d14">associated with,pathophysiological outcome&lt;SEP&gt;causation,disease causation,genetic association,oncogenic phenotype&lt;SEP&gt;disease association,genetic causation&lt;SEP&gt;disease causation,oncogenic potential&lt;SEP&gt;genetic causation,pathogenic variant&lt;SEP&gt;disease association,disease causation,genetic association,β cell dysfunction&lt;SEP&gt;associated_with,causes,predisposes</data>
  <data key="d15">chunk-9b3deb83588a816faad5340f542e1f43&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fffe587d9d8a94d6179115102ef90a2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e531f038e6fcc1cbb89c2336af984719&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-71db066aa18a18c64b2b33ad26f7bfab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6854465a5ab40a3dbe223209e2c5cd66&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-348e687c811009b30863b17f466ac662&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-74fc4f55c8c6d83ebd1d8dba07d90692&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5f38c4d8fe95ae0a2b5cc05069361348&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b1a171c046b7e074fd282a07d58cc39&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8304b17dc893b8c9bfb7bfdb03703396&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b861cee193cad9e0f142051047e83aae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3384cef9855a1b408c68f7d1ea3153c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f4fecd9e508da1daa4a0d2d27a7e759</data>
  <data key="d16">Sex-biased islet β cell dysfunction is caused by the MODY MAFA S64F variant by inducing premature aging and senescence in males.&lt;SEP&gt;MAFA missense mutation causes familial insulinomatosis and diabetes mellitus.</data>
  <data key="d17">1778562728</data>
  <data key="d18"></data>
</edge>
