<edge source="A0B0 Mice" target="High-Fat Diet (HFD)">
  <data key="d12">5.0</data>
  <data key="d13">A0B0 mice developed diabetes and severely impaired glucose tolerance after 5 months of high-fat diet treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;HFD increased body weights of all mouse groups including A0B0 to the same degree.&lt;SEP&gt;A0B0 mice were subjected to HFD treatment and exhibited severely impaired glucose tolerance, increased body weight, decreased islet numbers, and diabetic symptoms.&lt;SEP&gt;HFD treatment was used to induce obesity and reveal more severe metabolic phenotypes in A0B0 double-knockout mice, including diabetes development.&lt;SEP&gt;A0B0 mice were fed an HFD to induce metabolic stress and assess diabetes susceptibility and islet morphology.</data>
