<edge source="High-Fat Diet" target="beta cell">
  <data key="d12">1.0</data>
  <data key="d13">Chronic high-fat feeding induces both adaptive and maladaptive mechanisms in pancreatic β-cells.&lt;SEP&gt;HFD was used to assess beta cell insulin release and glucose homeostasis in vivo and in vitro alongside AL and CR conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;HFD beta cells show reduced expression of function-associated genes and increased expression of stress and diabetes-associated genes.&lt;SEP&gt;High-fat diet-induced diabetic mice show pancreatic beta cell senescence contributing to type 2 diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;HFD increases the fraction of non-dividing beta cells enriched for p53-mediated apoptotic DDR and compromises robust DNA repair during beta-cell replication.&lt;SEP&gt;HFD-induced metabolic stress impairs DNA repair in beta cells and increases DNA damage.</data>
  <data key="d14">metabolic stress,β-cell adaptation&lt;SEP&gt;affects,causes_senescence_in,impairs,increases,induces stress,reduces function,stresses</data>
