<edge source="p16Ink4a" target="beta cell">
  <data key="d12">4.0</data>
  <data key="d13">p16Ink4a is frequently upregulated in senescent beta cells in both mouse and human.&lt;SEP&gt;p16Ink4a marks a distinct subpopulation of senescent beta cells, comprising ~30-40% in NOD mice at 14-15 weeks.&lt;SEP&gt;p16Ink4a is frequently upregulated in senescent beta cells in both mouse and human.&lt;SEP&gt;p16Ink4a marks a distinct subpopulation of senescent beta cells, comprising ~30-40% in NOD mice at 14-15 weeks.&lt;SEP&gt;P16INK4A-induced senescence in pancreatic beta cells enhances insulin secretion.&lt;SEP&gt;P16INK4A expression in human beta cells is age-dependent, increasing from 8% of prenatal to about 63% of adult beta cells.&lt;SEP&gt;P16INK4A expression increases with age in pancreatic beta cells and regulates beta cell proliferation, function, and senescence.&lt;SEP&gt;P16INK4a-induced senescence of pancreatic beta cells enhances insulin secretion.</data>
  <data key="d14">expressed_in,marks,upregulated_in&lt;SEP&gt;expressed_in,increases_with_age,induces,regulates</data>
