<edge source="MAFAWT" target="MAFA_S64F">
  <data key="d12">2.0</data>
  <data key="d13">MAFAWT serves as the wild-type control in transfection experiments comparing wild-type and S64F mutant MAFA function in Human EndoC-βH2 cells.&lt;SEP&gt;MAFAS64F shows faster migrating properties compared to MAFAWT due to phosphorylation impairment, as confirmed by immunoblot analysis in EndoC-βH2 cells.&lt;SEP&gt;MAFAS64F and MAFAWT are compared in conditioned media and immunostaining experiments to evaluate differential effects on EndoC-βH2 cells.&lt;SEP&gt;MAFAWT serves as the reference for all phosphorylation sites, while MAFA_S64F excludes residues 49, 53, 57, 61, and 65 from phosphomimetic substitution to model partial phosphorylation.</data>
