<edge source="DNA Damage" target="beta cell">
  <data key="d12">1.0</data>
  <data key="d13">DNA damage to beta cells in culture recapitulates features of senescent beta cells that accumulate in type 1 diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;DNA damage to beta cells in culture recapitulates features of senescent beta cells accumulating in type 1 diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Unresolved DNA damage is a key early driver of beta-cell defects in diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;DNA damage was assessed in beta cells via 53BP1-positive foci quantification.&lt;SEP&gt;Accumulation of DNA damage drives beta-cell dysfunction, senescence, and death in type 1 and type 2 diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Beta cells exhibit DNA damage during neonatal growth, with approximately 50% of H2AX-positive beta cells also replicating.&lt;SEP&gt;Beta cells preferentially accumulate DNA damage under metabolic stress, obesity-induced T2D, and autoimmune T1D conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;Beta cells in 3aPKO mice show elevated DNA damage persisting from neonatal stage to adulthood.</data>
  <data key="d14">senescence induction,type 1 diabetes&lt;SEP&gt;accumulates,affects,assessed_in,associated_with,causes,drives,exhibits,vulnerability,vulnerable,vulnerable_to</data>
