<edge source="DNA Damage" target="alpha cell">
  <data key="d12">5.0</data>
  <data key="d13">Alpha cells exhibit higher replication rates and DNA damage during neonatal growth compared to beta cells.&lt;SEP&gt;Alpha cells display higher levels of DNA damage compared to beta cells during neonatal growth, declining from P7 to P21.&lt;SEP&gt;Alpha cells show higher DNA damage during replication compared to beta cells, corresponding to their higher replication rates.&lt;SEP&gt;Alpha cells show no significant increase in DNA damage under HFD, db/db, or 8-week NOD conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;Alpha cells show differential DNA damage vulnerability compared to beta cells, shaped by replication dynamics, metabolic stress, and epigenetic safeguards.</data>
