<edge source="P21" target="cellular senescence">
  <data key="d12">4.0</data>
  <data key="d13">p21 is a cell-cycle inhibitor activated during the early initiation phase of cellular senescence.&lt;SEP&gt;Senescence progression involves activation of p21 as a cell-cycle inhibitor.&lt;SEP&gt;P21 mediates cell cycle arrest and produces a bioactive secretome associated with cellular senescence.&lt;SEP&gt;Patterns of early P21 dynamics determine proliferation-senescence cell fate after chemotherapy.&lt;SEP&gt;P21 is a marker of cellular senescence and cell cycle arrest studied in beta cells.&lt;SEP&gt;p21WAF1/Cip1 limits senescence and acinar-to-ductal metaplasia formation during pancreatitis.&lt;SEP&gt;p21 expression serves as a marker of cellular senescence in beta cells.</data>
