<edge source="SST" target="delta cell">
  <data key="d12">9.0</data>
  <data key="d13">SST (Somatostatin) is a well-established marker gene closely associated with delta cells in the pancreatic islets, and its relationship to this cell type has been characterized across multiple genomic and transcriptomic methodologies.

In the context of single-cell RNA sequencing (scRNA-seq), SST is identified as a marker gene expressed specifically in delta cells of human pancreatic islets, and it is routinely used to identify and define delta cell clusters based on its expression profile. Notably, SST has been recognized as a top upregulated marker gene in delta cells, with this upregulation occurring independently of sex and race/ethnicity, underscoring its robustness and specificity as a delta cell marker across diverse human populations.

Beyond transcriptomic approaches, SST also plays a critical role in chromatin accessibility-based analyses. In single-nucleus ATAC sequencing (snATAC-seq), SST is employed as a gene accessibility marker to validate and annotate delta cell cluster identity. Its chromatin accessibility signal serves as a cell type-specific indicator, confirming the identity of delta cell clusters in these epigenomic datasets. Additionally, SST has been utilized in ATAC-seq chromatin accessibility analyses as a hormone marker gene to identify delta cells, further extending its utility as a multi-modal biomarker.

SST is also applied in integrative analyses that compare gene accessibility with predicted RNA expression, enabling the identification of delta cells through a cross-modal validation approach. Collectively, SST functions as a highly reliable, cell type-specific marker for delta cells, consistently used for cluster annotation, validation, and identification across scRNA-seq, snATAC-seq, and integrative genomic frameworks.</data>
  <data key="d14">annotated_by,expressed_in,marker,marker_gene,marker_of</data>
  <data key="d15">chunk-9e607d2cca86a6257f1db73bacae2c96&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c0d05211cf3080af14ec050e5cc97ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a7873cb15c71b20e5fc369a6f0ab52a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d7bd4bfe81f828dceb60b520d85bcf2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73a24341c9b63bd3b6313252fe6ed4b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f02465fe113dd488219949222d1430e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-87d48756321bdf8ef533359c0655a3d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da10e6374cdbd3d6e4a07d773cd172d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e42c3b77d3170e854edbbc691159609d</data>
  <data key="d16">Single cell regulatory architecture of human pancreatic islets suggests sex differences in β cell function and the pathogenesis of type 2 diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Calorie restriction increases insulin sensitivity to promote beta cell homeostasis and longevity in mice.&lt;SEP&gt;Sex-specific regulatory architecture of pancreatic islets from subjects with and without type 2 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d17">1778570397</data>
  <data key="d18"></data>
</edge>
