<edge source="PPY" target="gamma cell">
  <data key="d12">9.0</data>
  <data key="d13">PPY (Pancreatic Polypeptide) serves as a well-established marker gene for gamma cells in pancreatic islets, with its relationship to this cell type documented across multiple analytical approaches and study contexts.

PPY is consistently identified as a cell type-specific marker gene expressed in pancreatic gamma cells, playing a central role in the identification and annotation of gamma cell clusters. Its expression is utilized in single-cell RNA sequencing (scRNA-seq) analyses to identify and validate gamma cell populations within human pancreatic islets, where it functions as a reliable transcriptomic signal for this specific cell type.

Beyond transcriptomic approaches, PPY also serves as a gene accessibility marker in single-nucleus ATAC sequencing (snATAC-seq) and broader ATAC-seq chromatin accessibility analyses. In these epigenomic contexts, PPY is used to validate gamma cell cluster identity by confirming open chromatin regions associated with its locus, bridging both gene expression and chromatin accessibility methodologies for gamma cell characterization.

Notably, PPY has been identified as a top upregulated marker gene in gamma cells in a manner that is independent of sex and race/ethnicity, underscoring its robustness and consistency as a gamma cell identifier across diverse human populations. This cross-demographic stability reinforces its utility as a universal reference marker for gamma cell annotation.

In summary, PPY functions as a multi-platform, hormone-associated marker gene that is integral to the identification, validation, and annotation of gamma cell clusters in pancreatic islet research, applicable across scRNA-seq, snATAC-seq, and chromatin accessibility studies.</data>
  <data key="d14">annotated_by,expressed_in,marker,marker_gene,marker_of</data>
  <data key="d15">chunk-9e607d2cca86a6257f1db73bacae2c96&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c0d05211cf3080af14ec050e5cc97ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a7873cb15c71b20e5fc369a6f0ab52a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d7bd4bfe81f828dceb60b520d85bcf2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73a24341c9b63bd3b6313252fe6ed4b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f02465fe113dd488219949222d1430e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-87d48756321bdf8ef533359c0655a3d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da10e6374cdbd3d6e4a07d773cd172d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e42c3b77d3170e854edbbc691159609d</data>
  <data key="d16">Single cell regulatory architecture of human pancreatic islets suggests sex differences in β cell function and the pathogenesis of type 2 diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Calorie restriction increases insulin sensitivity to promote beta cell homeostasis and longevity in mice.&lt;SEP&gt;Sex-specific regulatory architecture of pancreatic islets from subjects with and without type 2 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d17">1778570400</data>
  <data key="d18"></data>
</edge>
