<edge source="Unfolded Protein Response (UPR)" target="ATF6">
  <data key="d12">3.0</data>
  <data key="d13">ATF6 is one of three ER-membrane localized proteins that mediate the UPR in response to ER stress.&lt;SEP&gt;ATF6 is a sensor branch of the UPR whose specific loss in β-cells leads to senescence features.&lt;SEP&gt;ATF6 is a key sensor of the unfolded protein response, mediating prosurvival homeostatic functions on ER proteostasis.&lt;SEP&gt;Atf6 is a component of the unfolded protein response, and its deletion in β-cells compromises UPR signaling, leading to downstream effects including senescence.</data>
  <data key="d14">UPR branch,UPR sensor,sensor,stress signaling&lt;SEP&gt;gene regulation,stress response pathway</data>
