<edge source="p21Cip1" target="cellular senescence">
  <data key="d12">1.0</data>
  <data key="d13">p21Cip1 is a cyclin-dependent kinase inhibitor that drives the early senescence program in β-cells and mediates stable growth arrest.&lt;SEP&gt;P21CIP1 has emerged as a major driver of senescence in a broad range of cell types, established from studies on fibroblast senescence, genetic knockout mice, and cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;P21CIP1 is a major driver of senescence across a broad range of cell types.&lt;SEP&gt;P21CIP1 is expressed in a population of senescent beta-cells with SASP in diabetes models.</data>
  <data key="d14">growth arrest,mediator&lt;SEP&gt;activates,drives,marker_of,regulates</data>
  <data key="d15">chunk-ea9634b81ecdb467a2b26648246e5b5c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ef7d4c1829099c6037d8b8b7a83c3cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b861cee193cad9e0f142051047e83aae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-58c0cbc7de7a8a1060e8f1608271a28c</data>
  <data key="d16">Stress-induced β cell early senescence confers protection against type 1 diabetes.</data>
