<edge source="Immune Surveillance" target="cellular senescence">
  <data key="d12">1.0</data>
  <data key="d13">Impaired immune surveillance accelerates accumulation of senescent cells and aging.&lt;SEP&gt;Activation of early senescence response and subsequent immune surveillance are integral parts of a hormetic response to achieve resolution of stress and re-establishment of homeostasis.&lt;SEP&gt;Clearance of accumulated senescent cells by the immune system is the primary way senescence is resolved in most tissues during aging.&lt;SEP&gt;Immune surveillance of beta cell senescence is being studied as a component of type 1 diabetes pathogenesis.&lt;SEP&gt;Senescence response facilitates clearance of damaged beta cells by immune cells.</data>
  <data key="d14">accumulation,impaired surveillance&lt;SEP&gt;clearance,immune response&lt;SEP&gt;associated_with,clears,facilitates,resolves</data>
