<edge source="GCG" target="alpha cell">
  <data key="d12">9.0</data>
  <data key="d13">GCG (Glucagon) is a well-established marker gene with a strong and consistent association with pancreatic alpha cells, as evidenced across multiple analytical contexts and methodologies.

GCG serves as a canonical cell type-specific marker gene for pancreatic alpha cells, playing a central role in their identification and annotation. It is expressed in alpha cells within human pancreatic islets, as detected by single-cell RNA sequencing (scRNA-seq), where it is used to identify and validate alpha cell clusters. Its expression is consistently observed as a top upregulated marker gene in alpha cells, and notably, this upregulation occurs independently of sex and race/ethnicity, underscoring its robustness as a universal marker across diverse human populations.

Beyond transcriptomic analyses, GCG is also employed in chromatin accessibility studies. In single-nucleus ATAC sequencing (snATAC-seq), GCG functions as a gene accessibility marker to validate and confirm the identity of alpha cell clusters, reflecting its open chromatin state in these cells. Similarly, in broader ATAC-seq chromatin accessibility analyses, GCG is recognized as a hormone marker gene used to distinguish and identify alpha cells.

Collectively, GCG's utility spans both gene expression (scRNA-seq) and epigenomic (snATAC-seq, ATAC-seq) platforms, where it consistently serves as a reliable and specific marker for the annotation, identification, and validation of pancreatic alpha cell populations. Its role as a hormone-encoding gene — glucagon being a key pancreatic hormone produced by alpha cells — further reinforces its biological relevance and specificity to this cell type.&lt;SEP&gt;Adult glucagon-producing alpha cells express the glucagon gene and differentiate from an independent cell lineage.</data>
  <data key="d14">annotated_by,expressed_in,expresses,marker,marker_gene,marker_of</data>
  <data key="d15">chunk-9e607d2cca86a6257f1db73bacae2c96&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c0d05211cf3080af14ec050e5cc97ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a7873cb15c71b20e5fc369a6f0ab52a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d7bd4bfe81f828dceb60b520d85bcf2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73a24341c9b63bd3b6313252fe6ed4b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f02465fe113dd488219949222d1430e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-87d48756321bdf8ef533359c0655a3d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da10e6374cdbd3d6e4a07d773cd172d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce72a72ed1aaea72aac97c28374f8f86</data>
