<edge source="beta cell" target="DNA damage response">
  <data key="d12">5.0</data>
  <data key="d13">Senescent beta cells exhibit a DNA damage response as a hallmark of senescence.&lt;SEP&gt;Beta-cells require robust DNA damage response mechanisms to maintain genomic integrity throughout their lifespan.&lt;SEP&gt;Beta cell DNA damage response promotes islet inflammation in type 1 diabetes and modulates beta cell functional mass.&lt;SEP&gt;Beta cells accumulate DNA damage and activate DDR in response to various stressors in diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;DNA damage response pathways are activated in beta cells in both T1D and T2D, underscoring their importance in beta-cell biology.</data>
  <data key="d14">activated_in,activates,associated_with,exhibits,expressed_in,regulates,requires,undergoes</data>
  <data key="d15">chunk-e32fd907a01d621388ff41b9b47bfa34&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-80318e0997c6182c0124775c5f01f6a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-58f0193e389064a60d513f13c5cad52b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-72bf1fbaf7a329c364247108f8b30408&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28a44d52c17c29e9741a935aa76e8afe</data>
