<edge source="beta cell" target="diabetes">
  <data key="d12">4.0</data>
  <data key="d13">Beta-cell dysfunction and death deplete the beta-cell reserve, resulting in the development of diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;DNA damage may causally drive beta cell failure in diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Beta cell structure-function is compromised during aging and diabetes; CR may help preserve it.&lt;SEP&gt;Acceleration of beta cell aging plays a key role in diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Loss or dysfunction of β-cells disrupts glucose homeostasis and leads to the development of diabetes.</data>
