<edge source="beta cell" target="DNA repair">
  <data key="d12">4.0</data>
  <data key="d13">Failure to repair endogenous DNA damage in beta cells causes adult-onset diabetes in mice, highlighting the importance of DNA repair.&lt;SEP&gt;Effective and timely DNA repair is a prerequisite for healthy beta-cell function and appropriate differentiation.&lt;SEP&gt;Beta cells resolve DNA breaks more efficiently before mitosis compared to alpha cells.&lt;SEP&gt;Beta cells show robust DNA repair during homeostatic replication, which is compromised under metabolic stress from HFD.</data>
  <data key="d14">compromised_under_stress,higher_efficiency,maintains,protects,resolves,robust_under_homeostasis</data>
  <data key="d15">chunk-58f0193e389064a60d513f13c5cad52b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-72bf1fbaf7a329c364247108f8b30408&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7af94fcbbc3d167377ece712218fa36b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6204b07313b33d741c243f18ce86735</data>
  <data key="d16">Safeguarding genomic integrity in beta-cells: implications for beta-cell differentiation, growth, and dysfunction.&lt;SEP&gt;Developmental control of DNA damage responses in α- and β-cells shapes the selective beta-cell susceptibility in diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d17">1778571514</data>
  <data key="d18"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="beta cell" target="progenitor cell">
  <data key="d12">1.0</data>
  <data key="d13">Healthy progenitor pools requiring effective DDR give rise to differentiated beta cells; cell cycle arrest can trigger differentiation during lineage refinement.</data>
  <data key="d14">differentiated_from,related_to</data>
  <data key="d15">chunk-58f0193e389064a60d513f13c5cad52b</data>
  <data key="d16">Safeguarding genomic integrity in beta-cells: implications for beta-cell differentiation, growth, and dysfunction.</data>
  <data key="d17">1778568835</data>
  <data key="d18"></data>
</edge>
