<edge source="beta cell" target="DNMT3A">
  <data key="d12">4.0</data>
  <data key="d13">Loss of DNMT3A in pancreatic progenitors selectively increases DNA damage vulnerability of beta cells from neonatal growth through adulthood.&lt;SEP&gt;DNMT3A-dependent methylation during differentiation shapes DNA damage susceptibility selectively in beta cells, with 3aPKO mice showing higher beta-cell DNA damage.&lt;SEP&gt;DNMT3A is crucial for beta cell genomic integrity during rapid postnatal expansion; its knockout leads to increased DNA damage and apoptosis.&lt;SEP&gt;DNMT3A is expressed in beta cells through postnatal growth and is required for their genomic stability and identity maintenance.</data>
  <data key="d14">expressed_in,maintains,protects,regulates,required_for</data>
  <data key="d15">chunk-28a44d52c17c29e9741a935aa76e8afe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c63b5ad461844f8e5d9a90f5dfc52f1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-35d7a41162ea60151fe17b4e60e06d1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6204b07313b33d741c243f18ce86735</data>
