<edge source="alpha cell" target="KDM5D">
  <data key="d12">9.0</data>
  <data key="d13">KDM5D is a gene encoded exclusively on the male Y chromosome that exhibits notable sex-specific expression patterns in pancreatic alpha cells. Across multiple islet transcriptome analyses, KDM5D is consistently found to be upregulated and overexpressed in male alpha cells compared to their female counterparts.

This differential expression is not limited to transcriptional output alone; KDM5D is also associated with sex differences in chromatin accessibility within alpha cells, suggesting it plays a role in remodeling the epigenetic landscape in a sex-specific manner. Given its function as a lysine demethylase, KDM5D's overexpression in male alpha cells may influence the broader regulatory architecture of these cells, potentially driving sex-specific differences in islet function. Its origin on the Y chromosome ensures that its expression is inherently male-restricted, making it a key candidate gene for understanding why male and female islets may differ in their physiological and pathological responses.</data>
  <data key="d14">associated_with,expressed_in,overexpressed,overexpressed_in,regulates,sex_differences,upregulated</data>
  <data key="d15">chunk-fe5b7d8c678cb311e300af3b74f19ed6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e607d2cca86a6257f1db73bacae2c96&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-794cb97944fe847e61831fceed4d92ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d7bd4bfe81f828dceb60b520d85bcf2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dfd4ac2599dc6d5dc028ad0e83ccf82f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-87d48756321bdf8ef533359c0655a3d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ea44d17d2377f3dd0f15239a73e15e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e42c3b77d3170e854edbbc691159609d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-822d03d11fbf61e2a25591e2663ef1ca</data>
