<edge source="cellular senescence" target="senolytic">
  <data key="d12">6.0</data>
  <data key="d13">Pharmacologic strategies targeting senescence have shown beneficial effects in mouse models of diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Senolytics are drugs designed to selectively clear senescent cells, with applications across multiple diseases.&lt;SEP&gt;Senolytics remove senescent cells and alleviate doxorubicin-induced ovarian injury.&lt;SEP&gt;Senolytics are used to pharmacologically clear senescent cells, and disease phenotypes in Alzheimer and tauopathy mouse models show responsiveness to senolytics.&lt;SEP&gt;Senolytics are therapeutic agents used for the clearance of senescent cells, monitored using validated senescence biomarkers.&lt;SEP&gt;Senolytics can be used to ablate senescent beta cells and study the impact of senescence on beta cell EV cargo by comparing control and senolytic-treated animal islets.</data>
  <data key="d14">clearance,clears,eliminates,eliminates senescent cells,mitigates,removes,targets,therapeutic</data>
  <data key="d15">chunk-9bdc00ebaa404f286432a974cec96702&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d3b1de44d6b73a10793a43351e18e6e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ff588c6efe73ecb07c6b95acb392e92&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-682da4208f0eb800bc5523bd70a84eb7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf5aeca434044079720fd4ae2d32c9b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e32fd907a01d621388ff41b9b47bfa34</data>
  <data key="d16">Pancreatic β-cell senescence in diabetes: mechanisms, markers and therapies.&lt;SEP&gt;SenNet recommendations for detecting senescent cells in different tissues.&lt;SEP&gt;Exploring senescence as a modifier of β cell extracellular vesicles in type 1 diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d17">1778568520</data>
  <data key="d18"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="cellular senescence" target="aging">
  <data key="d12">4.0</data>
  <data key="d13">Accumulation of senescent cells is associated with aging-related disease and reduced longevity.&lt;SEP&gt;Accumulation of senescent cells contributes to aging phenotypes and age-related tissue deterioration.&lt;SEP&gt;Aging drives multiple senescence-related processes across tissues including kidney, liver, adipose, and brain.&lt;SEP&gt;Cellular senescence in post-mitotic cells is a driver of aging and age-related diseases.&lt;SEP&gt;Cellular senescence in ageing encompasses mechanisms from cell cycle arrest to therapeutic targeting opportunities.&lt;SEP&gt;An aged immune system drives senescence and ageing of solid organs.</data>
  <data key="d14">associated_with,causes,drives,promotes&lt;SEP&gt;immune-driven senescence,mechanisms,organ aging,therapeutic opportunities</data>
  <data key="d15">chunk-9bdc00ebaa404f286432a974cec96702&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-71a6a7a3a4894dbd7d979b7e5766d5a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b02375738a9ebacd53446fec2077ee76&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ff588c6efe73ecb07c6b95acb392e92&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d13aa78bf917b6b3ed2e772b6f010e3</data>
  <data key="d16">Pancreatic β-cell senescence in diabetes: mechanisms, markers and therapies.&lt;SEP&gt;SenNet recommendations for detecting senescent cells in different tissues.</data>
  <data key="d17">1778567669</data>
  <data key="d18"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="cellular senescence" target="embryonic development">
  <data key="d12">4.0</data>
  <data key="d13">Senescent cells are beneficial in embryonic development by facilitating organogenesis.&lt;SEP&gt;Programmed cell senescence is a developmental mechanism contributing to embryonic growth and patterning.&lt;SEP&gt;Cellular senescence plays a physiologically programmed function during embryonic development.&lt;SEP&gt;Cellular senescence is observed and plays a programmed role during embryonic development.</data>
  <data key="d14">beneficial_in,contributes_to,occurs_in,physiological role,regulates</data>
  <data key="d15">chunk-9bdc00ebaa404f286432a974cec96702&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-25d34b513b15180c8a2d7b57ae829067&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b02375738a9ebacd53446fec2077ee76&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ff588c6efe73ecb07c6b95acb392e92</data>
