<edge source="cellular senescence" target="DNA damage response">
  <data key="d12">6.0</data>
  <data key="d13">DNA damage markers are commonly seen in senescent cells, particularly with DNA damage-induced senescence.&lt;SEP&gt;Persistent DNA damage signaling triggers senescence-associated inflammatory cytokine secretion and senescence.&lt;SEP&gt;DNA damage response is associated with cellular senescence in tissues of aging mice and following telomeric DNA damage.&lt;SEP&gt;The DDR triggers cellular senescence through ATM/ATR-mediated p53 stabilization.&lt;SEP&gt;Chronic DNA damage response activates regulatory pathways involving miR-29 and p53 associated with cellular senescence.&lt;SEP&gt;Chronic DDR can lead to cellular senescence and cell death in beta cells.</data>
  <data key="d14">associated_with,causes,triggered_by,triggers</data>
