  <data key="d13">Naturally occurring p16INK4a-positive cells shorten healthy lifespan and are markers of senescence.&lt;SEP&gt;CDKN2A is a cell cycle inhibitor and senescence marker upregulated in senescent cells.&lt;SEP&gt;CDKN2A is a key senescence marker upregulated across multiple tissues and disease contexts.&lt;SEP&gt;p16(INK4a) (CDKN2A) is a marker of senescent cells; p16-positive senescent cells are distinct targets from p21-positive cells in senolytic strategies.&lt;SEP&gt;CDKN2A/p16INK4a is a well-established marker of cellular senescence studied in beta cells.</data>
  <data key="d14">associated_with,marker_of,upregulated_in,upregulates</data>
  <data key="d15">chunk-3d3b1de44d6b73a10793a43351e18e6e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-71a6a7a3a4894dbd7d979b7e5766d5a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a471400d67fa8643230222fb3576486&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-732255e9544dde6a7dbc319c61cd8e1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49e5c8949dfa6aa24ddf3e3b92d956e4</data>
  <data key="d16">SenNet recommendations for detecting senescent cells in different tissues.&lt;SEP&gt;Exploring senescence as a modifier of β cell extracellular vesicles in type 1 diabetes.&lt;SEP&gt;Nucleolar stress facilitates islet β cell senescence via hijacking the DNA damage response pathways.</data>
  <data key="d17">1778571250</data>
  <data key="d18"></data>
</edge>
