<edge source="cellular senescence" target="Senescence-Associated Secretory Phenotype">
  <data key="d12">4.0</data>
  <data key="d13">SASP is a key component of the senescent cell phenotype, with factors including cytokines, chemokines, and proteases upregulated in senescent cells.&lt;SEP&gt;SASP is a well-established senescence-associated feature used as a reference for cataloguing senescence markers.&lt;SEP&gt;Cellular senescence leads to the development of SASP, which includes increased EV release and altered EV cargo.&lt;SEP&gt;Senescent beta cells produce and secrete SASP, exacerbating the inflammatory response within the islets.</data>
