  <data key="d12">2.0</data>
  <data key="d13">Specific deletion of c-MAF in endothelial cells inhibits the development of the liver sinusoid.&lt;SEP&gt;C-MAF in endothelial cells is required for normal liver sinusoid development; its deletion causes aberrant liver hematopoiesis.</data>
  <data key="d14">regulates</data>
  <data key="d15">chunk-01e46f30e47340f5c5b95376196543ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0be98cbe29b4c692e555154146fad640</data>
  <data key="d16">Exploring Large MAF Transcription Factors: Functions, Pathology, and Mouse Models with Point Mutations.</data>
  <data key="d17">1778566163</data>
  <data key="d18"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="C-MAF" target="lens maintenance">
  <data key="d12">1.0</data>
  <data key="d13">C-MAF is required for lens maintenance in adult mice; its loss leads to cataract development.</data>
  <data key="d14">regulates</data>
  <data key="d15">chunk-01e46f30e47340f5c5b95376196543ed</data>
  <data key="d16">Exploring Large MAF Transcription Factors: Functions, Pathology, and Mouse Models with Point Mutations.</data>
  <data key="d17">1778566164</data>
  <data key="d18"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="C-MAF" target="sinusoidal cell">
  <data key="d12">1.0</data>
  <data key="d13">Deletion of c-MAF in endothelial cells accelerates excessive proliferation of sinusoidal cells during the postnatal period.</data>
  <data key="d14">regulates</data>
  <data key="d15">chunk-01e46f30e47340f5c5b95376196543ed</data>
  <data key="d16">Exploring Large MAF Transcription Factors: Functions, Pathology, and Mouse Models with Point Mutations.</data>
  <data key="d17">1778566164</data>
  <data key="d18"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="C-MAF" target="lens epithelial cell">
  <data key="d12">1.0</data>
  <data key="d13">C-MAF is required for the differentiation of lens epithelial cells into lens fiber cells; its absence causes abnormal lens structure and cataracts.</data>
  <data key="d14">regulates,required_for</data>
  <data key="d15">chunk-0be98cbe29b4c692e555154146fad640</data>
  <data key="d16">Exploring Large MAF Transcription Factors: Functions, Pathology, and Mouse Models with Point Mutations.</data>
  <data key="d17">1778566165</data>
  <data key="d18"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="C-MAF" target="liver hematopoiesis">
  <data key="d12">1.0</data>
  <data key="d13">Specific deletion of C-MAF in endothelial cells induces aberrant expansion of postnatal liver hematopoiesis.</data>
