<edge source="ATM" target="beta cell senescence">
  <data key="d12">5.0</data>
  <data key="d13">Phosphorylated ATM (Ser1981-P) is detected in senescent human beta cells as a marker of DNA damage response.&lt;SEP&gt;Pharmaceutical blockade of ATM markedly attenuates the senescent phenotype of beta cells, indicating ATM promotes senescence downstream of nucleolar stress.&lt;SEP&gt;ATM activation is a critical mediator of nucleolar stress-induced beta cell senescence.&lt;SEP&gt;ATM activation by nucleolar stress drives beta cell senescence, as evidenced by suppression of senescence markers upon ATM inhibition with KU60019.&lt;SEP&gt;ATM activation by nucleolar stress promotes beta cell senescence; inhibition of ATM abrogates the senescent phenotype following nucleolar stress.</data>
  <data key="d14">associated_with,drives,marker_of,mediates,promotes,regulates</data>
