<edge source="DNA damage response" target="nucleolar stress">
  <data key="d12">5.0</data>
  <data key="d13">Nucleolar stress activates DDR-related signaling pathways including p53, ATR, and ATM.&lt;SEP&gt;Nucleolar stress induces senescence by hijacking DNA damage response pathways.&lt;SEP&gt;Nucleolar stress induced by CX-5461 and ActD activates the DNA damage response pathway in beta cells, as evidenced by γ-H2AX foci formation.&lt;SEP&gt;Nucleolar stress initiates a pseudo-DDR characterized by gamma-H2AX foci formation in the absence of actual double-strand breaks.&lt;SEP&gt;Nucleolar stress induced by chemical or genetic inhibition of rRNA transcription activates DNA damage-associated pathways including p53, PCNA, ATM, and RAD51, even in the absence of DSBs.</data>
  <data key="d14">activates,hijacks,pseudo-DDR,triggers</data>
  <data key="d15">chunk-6f008854d459401e11c35e6bd2541318&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93bb74bfaf0604b4b9f891e16fc9f0ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ce4f6e2d90d0c06e4549d7d45037298&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-787de2a35f76e08d5b7cddadbcc01954&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-15ab370ab273e97005ced113e59cc48a</data>
  <data key="d16">Nucleolar stress facilitates islet β cell senescence via hijacking the DNA damage response pathways.</data>
  <data key="d17">1778571204</data>
  <data key="d18"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="DNA damage response" target="beta cell senescence">
  <data key="d12">3.0</data>
  <data key="d13">Diverse stress stimuli converge on DDR pathways including γ-H2AX foci formation and p53 activation to initiate beta cell senescence.&lt;SEP&gt;Activation of the DNA damage response pathway, evidenced by γ-H2AX foci formation, contributes to the nucleolar stress-induced senescent phenotype in beta cells.&lt;SEP&gt;Persistent DNA damage and increased DDR contribute to beta-cell senescence and dysfunction in T1D.</data>
  <data key="d14">associated_with,contributes_to,initiates</data>
  <data key="d15">chunk-6f008854d459401e11c35e6bd2541318&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ce4f6e2d90d0c06e4549d7d45037298&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dad82642ce24967122d02819b52a6f45</data>
  <data key="d16">Nucleolar stress facilitates islet β cell senescence via hijacking the DNA damage response pathways.&lt;SEP&gt;Developmental control of DNA damage responses in α- and β-cells shapes the selective beta-cell susceptibility in diabetes.</data>
  <data key="d17">1778571531</data>
  <data key="d18"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="DNA damage response" target="nucleolus">
  <data key="d12">3.0</data>
  <data key="d13">The nucleolus is recognized as a sensor of DNA damage that may trigger the DDR.&lt;SEP&gt;The nucleolus coordinates stress response and genomic stability including DNA damage recognition.&lt;SEP&gt;The nucleolus serves as a sensor of various stress signals, particularly for surveillance of genomic stability and activation of DDR pathways.</data>
  <data key="d14">coordinates,senses,sensor,triggers</data>
  <data key="d15">chunk-93bb74bfaf0604b4b9f891e16fc9f0ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ce4f6e2d90d0c06e4549d7d45037298&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-15ab370ab273e97005ced113e59cc48a</data>
