<edge source="beta cell senescence" target="Senescence-Associated Secretory Phenotype">
  <data key="d12">1.0</data>
  <data key="d13">Senescent beta cells develop a Senescence-Associated Secretory Phenotype (SASP) as one of the defining features.&lt;SEP&gt;Chronic metabolic stress induces beta cells to adopt a SASP, spreading cytokines and ECM remodelling factors that promote beta cell failure.</data>
  <data key="d14">associated_with,causes&lt;SEP&gt;associated_with,causes</data>
  <data key="d15">chunk-58ad905d1d148d4bbfe7ce4c29566fc6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8f09e5d1418f8ae04b43a24b97c1d52d</data>
  <data key="d16">Pancreatic β-cell senescence in diabetes: mechanisms, markers and therapies.</data>
  <data key="d17">1778566689</data>
  <data key="d18"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="beta cell senescence" target="metabolic stress">
  <data key="d12">3.0</data>
  <data key="d13">Metabolic stress can trigger senescence in pancreatic beta cells.&lt;SEP&gt;Metabolic stress is implicated in promoting beta cell senescence through DDR activation.&lt;SEP&gt;Nucleolar stress observed in metabolic stress-induced senescent beta cells suggests broad involvement in beta cell deterioration during diabetic progression.</data>
  <data key="d14">causes,facilitates,promotes via DDR,triggers</data>
  <data key="d15">chunk-58ad905d1d148d4bbfe7ce4c29566fc6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93bb74bfaf0604b4b9f891e16fc9f0ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ce4f6e2d90d0c06e4549d7d45037298</data>
  <data key="d16">Pancreatic β-cell senescence in diabetes: mechanisms, markers and therapies.&lt;SEP&gt;Nucleolar stress facilitates islet β cell senescence via hijacking the DNA damage response pathways.</data>
  <data key="d17">1778571217</data>
  <data key="d18"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="beta cell senescence" target="NOD/ShiLtJ">
  <data key="d12">1.0</data>
