  <data key="d13">Senescent beta cells could exert paracrine effects on neighboring islet cells by virtue of SASP.</data>
  <data key="d14">exerts</data>
  <data key="d15">chunk-bcadefd5324392c8a202934109c8c242</data>
  <data key="d16">Pancreatic β-cell senescence in diabetes: mechanisms, markers and therapies.</data>
  <data key="d17">1778566807</data>
  <data key="d18"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="beta cell senescence" target="caloric restriction">
  <data key="d12">3.0</data>
  <data key="d13">Caloric restriction reduces the onset and expression of beta cell senescence signatures.&lt;SEP&gt;Long-term CR delays beta cell aging signatures including ER stress, DNA damage, and loss of Lamin B1.&lt;SEP&gt;CR is associated with reduced expression of 4 different markers of beta cell aging and/or senescence.</data>
  <data key="d14">associated_with,delays,reduces</data>
  <data key="d15">chunk-68a87a3a1f3eb5d8b0e53b41df492512&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-75f39153d9f864070e17a74724a6c8c6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-363f3a19905f833d29a7d1242acc6641</data>
  <data key="d16">Calorie restriction increases insulin sensitivity to promote beta cell homeostasis and longevity in mice.</data>
  <data key="d17">1778569489</data>
  <data key="d18"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="beta cell senescence" target="nucleolar stress">
  <data key="d12">6.0</data>
  <data key="d13">Nucleolar stress is identified as a crucial initiator and driver of pancreatic beta cell senescence.&lt;SEP&gt;Nucleolar stress is identified as a key upstream event that drives beta cell senescence.&lt;SEP&gt;Nucleolar stress induction triggers senescent phenotypes in established pancreatic beta cells.&lt;SEP&gt;Both chemical and genetic induction of nucleolar stress triggers senescent phenotypes in established beta cells.&lt;SEP&gt;Nucleolar stress promotes senescence in beta cells via ATM activation and pseudo-DNA damage responses.&lt;SEP&gt;Nucleolar stress, induced by both genetic and chemical means, robustly triggers beta cell senescence evidenced by increased SA-beta-gal activity, elevated senescence markers, and SASP secretion.</data>
  <data key="d14">causes,drives,facilitates,induces,promotes,triggers,upstream event</data>
  <data key="d15">chunk-6f008854d459401e11c35e6bd2541318&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a0590fd9be1db550e8a84c0781e8955&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93bb74bfaf0604b4b9f891e16fc9f0ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ce4f6e2d90d0c06e4549d7d45037298&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f082082b0871749ee637b1571aa95c0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e33cd1d99c96a7f6ffdd0fbea902670</data>
  <data key="d16">Nucleolar stress facilitates islet β cell senescence via hijacking the DNA damage response pathways.</data>
  <data key="d17">1778571204</data>
  <data key="d18"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="beta cell senescence" target="TIF-IA">
  <data key="d12">3.0</data>
  <data key="d13">Genetic depletion of TIF-IA induces nucleolar stress that triggers beta cell senescence.&lt;SEP&gt;TIF-IA depletion triggers robust beta cell senescence as evidenced by SA-β-gal activity and elevated senescence markers.&lt;SEP&gt;TIF-IA knockdown via shRNA in beta-TC-6 cells leads to examination of senescence-associated phenotypes.</data>
  <data key="d14">induces,regulates</data>
  <data key="d15">chunk-6f008854d459401e11c35e6bd2541318&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b377c464e48f2efecc4b62133585c2f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f082082b0871749ee637b1571aa95c0</data>
  <data key="d16">Nucleolar stress facilitates islet β cell senescence via hijacking the DNA damage response pathways.</data>
  <data key="d17">1778571205</data>
  <data key="d18"></data>
</edge>
